helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762				0	br	\<emph\>Object\</emph\> variables can store objects of various types, like tables and documents within a document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154807				0	br	\<emph\>String variables\</emph\> are assigned an empty-string ("") when they are declared.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155072				0	br	The \<emph\>Option Explicit\</emph\> statement has to be the first line in the module, before the first SUB. Generally, only arrays need to be declared explicitly. All other variables are declared according to the type-declaration character, or - if omitted - as the default type \<emph\>Single\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155383				0	br	$[officename] Basic supports four variable classes:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	br	5MyNumber=12				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155507				0	br	Declares one variable as a String and one as an Integer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155950				0	br	DIM text$(-15 to 5)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156357				0	br	Constants have a fixed value. They are only defined once in the program and cannot be redefined later:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156365				0	br	Dim Variable as Long				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	br	Examples for variable identifiers:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	br	Correct				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159116				0	br	Date variables can only contain dates and time values stored in an internal format. Values assigned to Date variables with \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030101.xhp\" name=\"Dateserial\"\>\<emph\>Dateserial\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030102.xhp\" name=\"Datevalue\"\>\<emph\>Datevalue\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030205.xhp\" name=\"Timeserial\"\>\<emph\>Timeserial\</emph\>\</link\> or \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030206.xhp\" name=\"Timevalue\"\>\<emph\>Timevalue\</emph\>\</link\> are automatically converted to the internal format. Date-variables are converted to normal numbers by using the \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030103.xhp\" name=\"Day\"\>\<emph\>Day\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030104.xhp\" name=\"Month\"\>\<emph\>Month\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030106.xhp\" name=\"Year\"\>\<emph\>Year\</emph\>\</link\> or the \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030201.xhp\" name=\"Hour\"\>\<emph\>Hour\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030202.xhp\" name=\"Minute\"\>\<emph\>Minute\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030204.xhp\" name=\"Second\"\>\<emph\>Second\</emph\>\</link\> function. The internal format enables a comparison of date/time values by calculating the difference between two numbers. These variables can only be declared with the key word \<emph\>Date\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159226				0	br	\<emph\>String\</emph\> variables contain character strings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3163798				0	br	MyNumber=5				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3166467				0	br	Dim Variable$				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id7617114				0	br	You can use plus (+) or minus (-) signs as prefixes for decimal numbers (with or without spaces).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10854				0	br	DIM c As Boolean				2002-02-02 02:02:02
