helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	br	Unlike the \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090201.xhp\" name=\"Do...Loop\"\>Do...Loop\</link\> statement, you cannot cancel a \<emph\>While...Wend\</emph\> loop with \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090412.xhp\" name=\"Exit\"\>Exit\</link\>. Never exit a While...Wend loop with \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090302.xhp\" name=\"GoTo\"\>GoTo\</link\>, since this can cause a run-time error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151114				0	br	Dim stext As String				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211	2			0	br	When a program encounters a While statement, it tests the condition. If the condition is False, the program continues directly following the Wend statement. If the condition is True, the loop is executed until the program finds Wend and then jumps back to the\<emph\> While \</emph\>statement. If the condition is still True, the loop is executed again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
