helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150359				0	br	oLib.addContainerListener( oListener ) ' Register the listener				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150592				0	br	An event structure type that contains information about an event exists for every Listener type. When a Listener method is called, an instance of this event is passed to the method as a parameter. Basic Listener methods can also call these event objects, so long as the appropriate parameter is passed in the Sub declaration. For example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	br	End Sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150768				0	br	In this example, the Listener-Interface uses the following methods:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150940				0	br	Listener methods must \<emph\>always\</emph\> be implemented to avoid Basic run-time errors.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
