helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\keys.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	br	A running macro can be aborted with Shift+Ctrl+Q, also from outside of the Basic IDE. If you are inside the Basic IDE and the macro halts at a breakpoint, Shift+Ctrl+Q stops execution of the macro, but you can recognize this only after the next F5, F8, or Shift+F8.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
