helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155738				0	br	Right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748				0	br	To automatically continue a series using the assumed completion rules, choose the \<emph\>AutoFill\</emph\> option after opening the \<emph\>Fill Series\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3146976				0	br	Before filling a series, first select the cell range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3148605				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_DAY\"\>Use the \<emph\>Date\</emph\> series type and this option to create a series using seven days.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	br	\<variable id=\"reihenfuellentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FillSeries\"\>Automatically generate series with the options in this dialog. Determine direction, increment, time unit and series type.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_MONTH\"\>Use the \<emph\>Date\</emph\> series type and this option to form a series from the names or abbreviations of the months.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149257	15			0	br	Defines the series type. Choose between \<emph\>Linear, Growth, Date \</emph\>and \<emph\>AutoFill\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149381				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:ED_START_VALUES\"\>Determines the start value for the series.\</ahelp\> Use numbers, dates or times.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149402				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_RIGHT\"\>Creates a series running from left to right within the selected cell range using the defined increment to the end value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150108				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_DAY_OF_WEEK\"\>Use the \<emph\>Date\</emph\> series type and this option to create a series of five day sets.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150364				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_GEOMETRIC\"\>Creates a growth series using the defined increment and end value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150887				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_DATE\"\>Creates a date series using the defined increment and end date.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3151300				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_YEAR\"\>Use the \<emph\>Date\</emph\> series type and this option to create a series of years.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153308				0	br	In this area you can specify the desired unit of time. This area is only active if the \<emph\>Date\</emph\> option has been chosen in the \<emph\>Series type\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153487				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:ED_END_VALUES\"\>Determines the end value for the series.\</ahelp\> Use numbers, dates or times.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_TOP\"\>Creates an upward series in the cell range of the column using the defined increment to the end value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	br	Determines the direction of series creation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154739				0	br	The term "increment" denotes the amount by which a given value increases.\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:ED_INCREMENT\"\> Determines the value by which the series of the selected type increases by each step.\</ahelp\> Entries can only be made if the linear, growth or date series types have been selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155418				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_BOTTOM\"\>Creates a downward series in the selected cell range for the column using the defined increment to the end value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155811				0	br	AutoFill tries to complete a value series by using a defined pattern. The series 1,3,5 is automatically completed with 7,9,11,13, and so on. Date and time series are completed accordingly; for example, after 01.01.99 and 15.01.99, an interval of 14 days is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156288				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_AUTOFILL\"\>Forms a series directly in the sheet.\</ahelp\> The AutoFill function takes account of customized lists. For example, by entering \<emph\>January\</emph\> in the first cell, the series is completed using the list defined under \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_LEFT\"\>Creates a series running from right to left in the selected cell range using the defined increment to the end value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3159238				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_ARITHMETIC\"\>Creates a linear number series using the defined increment and end value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Fill Series				2002-02-02 02:02:02
