helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153623				0	br	In the example above (scroll up, please), we want to know how many children have to travel more than 600 meters to school. The result is to be stored in cell B16. Set the cursor in cell B16. Enter the formula =DCOUNT(A1:E10;0;A13:E14) in B16. The \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> helps you to input ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153676				0	br	=DVAR(A1:E10;"Weight";A13:E14)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
