helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538				0	br	When a function expects a single value, but you entered a cell range, then the value from the cell range is taken that is in the same column or row as the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150867	57			0	br	IF(A1>5;100;"too small") If the value in A1 is higher than 5, the value 100 is entered in the current cell; otherwise, \<emph\>too small\</emph\> is entered in text format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
