helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1180455				0	br	ROUNDUP(45.67; 0) returns 46.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1278420				0	br	MOD(11.25; 2.5) returns 1.25.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1371501				0	br	ROUND(2.348; 0) returns 2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1477095				0	br	DEGREES(ATAN2(12.3; 12.3)) returns 45. The tangent of 45 degrees is 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1501510				0	br	Returns the positive square root of (PI multiplied by \<emph\>number\</emph\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id153508				0	br	Negative numbers round down to the integer below.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1589098				0	br	PRODUCT returns number1 * number2 * number3 * ...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id159611				0	br	EVEN(0) returns 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1604663				0	br	GCD(B1:B3) where cells B1, B2, B3 contain 9, 12, 9 gives 3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1614429				0	br	4^3 also returns 4 to the power of 3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id166020				0	br	=COUNTIF(A1:A10;C2) where cell C2 contains the text ">2006" (without the double quotes) - counts the number of cells in the range A1:A10 which are > 2006 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1804864				0	br	TAN(RADIANS(45)) returns 1, the tangent of 45 degrees.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1912289				0	br	ISEVEN(-2.1) returns TRUE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1997131				0	br	COMBINA returns the number of ways to choose these items, where the order of choosing is important. For example if there are 3 items A, B and C in a set, you can choose 2 items in 6 different ways, namely AB, BA, AC, CA, BC and CB.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id203863				0	br	To return the angle in degrees, use the DEGREES function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2052064				0	br	COMBINA implements the formula: count_1!/(count_1-count_2)!				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2091433				0	br	To generate random numbers which never recalculate, copy cells containing this function, and use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Paste Special\</item\> (with \<emph\>Paste All\</emph\> and \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> not marked and \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> marked).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2118594				0	br	=COUNTIF(A1:A10;"<"&B1) - when B1 contains 2006, this returns 6				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2188787				0	br	This function rounds towards zero. See ROUNDUP and ROUND for alternatives.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2361217				0	br	Either \<emph\>currency1\</emph\> or \<emph\>currency2\</emph\> must be specified as Euros.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2769249				0	br	The greatest common divisor is the positive largest integer which will divide, without remainder, each of the given integers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2855616				0	br	This function produces a new random number each time Calc recalculates. To force Calc to recalculate manually press Shift+Ctrl+F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3001800				0	br	To return the angle in degrees, use the DEGREES function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3068636				0	br	An alternative implementation would be \<item type=\"literal\"\>Multiple * ROUND(Number/Multiple)\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3109841				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LOG\"\>Returns the logarithm of a number to the specified base.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143229				0	br	The inverse trigonometric tangent of -1 returns the value -0.79.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143280				0	br	COTH(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143316				0	br	6				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143339				0	br	PRODUCT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143366				0	br	7				2002-02-02 02:02:02
