helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143606				0	br	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the range whose cells are included.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143638				0	br	You have a table in the cell range A1:B5 containing cities in column A and accompanying figures in column B. You have used an AutoFilter so that you only see rows containing the city Hamburg. You want to see the sum of the figures that are displayed; that is, just the subtotal for the filtered rows. In this case the correct formula would be:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143658				0	br	=SUBTOTAL(9; B2:B5)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143708				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_UMRECHNEN\"\>This function allows you to convert a European currency value into Euros.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143731				0	br	\<emph\>Syntax:\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143748				0	br	CONVERT(value;"Text"; "Text")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143763				0	br	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is the amount in the currency to be converted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143782				0	br	\<emph\>Text\</emph\> is the official abbreviation for the currency in question (for example, "EUR"). The first \<emph\>Text\</emph\> parameter gives the source value to be converted, the second \<emph\>Text\</emph\> parameter gives the destination value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143819				0	br	\<emph\>Example:\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143837				0	br	=CONVERT(100;"ATS";"EUR") converts 100 Austrian Schilling into Euro.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143853				0	br	=CONVERT(100;"EUR";"DEM") converts 100 Euro into German Mark.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144344				0	br	n: the starting power				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144357				0	br	m: the increment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144370				0	br	coefficients: a series of coefficients. For each coefficient the series sum is extended by one section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144414				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PRODUKT\"\>Multiplies all the numbers given as arguments and returns the product.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144446				0	br	PRODUCT(number 1 to 30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144460				0	br	\<emph\>Number 1 to number 30\</emph\> are up to 30 arguments whose product is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144494				0	br	If you enter the numbers 2; 3 and 4 in the Number 1; 2 and 3 text boxes, 24 will be returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144627				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_QUOTIENT\"\>Returns the integer result of a division operation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144659				0	br	QUOTIENT(Numerator;Denominator)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144687				0	br	=QUOTIENT(11;3) returns 3. The remainder of 2 is omitted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144732				0	br	LOG(number; base)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144746				0	br	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value whose logarithm is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144754				0	br	Entering the value 90 returns a hyperbolic cotangent of 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144786				0	br	Entering the value 123.343 and the value 2 in the \<emph\>count\</emph\> field will return the value 123.35.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144906				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SIN\"\>Returns the sine of the given number (angle).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144937				0	br	SIN(number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144950				0	br	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the angle in radians.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144983				0	br	The sine of the angle (in radians) 3.14 (Pi) is 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145135				0	br	=LCM_ADD(5;15;25) returns 75.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145150				0	br	\<emph\>Number(s)\</emph\>: a list of up to 30 numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145163				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCCOS\"\>Returns the inverse trigonometric cosine of a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	br	The inverse hyperbolic tangent of 0.99 returns the value 2.65.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145600				0	br	DEG(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145629				0	br	The inverse hyperbolic cosine of 1 returns the value 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145710				0	br	=CEILING( -11; -2) returns -10				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145725				0	br	=CEILING( -11; -2; 0) returns -10				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145740				0	br	=CEILING( -11; -2; 1) returns -12				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145765				0	br	COMBINA(count 1; count 2)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145876				0	br	If you enter the number 17.546 in the \<emph\>number\</emph\> field, with 1 specified as the number of rounding places, 17.5 will be returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145899				0	br	=ROUND(-32.4834; 3) returns -32.483. Change the cell format to see all decimals.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146020				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ABRUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number down, toward zero.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146051				0	br	ROUNDDOWN(number; count)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
