helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155284				0	br	LN(number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155297				0	br	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value whose natural logarithm is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155345				0	br	If you enter the value 642, FALSE will be returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155375				0	br	The inverse cotangent of -1 returns the value 2.36.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155476				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LOG10\"\>Returns the base-10 logarithm of a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155544				0	br	\<emph\>Count 2\</emph\> is the select count from the elements.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155608				0	br	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the power to which e is to be raised.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
