helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163704				0	br	If you enter the numbers 2; 3 and 4 in the Number 1; 2 and 3 text boxes, 9 will be returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163792				0	br	If both parameters \<emph\>Number\</emph\> and \<emph\>Significance\</emph\> are negative and the Mode value is equal to zero or is not given, the results in $[officename] and Excel will differ after the import has been completed. If you export the spreadsheet to Excel, use Mode=1 to see the same results in Excel as in Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163813				0	br	If you enter the value 642, TRUE will be returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163894				0	br	If both parameters \<emph\>Number\</emph\> and \<emph\>Significance\</emph\> are negative, and if the \<emph\>Mode\</emph\> value is equal to zero or is not specified, then the results in $[officename] Calc and Excel will differ after exporting. If you export the spreadsheet to Excel, use Mode=1 to see the same results in Excel as in Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163945				0	br	=FLOOR( -11; -2) returns -12				2002-02-02 02:02:02
