helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164926				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZAEHLENWENN\"\>Returns the number of elements that meet with certain criteria within a cell range.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164967				0	br	COUNTIF(range; criteria)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164980				0	br	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the range to which the criteria are to be applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165000				0	br	\<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> indicates the criteria in the form of a number, an expression or a character string. These criteria determine which cells are counted. You may also enter a search text in the form of a regular expression, e.g. "b.*" for all words that begin with b. You may also indicate a cell range that contains the search criterion. If you search for literal text, enclose the text in double quotes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165462				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TANHYP\"\>Returns the hyperbolic tangent of a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
