helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id4808496				0	br	ASINH(SINH(4)) returns 4.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5036164				0	br	ATAN2 returns the inverse trigonometric tangent, that is, the angle (in radians) between the x-axis and a line from point \<emph\>number_x, number_y\</emph\> to the origin. The angle returned is between -PI and PI.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5081637				0	br	The same result may be achieved by using the exponentiation operator ^:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5092318				0	br	This function produces a new random number each time Calc recalculates. To force Calc to recalculate manually press Shift+Ctrl+F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5169225				0	br	=COUNTIF(A1:A10;">=2006") - this returns 3				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5577562				0	br	LOG(7^4; 7) returns 4.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5627307				0	br	ISEVEN(3.999) returns FALSE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
