helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155276				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MTRANS\"\>Transposes the rows and columns of an array.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155325				0	br	C				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155355				0	br	A formula in which the individual values in a cell range are evaluated is referred to as an array formula. The difference between an array formula and other formulas is that the array formula deals with several values simultaneously instead of just one.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155468				0	br	The results returned by the system (if Stats = 0), will at least show the slope of the regression line and its intersection with the Y axis. If \<emph\>Stats\</emph\> do not equal 0, other results are to be displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155498				0	br	FREQUENCY(Data; Classes)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155652				0	br	105				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155684				0	br	5,46				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155707				0	br	10,96				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155730				0	br	9,35				2002-02-02 02:02:02
