helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149577	200			0	br	=COLUMNS(B5) returns 1 because a cell only contains one column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149711				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SPALTE\"\>Returns the column number of a cell reference.\</ahelp\> If the reference is a cell the column number of the cell is returned; if the parameter is a cell area, the corresponding column numbers are returned in a single-row \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060107.xhp#wasmatrix\" name=\"array\"\>array\</link\> if the formula is entered \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060107.xhp#somatrixformel\" name=\"as an array formula\"\>as an array formula\</link\>. If the COLUMN function with an area reference parameter is not used for an array formula, only the column number of the first cell within the area is determined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149744	121			0	br	=OFFSET(A1; 2; 2) returns the value in cell C3 (A1 moved by two rows and two columns down). If C3 contains the value 100 this function returns the value 100.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149809	131			0	br	=LOOKUP(A1; D1:D100;F1:F100) searches the corresponding cell in range D1:D100 for the number you entered in A1. For the instance found, the index is determined, for example, the 12th cell in this range. Then, the contents of the 12th cell are returned as the value of the function (in the result vector).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
