helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id1539353				0	br	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is any number. "Baht" is appended to the integral part of the number, and "Satang" is appended to the decimal part of the number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id1551561				0	br	See \<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/mwiki/index.php?title=Calc/Features/JIS_and_ASC_functions\"\>http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/mwiki/index.php?title=Calc/Features/JIS_and_ASC_functions\</link\> for a conversion table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id1993774				0	br	ASC(text)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id2355113				0	br	See also JIS function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id2504654				0	br	JIS(text)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id2949919				0	br	\<emph\>text\</emph\> is the text that contains characters to be converted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3083452				0	br	FIND(find_text; text; position)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3144733	191			0	br	VALUE("4321") returns 4321.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145208	42			0	br	FIXED(1234567.89;3) returns 1,234,567.890. FIXED(1234567.89;3;1) returns 1234567.890.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145226	223			0	br	BASE(255;16;4) returns 00FF in the hexadecimal system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241	231			0	br	\<emph\>radix\</emph\> indicates the base of the number system. It may be any positive integer between 2 and 36.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145299	15			0	br	\<emph\>value\</emph\> is a number, a reference to a cell containing a number, or a formula which returns a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145355	233			0	br	DECIMAL("17";10) returns 17.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145375				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RECHTS\"\>Defines the last character or characters in a text string.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145629	16			0	br	\<emph\>decimals\</emph\> is the optional number of decimal places.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145634				0	br	CHAR(number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145779	180			0	br	\<emph\>new text\</emph\> is the text that is to replace the text segment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3146080	126			0	br	\<emph\>find_text\</emph\> is the text to be searched for.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3146149				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_FINDEN\"\>Looks for a string of text within another string.\</ahelp\> You can also define where to begin the search. The search term can be a number or any string of characters. The search is case-sensitive.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3146757	68			0	br	UPPER("Good Morning") returns GOOD MORNING.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3146786				0	br	LEFT(text; number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3146847	171			0	br	\<emph\>Text 1; text 2; ...\</emph\> represent up to 30 text passages which are to be combined into one string.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3146894	108			0	br	\<emph\>text\</emph\> is the text whose length is to be determined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
