helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3148692				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SUCHEN\"\>Returns the position of a text segment within a character string.\</ahelp\> You can set the start of the search as an option. The search text can be a number or any sequence of characters. The search is not case-sensitive.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3148746	219			0	br	\<emph\>Minimum length\</emph\> (optional) determines the minimum length of the character sequence that has been created. If the text is shorter than the indicated minimum length, zeros are added to the left of the string.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3148820	152			0	br	\<emph\>text\</emph\> is the text containing the characters to extract.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3148925				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ERSETZEN\"\>Replaces part of a text string with a different text string.\</ahelp\> This function can be used to replace both characters and numbers (which are automatically converted to text). The result of the function is always displayed as text. If you intend to perform further calculations with a number which has been replaced by text, you will need to convert it back to a number using the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060110.xhp\" name=\"VALUE\"\>VALUE\</link\> function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3149141	102			0	br	LEFT("output";3) returns \<emph\>out\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
