helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3155833				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_FEST\"\>Specifies that a number be displayed with a fixed number of decimal places and with or without a thousands separator. This function can be used to apply a uniform format to a column of numbers.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3155871				0	br	T(value)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3155906	205			0	br	\<emph\>number\</emph\> is a number between 1 and 255 representing the code value for the character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3155954				0	br	CONCATENATE(Text 1;...;Text 30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156008	110			0	br	LEN("Good Afternoon") returns \<emph\>14\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156040	29			0	br	\<emph\>length\</emph\> is the number of characters in \<emph\>text\</emph\> to be replaced.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156074	60			0	br	TRIM(" hello") returns "hello".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156139	252			0	br	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number that is to be converted into a Roman numeral.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155	179			0	br	\<emph\>search_text \</emph\>is the text segment that is to be replaced (a number of times).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156167	163			0	br	\<emph\>Format\</emph\> is the text which defines the format. Use decimal and thousands separators according to the language set in the cell format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156263	85			0	br	EXACT("Sun microsystems";"Sun Microsystems") returns FALSE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156322	39			0	br	\<emph\>Decimals\</emph\> refers to the number of decimal places to be displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156361				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DEZIMAL\"\>Converts text with characters from a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#zahlensystem\" name=\"number system\"\>number system\</link\> to a positive integer in the base radix given.\</ahelp\> The radix must be in the range 2 to 36. Spaces and tabs are ignored. The\<emph\> text\</emph\> field is not case-sensitive.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156375	52			0	br	FIND(76;998877665544) returns 6.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156399	221			0	br	BASE(17;10;4) returns 0017 in the decimal system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871	222			0	br	BASE(17;2) returns 10001 in the binary system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3157888				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_GLAETTEN\"\>Removes spaces from a string, leaving only a single space character between words.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3157994				0	br	If the radix is 16, a leading x or X or 0x or 0X, and an appended h or H, is disregarded. If the radix is 2, an appended b or B is disregarded. Other characters that do not belong to the number system generate an error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3158407	156			0	br	MID("Sun Microsystems";5;5) returns \<emph\>Micro\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3158413				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_IDENTISCH\"\>Compares two text strings and returns TRUE if they are identical.\</ahelp\> This function is case-sensitive.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3158426				0	br	Any text containing numbers must be enclosed in quotation marks if you do not want it to be interpreted as a number and automatically converted to text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3159188	30			0	br	\<emph\>new text\</emph\> refers to the text which replaces \<emph\>text\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3159209	9			0	br	CODE("Hieronymus") returns 72, CODE("hieroglyphic") returns 104.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3159262	218			0	br	\<emph\>radix\</emph\> indicates the base of the number system. It may be any positive integer between 2 and 36.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3162905				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_GROSS\"\>Converts the string specified in the \<emph\>text\</emph\> field to uppercase.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3166451	28			0	br	\<emph\>position\</emph\> refers to the position within the text where the replacement will begin.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3289284				0	br	BAHTTEXT(12.65) returns a string in Thai characters with the meaning of "Twelve Baht and sixty five Satang".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id354014				0	br	Converts a number to Thai text, including the Thai currency names.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3674123				0	br	=TEXT(12.34567;"000.00") returns the text 012.35				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3984496				0	br	See also ASC function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id4650105				0	br	T("12345") returns the string 12345.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id5282143				0	br	FIXED(1234567.89;3;1) returns 1234567.890 as a text string.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id5292519				0	br	\<emph\>text\</emph\> is the text that contains characters to be converted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id8455153				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The ASC function converts full-width to half-width ASCII and katakana characters. Returns a text string.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
