helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3147410				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DAI_FUNC_WEEKSINYEAR\"\>Calculates the number of weeks of the year in which the date entered occurs.\</ahelp\> The number of weeks is defined as follows: a week that spans two years is added to the year in which most days of that week occur.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427	2			0	br	\<variable id=\"addintext\"\>The following describes and lists some of the available add-in functions. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3147501				0	br	Date: Any date in the respective month of the desired year. The Date parameter must be a valid date according to the locale settings of %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3147614				0	br	WEEKSINYEAR(A1) returns 53 if A1 contains 2/17/70, a valid date for the year 1970.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3149316				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DAI_FUNC_DAYSINMONTH\"\>Calculates the number of days of the month in which the date entered occurs.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3149351				0	br	Add-ins can also be implemented through the %PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"http://api.openoffice.org/\"\>API\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3149946				0	br	Date: Any date in the respective year. The Date parameter must be a valid date according to the locale settings of %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150111				0	br	Type: Calculates the type of difference. Possible values include 0 (interval) and 1 (in calendar months).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150205				0	br	ISLEAPYEAR(Date)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150297				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Determines whether a year is a leap year.\</ahelp\> If yes, the function will return the value 1 (TRUE); if not, it will return 0 (FALSE).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150786				0	br	ISLEAPYEAR(A1) returns 1, if A1 contains 2/29/68, the valid date 29th of February 1968 in your locale setting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150886				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DAI_FUNC_DIFFYEARS\"\>Calculates the difference in years between two dates.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
