helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148747				0	br	PTR_DOUBLE_ARR =2 pointer to a double array				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148750				0	br	Output: Pointer to an array of exactly 16 variables of type Paramtype. The first nParamCount entries are filled with the suitable type of parameter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837				0	br	At a minimum, the administrative functions \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"GetFunctionCount\"\>GetFunctionCount\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"GetFunctionData\"\>GetFunctionData\</link\> must exist. Using these, the functions as well as parameter types and return values can be determined. As return values, the Double and String types are supported. As parameters, additionally the cell areas \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"Double Array\"\>Double Array\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"String Array\"\>String Array\</link\>, and \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"Cell Array\"\>Cell Array\</link\> are supported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148888				0	br	\<emph\>Syntax\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148901				0	br	If type == 1: Length of the following string, including closing zero byte. If the length including closing zero byte equals an odd value a second zero byte is added to the string so that an even value is achieved. Therefore, Len is calculated using ((StrLen+2)&~1).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148923				0	br	Table number in the upper-left corner of the cell area; numbering starts at 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
