helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3143222				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MIN\"\>Returns the minimum value in a list of arguments.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3143236				0	br	PHI(-2.25) = 0.03				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145078				0	br	for an odd number: =MEDIAN(1; 5; 9; 20; 21) returns 9 as the median value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145080				0	br	\<emph\>C\</emph\> = 0 calculates the density function; \<emph\>C\</emph\> = 1 calculates the distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145138				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MITTELWERTA\"\>Returns the average of the arguments. The value of a text is 0.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
