helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3155327	114			0	br	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> is the kind of t-test to perform. Type 1 means paired. Type 2 means two samples, equal variance (homoscedastic). Type 3 means two samples, unequal variance (heteroscedastic).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3155757	16			0	br	\<emph\>Number 1, number 2...number 30\</emph\> are numerical values or ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3155919	10			0	br	=RANK(A10; A1:A50) returns the ranking of the value in A10 in value range A1:A50. If \<emph\>Value\</emph\> does not exist within the range an error message is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3155984	70			0	br	=NORMSDIST(1) returns 0.84. The area below the standard normal distribution curve to the left of X value 1 is 84% of the total area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3155995	94			0	br	\<emph\>Number 1,number 2,...number 30\</emph\> numerical values or ranges representing a sample.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
