helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3144507				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:NUMERICFIELD:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:ED_SCALEPAGENUM\"\>Enter the maximum number of pages to be printed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145074				0	br	Specifies the maximum number of pages on which every sheet with the current Page Style is to be printed. The scale will be reduced as necessary to fit the defined number of pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145389				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:NUMERICFIELD:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:ED_PAGENO\"\>The first page receives the page number specified in the spin box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_HEADER\"\>Specifies whether you want the column and row headers to be printed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_GRID\"\>Prints out the borders of the individual cells as a grid.\</ahelp\> For the view on screen, make your choice under \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"View\"\>\<emph\>View\</emph\>\</link\> - \<emph\>Grid lines\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148455				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_CHARTS\"\>Prints the charts that have been inserted into your spreadsheet.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149122				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_DRAWINGS\"\>Includes all drawing objects in the printed document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149258				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_NULLVALS\"\>Specifies that cells with a zero value are printed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149408				0	br	Defines a page scale for the printed spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149581				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_OBJECTS\"\>Includes all inserted objects (if printable) and graphics with the printed document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_NOTES\"\>Prints the notes defined in your spreadsheet.\</ahelp\> They will be printed on a separate page, along with the corresponding cell reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150205				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_TOPDOWN\"\>Prints vertically from the left column to the bottom of the sheet.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCPAGE_TABLE\"\>Specifies the elements to be included in the printout of all sheets with the current Page Style. Additionally, you can set the print order, the first page number, and the page scale.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3152899				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_METRICFIELD_RID_SCPAGE_TABLE_ED_SCALEALL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a scaling factor. Factors less than 100 reduce the pages, higher factors enlarge the pages.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153715				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_FORMULAS\"\>Prints the formulas contained in the cells, instead of the results.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_LEFTRIGHT\"\>Prints horizontally from the top row of the sheet to the right column.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3155378				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:BTN_PAGENO\"\>Select this option if you want the first page to start with a number other than 1.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3159171				0	br	Specifies a scaling factor to scale all printed pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3166423				0	br	Defines the order in which data in a sheet is numbered and printed when it does not fit on one printed page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN1096D				0	br	Scaling mode				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10971				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:ListBox:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:LB_SCALEMODE\"\>Select a scaling mode from the list box. Appropriate controls will be shown at the side of the list box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN1099A				0	br	Scaling factor				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109B2				0	br	Fit print range(s) to width/height				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109B5				0	br	Specifies the maximum number of pages horizontally (width) and vertically (height) on which every sheet with the current Page Style is to be printed. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109BB				0	br	The print ranges are always scaled proportionally, so the resulting number of pages may be less than specified.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109BF				0	br	You may clear one of the boxes, then the unspecified dimension will use as many pages as necessary.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109C3				0	br	If you clear both boxes, this will result in a scaling factor of 100%.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109CE				0	br	Width in pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109D1				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:NumericField:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:ED_SCALEPAGEWIDTH\"\>Enter the maximum number of pages to be printed horizontally across.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E8				0	br	Height in pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109EB				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:NumericField:RID_SCPAGE_TABLE:ED_SCALEPAGEHEIGHT\"\>Enter the maximum number of pages to be printed vertically stacked.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A26				0	br	Number of pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154013				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080000.xhp\" name=\"Print Ranges\"\>Print Ranges\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154729				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Edit\"\>Edit\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	br	If you do not define any print range manually, Calc assigns an automatic print range to include all the cells that are not empty.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Manages print ranges. Only cells within the print ranges will be printed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Print Ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145673				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080100.xhp\" name=\"Define\"\>Define\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DefinePrintArea\"\>Defines an active cell or selected cell area as the print range.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Define				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153562				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080200.xhp\" name=\"Remove\"\>Remove\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DeletePrintArea\"\>Removes the defined print area.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Remove				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149260				0	br	Rows to repeat				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149581				0	br	Columns to repeat				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153088				0	br	Edit Print Ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156281				0	br	Print range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145174				0	br	Select \<emph\>-none-\</emph\> to remove a print range definition for the current spreadsheet. Select \<emph\>-entire sheet-\</emph\> to set the current sheet as a print range. Select \<emph\>-selection-\</emph\> to define the selected area of a spreadsheet as the print range. By selecting \<emph\>-user-defined-\</emph\>, you can define a print range that you have already defined using the \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Define\</emph\> command. If you have given a name to a range using the \<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\> command, this name will be displayed and can be selected from the list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	br	In the right-hand text box, you can enter a print range by reference or by name. If the cursor is in the \<emph\>Print range\</emph\> text box, you can also select the print range in the spreadsheet with your mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_AREAS:ED_PRINTAREA\"\>Allows you to modify a defined print range.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_AREAS:ED_REPEATROW\"\>Choose one or more rows to print on every page. In the right text box enter the row reference, for example, "1" or $1" or "$2:$3".\</ahelp\> The list box displays \<emph\>-user defined-\</emph\>. You can also select \<emph\>-none-\</emph\> to remove a defined repeating row.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	br	You can also define repeating columns by dragging the mouse in the spreadsheet, if the cursor is in the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> text field in the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155418				0	br	You can also define repeating rows by dragging the mouse in the spreadsheet, if the cursor is in the \<emph\>Rows to repeat\</emph\> text field in the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_AREAS:ED_REPEATCOL\"\>Choose one or more columns to print on every page. In the right text box enter the column reference, for example, "A" or "AB" or "$C:$E".\</ahelp\> The list box then displays \<emph\>-user defined-\</emph\>. You can also select \<emph\>-none-\</emph\> to remove a defined repeating column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3159488				0	br	\<variable id=\"druckbereichetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:EditPrintArea\"\>Opens a dialog where you can specify the print range.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> You can also set the rows or columns which are to be repeated in every page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
