helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153252				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030300.xhp\" name=\"Trace Dependents\"\>Trace Dependents\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148948				0	br	The area of all cells that are used together with the active cell in a formula is highlighted by a blue frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112				0	br	This function works per level. For instance, if one level of traces has already been activated to show the precedents (or dependents), then you would see the next dependency level by activating the \<emph\>Trace\</emph\> function again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowDependents\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Draws tracer arrows to the active cell from formulas that depend on values in the active cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
