helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153821				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030800.xhp\" name=\"Mark Invalid Data\"\>Mark Invalid Data\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowInvalid\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Marks all cells in the sheet that contain values outside the validation rules.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211				0	br	The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12120000.xhp\" name=\"validity rules\"\>validity rules\</link\> restrict the input of numbers, dates, time values and text to certain values. However, it is possible to enter invalid values or copy invalid values into the cells if the \<emph\>Stop\</emph\> option is not selected. When you assign a validity rule, existing values in a cell will not be modified.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Mark Invalid Data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030900.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152349				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>cells; refreshing traces\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>traces; refreshing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;traces\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152349				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030900.xhp\" name=\"Refresh Traces\"\>Refresh Traces\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030900.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	br	Detective arrows in the document are updated under the following circumstances:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030900.xhp	0	help	par_id3148947				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RefreshArrows\"\>Redraws all traces in the sheet. Formulas modified when traces are redrawn are taken into account.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030900.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	br	If \<emph\>Tools - Detective - Update Automatically\</emph\> is turned on, every time formulas are changed in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030900.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	br	Starting \<emph\>Tools - Detective - Update Refresh Traces\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
