helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155629				0	br	Goal Seek				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	br	\<variable id=\"zielwertsuchetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:GoalSeekDialog\"\>Opens a dialog where you can solve an equation with a variable.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> After a successful search, a dialog with the results opens, allowing you to apply the result and the target value directly to the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146984				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_SOLVER:ED_TARGETVAL\"\>Specifies the value you want to achieve as a new result.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_SOLVER:ED_VARCELL\"\>Specifies the reference for the cell that contains the value you want to adjust in order to reach the target.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211				0	br	In this section, you can define the variables in your formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_SOLVER:ED_FORMULACELL\"\>In the formula cell, enter the reference of the cell which contains the formula. It contains the current cell reference.\</ahelp\> Click another cell in the sheet to apply its reference to the text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06040000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Goal Seek				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145273				0	br	Settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145367				0	br	Display border				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149402				0	br	Copy entire sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149582				0	br	Copy back				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153954				0	br	Comment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156023				0	br	Create Scenario				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156280				0	br	Name of scenario				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969	23			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:CB_COPYALL\"\>Copies the entire sheet into an additional scenario sheet. \</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	br	\<variable id=\"szenariotext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ScenarioManager\"\>Defines a scenario for the selected sheet area.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041	13			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_SCENWIN_TOP\"\>Defines the name for the scenario. Use a clear and unique name so you can easily identify the scenario.\</ahelp\> You can also modify a scenario name in the Navigator through the \<emph\>Properties \</emph\>context menu command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:LB_COLOR\"\>Highlights the scenario in your table with a border. The color for the border is specified in the field to the right of this option.\</ahelp\> The border will have a title bar displaying the name of the last scenario. The button on the right of the scenario border offers you an overview of all the scenarios in this area, if several have been defined. You can choose any of the scenarios from this list without restrictions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153364				0	br	This section is used to define some of the settings used in the scenario display.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:CB_TWOWAY\"\>Copies the values of cells that you change into the active scenario. If you do not select this option, the scenario is not changed when you change cell values. The behavior of the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> setting depends on the cell protection, the sheet protection, and the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> settings.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411	15			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_SCENWIN_BOTTOM\"\>Specifies additional information about the scenario. This information will be displayed in the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> when you click the \<emph\>Scenarios\</emph\> icon and select the desired scenario.\</ahelp\> You can also modify this information in the Navigator through the \<emph\>Properties \</emph\>context menu command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10637				0	br	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/guide/scenario.xhp#scenario\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075A				0	br	Prevent changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075E				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:CheckBox:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:CB_PROTECT\"\>Prevents changes to the active scenario. The behavior of the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> setting depends on the cell protection, the sheet protection, and the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> settings.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10778				0	br	You can only change the scenario properties if the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> option is not selected and if the sheet is not protected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10780				0	br	You can only edit cell values if the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> option is selected, if the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> is option is not selected, and if the cells are not protected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078C				0	br	You can only change scenario cell values and write them back into the scenario if the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> option is not selected, if the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> option is selected, and if the cells are not protected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Create Scenario				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147228				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06060100.xhp\" name=\"Sheets\"\>Sheets\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148946				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06060000.xhp\" name=\"Protect Document\"\>Protect Document\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06060200.xhp\" name=\"Documents\"\>Documents\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153362	2			0	br	The\<emph\> Protect Document \</emph\>command prevents changes from being made to cells in the sheets or to sheets in a document. As an option, you can define a password. If a password is defined, removal of the protection is only possible if the user enters the correct password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10622				0	br	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_protect.xhp#cell_protect\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Protect Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150206				0	br	Password (optional)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153087				0	br	Protecting Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148664				0	br	\<variable id=\"tabelletext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Protect\"\>Protects the cells in the current sheet from being modified.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Choose \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Protect Sheet\</emph\> dialog in which you then specify sheet protection with or without a password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148700				0	br	Complete protection of your work can be achieved by combining both options on the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\> menu, including password protection. To prohibit opening the document altogether, in the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> dialog mark the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> box before you click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149123				0	br	Select the cells that will be unprotected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149566	9			0	br	To later change an unprotected area to a protected area, select the range. Next, on the \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\> tab page, check the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> box. Finally, choose the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet \</emph\>menu. The previously editable range is now protected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	br	To protect cells from further editing, the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> check box must be checked on the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020600.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Cell Protection\"\>\<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\>\</link\> tab page or on the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149815				0	br	Once saved, protected sheets can only be saved again by using the \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150301				0	br	If a sheet is protected, you will not be able to modify or delete any Cell Styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	br	Select \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\>. Unmark the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Protect\"\>Allows you to enter a password to protect the sheet from unauthorized changes.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153964				0	br	Sheet protection also affects the context menu of the sheet tabs at the bottom of the screen. The \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> and \<emph\>Move/Copy\</emph\> commands cannot be selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490	8			0	br	Unprotected cells or cell ranges can be set up on a protected sheet by using the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> and \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\> menus: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	br	A protected sheet or cell range can no longer be modified until this protection is disabled. To disable the protection, choose the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> command. If no password was set, the sheet protection is immediately disabled. If the sheet was password protected, the \<emph\>Remove Protection\</emph\> dialog opens, where you must enter the password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156384				0	br	On the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> menu, activate protection for the sheet. Effective immediately, only the cell range you selected in step 1 can be edited.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Protecting Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150541				0	br	Protecting document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	br	Password (optional)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145172				0	br	\<variable id=\"dokumenttext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToolProtectionDocument\"\>Protects the sheet structure of your document from modifications. It is impossible to insert, delete, rename, move or copy sheets.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Open the \<emph\>Protect document\</emph\> dialog with \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</emph\>. Optionally enter a password and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	7			0	br	A protected document, once saved, can only be saved again with the \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> menu command. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717	9			0	br	You can completely protect your work by combining both options from \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\>, including password entry. If you want to prevent the document from being opened by other users, select \<emph\>Save With Password \</emph\>and click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> button. The \<emph\>Enter Password\</emph\> dialog appears. Consider carefully when choosing a password; if you forget it after you close a document you will be unable to access the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	br	The structure of protected spreadsheet documents can be changed only if the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> option is disabled. On the context menus for the spreadsheet tabs at the lower graphic border, only the menu item \<emph\>Select All Sheets\</emph\> can be activated. All other menu items are deactivated. To remove the protection, call up the command \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</emph\> again. If no password is assigned, protection is immediately removed. If you were assigned a password, the \<emph\>Remove Spreadsheet Protection\</emph\> dialog appears, in which you must enter the password. Only then can you remove the check mark specifying that protection is active.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155412				0	br	You can create a password to protect your document against unauthorized or accidental modifications.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Protecting document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06070000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145673				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; auto calculating sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoCalculate function in sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>correcting sheets automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas;AutoCalculate function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell contents;AutoCalculate function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145673				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06070000.xhp\" name=\"AutoCalculate\"\>AutoCalculate\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145173				0	br	All cells are recalculated after a sheet cell has been modified. Any charts in the sheet will also be refreshed. If the\<emph\> AutoCalculate\</emph\> function is activated, the \<emph\>Recalculate\</emph\> function F9 is not available.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AutomaticCalculation\"\>Automatically recalculates all formulas in the document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06070000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	AutoCalculate				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157909				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>recalculating;all formulas in sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; recalculating manually\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell contents; recalculating\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157909				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Recalculate\"\>Recalculate\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	br	After the document has been recalculated, the display is refreshed. Any charts contained in the sheet are also refreshed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Calculate\"\>Recalculates the current sheet manually. Use this command to update all calculations in the document if you have deselected the automatic recalculation function, and also to update the NOW() function.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Recalculate				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	bm_id2486037				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>entering entries with AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>capital letters;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148492				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"AutoInput\"\>AutoInput\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	br	When typing formulas using characters that match previous entries, a Help tip will appear listing the last ten functions used from \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>, from all defined range names, from all database range names, and from the content of all label ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AutoComplete\"\>Switches the AutoInput function on and off, which automatically completes entries, based on other entries in the same column.\</ahelp\> The column is scanned up to a maximum of 2000 cells or 200 different strings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	br	AutoInput is case-sensitive. If, for example, you have written "Total" in a cell, you cannot enter "total" in another cell of the same column without first deactivating AutoInput.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	br	The completion text is highlighted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065D				0	br	To accept the completion, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> or a cursor key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10665				0	br	To append text or to edit the completion, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066D				0	br	To view more completions, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> to scroll forward, or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> to scroll backward.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10679				0	br	To see a list of all available AutoInput text items for the current column, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+D\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	AutoInput				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06990000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153087				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06990000.xhp\" name=\"Cell Contents\"\>Cell Contents\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06990000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	br	Opens a submenu with commands to calculate tables and activate AutoInput.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06990000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Cell Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\07080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163800				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07080000.xhp\" name=\"Split\"\>Split\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\07080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149263				0	br	A split window has its own scrollbars in each partial section; by contrast, \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07090000.xhp\" name=\"fixed window sections\"\>fixed window sections\</link\> are not scrollable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\07080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SplitWindow\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Divides the current window at the top left corner of the active cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\07080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154910				0	br	You can also use the mouse to split the window horizontally or vertically. To do this, drag the thick black line located directly above the vertical scrollbar or directly to the right of the horizontal scrollbar into the window. A thick black line will show where the window is split.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\07080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Split				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\07090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150517				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07090000.xhp\" name=\"Freeze\"\>Freeze\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\07090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156289				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FreezePanes\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Divides the sheet at the top left corner of the active cell and the area to the top left is no longer scrollable.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\07090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Freeze				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147228				0	br	Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150010				0	br	More >>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153188				0	br	Add/Modify				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156422				0	br	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157909				0	br	Define Database Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
