helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150768	19			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_DPLAY_SELECT\"\>To define the layout of a DataPilot table, drag and drop data field buttons onto the \<emph\>Page Fields, Row Fields, Column Fields, \</emph\>and\<emph\> Data Fields \</emph\>areas.\</ahelp\> You can also use drag and drop to rearrange the data fields on a DataPilot table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3152583				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_PIVOT_LAYOUT:BTN_TOTALROW\"\>Calculates and displays the grand total of the row calculation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153838				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_PIVOT_LAYOUT:ED_OUTAREA\"\>Select the area where you want to display the results of the DataPilot table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_PIVOT_LAYOUT:BTN_IGNEMPTYROWS\"\>Ignores empty fields in the data source.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155417				0	br	Specify the settings for displaying the results of the DataPilot table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DataPilotExec\"\>Specify the layout of the table that is generated by the DataPilot.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155961				0	br	If the selected area contains data, the DataPilot overwrites the data. To prevent the loss of existing data, let the DataPilot automatically select the area to display the results.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_PIVOT_LAYOUT:BTN_TOTALCOL\"\>Calculates and displays the grand total of the column calculation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN10897				0	br	Add filter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN1089B				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Adds a Filter button to DataPilot tables that are based on spreadsheet data.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108B2				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the Filter dialog.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C9				0	br	Enable drill to details				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108CD				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select this check box and double-click an item label in the table to show or hide details for the item. Clear this check box and double-click a cell in the table to edit the contents of the cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108DC				0	br	To examine details inside a DataPilot table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E0				0	br	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E6				0	br	Select a range of cells and choose \<emph\>Data - Outline - Show Details\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108EE				0	br	Double-click a field in the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108F1				0	br	If you double-click a field which has adjacent fields at the same level, the \<emph\>Show Detail\</emph\> dialog opens:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN10900				0	br	Show Detail				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090102.xhp	0	help	par_idN10904				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Choose the field that you want to view the details for.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
