helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147102				0	br	\<variable id=\"zusaetzetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Displays or hides additional filtering options.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264				0	br	If the \<emph\>Regular Expression\</emph\> check box is selected, you can use EQUAL (=) and NOT EQUAL (<>) also in comparisons. You can also use the following functions: DCOUNTA, DGET, MATCH, COUNTIF, SUMIF, LOOKUP, VLOOKUP and HLOOKUP.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150768				0	br	Displays the name of the filtered data area in the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151245				0	br	Allows you to use wildcards in the filter definition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100001.xhp\" name=\"List of Regular Expressions\"\>List of Regular Expressions\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	br	Excludes duplicate rows in the list of filtered data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
