helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456				0	br	\<variable id=\"auto_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/auto_off.xhp\" name=\"Deactivating Automatic Changes\"\>Deactivating Automatic Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149565				0	br	Cell content always begins with uppercase				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150043				0	br	Quotation marks replaced by custom quotes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150345				0	br	Replace word with another word				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	br	The following shows you how to deactivate and reactivate the automatic changes in $[officename] Calc:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>. Go to the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab. Unmark \<emph\>Capitalize first letter of every sentence\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3152992				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\"\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	br	$[officename] Calc automatically converts certain entries to dates. For example, the entry \<emph\>1.1\</emph\> may be interpreted as January 1 of the current year, according to the locale settings of your operating system, and then displayed according to the date format applied to the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	br	To turn the AutoInput on and off, set or remove the check mark in front of \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - AutoCorrect\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730				0	br	When making an entry in a cell, $[officename] Calc automatically suggests matching input found in the same column. This function is known as \<emph\>AutoInput\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>. Go to the \<emph\>Custom Quotes\</emph\> tab and unmark \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	br	By default, $[officename] automatically corrects many common typing errors and applies formatting while you type. You can immediately undo any automatic changes with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267				0	br	To ensure that an entry is interpreted as text, add an apostrophe at the beginning of the entry. The apostrophe is not displayed in the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3166425				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>. Go to the \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> tab. Select the word pair and click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Deactivating Automatic Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156423				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>AutoFilter function;applying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; filter values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; filter sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drop-down menus in sheet columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	br	\<variable id=\"autofilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/autofilter.xhp\" name=\"Applying AutoFilter\"\>Applying AutoFilter\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340				0	br	To stop using AutoFilter, reselect all cells selected in step 1 and once again choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	br	The \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> function inserts a combo box on one or more data columns that lets you select the records (rows) to be displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	br	Select the columns you want to use AutoFilter on.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12040100.xhp\" name=\"Data - Filter - AutoFilter\"\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</emph\>. The combo box arrows are visible in the first row of the range selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714	12			0	br	To display all records again, select the \<emph\>-all-\</emph\> entry in the AutoFilter combo box. If you choose \<emph\>-Standard-\</emph\>, the \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> dialog appears, allowing you to set up a standard filter. Choose \<emph\>-Top 10-\</emph\> to display the highest 10 values only. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060106.xhp\" name=\"SUBTOTAL\"\>SUBTOTAL\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	br	Run the filter by clicking the drop-down arrow in the column heading and choosing an item.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	br	Only those rows whose contents meet the filter criteria are displayed. The other rows are filtered. You can see if rows have been filtered from the discontinuous row numbers. The column that has been used for the filter is identified by a different color for the arrow button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236				0	br	The arithmetic functions also take account of the cells that are not visible due to an applied filter. For example, a sum of an entire column will also total the values in the filtered cells. Apply the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060106.xhp\" name=\"SUBTOTAL\"\>SUBTOTAL\</link\> function if only the cells visible after the application of a filter are to be taken into account.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id4303415				0	br	To assign different AutoFilters to different sheets, you must first define a database range on each sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id9216589				0	br	When you apply an additional AutoFilter on another column of a filtered data range, then the other combo boxes list only the filtered data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Applying AutoFilter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155132				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>tables; AutoFormat function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;AutoFormat function for tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoFormat function;defining and applying formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; automatically formatting spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic formatting in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets;AutoFormat function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>applying;automatic formatting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155132				0	br	\<variable id=\"autoformat\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/autoformat.xhp\" name=\"Using AutoFormat for Tables\"\>Applying Automatic Formatting to a Selected Cell Range\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	br	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Select All\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868				0	br	You can define a new AutoFormat that is available to all spreadsheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3149210				0	br	If you do not see any change in color of the cell contents, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Value Highlighting\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3149401				0	br	You can use the AutoFormat feature to quickly apply format a sheet or a selected cell range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242				0	br	To select which properties to include in an AutoFormat, click \<emph\>More\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	br	Format a sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153815				0	br	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - AutoFormat\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
