helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	br	Only the visible cells of the selection are copied, deleted, moved, or formatted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3148577				0	br	Assume you have hidden a few rows in a cell range. Now you want to copy, delete, or format only the remaining visible rows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	br	Cells were filtered by AutoFilters, standard filters or advanced filters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150044				0	br	Copy, delete, move, or format a selection of currently visible cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150751				0	br	Result				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	br	Copy, delete, move, or format a selection of currently visible cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154371				0	br	All cells of the selection, including the hidden cells, are copied, deleted, moved, or formatted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	br	$[officename] behavior depends on how the cells were made invisible, by a filter or manually.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	br	Method and Action				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3166427				0	br	Cells were hidden using the \<emph\>Hide\</emph\> command in the context menu of the row or column headers, or through an \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"outline\"\>outline\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Only Copy Visible Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154686				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; referencing cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; referencing by drag and drop \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references;inserting by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;references, by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154686				0	br	\<variable id=\"cellreference_dragdrop\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreference_dragdrop.xhp\" name=\"Referencing Cells by Drag-and-Drop\"\>Referencing Cells by Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	br	This method can also be used to insert a range from another sheet of the same document into the current sheet. Select the active document as source in step 4 above.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752				0	br	In the Navigator, the source file object appears under "Range names".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	br	Open the sheet in which you want to insert something.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	br	Open the document that contains the source cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	br	To set the source range as the range, select the cells and choose \<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>. Save the source document, and do not close it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	br	Click the name under "Range names" in the Navigator, and drag into the cell of the current sheet where you want to insert the reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154732				0	br	Open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>. In the lower box of the Navigator select the source file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	br	Using the \<emph\>Drag Mode\</emph\> icon in Navigator, choose whether you want the reference to be a hyperlink, link, or copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3156444				0	br	With the help of the Navigator you can reference cells from one spreadsheet to another sheet in the same document or in a different document. The cells can be inserted as a copy, link or hyperlink. The range to be inserted must be defined with a name in the original file so that it can be inserted in the target file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Referencing Cells by Drag-and-Drop				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147436				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>sheet references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; to cells in another document\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; operating in another document\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436				0	br	\<variable id=\"cellreferences\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences.xhp\" name=\"Referencing Other Sheets\"\>Referencing Other Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id1879329				0	br	In the same way, a reference can also be made to a cell from another document provided that this document has already been saved as a file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id2078005				0	br	Open a new, empty spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id4943693				0	br	By way of example, enter the following formula in cell A1 of Sheet1:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5888241				0	br	The reference to a cell of another document contains the name of the other document in single inverted commas, then a hash #, then the name of the sheet of the other document, followed by a point and the name of the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5949278				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>, to load an existing spreadsheet document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id674459				0	br	If you examine the name of the other document in this formula, you will notice that it is written as a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\>. This means that you can also enter a URL from the Internet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7099826				0	br	If you drag the box in the lower right corner of the active cell to select a range of cells, $[officename] automatically inserts the corresponding references in the adjacent cells. As a result, the sheet name is preceded with a "$" sign to designate it as an absolute reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7609790				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Sheet 2\</emph\> tab at the bottom of the spreadsheet. Set the cursor in cell A1 there and enter text or a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7697683				0	br	Confirm the formula by clicking the green check mark.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8001953				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, to open a new spreadsheet document. Set the cursor in the cell where you want to insert the external data and enter an equals sign to indicate that you want to begin a formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id809961				0	br	If you switch back to Sheet1, you will see the same content in cell A1 there. If the contents of Sheet2.A1 change, then the contents of Sheet1.A1 also change.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8261665				0	br	Switch back to the new spreadsheet. In the input line you will now see how $[officename] Calc has added the reference to the formula for you. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8571123				0	br	Now switch to the document you have just loaded. Click the cell with the data that you want to insert in the new document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9064302				0	br	=Sheet2.A1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9663075				0	br	In a sheet cell you can show a reference to a cell in another sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Referencing a Cell in Another Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150441				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>HTML; in sheet cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; URL in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; Internet references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL; in Calc\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150441				0	br	\<variable id=\"cellreferences_url\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences_url.xhp\" name=\"Referencing URLs\"\>Referencing URLs\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id1955626				0	br	For example, if you found an Internet page containing current stock exchange information in spreadsheet cells, you can load this page in $[officename] Calc by using the following procedure:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768				0	br	Save your spreadsheet. When you open it again later, $[officename] Calc will update the linked cells following an inquiry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Link to External Data\</emph\>. The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"External Data\"\>\<emph\>External Data\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152892				0	br	Enter the URL of the document or Web page in the dialog. The URL must be in the format: http://www.my-bank.com/table.html. The URL for local or local area network files is the path seen in the \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993				0	br	In a $[officename] Calc document, position the cursor in the cell into which you want to insert the external data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153068				0	br	$[officename] loads the Web page or file in the "background", that is, without displaying it. In the large list box of the \<emph\>External Data\</emph\> dialog, you can see the name of all the sheets or named ranges you can choose from.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	br	Select one or more sheets or named ranges. You can also activate the automatic update function every "n" minutes and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3157979				0	br	The contents will be inserted as a link in the $[officename] Calc document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3159204				0	br	Under \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040900.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Spreadsheet - General\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - General\</emph\>\</link\> you can choose to have the update, when opened, automatically carried out either always, upon request or never. The update can be started manually in the dialog under \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	References to Other Sheets and Referencing URLs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145673				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>formats; assigning by formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell formats; assigning by formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>STYLE function example\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell styles;assigning by formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas;assigning cell formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>applying;cell formats\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145673	13			0	br	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_by_formula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_by_formula.xhp\" name=\"Assigning Formats by Formula\"\>Assigning Formats by Formula\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3144767				0	br	All cells with contents that were included in the selection are now highlighted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	br	The "&" symbol designates the current contents of the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> field. The line must begin with an equal sign, since it is a formula. It is assumed that the cell styles "Red" and "Green" already exist.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3147127				0	br	Click\<emph\> Replace all\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	br	Select the menu command \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	br	Mark the fields \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\" name=\"Regular expressions\"\>\<emph\>Regular expressions\</emph\>\</link\> and \<emph\>Current selection only\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	br	Select all the desired cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	br	The STYLE() function can be added to an existing formula in a cell. For example, together with the CURRENT function, you can color a cell depending on its value. The formula =...+STYLE(IF(CURRENT()>3; "Red"; "Green")) applies the cell style "Red" to cells if the value is greater than 3, otherwise the cell style "Green" is applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767	18			0	br	For the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> term, enter: .*				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385				0	br	If you would like to apply a formula to all cells in a selected area, you can use the\<emph\> Find & Replace\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143	20			0	br	Enter the following formula in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> field: =&+STYLE(IF(CURRENT()>3;"Red";"Green"))				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153770				0	br	".*" is a regular expression that designates the contents of the current cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Assigning Formats by Formula				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149263				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>conditional formatting; cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; conditional formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; conditional formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles;conditional styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; conditional\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell formats; conditional\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>random numbers;examples\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell styles; copying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; cell styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; copying cell styles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148704				0	br	Example of Conditional Formatting: Calculate Average				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149211				0	br	Example of Conditional Formatting: Define Cell Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149263				0	br	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_conditional\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_conditional.xhp\" name=\"Applying Conditional Formatting\"\>Applying Conditional Formatting\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149898				0	br	Example of Conditional Formatting: Apply Cell Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155761				0	br	Example of Conditional Formatting: Copy Cell Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	br	Example of Conditional Formatting: Generate Number Values				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768				0	br	Set the cursor in a blank cell, for example, J14, and choose \<emph\>Insert - Function\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3145320				0	br	To apply the conditional formatting to other cells later:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	br	Enter the condition(s) into the dialog box. The dialog is described in detail in \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05120000.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Help\"\>$[officename] Help\</link\>, and an example is provided below:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3147298				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837				0	br	In our particular example, we are calculating the average of the random values. The result is placed in a cell:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149051				0	br	Copy the cell to the clipboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	br	Now you can apply the conditional formatting to the sheet:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149258				0	br	Copy the formula to create a row of random numbers. Click the bottom right corner of the selected cell, and drag to the right until the desired cell range is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	br	In one of the cells enter the formula =RAND(), and you will obtain a random number between 0 and 1. If you want integers of between 0 and 50, enter the formula =INT(RAND()*50).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150043				0	br	You want to give certain values in your tables particular emphasis. For example, in a table of turnovers, you can show all the values above the average in green and all those below the average in red. This is possible with conditional formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150049				0	br	Select all cells with the random numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150436				0	br	Select the cells that are to receive this same formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150883				0	br	Click in a blank cell and select the command \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> in the context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3152889				0	br	To define a second style, click again in a blank cell and proceed as described above. Assign a different background color for the cell and assign a name (for this example, "Below").				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153013				0	br	Define the condition as follows: If cell value is less than J14, format with cell style "Below", and if cell value is greater than or equal to J14, format with cell style "Above".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153074				0	br	Click one of the cells that has been assigned conditional formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153246				0	br	Close Function Wizard with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153801				0	br	Choose the \<emph\>Format - Conditional Formatting\</emph\> command to open the corresponding dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	br	In the Styles and Formatting window, click the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon. Enter the name of the new style. For this example, name the style "Above".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	br	Select the cells to which you want to apply a conditional style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154659				0	br	The next step is to apply a cell style to all values that represent above-average turnover, and one to those that are below the average. Ensure that the Styles and Formatting window is visible before proceeding.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	br	With conditional formatting, you can, for example, highlight the totals that exceed the average value of all totals. If the totals change, the formatting changes correspondingly, without having to apply other styles manually.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3155337				0	br	First of all, write a table in which a few different values occur. For your test you can create tables with any random numbers:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	br	In the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog on the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab, select a background color. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Conditional Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3156016				0	br	Select the AVERAGE function. Use the mouse to select all your random numbers. If you cannot see the entire range, because Function Wizard is obscuring it, you can temporarily shrink the dialog using the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#eingabesymbol\" name=\"Shrink or Maximize\"\>Shrink / Maximize\</link\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3159123				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05120000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Conditional formatting\"\>Format - Conditional formatting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3159156				0	br	Using the menu command \<emph\>Format - Conditional formatting\</emph\>, the dialog allows you to define up to three conditions per cell, which must be met in order for the selected cells to have a particular format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236				0	br	In the same way as described above, drag down the corner of the rightmost cell in order to create more rows of random numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3166465				0	br	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> area, check only the \<emph\>Formats\</emph\> box. All other boxes must be unchecked. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id8039796				0	br	To apply conditional formatting, AutoCalculate must be enabled. Choose \<emph\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoCalculate\</emph\> (you see a check mark next to the command when AutoCalculate is enabled).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Applying Conditional Formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147434				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>negative numbers; highlighting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; highlighting negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>highlighting;negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>colors;number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number formats;colors\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434				0	br	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_minusvalue\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp\" name=\"Highlighting Negative Numbers\"\>Highlighting Negative Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	br	The cell number format is defined in two parts. The format for positive numbers and zero is defined in front of the semicolon; after the semicolon the formula for negative numbers is defined. You can change the code (RED) under \<emph\>Format code\</emph\>. For example, instead of "RED," enter "YELLOW". If the new code appears in the list after clicking the \<emph\>Add\</emph\> icon, this is a valid entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	br	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab, select a number format and mark \<emph\>Negative numbers red\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	br	You can format cells with a number format that highlights negative numbers in red. Alternatively, you can define your own number format in which negative numbers are highlighted in other colors.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	br	Select the cells and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Highlighting Negative Numbers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>values; consolidating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>consolidating data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ranges; combining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>combining;cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; combining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; merging ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging;data ranges\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791				0	br	\<variable id=\"consolidate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/consolidate.xhp\" name=\"Consolidating Data\"\>Consolidating Data\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147250				0	br	Click \<emph\>More\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Consolidate\</emph\> dialog to display additional settings:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	br	From the \<emph\>Source data area\</emph\> box select a source cell range to consolidate with other areas.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147468				0	br	The data from the consolidation ranges and target range will be saved when you save the document. If you later open a document in which consolidation has been defined, this data will again be available.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149209				0	br	If the range is not named, click in the field next to the \<emph\>Source data area\</emph\>. A blinking text cursor appears. Type a reference for the first source data range or select the range with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149315				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to consolidate the ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149945				0	br	Under \<emph\>Consolidate by\</emph\>, select either \<emph\>Row labels\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column labels\</emph\> if the cells of the source data range are not to be consolidated corresponding to the identical position of the cell in the range, but instead according to a matching row label or column label.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150215				0	br	If the target range is not named, click in the field next to \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> and enter the reference of the target range. Alternatively, you can select the range using the mouse or position the cursor in the top left cell of the target range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150478				0	br	The text in the labels must be identical, so that rows or columns can be accurately matched. If the row or column label does not match any that exist in the target range, it will be appended as a new row or column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538				0	br	The corresponding cell references in the target range are inserted in consecutive rows, which are automatically ordered and then hidden from view. Only the final result, based on the selected function, is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	br	Open the document that contains the cell ranges to be consolidated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153039				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Data - Consolidate\"\>Data - Consolidate\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153191				0	br	During consolidation, the contents of the cells from several sheets will be combined in one place.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153813				0	br	Select a function from the \<emph\>Function\</emph\> box. The function specifies how the values of the consolidation ranges are linked. The "Sum" function is the default setting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153816				0	br	Select additional ranges and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> after each selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154513				0	br	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Consolidate\</item\> to open the \<emph\>Consolidate\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	br	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to insert the selected range in the \<emph\>Consolidation areas\</emph\> field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3156400				0	br	Select \<emph\>Link to source data\</emph\> to insert the formulas that generate the results in the target range, rather than the actual results. If you link the data, any values modified in the source range are automatically updated in the target range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	br	To consolidate by row labels or column labels, the label must be contained in the selected source ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3157983				0	br	Specify where you want to display the result by selecting a target range from the \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DE				0	br	Additional Settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Consolidating Data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
