helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3153487				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Spreadsheet - View\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3155595				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Import text files\"\>Import text files\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_id8444166				0	br	Right-click a column in the preview to set the format or to hide the column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FC				0	br	When you export a spreadsheet to CSV format, only the data on the current sheet is saved. All other information, including formulas and formatting, is lost.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AF				0	br	Only the current sheet can be exported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DD				0	br	(Optional) Set the field options for the Text CSV file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107ED				0	br	In the \<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\> dialog, select the options that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FC				0	br	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082D				0	br	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	br	The \<emph\>Text Import\</emph\> dialog opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10862				0	br	\<variable id=\"csv_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/csv_files.xhp\"\>Opening and Saving Text CSV Files\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10880				0	br	Comma Separated Values (CSV) is text file format that you can use to exchange data from a database or a spreadsheet between applications. Each line in a Text CSV file represents a record in the database, or a row in a spreadsheet. Each field in a database record or cell in a spreadsheet row is usually separated by a comma. However, you can use other characters to delimit a field, such as a tabulator character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10886				0	br	If the content of a field or cell contains a comma, the contents of the field or cell \<emph\>must\</emph\> be enclosed by single quotes (') or double quotes (").				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10890				0	br	To Open a Text CSV file				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10897				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1089F				0	br	Locate the CSV file that you want to open.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A2				0	br	If the file has a *.csv extension, select the file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A5				0	br	If the CSV file has another extension, select the file, and then select "Text CSV" in the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108B1				0	br	Specify the options to divide the text in the file into columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108BB				0	br	You can preview the layout of the imported data at the bottom of the \<emph\>Text Import\</emph\> dialog. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C5				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E2				0	br	If the CSV file uses a text delimiter character that is not listed in the \<emph\>Text delimiter\</emph\> box, click in the box, and type the character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FA				0	br	To Save a Sheet as a Text CSV File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10901				0	br	Open the Calc sheet that you want to save as a Text CSV file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10905				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1090D				0	br	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box, select "Text CSV".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10915				0	br	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, enter a name for the file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091C				0	br	Select \<emph\>Edit filter settings\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	 Importing and Exporting CSV Files 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153726				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>csv files;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; saving as csv files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; tables as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; tables as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; importing/exporting as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; importing to spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715				0	br	Importing a CSV File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726				0	br	\<variable id=\"csv_formula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/csv_formula.xhp\" name=\"Importing and Exporting Text Files\"\>Importing and Exporting Text Files\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154022				0	br	Exporting Formulas and Values as CSV Files				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3146781				0	br	Caution: If the numbers use commas as decimal separators or thousands separators, do not select the comma as the field delimiter. If the text contains double quotation marks, you must select the single quotation mark as separator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3148702				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Save as\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255				0	br	If the csv file contains formulas, but you want to import the results of those formulas, then choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149402				0	br	Comma separated values (CSV) files are text files that contain the cell contents of a single sheet. Commas, semicolons, or other characters can be used as the field delimiters between the cells. Text strings are put in quotation marks, numbers are written without quotation marks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	br	You will see the \<emph\>Import text files\</emph\> dialog. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150050				0	br	If necessary, after you have saved, clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box to see the calculated results in the table again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150200				0	br	Under \<emph\>Display\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	br	Click the sheet to be written as a csv file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	br	From the \<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\> dialog that appears, select the character set and the field and text delimiters for the data to be exported, and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153008				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"Export text files\"\>Export text files\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153487				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Spreadsheet - View\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153709				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153912				0	br	In the\<emph\> File type\</emph\> field select the format "Text CSV".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	br	If you want to export the calculation results instead of the formulas, do not mark \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155111				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155445				0	br	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> field, select the format "Text CSV". Select the file and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. When a file has the .csv extension, the file type is automatically recognized.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155595				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Import text files\"\>Import text files\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3157978				0	br	Enter a name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3166423				0	br	If you want to export the formulas as formulas, for example, in the form =SUM(A1:B5), proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Importing and Exporting Text Files				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156329				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>currency formats; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>international currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; currency formats in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currencies; default currencies\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;currency formats\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156329				0	br	\<variable id=\"currency_format\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/currency_format.xhp\" name=\"Cells in Currency Format\"\>Cells in Currency Format\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	br	If, under \<emph\>Language\</emph\>, you convert the cells to "English (US)", the English-language locale setting is also transferred and the default currency format is now "$ 1,234.00".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	br	Exchanging of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc documents can lead to misunderstandings, if your \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc document is loaded by a user who uses a different default currency format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	br	For example, if the language is set to "Default" and you are using a german locale setting, the currency format will be "1.234,00 €". A point is used before the thousand digits and a comma before the decimal places. If you now select the subordinate currency format "$ English (US)" from the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list box , you will get the following format: "$ 1.234,00". As you can see, the separators have remained the same. Only the currency symbol has been changed and converted, but the underlying format of the notation remains the same as in the locale setting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3151075				0	br	You can change the currency format in the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog (choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\> tab) by two country settings. In the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> combo box select the basic setting for currency symbol, decimal and thousands separators. In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list box you can select possible variations from the default format for the language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	br	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can give numbers any currency format. When you click the \<emph\>Currency\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3150791\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_currencyfield.png\" width=\"4.23mm\" height=\"4.23mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150791\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>bar to format a number, the cell is given the default currency format set under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Options - Language Settings - Languages\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cell - Numbers\"\>Format - Cell - Numbers\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	br	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can define that a number that you have formatted as "1,234.50 €", still remains in euro in another country and does not become dollars.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Cells in Currency Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154758				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>tables; database ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; defining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ranges; defining database ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;database ranges\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154758				0	br	\<variable id=\"database_define\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_define.xhp\" name=\"Defining Database Ranges\"\>Defining a Database Range\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801	82			0	br	You can only edit and access a database range in the spreadsheet that contains the range. You cannot access the database range in the %PRODUCTNAME Data Sources view. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153715				0	br	In the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box, enter a name for the database range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	br	You can define a range of cells in a spreadsheet to use as a database. Each row in this database range corresponds to a database record and each cell in a row corresponds to a database field. You can sort, group, search, and perform calculations on the range as you would in a database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	br	Specify the options for the database range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	br	Select the range of cells that you want to define as a database range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10648				0	br	To Define a Database Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10654				0	br	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Define Range\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066A				0	br	Click \<emph\>More\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10675				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Defining Database Ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153541				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; filtering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell ranges;filtering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering; database ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering;cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; removing filters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153541				0	br	\<variable id=\"database_filter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_filter.xhp\" name=\"Filtering Cell Ranges\"\>Filtering Cell Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	br	Click in a cell range or a database range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069				0	br	You can use several filters to filter cell ranges in spreadsheets. A standard filter uses the options that you specify to filter the data. An AutoFilter filters data according to a specific value or string. An advanced filter uses filter criteria from specified cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398				0	br	Click in a cell range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	br	The records that match the filter options that you specified are shown.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	br	To Apply an AutoFilter to a Cell Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	br	Click the arrow button in the column that contains the value or string that you want to set as the filter criteria.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	br	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	br	In the \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> dialog, specify the filter options that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id9303872				0	br	If you want to apply multiple AutoFilters to the same sheet, you must first define database ranges, then apply the AutoFilters to the database ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	br	To Apply a Standard Filter to a Cell Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10693				0	br	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Standard Filter\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A5				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DB				0	br	An arrow button is added to the head of each column in the database range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	br	To Remove a Filter From a Cell Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EC				0	br	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Remove Filter\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	br	Select the value or string that you want to use as the filter criteria.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074C				0	br	The records that match the filter criteria that you selected are shown.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075C				0	br	Click in a filtered cell range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Filtering Cell Ranges 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150767				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; sorting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sorting; database ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data;sorting in databases\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150767				0	br	\<variable id=\"database_sort\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_sort.xhp\" name=\"Sorting Database Ranges\"\>Sorting Database Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3145751				0	br	Click in a database range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN10635				0	br	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Sort\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063D				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	br	Select the sort options that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Sorting Database Ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150448				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot function; introduction\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Pivot table, see DataPilot function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150448				0	br	\<variable id=\"datapilot\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot.xhp\" name=\"DataPilot\"\>DataPilot\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069				0	br	A table that has been created with the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090000.xhp\" name=\"DataPilot\"\>DataPilot\</link\> is an interactive table. Data can be arranged, rearranged or summarized according to different points of view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024				0	br	The \<emph\>DataPilot\</emph\> (sometimes known as \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\>) allows you to combine, compare, and analyze large amounts of data. You can view different summaries of the source data, you can display the details of areas of interest, and you can create reports.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	DataPilot				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148491				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot function; calling up and applying\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148491				0	br	\<variable id=\"datapilot_createtable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_createtable.xhp\" name=\"Creating DataPilot Tables\"\>Creating DataPilot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	br	By double-clicking on one of the fields in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area you can call up the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Data - DataPilot - Start\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Select Source\</emph\> dialog appears. Choose \<emph\>Current selection\</emph\> and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The table headings are shown as buttons in the \<emph\>DataPilot\</emph\> dialog. Drag these buttons as required and drop them into the layout areas "Page Fields", "Column Fields", "Row Fields" and "Data Fields".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	br	To open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, double-click one of the buttons in the \<emph\>Row\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column\</emph\> area. Use the dialog to select if and to what extent \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> calculates display subtotals.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	br	The order of the buttons can be changed at any time by moving them to a different position in the area with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	br	Drag the desired buttons into one of the four areas.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	br	Remove a button by dragging it back to the area of the other buttons at the right of the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	br	If the button is dropped in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area it will be given a caption that also shows the formula that will be used to calculate the data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	br	Exit the DataPilot dialog by pressing OK. A \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> button will now be inserted, or a page button for every data field that you dropped in the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area. The DataPilot table is inserted further down.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023				0	br	Position the cursor within a range of cells containing values, row and column headings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	br	Use the \<emph\>Data Field\</emph\> dialog to select the calculations to be used for the data. To make a multiple selection, press the Ctrl key while clicking the desired calculation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id7599414				0	br	Drag a button to the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area to create a button and a listbox on top of the generated datapilot table. The listbox can be used to filter the DataPilot table by the contents of the selected item. You can use drag-and-drop within the generated DataPilot table to use another page field as a filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Creating DataPilot Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153726				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot function; deleting tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726				0	br	\<variable id=\"datapilot_deletetable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_deletetable.xhp\" name=\"Deleting DataPilot Tables\"\>Deleting DataPilot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	br	In order to delete a DataPilot table, select any cell in the DataPilot table, then choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> in the context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Deleting DataPilot Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148663				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot function; editing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148663				0	br	\<variable id=\"datapilot_edittable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_edittable.xhp\" name=\"Editing DataPilot Tables\"\>Editing DataPilot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id1648915				0	br	In the DataPilot dialog, you can drag a button to the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area to create a button and a listbox on top of the generated DataPilot table. The listbox can be used to filter the DataPilot table by the contents of the selected item. You can use drag-and-drop within the generated DataPilot table to use another page field as a filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id2666096				0	br	In the DataPilot table, you can use drag-and-drop or cut/paste commands to rearrange the order of data fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	br	By dragging the button to a different position in the same row you can alter the order of the columns. If you drag a button to the left edge of the table into the row headings area, you can change a column into a row.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	br	To remove a button from the table, just drag it out of the DataPilot table. Release the mouse button when the mouse pointer positioned within the sheet has become a 'not allowed' icon. The button is deleted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3149401	38			0	br	By double-clicking on some buttons inside the DataPilot table you can hide the subelements below it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	br	Click one of the buttons in the table that the DataPilot has created and hold the mouse button down. A special symbol will appear next to the mouse pointer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	br	To edit the DataPilot table, click a cell inside the DataPilot table and open the context menu. In the context menu you find the command \<emph\>Start\</emph\>, which displays the \<emph\>DataPilot\</emph\> dialog for the current DataPilot table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Editing DataPilot Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150792				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot function; filtering tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering;DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filters;DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792	35			0	br	\<variable id=\"datapilot_filtertable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_filtertable.xhp\" name=\"Filtering DataPilot Tables\"\>Filtering DataPilot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150441	37			0	br	Click the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> button in the sheet to call up the dialog for the filter conditions. Alternatively, call up the context menu of the DataPilot table and select the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> command. The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090103.xhp\" name=\"Filter\"\>\<emph\>Filter\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears. Here you can filter the DataPilot table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192	36			0	br	You can use filters to remove unwanted data from a DataPilot table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Filtering DataPilot Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	bm_id4195684				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot function;grouping table entries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ungrouping entries in DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_id3328653				0	br	The DataPilot table must be organized in a way that grouping can be applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10643				0	br	\<variable id=\"datapilot_grouping\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_grouping.xhp\"\>Grouping DataPilot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10661				0	br	The resulting DataPilot table can contain many different entries. By grouping the entries, you can improve the visible result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10667				0	br	Select a cell or range of cells in the DataPilot table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Data - Outline - Group\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066E				0	br	Depending on the format of the selected cells, either a new group field is added to the DataPilot table, or you see one of the two \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090400.xhp\"\>Grouping\</link\> dialogs, either for numeric values, or for date values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	br	To remove a grouping, click inside the group, then choose \<emph\>Data - Outline - Ungroup\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Grouping DataPilot Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148663				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot function; preventing data overwriting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>output ranges of DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148663				0	br	\<variable id=\"datapilot_tipps\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_tipps.xhp\" name=\"Selecting DataPilot Output Ranges\"\>Selecting DataPilot Output Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	br	If the \<emph\>Identify categories\</emph\> check box is marked, the categories will be identified by their headings and assigned accordingly when the DataPilot table is created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	br	If you mark the \<emph\>Ignore empty rows \</emph\>check box, they will not be taken into account when the DataPilot table is created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	br	You can select a named range in which the DataPilot table is to be created, from the \<emph\>Results to\</emph\> box. If the results range does not have a name, enter the coordinates of the upper left cell of the range into the field to the right of the \<emph\>Results to\</emph\> box. You can also click on the appropriate cell to have the coordinates entered accordingly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123				0	br	Click the button \<emph\>More\</emph\> in the \<emph\>DataPilot\</emph\> dialog. The dialog will be extended.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Selecting DataPilot Output Ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150792				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>Pivot table import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot function; refreshing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recalculating;DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	br	\<variable id=\"datapilot_updatetable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_updatetable.xhp\" name=\"Updating DataPilot Tables\"\>Updating DataPilot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	br	If the data of the source sheet has been changed, $[officename] recalculates the DataPilot table. To recalculate the tables, choose \<emph\>Data - DataPilot - Refresh\</emph\>. Do the same after you have imported an Excel Pivot table into $[officename] Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Updating DataPilot Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id1226844				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>exporting;spreadsheets to dBase\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing;dBase files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dBase import/export\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; importing dBase files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; exporting to dBase files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>database tables;importing dBase files\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071F				0	br	Locate the *.dbf file that you want to import. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10730				0	br	The \<emph\>Import dBase files\</emph\> dialog opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10738				0	br	\<variable id=\"dbase_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/dbase_files.xhp\"\>Importing and Exporting dBase Files\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074E				0	br	If you want to save the spreadsheet as a dBase file, do not alter or delete the first row in the imported file. This row contains information that is required by a dBase database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10756				0	br	You can open and save data in the dBase file format (*.dbf file extension) in $[officename] Base or a spreadsheet. In %PRODUCTNAME Base, a dBase database is a folder that contains files with the .dbf file extension. Each file corresponds to a table in the database. Formulas and formatting are lost when you open and save a dBase file from %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10759				0	br	To Import a dBase File Into a Spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10768				0	br	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076C				0	br	A %PRODUCTNAME Base database table is actually a link to an existing database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10777				0	br	The dBase file opens as a new Calc spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077A				0	br	To Import a dBase File Into a Database Table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10786				0	br	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialog, enter a name for the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10792				0	br	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10796				0	br	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - New - Database\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079A				0	br	In the \<emph\>Database type \</emph\>box of the \<emph\>Database Properties\</emph\> dialog, select "dBASE".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A6				0	br	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AE				0	br	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B6				0	br	Locate the directory that contains the dBase file, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	br	Click \<emph\>Create\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F1				0	br	To Export a Spreadsheet to a dBase File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Export\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F9				0	br	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, type a name for the dBase file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10800				0	br	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> box, select "dBase file".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10801				0	br	Click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10808				0	br	Only the data on the current sheet is exported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Importing and Exporting dBase Files				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>theme selection for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>layout;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell styles; selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>applying;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791	6			0	br	\<variable id=\"design\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/design.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Themes for Sheets\"\>Selecting Themes for Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	br	$[officename] Calc comes with a predefined set of formatting themes that you can apply to your spreadsheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920	15			0	br	Click the \<emph\>Choose Themes\</emph\> icon in the \<emph\>Tools\</emph\> bar. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146979				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/02/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Theme selection\"\>Theme selection\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	br	The \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog appears. This dialog lists the available themes for the whole spreadsheet and the Styles and Formatting window lists the custom styles for specific cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090				0	br	Click OK				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150201				0	br	As soon as you select another theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog, some of the properties of the custom style will be applied to the current spreadsheet. The modifications will be immediately visible in your spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	br	To apply a theme to a spreadsheet:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	br	It is not possible to add themes to Calc, and they cannot be modified. However, you can modify their styles after you apply them to a spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	br	Before you format a sheet with a theme, you have to apply at least one custom cell style to the cells on the sheet. You can then change the cell formatting by selecting and applying a theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114	9			0	br	In the \<emph\>Theme Selection \</emph\>dialog, select the theme that you want to apply to the spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	br	To apply a custom cell style to a cell, you can open the Styles and Formatting window and, in its lower list box, set the Custom Styles view. A list of the existing custom defined cell styles will be displayed. Double click a name from the Styles and Formatting window to apply this style to the selected cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Selecting Themes for Sheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; transferring values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;values, to multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;values in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values;inserting in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456	3			0	br	\<variable id=\"edit_multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/edit_multitables.xhp\" name=\"Copying to Multiple Sheets\"\>Copying to Multiple Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435				0	br	Now when you insert values, text or formulas into the sheets, they will also appear in the identical positions in the other selected sheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	br	In $[officename] Calc, you can insert values, text or formulas that are simultaneously copied to other selected sheets of your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	br	Select all desired sheets by holding down the Shift or Ctrl key and clicking the corresponding register tabs that are still gray at the bottom margin of the workspace. All selected register tabs are now white.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	br	You can use Shift+Ctrl+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Copying to Multiple Sheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153896				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>filters; introduction\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>advanced filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; deleting with filters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896				0	br	\<variable id=\"filters\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/filters.xhp\" name=\"Applying Filters\"\>Applying Filters\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	br	In the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> dialog, you can also define ranges which contain the values in particular data fields. You can use the standard filter to connect up to three conditions with either a logical AND or a logical OR operator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	br	The \<emph\>Advanced filter\</emph\> exceeds the three condition limitation and allows up to a total of eight filter conditions. With advanced filters you enter the conditions directly into the sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	br	Filters and advanced filters allow you to work on certain filtered rows (records) of a data range. In the spreadsheets in $[officename] there are various possibilities for applying filters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	br	One use for the \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> function is to quickly restrict the display to records with identical entries in a data field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	br	When you select filtered rows and then either apply formatting, or delete the selected rows, this action then applies only to the filtered rows. The hidden rows are not affected. This is the opposite to rows that you have hidden manually by the \<emph\>Format - Rows - Hide Rows\</emph\> command. Manually hidden rows are deleted when you delete a selection that contains them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Applying Filters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	bm_id3769341				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>searching, see also finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>finding;formulas/values/text/objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing; cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;multiple cell texts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id2423780				0	br	To find formulas or values				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149204				0	br	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Calc\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3610644				0	br	The Find & Replace dialog				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id7359233				0	br	Finding text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8531449				0	br	The Navigator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	br	With "Formulas" you will find all parts of the formulas. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2186346				0	br	Select "Formulas" or "Values" in the \<emph\>Search in\</emph\> list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2224494				0	br	Cells can contain text or numbers that were entered directly as in a text document. But cells can also contain text or numbers as the result of a calculation. For example, if a cell contains the formula =1+2 it displays the result 3. You must decide whether to search for the 1 respective 2, or to search the 3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2394482				0	br	If you closed the dialog, you can press a key combination (Ctrl+Shift+F) to find the next cell without opening the dialog. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	br	You can specify in the Find & Replace dialog either to find the parts of a formula or the results of a calculation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	br	Cell contents can be formatted in different ways. For example, a number can be formatted as a currency, to be displayed with a currency symbol. You see the currency symbol in the cell, but you cannot search for it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3808404				0	br	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Calc will select the next cell that contains your text. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found cell. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id393993				0	br	With "Values" you will find the results of the calculations. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id631733				0	br	By default, Calc searches the current sheet. Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\>, then enable \<emph\>Search in all sheets\</emph\> to search through all sheets of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6394238				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6529740				0	br	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6549272				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7214270				0	br	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7811822				0	br	When you click \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>, Calc selects all cells that contain your entry. Now you can for example set all found cells to bold, or apply a Cell Style to all at once.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9121982				0	br	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9363689				0	br	In spreadsheet documents you can find words, formulas, and styles. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all matching cells at once, then apply another format or replace the cell content by other content.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	br	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	br	Use the Navigator for inserting objects and links within the same document or from other open documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Finding and Replacing in Calc				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154125				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds;cells and pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders;cells and pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149899				0	br	Formatting Numbers in a Spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153483				0	br	Formatting Borders and Backgrounds for Cells and Pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153912	13			0	br	Formatting Text in a Spreadsheet 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154125				0	br	\<variable id=\"format_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_table.xhp\" name=\"Designing Spreadsheets\"\>Formatting Spreadsheets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3144772				0	br	Select the text you want to format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116				0	br	To apply formatting attributes to an entire sheet, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>. You can define headers and footers, for example, to appear on each printed page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145389				0	br	An image that you have loaded with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Background\</item\> is only visible in print or in the page preview. To display a background image on screen as well, insert the graphic image by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Picture - From File\</item\> and arrange the image behind the cells by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Arrange - To Background\</item\>. Use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> to select the background image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3150046	18			0	br	To format numbers in the default currency format or as percentages, use the icons on the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>Bar. For other formats, choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. You can choose from the preset formats or define your own on the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154733				0	br	You can assign a format to any group of cells by first selecting the cells (for multiple selection, hold down the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl\</item\> key when clicking), and then activating the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cell\</item\>. In this dialog, you can select attributes such as shadows and backgrounds.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155268	15			0	br	Choose the desired text attributes from the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>Bar. You can also choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog will appear in which you can choose various text attributes on the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3159226				0	br	Select the cells containing the numbers you want to format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Formatting Spreadsheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145367				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>numbers; formatting in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; numbers in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults; number formats in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places;formatting numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;numbers with decimals\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;adding/deleting decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number formats; adding/deleting decimal places in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting; decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places; adding/deleting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145367				0	br	\<variable id=\"format_value\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Numbers With Decimals\"\>Formatting Numbers With Decimals\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	br	Set the cursor at the number and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> to start the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	br	Enter a number into the sheet, for example, 1234.5678. This number will be displayed in the default number format, with two decimal places. You will see 1234.57 when you confirm the entry. Only the display in the document will be rounded off; internally, the number retains all four decimal places after the decimal point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3149256				0	br	If you only want to modify the number of the decimal places displayed, the easiest method is to use the \<emph\>Number Format: Add Decimal Place\</emph\> or \<emph\>Number Format: Delete Decimal Place\</emph\> icons on the Formatting Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	br	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab you will see a selection of predefined number formats. In the bottom right in the dialog you will see a preview of how your current number would look if you were to give it a particular format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012				0	br	To format numbers with decimals:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3155766				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3149021\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_numberformatincdecimals.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149021\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Formatting Numbers With Decimals				2002-02-02 02:02:02
