helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3148646				0	br	In the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> text box enter the following code:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	br	In the \<emph\>Categories\</emph\> list box select "User-defined".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150369				0	br	500000				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400				0	br	You can define your own number formats to display numbers in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	br	As an example, to display the number 10,200,000 as 10.2 Million:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	br	Select the cells to which you want to apply a new, user-defined format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241				0	br	100.0 Million				2002-02-02 02:02:02
