helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151113				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>formulas; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;formulas\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151113				0	br	\<variable id=\"formula_copy\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_copy.xhp\" name=\"Copying Formulas\"\>Copying Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	br	Select the cell containing the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961				0	br	If you want to copy a formula into multiple cells, there is a quick and easy way to copy into adjacent cell areas:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	br	Select the cell containing the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	br	With the mouse button pressed, drag it down or to the right over all the cells into which you want to copy the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	br	When you release the mouse button, the formula will be copied into the cells and automatically adjusted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V. The formula will be positioned in the new cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	br	Position the mouse on the bottom right of the highlighted border of the cell, and continue holding down the mouse button until the pointer changes to a cross-hair symbol.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Copy\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+ C to copy it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3156385				0	br	If you do not want values and texts to be automatically adjusted, then hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key when dragging. Formulas, however, are always adjusted accordingly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	br	There are various ways to copy a formula. One suggested method is:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155				0	br	Select the cell into which you want the formula to be copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Copying Formulas				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150868				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>formula bar; input line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>input line in formula bar\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; inputting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;formulas\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150868				0	br	\<variable id=\"formula_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_enter.xhp\" name=\"Entering Formulas in the Formula Bar\"\>Entering Formulas in the Formula Bar\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1836909				0	br	+ 5 0 - 8 Enter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364				0	br	Click the cell in which you want to enter the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	br	You can also enter the values and the formulas directly into the cells, even if you cannot see an input cursor. Formulas must always begin with an equals sign.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149210	7			0	br	\<variable id=\"tip\"\>If you would like to view the calculation of individual elements of a formula, select the respective elements and press F9. For example, in the formula =SUM(A1:B12)*SUM(C1:D12) select the section SUM(C1:D12) and press F9 to view the subtotal for this area. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Function\</emph\> icon on the Formula Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	br	If an error occurs when creating the formula, an \<link href=\"text/scalc/05/02140000.xhp\" name=\"error message\"\>error message\</link\> appears in the active cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/main0206.xhp\" name=\"Formula bar\"\>Formula bar\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	br	After entering the required values, press Enter or click \<emph\>Accept\</emph\> to insert the result in the active cell. If you want to clear your entry in the input line, press Escape or click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764				0	br	If you are editing a formula with references, the references and the associated cells will be highlighted with the same color. You can now resize the reference border using the mouse, and the reference in the formula displayed in the input line also changes. \<emph\>Show references in color \</emph\>can be deactivated under \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060300.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Spreadsheet - View\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	br	You will now see an equals sign in the input line and you can begin to input the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id4206976				0	br	You can also press the + or - key on the numerical keyboard to start a formula. NumLock must be "on". For example, press the following keys in succession:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id6848353				0	br	You can enter formulas in several ways: using the icons, or by typing on the keyboard, or by a mixture of both methods.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8171330				0	br	You see the result \<item type=\"literal\"\>42\</item\> in the cell. The cell contains the formula \<item type=\"literal\"\>=+50-8\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Entering Formulas in the Formula Bar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153195				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>formulas; displaying in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values; displaying in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; displaying formulas/values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>results display vs. formulas display\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>displaying; formulas instead of results\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153195				0	br	\<variable id=\"formula_value\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_value.xhp\" name=\"Displaying Formulas or Values\"\>Displaying Formulas or Values\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	br	In the \<emph\>Display\</emph\> area mark the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> box. Click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	br	If you want to view the calculation results instead of the formula, do not mark the Formulasbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	br	If you want to display the formulas in the cells, for example in the form =SUM(A1:B5), proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Spreadsheet - View\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Displaying Formulas or Values				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>formulas;calculating with\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating; with formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples;formula calculation\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411				0	br	\<variable id=\"formulas\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formulas.xhp\" name=\"Calculating With Formulas\"\>Calculating With Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	br	Remember that the basic arithmetic signs (+, -, *, /) can be used in formulas using the "Multiplication and Division before Addition and Subtraction" rule. Instead of writing =SUM(A1:B1) it is better to write =A1+B1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3145643				0	br	=A1*16%				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146114				0	br	=B8-SUM(B10:B14)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	br	Parentheses can also be used. The result of the formula =(1+2)*3 produces a different result than =1+2*3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146315				0	br	Displays the result of the multiplication of A1 and A2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146917				0	br	=A1 * A2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972				0	br	Displays the contents of cell A1 plus 10.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3148604	50			0	br	=SUM(B1:B65536)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150109				0	br	It is also possible to nest functions in formulas, as shown in the example. You can also nest functions within functions. The Function Wizard assists you with nested functions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150209				0	br	=EFFECTIVE(5%;12)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060100.xhp\" name=\"Functions list\"\>Functions list\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150363				0	br	Rounds the contents in cell A1 to one decimal place.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150883				0	br	Calculates the effective interest for 5% annual nominal interest with 12 payments a year.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"AutoPilot: Functions\"\>Function Wizard\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3152890				0	br	=SUM(B8;SUM(B10:B14))				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154015				0	br	=A1+10				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	br	=ROUND(A1;1)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	br	Displays 16% of the contents of A1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154486				0	br	Calculates B8 minus the sum of the cells B10 to B14.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281				0	br	All formulas begin with an equals sign. The formulas may contain numbers or text, and other data is also possible such as format details. The formulas also contain arithmetic operators, logic operators or function starts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3156285				0	br	Here are a few examples of $[officename] Calc formulas:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3157982	51			0	br	Sums all numbers in column B.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3159171				0	br	Calculates the sum of cells B10 to B14 and adds the value to B8.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Calculating With Formulas				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>fractions; entering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; entering fractions \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;fractions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411				0	br	\<variable id=\"fraction_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/fraction_enter.xhp\" name=\"Entering Fractions \"\>Entering Fractions \</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145367	44			0	br	If you want to see multi-digit fractions such as "1/10", you must change the cell format to the multi-digit fraction view. Open the context menu of the cell, and choose \<emph\>Format cells. \</emph\>Select "Fraction" from the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> field, and then select "-1234 10/81". You can then enter fractions such as 12/31 or 12/32 - the fractions are, however, automatically reduced, so that in the last example you would see 3/8.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	br	If you enter "0 1/2" AutoCorrect causes the three characters 1, / and 2 to be replaced by a single character. The same applies to 1/4 and 3/4. This replacement is defined in \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\> - \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	br	You can enter a fractional number in a cell and use it for calculation:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155133				0	br	Enter "0 1/5" in a cell (without the quotation marks) and press the input key. In the input line above the spreadsheet you will see the value 0.2, which is used for the calculation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Entering Fractions 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>goal seek example\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>equations in goal seek\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;variables in equations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variables;calculating equations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples;goal seek\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	br	\<variable id=\"goalseek\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/goalseek.xhp\" name=\"Applying Goal Seek\"\>Applying Goal Seek\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153966				0	br	Goal Seek Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	br	With the help of Goal Seek you can calculate a value that, as part of a formula, leads to the result you specify for the formula. You thus define the formula with several fixed values and one variable value and the result of the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3146978				0	br	A dialog appears informing you that the Goal Seek was successful. Click \<emph\>Yes\</emph\> to enter the result in the cell with the variable value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	br	Place the cursor in the cell containing the interest \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\>, and choose \<emph\>Tools - Goal Seek\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Goal Seek\</emph\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3149409				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Goal Seek\"\>Goal Seek\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	br	The correct cell is already entered in the field \<emph\>Formula Cell\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150369				0	br	Enter the expected result of the formula in the \<emph\>Target Value\</emph\> text box. In this example, the value is 15,000. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150871				0	br	To calculate annual interest (I), create a table with the values for the capital (C), number of years (n), and interest rate (i). The formula is:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596				0	br	I = C * n* i				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	br	Let us assume that the interest rate \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> of 7.5% and the number of years \<item type=\"literal\"\>n\</item\> (1) will remain constant. However, you want to know how much the investment capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> would have to be modified in order to attain a particular return \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\>. For this example, calculate how much capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> would be required if you want an annual return of $15,000.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	br	Enter each of the values for Capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> (an arbitrary value like \<item type=\"literal\"\>$100,000\</item\>), number of years \<item type=\"literal\"\>n \</item\>(\<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\>), and interest rate \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> (\<item type=\"literal\"\>7.5%\</item\>) in one cell each. Enter the formula to calculate the interest \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\> in another cell. Instead of \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>n\</item\>, and \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/relativ_absolut_ref.xhp\"\>reference to the cell\</link\> with the corresponding value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	br	Place the cursor in the field \<emph\>Variable Cell\</emph\>. In the sheet, click in the cell that contains the value to be changed, in this example it is the cell with the capital value \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Applying Goal Seek				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150542				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>HTML; sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving; sheets in HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening; sheets in HTML\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149379				0	br	Opening Sheets in HTML				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150542				0	br	\<variable id=\"html_doc\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/html_doc.xhp\" name=\"Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML\"\>Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154124				0	br	Saving Sheets in HTML				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	br	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc saves all the sheets of a Calc document together as an HTML document. At the beginning of the HTML document, a heading and a list of hyperlinks are automatically added which lead to the individual sheets within the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	br	Choose the file type "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc)" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	br	In the \<emph\>Save as type\</emph\> list box, in the area with the other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc filters, choose the file type "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc)".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	br	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> offers various filters for opening HTML files, which you can select under \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Files of type\</emph\> list box:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"File - Save As\"\>File - Save As\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"File - Open\"\>File - Open\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	br	To save the current Calc document as HTML, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	br	Enter a \<emph\>File name\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446				0	br	All \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc options are now available to you. However, not all options that \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc offers for editing can be saved in HTML format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	br	Numbers are shown as written. In addition, in the <SDVAL> HTML tag, the exact internal number value is written so that after opening the HTML document with \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> you know you have the exact values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147560				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>zero values; entering leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>integers with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; changing text/number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; changing text/number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; changing text/number\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; changing to numbers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147560				0	br	\<variable id=\"integer_leading_zero\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/integer_leading_zero.xhp\" name=\"Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\"\>Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	br	Enter the number as text. The easiest way is to enter the number starting with an apostrophe (for example, '0987). The apostrophe will not appear in the cell, and the number will be formatted as text. Because it is in text format, however, you cannot calculate with this number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146916	65			0	br	Click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018	63			0	br	Check \<emph\>Regular expressions\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	br	Select the column in which the digits are found in text format. Set the cell format in that column as "Number".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	br	If you want to apply a numerical format to a column of numbers in text format (for example, text "000123" becomes number "123"), do the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194				0	br	There are various ways to enter integers starting with a zero:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	br	Format a cell with a number format such as \\0000. This format can be assigned in the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> field under the \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\> tab, and defines the cell display as "always put a zero first and then the integer, having at least three places, and filled with zeros at the left if less than three digits".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510	61			0	br	In the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, enter ^[0-9]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944	60			0	br	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3155068	62			0	br	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, enter &				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	64			0	br	Check \<emph\>Current selection only\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Entering a Number with Leading Zeros				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145120				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; %PRODUCTNAME Calc shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>shortcut keys;%PRODUCTNAME Calc accessibility\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145120				0	br	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcut Keys (%PRODUCTNAME Calc Accessibility)\"\>Shortcut Keys (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc Accessibility)\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147343				0	br	Selecting a Drawing Object or a Graphic				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148646				0	br	Controlling the Outline				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153360				0	br	Cell Selection Mode				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	br	In the cell selection mode, you can use the common navigation keys to select cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	br	You can use the keyboard in \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"Outline\"\>Outline\</link\>:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	br	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F6\</item\> until the vertical or horizontal outline window has the focus.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	br	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> - cycle through all visible buttons from top to bottom or from left to right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149403				0	br	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+1\</item\> to \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+8\</item\> - show all levels up to the specified number; hide all higher levels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	br	Use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>+\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>-\</item\> to show or hide the focused outline group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150345				0	br	If the selection tool is active, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\>. This selects the first drawing object or graphic in the sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3150439\" src=\"sc/res/refinp1.png\" width=\"0.1327inch\" height=\"0.1327inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150439\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	br	Use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Up\</item\>, \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Down\</item\>, \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Left\</item\>, or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> arrow to cycle through all buttons in the current level.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	br	In a text box that has a button to minimize the dialog, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\> to enter the cell selection mode. Select any number of cells, then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\> again to show the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	br	Refer also to the lists of shortcut keys for \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> in general.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	br	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> until the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155379				0	br	Now you can use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> to select the next drawing object or graphic and \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> to select the previous one.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446				0	br	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> to activate the focused button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	br	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> - cycle through all visible buttons in the opposite direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159240				0	br	With \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+F6\</item\> you set the focus to the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AA				0	br	Choose View - Toolbars - Drawing to open the Drawing toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Shortcut Keys (%PRODUCTNAME Calc Accessibility)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154684				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>tables; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title rows; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>freezing rows or columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scrolling prevention in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>windows; splitting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; splitting windows\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154684				0	br	\<variable id=\"line_fix\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/line_fix.xhp\" name=\"Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\"\>Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147004				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07090000.xhp\" name=\"Window - Freeze\"\>Window - Freeze\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	br	If you want to print a certain row on all pages of a document, choose \<emph\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	br	If you have long rows or columns of data that extend beyond the viewable area of the spreadsheet, you can freeze them, which allows you to see the columns or rows as you scroll through the rest of the data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07080000.xhp\" name=\"Window - Split\"\>Window - Split\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Print ranges - Edit\"\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073	5			0	br	To deactivate, choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze \</emph\>again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	br	To freeze both horizontally and vertically, select the \<emph\>cell\</emph\> that is below the row and to the right of the column that you want to freeze.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	br	If the area defined is to be scrollable, apply the \<emph\>Window - Split\</emph\> command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	br	Select the row below, or the column to the right of the row or column that you want to be in the frozen region. All rows above, or all columns to the left of the selection are frozen.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
