helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153361				0	br	\<variable id=\"mark_cells\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/mark_cells.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Multiple Cells\"\>Selecting Multiple Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154942				0	br	Select various dispersed cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587				0	br	ADD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	br	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3148486				0	br	A mouse click selects the cell you have clicked on. Unmarks all marked cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149261				0	br	With the mouse button pressed, drag from one corner to the diagonally opposed corner of the range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568				0	br	STD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	br	Pressing the mouse button, drag a range across two cells, do not release the mouse button, and then drag back to the first cell. You can now move the individual cell by drag and drop.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090				0	br	EXT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3150305				0	br	A mouse click marks a rectangular range from the current cell to the cell you clicked.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	br	A mouse click in a cell adds it to the already marked cells. A mouse click in a marked cell unmarks it. Alternatively, Ctrl-click the cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3154487				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/main0208.xhp\" name=\"Status bar\"\>Status bar\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	br	On the status bar, click the box with the legend STD / EXT / ADD to switch the marking mode:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155337				0	br	Effect of clicking the mouse				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	br	Mark at least one cell. Then while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, click each of the additional cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3159264				0	br	Field contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	br	Click, then Shift-click the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Selecting Multiple Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153969				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>matrices; entering matrix formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; matrix formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;matrix formulas\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153969				0	br	\<variable id=\"matrixformula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/matrixformula.xhp\" name=\"Entering Matrix Formulas\"\>Entering Matrix Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3144767				0	br	Press the (+) key from the numerical keypad.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	br	Select the range A1:A10, which contains the first values for the sum formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	br	The matrix area is automatically protected against modifications, such as deleting rows or columns. It is, however, possible to edit any formatting, such as the cell background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	br	Press F2, or click in the input line of the Formula bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150716				0	br	End the input with the matrix key combination: Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	br	The following is an example of how you can enter a matrix formula, without going into the details of matrix functions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	br	Assume you have entered 10 numbers in Columns A and B (A1:A10 and B1:B10), and would like to calculate the sum of each row in Column C.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	br	Select the numbers in the second column in cells B1:B10.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321				0	br	Using the mouse, select the range C1:C10, in which the results are to be displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	br	Enter an equal sign (=).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Entering Matrix Formulas				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155686				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; moving cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; moving by drag and drop \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;cells by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;cells, by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	hd_id986358				0	br	\<variable id=\"move_dragdrop\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/move_dragdrop.xhp\"\>Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2586748				0	br	In both modes, you can hold down the Ctrl key, or Ctrl+Shift keys while you release the mouse button to insert a copy or a link, respectively. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2760093				0	br	When you drag-and-drop a selection of cells on a Calc sheet, the cells normally overwrite the existing cells in the area where you drop. This is the normal \<emph\>overwrite mode\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2783898				0	br	Alt+Ctrl keys				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2785119				0	br	Cells are copied and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2805566				0	br	Ctrl+Shift keys				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2815637				0	br	Cells are moved and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells are emptied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2926419				0	br	Cells are moved and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells are emptied, except if you move within the same rows on the same sheet. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3968932				0	br	In overwrite mode you see all four borders around the selected area. In insert mode you see only the left border when target cells will be shifted to the right. You see only the upper border when target cells will be shifted down. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4021423				0	br	If you move within the same rows on the same sheet, the cells in the target area shift to the right, and then the whole row shifts to fill the source area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4278389				0	br	Cells are copied and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5369121				0	br	Links to the source cells are inserted and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5590990				0	br	Links to the source cells are inserted and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5814081				0	br	Keys pressed while releasing the mouse button				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id584124				0	br	Alt+Ctrl+Shift keys				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6161687				0	br	Ctrl key				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6581316				0	br	Result				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id7399517				0	br	Whether the target area will be shifted to the right or to the bottom depends on the distance between source and target cells, if you move within the same sheet. It depends on the number of horizontal or vertical cells in the moved area, if you move to a different sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id79653				0	br	In insert mode, the existing cells where you drop will be shifted to the right or to the bottom, and the dropped cells are inserted into the now empty positions without overwriting. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8040406				0	br	If you move cells in insert mode within the same row (only horizontally), then after insertion of the cells, all cells will be shifted to the left to fill the source area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8676717				0	br	The surrounding box of the moved cells looks different in insert mode. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9518723				0	br	Alt key				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9527268				0	br	When you hold down the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Alt\</item\> key while releasing the mouse button, you enter the \<emph\>insert mode\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9906613				0	br	No key				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150769				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; showing multiple\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheet tabs;using\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>views;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769	4			0	br	\<variable id=\"multi_tables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multi_tables.xhp\" name=\"Navigating Through Sheets Tabs\"\>Navigating Through Sheets Tabs\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	br	Use the navigation buttons to display all the sheets belonging to your document. Clicking the button on the far left or the far right displays, respectively, the first or last sheet tab. The middle buttons allow the user to scroll forward and backward through all sheet tabs. To display the sheet itself click on the sheet tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	br	If there is insufficient space to display all the sheet tabs, you can increase it by pointing to the separator between the scrollbar and the sheet tabs, pressing the mouse button and, keeping the mouse button pressed, dragging to the right. In doing so you will be sharing the available space between the sheet tabs and horizontal scrollbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3156441\" src=\"res/helpimg/calcnav.png\" width=\"1.667cm\" height=\"0.37cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156441\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Navigating Through Sheets Tabs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147559				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>multiple operations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>what if operations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-classified tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145171				0	br	Multiple Operations in Columns or Rows				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145239				0	br	Calculating With One Formula and One Variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146139				0	br	Multiple Operations Across Rows and Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147559				0	br	\<variable id=\"multioperation\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multioperation.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Operations\"\>Applying Multiple Operations\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148725				0	br	Calculating with Several Formulas Simultaneously				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149949				0	br	Calculating with Two Variables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159153				0	br	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146880				0	br	Delete column E.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146888				0	br	To calculate the profit, first enter any number as the quantity (items sold) - in this example 2000. The profit is found from the formula Profit=Quantity * (Selling price - Direct costs) - Fixed costs. Enter this formula in B5.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3147474				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple Operations\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3148584				0	br	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> allows you to carry out joint multiple operations for columns and rows in so-called cross-tables. The formula cell has to refer to both the data range arranged in rows and the one arranged in columns. Select the range defined by both data ranges and call the multiple operation dialog. Enter the reference to the formula in the \<emph\>Formula\</emph\> field. The \<emph\>Row\</emph\> field is used to enter the reference to the first cell of the range arranged in rows, and the \<emph\>Column\</emph\> field the first cell of the range arranged in columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3148885				0	br	Select the range D2;F11, thus three columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149009				0	br	Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You will see the profit in column E.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149141				0	br	Close the dialog with OK. You will see the profits in the range E2:H11. In some cases you must first press F9 to update the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149149	46			0	br	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas \</emph\>field, click cell B5.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149355				0	br	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column\</emph\> field and click cell B4. This means that: B4, the quantity, is the variable in the formula, which is replaced by the marked column values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149723				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple operations\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149731				0	br	Expand the table shown above. D2 thru D11 contain the numbers 500, 1000 and so on, up to 5000. In E1 through H1 enter the numbers 8, 10, 15 and 20.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149981				0	br	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas \</emph\>field, click cell B5.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3150862				0	br	Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You will now see the profits in column E and the annual profit per item in column F.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3152810				0	br	Select the range D1:H11.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153189				0	br	You produce toys which you sell for $10 each. Each toy costs $2 to make, in addition to which you have fixed costs of $10,000 per year. How much profit will you make in a year if you sell a particular number of toys?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153620				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple Operations\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153931				0	br	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Columns\</emph\> field and click cell B4.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154049				0	br	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column\</emph\> field and click in B4. This means that B4, the quantity, is the vertically entered variable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154675				0	br	Enter the following formula in C5: = B5 / B4. You are now calculating the annual profit per item sold.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154808				0	br	Consider columns A and B of the sample table above. You now want to vary not just the quantity produced annually, but also the selling price, and you are interested in the profit in each case.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154846				0	br	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, mark cells B5 thru C5.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3155104				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12060000.xhp\" name=\"Multiple operations\"\>Multiple operations\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	br	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Rows\</emph\> field and click cell B1. This means that B1, the selling price, is the horizontally entered variable (with the values 8, 10, 15 and 20).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	br	If the data of a data range is arranged in columns or arranged in rows, select the data range together with the cell or cell range next to or below it as the target range. In the \<emph\>Column/Row\</emph\> field, enter the cell reference to the first cell in the data range. In the \<emph\>Formula\</emph\> field, enter the cell reference to the cell with the formula that applies to the data range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3157875				0	br	In column D enter certain annual sales, one under the other; for example, in steps of 500 from 500 to 5000.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3159115				0	br	Mark the range D2:E11, and thus the values in column D and the empty cells alongside in column E.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id4123966				0	br	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Multiple Operations\</item\> command provides a planning tool for "what if" questions.In your spreadsheet, you enter a formula to calculate a result from values that are stored in other cells. Then, you set up a cell range where you enter some fixed values, and the Multiple Operations command will calculate the results depending on the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id6478774				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id1621753\" src=\"res/helpimg/what-if.png\" width=\"8.5543inch\" height=\"3.1937inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1621753\"\>what-if sheet area\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Applying Multiple Operations				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154759				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; selecting multiple\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; simultaneous multiple filling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>appending sheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148576				0	br	Inserting a Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154491				0	br	Selecting Multiple Sheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154759				0	br	\<variable id=\"multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multitables.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Sheets\"\>Applying Multiple Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155600				0	br	Undoing a Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156382				0	br	Calculating Across Multiple Sheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	br	The sheet tab of the current sheet is always visible in white in front of the other sheet tabs. The other sheet tabs are gray when they are not selected. By clicking other sheet tabs while pressing \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl\</item\> you can select multiple sheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	br	To undo the selection of a sheet, click its sheet tab again while pressing the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl\</item\> key. The sheet that is currently visible cannot be removed from the selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731				0	br	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Sheet\</item\> to insert a new sheet or an existing sheet from another file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	br	You can refer to a range of sheets in a formula by specifying the first and last sheet of the range, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=SUM(Sheet1.A1:Sheet3.A1) \</item\>sums up all A1 cells on Sheet1 through Sheet3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	br	You can use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift\</item\>+\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl\</item\>+\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Page Up\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Page Down\</item\> to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Applying Multiple Sheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153968				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>notes; on cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells;notes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comments; on cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>remarks on cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;notes on cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;notes on cells\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153968				0	br	\<variable id=\"note_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/note_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Notes\"\>Inserting and Editing Notes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	br	To show or hide the note indicator, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and mark or unmark the \<emph\>Note indicator\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	br	The note is visible whenever the mouse pointer is over the cell, provided you have activated \<emph\>Help - Tips\</emph\> or - \<emph\>Extended Tips\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	br	When you select the cell, you can choose \<emph\>Show Note\</emph\> from the context menu of the cell. Doing so keeps the note visible until you deactivate the \<emph\>Show Note\</emph\> command from the same context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	br	To edit a permanently visible note, just click in it. If you delete the entire text of the note, the note itself is deleted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150440				0	br	You can assign a note to each cell by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Note\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Note\</emph\>\</link\>. The note is indicated by a small red square, the note indicator, in the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	br	To display a help tip for a selected cell, use \<emph\>Data - Validity - Input Help\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Note\"\>Insert - Note\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN10699				0	br	Move or resize each note as you like.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	br	Format each note by specifying background color, transparency, border style, and text alignment. Choose the commands from the context menu of the note.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Inserting and Editing Notes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
