helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3145800				0	br	The dialog shrinks so that you can see more of the sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3146113				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05070000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Page - (Header / Footer)\"\>Format - Page - (Header / Footer)\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	br	As an example, If you want to print the top two rows of the sheet as well as the first column (A)on all pages, do the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	br	Click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Rows to repeat\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	br	Rows to repeat are rows from the sheet. You can define headers and footers to be printed on each print page independently of this in \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	br	Click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Rows to repeat\</emph\> area. The dialog is restored again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	br	If you have a sheet that is so large that it will be printed multiple pages, you can set up rows or columns to repeat on each printed page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	br	In the shrunk dialog you will see $1:$2. Rows 1 and 2 are now rows to repeat.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	br	Click column A (not in the column header).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154371				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Print ranges - Edit\"\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704				0	br	Click the icon again at the far right of the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155380				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	br	If you also want column A as a column to repeat, click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	br	Select the first two rows and, for this example, click cell A1 and drag to A2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
