helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762	41			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_Y_SECONDARY\"\>The major axis and the secondary axis can have different scaling. For example, you can scale one axis to 2 in. and the other to 1.5 in. \</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155113				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_Z_PRIMARY\"\>Displays the Z axis as a line with subdivisions.\</ahelp\> This axis can only be displayed in 3D charts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156445				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_X_SECONDARY\"\>Displays a secondary X axis in the chart.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428				0	br	Use this area to assign a second axis to your chart. If a data row is already assigned to this axis, $[officename] automatically displays the axis and the label. You can turn off these settings later on. If no data has been assigned to this axis and you activate this area, the values of the primary Y axis are applied for the secondary axis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
