helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145114				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_AXIS_LABEL:RB_AXIS_LABEL_UPDOWN\"\>Staggers numbers on the axis, even numbers lower than odd numbers.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147404				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_AXIS_LABEL:RB_AXIS_LABEL_AUTOORDER\"\>Automatically arranges numbers on the axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436	75			0	br	\<variable id=\"sytextbeschr\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleAxisDescr\"\>The\<emph\> AxesTitle On/Off \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> bar switches the labeling of all axes on or off.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCH_ALIGNMENT_CTR_DIAL\"\>Clicking anywhere on the wheel defines the variable text orientation.\</ahelp\> The letters "ABCD" on the button correspond to the new setting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149353				0	br	Problems may arise in displaying labels if the size of your chart is too small. You can avoid this by either enlarging the view or decreasing the font size.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCH_ALIGNMENT_DEGREES\"\>Allows you to manually enter the orientation angle.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	br	If you define a vertical x-axis label, the text may be cut off by the line of the x-axis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	br	Some of the options listed here are not available for all labels. For example, there are different options for 2D and 3D object labels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3151240				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_AXIS_LABEL:CB_AXIS_LABEL_TEXTOVERLAP\"\>Specifies that the text in cells may overlap other cells.\</ahelp\> This can be especially useful if there is a lack of space. This option is not available with different title directions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153958				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_AXIS_LABEL:RB_AXIS_LABEL_DOWNUP\"\>Stagger numbers on the axes, odd numbers lower than even numbers.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_AXIS_LABEL:CB_AXIS_LABEL_SCHOW_DESCR\"\>Specifies whether to show or hide the axis labels.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleAxisDescr\"\>Defines the text direction of cell contents.\</ahelp\> Click one of the ABCD buttons to assign the required direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCH_ALIGNMENT_STACKED\"\>Assigns vertical text orientation for cell contents.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3155089				0	br	Determines the text flow of the data label.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3155268				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_AXIS_LABEL:CB_AXIS_LABEL_TEXTBREAK\"\>Allows a text break.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3155758				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_AXIS_LABEL:RB_AXIS_LABEL_SIDEBYSIDE\"\>Arranges numbers on the axis side by side.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	br	Modifies the alignment of axes or title labels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159230				0	br	The options on this tab are only available for a 2D chart, under \<emph\>Format - Axis - Y Axis\</emph\> or \<emph\>X Axis\</emph\>. In this area, you can define the alignment of the number labels on the X or Y axis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
