helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3143218				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_Y_EDT_STEP_MAIN\"\>Defines the interval for the main division of the axes.\</ahelp\> The main interval cannot be larger than the value area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145360				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE_Y:CBX_LOGARITHM\"\>Specifies that you want the y axis to be subdivided logarithmically.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145389				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE_Y:CBX_AUTO_ORIGIN\"\>You must first deselect the \<emph\>Automatic\</emph\> option in order to modify the values.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	br	The Y axis is automatically scaled by $[officename] so that all values are optimally displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149129				0	br	Disable this feature if you are working with "fixed" values, as it does not permit automatic scaling.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	br	To achieve specific results, you can manually change the axis scaling. For example, you can display only the top areas of the columns by shifting the zero line upwards.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	br	You can enter values for subdividing axes in this area. You can automatically set the five properties \<emph\>Minimum, Maximum, Major interval, Minor interval\</emph\> and \<emph\>Axis at\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_Y_EDT_ORIGIN\"\>Specifies at which position to display the values along the y axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153713				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_Y_EDT_MIN\"\>Defines the minimum value for the beginning of the Y axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153956				0	br	Use this feature if you are working with values that differ sharply from each other. You can use logarithmic scaling to make the grid lines of the axis equidistant but have values that may increase or decrease.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	br	Controls the scaling of the Y axis. The X axis can also be scaled here for X-Y charts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_Y_EDT_STEP_HELP\"\>Defines the interval for the subdivision of the axes.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159266				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_Y_EDT_MAX\"\>Defines the maximum value for the end of the Y axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id5581835				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>\<emph\>Defines where the lower and where the higher values are displayed at \</emph\>\<emph\>the\</emph\>\<emph\> axis. The unchecked state is the\</emph\> mathematical direction.\</ahelp\> That means for Cartesian coordinate systems that the x-axis shows the lower values on the left and the y-axis shows the lower values at the bottom. For polar coordinate systems the mathematical angle axis direction is counterclockwise and the radial axis is from inner to outer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Scaling				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150654				0	br	inner				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151387				0	br	inner				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154677				0	br	outer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166469				0	br	outer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3146880				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE_Y:CBX_HELPTICKS_INNER\"\>Specifies that minor interval marks are placed on the inner side of the axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3146885				0	br	This area is used to define the marking dashes between the axis marks. It is possible to activate both fields. This will result in a marking line running from the outside to the inside.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150397				0	br	Specifies whether the marks are to be on the inner or outer side of the axis. It is possible to combine both: you will then see marks on both sides.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150745				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE_Y:CBX_HELPTICKS_OUTER\"\>Specifies that minor interval marks are placed on the outer side of the axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153120				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE_Y:CBX_TICKS_OUTER\"\>Specifies that marks are placed on the outer side of the axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3156399				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE_Y:CBX_TICKS_INNER\"\>Specifies that marks are placed on the inner side of the axis\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155602				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>grids; formatting axes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>axes; formatting grids\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
