helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	br	Allows you to modify the order of the data rows already set in the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Backward\"\>Sends the selected data row backward (to the left).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149259				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Forward\"\>Brings the selected data row forward (to the right).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	br	This function is only available if you have data displayed in columns. It is not possible to switch to data display in rows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411				0	br	The position of the data in the data table remains unchanged. You can only choose the commands after inserting a chart in $[officename] Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
