helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	bm_id3803827				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>curves;properties in line charts/XY charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>properties;smooth lines in line charts/XY charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id1228370				0	br	To change line properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3050325				0	br	Smooth Line Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id1068758				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Apply a B-spline model.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id1601611				0	br	Select Cubic Spline or B-Spline.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id2320932				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Set the resolution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3424481				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Apply a cubic spline model.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3464461				0	br	Optionally set the resolution. A higher value leads to a smoother line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id6998809				0	br	For B-spline lines optionally set the data points order.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id8638874				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Set the data points order.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id879848				0	br	These are mathematical models that influence the display of the curves. The cubic spline line passes through all points, while the B-spline line connects the first and last point and passes by the intermediate points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id9421979				0	br	In a chart that displays lines (Line type or XY type), you can choose to show curves instead of straight lines. Some options control the properties of those curves.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Smooth Line Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156423				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>3D charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts; 3D views\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>illumination; 3D charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id1939451				0	br	Illumination				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id2924283				0	br	Perspective				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id3464461				0	br	\<variable id=\"three_d_view\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/three_d_view.xhp\"\>3D View\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id7564012				0	br	Appearance				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id1186254				0	br	Select a scheme from the list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id121158				0	br	Use the Ambient light list box to define the ambient light which shines with a uniform intensity from all directions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id130619				0	br	When you leave the dialog with Cancel or Escape, the chart returns to the state when you opened the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a color using the color dialog.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id1579027				0	br	Mark \<emph\>Shading\</emph\> to use the Gouraud method for rendering the surface, otherwise a flat method is used. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2186346				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a color for the selected light source.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	br	An x value of 90, with y and z set to 0, provides a view from top down to the chart. With x set to -90, you see the bottom of the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2423780				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Drag the right slider to set the vertical height and direction of the selected light source.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Drag the bottom slider to set the horizontal position and direction of the selected light source.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2578203				0	br	The rotation axes always relate to the page, not to the chart's axes. This is different from some other chart programs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2761314				0	br	For the selected light source, you can then choose a color and intensity in the list box just below the eight buttons. The brightness values of all lights are added, so use dark colors when you enable multiple lights.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2861720				0	br	With Right-angled axes enabled, you can rotate the chart contents only in X and Y direction, that is, parallel to the chart borders.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	br	The button in the corner of the small preview switches the internal illumination model between a sphere and a cube.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3416547				0	br	Set the focus length with the spin button. 100% gives a perspective view where a far edge in the chart looks approximately half as big as a near edge.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3791924				0	br	Older versions of %PRODUCTNAME cannot display the percentage of perspective the same way as the current version.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3806878				0	br	When you leave the dialog with OK, the settings are applied permanently. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3912778				0	br	The small preview inside this tab page has two sliders to set the vertical and horizontal position of the selected light source. The light source always aims to the middle of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id393993				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a color for the ambient light.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id4407483				0	br	Mark \<emph\>Rounded Edges\</emph\> to smooth the edges of box shapes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id4721823				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the rotation of the chart on the x axis. The preview responds to the new settings.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id4923245				0	br	Select the Perspective check box to view the chart in central perspective as through a camera lens instead of using a parallel projection. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id533768				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to enable or disable the specular light source with highlights.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5624561				0	br	The flat method sets a single color and brightness for each polygon. The edges are visible, soft gradients and spot lights are not possible. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5781731				0	br	Enter the values for rotation of the chart on the three axes and for a perspective view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5806756				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the rotation of the chart on the y axis. The preview responds to the new settings.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5871761				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a color using the color dialog.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5901058				0	br	The Gouraud method applies gradients for a smoother, more realistic look.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6070436				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Mark the Perspective box to view the chart as through a camera lens. Use the spin button to set the percentage. With a high percentage nearer objects look bigger than more distant objects.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6173894				0	br	By default, the second light source is switched on. It is the first of seven "normal", uniform light sources. The light source number one projects a specular light with highlights.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6394238				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to switch between an illumination model of a sphere or a cube.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6531266				0	br	Click any of the eight buttons to switch a directed light source on or off.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6942045				0	br	The chart preview responds to the new settings that you enter in the dialog. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6998809				0	br	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> or in the context menu of a chart you can choose a chart type. \<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enables a three dimensional view for Column, Bar, Pie, and Area charts. For Line and XY (Scatter) charts you can see 3D lines.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7141026				0	br	If you mark or unmark a combination of check boxes that is not given by the Realistic or Simple scheme, you create a Custom scheme.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7214270				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to enable or disable the uniform light source.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7432477				0	br	By selecting a scheme, the check boxes and the light sources are set accordingly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7623828				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If Right-angled axes is enabled, you can rotate the chart contents only in X and Y direction, that is, parallel to the chart borders. Right-angled axes is enabled by default for newly created 3D charts. Pie and Donut charts do not support right-angled axes.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	br	The rotations are applied in the order first x, then y, last z.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8081911				0	br	For a 3D chart you can choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - 3D View\</item\> to set perspective, appearance and illumination.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8469191				0	br	Mark \<emph\>Object Borders\</emph\> to draw lines along the edges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8531449				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a scheme from the list box, or click any of the check boxes below.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8915372				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the rotation of the chart on the z axis. The preview responds to the new settings.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	br	Set the light sources for the 3D view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Applies Gouraud shading if marked, or flat shading if unmarked.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows borders around the areas by setting the line style to Solid.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Edges are rounded by 5%.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	br	When shading is enabled and you rotate a chart, the lights are rotated as if they are fixed to the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9999694				0	br	Set all angles to 0 for a front view of the chart. Pie charts and donut charts are shown as circles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	3D View 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	bm_id4130680				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>area charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;area\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	hd_id310678				0	br	\<variable id=\"type_area\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_area.xhp\"\>Chart Type Area\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	hd_id961943				0	br	Area				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id3640247				0	br	Stacked - this subtypes plots values cumulatively stacked on each other. It ensures that all values are visible, and no data set is hidden by others. However, the y values no longer represent absolute values, except for the last column which is drawn at the bottom of the stacked areas.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id4585100				0	br	Percent - this subtype plots values cumulatively stacked on each other and scaled as percentage of the category total.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id631733				0	br	An area chart shows values as points on the y axis. The x axis shows categories. The y values of each data series are connected by a line. The area between each two lines is filled with a color. The area chart's focus is to emphasize the changes from one category to the next.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id7811822				0	br	Normal - this subtype plots all values as absolute y values. It first plots the area of the last column in the data range, then the next to last, and so on, and finally the first column of data is drawn. Thus, if the values in the first column are higher than other values, the last drawn area will hide the other areas.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id916776				0	br	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Chart Type Area				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	bm_id4919583				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>column charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bar charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;column and bar\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	hd_id649433				0	br	\<variable id=\"type_column_bar\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_column_bar.xhp\"\>Chart Type Column and Bar\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	hd_id955839				0	br	Bar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	hd_id9826960				0	br	Column				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id1281167				0	br	Normal - this subtype shows all data values belonging to a category next to each other. Main focus is on the individual absolute values, compared to every other value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id2224494				0	br	You can enable a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/three_d_view.xhp\"\>3D view\</link\> of the data values. The "realistic" scheme tries to give the best 3D look. The "simple" scheme tries to mimic the chart view of other Office products.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id2244026				0	br	This type shows a bar chart or bar graph with vertical bars. The height of each bar is proportional to its value. The x axis shows categories. The y axis shows the value for each category.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id3249000				0	br	Stacked - this subtype shows the data values of each category on top of each other. Main focus is the overall category value and the individual contribution of each value within its category.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id3430585				0	br	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id6596881				0	br	This type shows a bar chart or bar graph with horizontal bars. The length of each bar is proportional to its value. The y axis shows categories. The x axis shows the value for each category.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id6968901				0	br	Percent - this subtype shows the relative percentage of each data value with regard to the total of its category. Main focus is the relative contribution of each value to the category's total.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id7359233				0	br	For 3D charts, you can select the shape of each data value from Box, Cylinder, Cone, and Pyramid.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id8750572				0	br	The subtypes are the same as for the Column type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Chart Type Column and Bar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id5976744				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>column and line charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;column and line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>combination charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id2451551				0	br	Column and Line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id265816				0	br	Editing data series				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id6667683				0	br	Organizing data series				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8297677				0	br	To specify a data range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8596453				0	br	\<variable id=\"type_column_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_column_line.xhp\"\>Chart Type Column and Line\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8996246				0	br	Inserting chart elements				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id974456				0	br	Editing categories or data labels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1446272				0	br	To organize the data series, select an entry in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1842097				0	br	You can insert a second y-axis with \<link href=\"text/schart/01/04040000.xhp\"\>Insert - Axes\</link\> after you finish the wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1924497				0	br	In the Data Ranges list box you see the role names and cell ranges of the data series components. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1944944				0	br	Check whether the data range has labels in the first row or in the first column or both.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2685323				0	br	Data labels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2767113				0	br	Enter or select a cell range that will be used as text for categories or data labels. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2932828				0	br	Chart titles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2952055				0	br	Select the data range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2958464				0	br	The label next to the text box states the currently selected role. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id301828				0	br	The values in the Categories range will be shown as labels on the x axis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3101901				0	br	A Column and Line chart is a combination of a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_column_bar.xhp\"\>Column chart\</link\> with a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_line.xhp\"\>Line chart\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3779717				0	br	Click Add to add another data series below the selected entry. The new data series has the same type as the selected entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id4818567				0	br	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5056611				0	br	Click Remove to remove the selected entry from the Data Series list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5081942				0	br	Click an entry, then edit the contents in the text box below. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5091708				0	br	The range for a data role, like Y-Values, must not include a label cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5244300				0	br	Columns and Lines. The rectangles of the column data series are drawn side by side so that you can easily compare their values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5729544				0	br	Use the Chart Elements page of the Chart Wizard to insert any of the following elements:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id594500				0	br	Click one of the options for data series in rows or in columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id6042664				0	br	Statistics, for example mean value, error indicator and regression curve				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id6354869				0	br	Minor grids				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id6768700				0	br	Click an entry in the list to view and edit the properties for that entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7163609				0	br	Stacked Columns and Lines. The rectangles of the column data series are drawn stacked above each other, so that the height of a column visualizes the sum of the data values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7616809				0	br	In the Data Series list box you see a list of all data series in the current chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7786492				0	br	Use the Up and Down arrow buttons to move the selected entry in the list up or down. This way you can convert a Column data series to a List data series and back. This does not change the order in the data source table, but changes only the arrangement in the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7889950				0	br	To set different data labels and statistics elements for each data series, use the properties dialog of the data series.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7910397				0	br	Select one of the variants				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8122196				0	br	Visible grid lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id883816				0	br	Enter the range or click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog and select the range with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8871120				0	br	The leftmost columns (or the top rows) of the selected data range provide the data that are shown as Columns objects. The other columns or rows of the data range provide the data for the Lines objects. You can change this assignment in the \<emph\>Data Series\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9141819				0	br	Secondary axes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9449446				0	br	Legend				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9770195				0	br	The column data series are positioned at the top of the list, the line data series at the bottom of the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	br	For additional elements use the Insert menu of the chart in edit mode. There you can define the following elements:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Chart Type Column and Line 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id2187566				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>line charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;line\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id9422894				0	br	\<variable id=\"type_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_line.xhp\"\>Chart Type Line\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id9826349				0	br	Line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2334665				0	br	A line chart shows values as points on the y axis. The x axis shows categories. The y values of each data series can be connected by a line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2655720				0	br	Mark \<emph\>Stack series\</emph\> to arrange the points' y values cumulative above each other. The y values no longer represent absolute values, except for the first column which is drawn at the bottom of the stacked points. If you select \<emph\>Percent\</emph\>, the y values are scaled as percentage of the category total.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3682058				0	br	Mark \<emph\>Smooth lines\</emph\> to draw curves through the points instead of straight lines. Click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> for a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/smooth_line_properties.xhp\"\>dialog\</link\> to change the curves' properties.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id389721				0	br	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id476393				0	br	3D lines - this subtype connects points of the same data series by a 3D line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id500808				0	br	Points and lines - this subtype plots points and connects points of the same data series by a line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8366649				0	br	Lines only - this subtype plots only lines.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8956572				0	br	Points only - this subtype plots only points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Chart Type Line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_net.xhp	0	help	bm_id2193975				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>net charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;net\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>radar charts, see net charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_net.xhp	0	help	hd_id1391338				0	br	Net				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_net.xhp	0	help	hd_id1990722				0	br	\<variable id=\"type_net\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_net.xhp\"\>Chart Type Net\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_net.xhp	0	help	par_id3512375				0	br	For each row of chart data, a radial is shown on which the data is plotted. All data values are shown with the same scale, so all data values should have about the same magnitude.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_net.xhp	0	help	par_id40589				0	br	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_net.xhp	0	help	par_id7812433				0	br	A Net chart displays data values as points connected by some lines, in a grid net that resembles a spider net or a radar tube display.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_net.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Chart Type Net				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	bm_id7621997				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>donut charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pie charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;pie/donut\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	hd_id3365276				0	br	\<variable id=\"type_pie\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_pie.xhp\"\>Chart Type Pie\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	hd_id5799432				0	br	Pie				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id2394482				0	br	Exploded donut - this subtype shows the outer sectors already separated from the remaining donut. In the created chart, you can click and drag an outer sector to move it along a radial from the donut's center.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id245979				0	br	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id3808404				0	br	Donut - this subtype can show multiple data columns. Each data column is shown as one donut shape with a hole inside, where the next data column can be shown. In the created chart, you can click and drag an outer sector to move it along a radial from the donut's center.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id6529740				0	br	Pie - this subtype shows sectors as colored areas of the total pie, for one data column only. In the created chart, you can click and drag any sector to separate that sector from the remaining pie or to join it back.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id6549272				0	br	A pie chart shows values as circular sectors of the total circle. The length of the arc, or the area of each sector, is proportional to its value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id9121982				0	br	Exploded pie - this subtype shows the sectors already separated from each other. In the created chart, you can click and drag any sector to move it along a radial from the pie's center.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Chart Type Pie 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
