helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id1589098				0	br	In Calc, click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog, then drag to select the data range. When you release the mouse, the data are entered. Click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> again to add a data range. In the input field of the minimized dialog, click after the entry and type a semicolon. Then drag to select the next range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id1614429				0	br	As long as the syntax is not correct, %PRODUCTNAME shows the text in red.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id1631824				0	br	Tuesday				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id166936				0	br	5				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id1687063				0	br	Wednesday				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id1911679				0	br	Based on \<emph\>open, low, high\</emph\>, and \<emph\>close\</emph\> column Type 2 generates the traditional "candle stick" chart. Type 2 draws the vertical line between the bottom and top price and adds a rectangle in front, which visualizes the range between the opening and closing price. If you click on the rectangle you see more information in the status bar. %PRODUCTNAME uses different fill colors for rising values (the opening price is lower than the closing price) and falling values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id1924192				0	br	B				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id1933957				0	br	Transaction volume				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2107303				0	br	To add a data series, select one of the existing data series and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>. You get an empty entry below the selected one, which has the same type. If you have no price data series or no volume data series, you must first select a range for these series in the \<emph\>Data Range\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2131412				0	br	For a Stock chart the order of the data series is important. The data should be arranged as shown in the example table below.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2136295				0	br	32				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2188787				0	br	Select one of the position options. When the chart is finished, you can specify other positions using the Format menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2374034				0	br	4				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2377697				0	br	The legend shows the value from the range, which you entered in the \<emph\>Range for Name\</emph\> field in the \<emph\>Data Range\</emph\> dialog. The default entry is the column header of the closing price column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2480849				0	br	In the \<emph\>data series\</emph\> area on the left side of the dialog, you can organize the data series of the actual chart. A stock chart has at least one data series containing the prices. It might have a second data series for transaction volume.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2656941				0	br	4600				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2799157				0	br	31				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2873622				0	br	30				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id291451				0	br	Based on\<emph\> low\</emph\>\<emph\>and high \</emph\>column the Type 1 shows the distance between bottom price (low) and top price (high) by a vertical line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2927335				0	br	To remove a data series, select the data series in the list and click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3004547				0	br	The open, low, high, and closing values of a row build together one data unit in the chart. A stock price data series consists of several rows containing such data units. The column containing the transaction volume builds an optional second data series.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3105868				0	br	47				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3161412				0	br	D				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3258156				0	br	C				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3341776				0	br	Based on\<emph\> low, high,\</emph\> and \<emph\>close\</emph\> column Type 1 shows an additional horizontal mark \<emph\>for\</emph\> the closing price.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3394573				0	br	You can choose or alter a data range on the second page of the Chart wizard or in the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_range.xhp\"\>Data Range\</link\> dialog. For fine tuning use the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_series.xhp\"\>Data Series\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3486434				0	br	You can organize data series and edit the source for parts of single data series on the third page of the Chart wizard or on the page Data Series in the Data Range dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3496200				0	br	Do not write the name of a data series in a row. Write the name into the field above the role name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3516953				0	br	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3892635				0	br	High (top price)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3908810				0	br	35				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3939634				0	br	The legend displays the labels from the first row or column or from the special range that you have set in the \<emph\>Data Series\</emph\> dialog. If your chart does not contain labels, the legend displays text like "Row 1, Row 2, ...", or "Column A, Column B, ..." according to the row number or column letter of the chart data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3998840				0	br	Monday				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4013794				0	br	3				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4181951				0	br	If you have got more than one price data series, use the Up and Down arrow buttons to order them. The order determines the arrangement in the chart. Do the same for volume data series. You cannot switch price and volume data series.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4186223				0	br	22				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4191717				0	br	Because measurement for transaction volume might be "units", a second y axis is introduced in chart Type 3 and Type 4. The price axis is shown on the right side and the volume axis on the left side.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4331797				0	br	Based on all five data columns \<emph\>volume, open, low, high\</emph\>, and \<emph\>close\</emph\>, Type 4 combines a chart of Type 2 with a column chart for the transaction volume.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4473403				0	br	Based on \<emph\>volume, low, high\</emph\>, and \<emph\>close\</emph\> column chart Type 3 draws a chart like Type 1, with additional columns for the transaction volume.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4641865				0	br	Closing price				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4897915				0	br	30				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id5044404				0	br	Low (bottom price)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id5081637				0	br	Enter the data range in the text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id5298318				0	br	To change the data series of a chart having its own data, choose \<link href=\"text/schart/01/03010000.xhp\"\>Chart Data Table\</link\> from the View menu or from the context menu of the chart in edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id5452436				0	br	15				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id5589159				0	br	15				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id5619373				0	br	E				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id61342				0	br	A Stock chart illustrates the market trend given by opening price, bottom price, top price and closing price. The transaction volume can also be shown.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6138492				0	br	Choose the \<emph\>Stock\</emph\> chart type on the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart wizard\</link\>. Then select one of the four variants.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6182744				0	br	If you have already got a stock chart and you want to change the variant, then first change the chart type to a column chart, add or remove columns so that it fits to the variant, and then change the chart type back to a stock chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6342356				0	br	17				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id636921				0	br	32				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6401867				0	br	Depending on the chosen variant, you do not need all columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6474501				0	br	F				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6478469				0	br	In the upper list you see the role name of the components and the current values. When you have selected a role, you can change the value in the text box below the list. The label shows the selected role.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6826990				0	br	Thursday				2002-02-02 02:02:02
