helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7003387				0	br	40				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7074190				0	br	15				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7271645				0	br	3500				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7411725				0	br	1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7588732				0	br	In an embedded chart data table, the data series are always organized in columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7594225				0	br	To specify a data range do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7599108				0	br	The order of the rows determines how the categories are arranged in the chart. Use Move Row Down to change the order.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7675099				0	br	2500				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7684560				0	br	2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7806329				0	br	20				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7844477				0	br	In the \<emph\>Data Ranges\</emph\> dialog you can set or change the data range of each component of the selected data series.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7921079				0	br	20				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7953123				0	br	17				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7985168				0	br	Select Open Values, Close Values, High Values, and Low Values in any order. Specify only the ranges for those roles which you need for the chosen variant of the stock chart. The ranges need not be next to each other in the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id8746910				0	br	Click one of the options for data series in rows or in columns. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id8982207				0	br	1000				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	br	Enter the range into the text box or click on \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog and select the range with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id9239173				0	br	Friday				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id9461653				0	br	6				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id9527878				0	br	17				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id95828				0	br	For a new stock chart first use a column chart. Add the columns you need and enter your data in the order which is shown in the example, omitting any columns not required for the desired variant. Use Move Series Right to change the column order. Close the chart data table. Now use the Chart Type dialog to change to the stock chart variant. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id9636524				0	br	Your stock chart data are "in columns", if the information in a row belongs to the same "candle stick".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id9759514				0	br	In Calc, an example data range would be "$Sheet1.$B$3:$B$14". Note that a data range may consist of more than one region in a spreadsheet, e.g. "$Sheet1.A1:A5;$Sheet1.D1:D5" is also a valid data range. In Writer, an example data range would be "Table1.A1:E4".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
