helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id7757194				0	br	XY (Scatter)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id9346598				0	br	\<variable id=\"type_xy\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_xy.xhp\"\>Chart Type XY (Scatter)\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1202124				0	br	Click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> to set details for the curves.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1221655				0	br	generate a parameter curve, for example a spiral				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1336710				0	br	scale the x‑axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id2003845				0	br	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id3397320				0	br	draw the graph of a function				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4381847				0	br	Choose an XY chart for the following example tasks:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4408093				0	br	This variant draws straight lines from one data point to the next. The data points are not shown by icons. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4634235				0	br	The chart is created with default settings. After the chart is finished, you can edit its properties to change the appearance. Line styles and icons can be changed on the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> tab page of the data series properties dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5482039				0	br	Double-click any data point to open the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data Series\</item\> dialog. Here you can click the \<emph\>Statistics\</emph\> tab and enable the display of statistical values. Some available values are mean value, variance, standard deviation, percentage, error margins, and regression curves or trend lines.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5977965				0	br	An XY chart in its basic form is based on one data series consisting of a name, a list of x‑values, and a list of y‑values. Each value pair (x|y) is shown as a point in a coordinate system. The name of the data series is associated with the y‑values and shown in the legend.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5989562				0	br	\<emph\>Cubic Spline\</emph\> interpolates your data points with polynomials of degree 3. The transitions between the polynomial pieces are smooth, having the same slope and curvature. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6128421				0	br	The \<emph\>Resolution\</emph\> determines how many line segments are calculated to draw a piece of polynomial between two data points. You can see the intermediate points if you click any data point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6571550				0	br	Each data point is shown by an icon. %PRODUCTNAME uses default icons with different forms and colors for each data series. The default colors are set in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Options - Charts - Default Colors\</item\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7261268				0	br	The drawing order is the same as the order in the data series. Mark \<emph\>Sort by X Values\</emph\> to draw the lines in the order of the x values. This sorting applies only to the chart, not to the data in the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7422711				0	br	The lines are shown like tapes. The data points are not shown by icons. In the finished chart choose \<link href=\"text/schart/01/three_d_view.xhp\"\>3D View\</link\> to set properties like illumination and angle of view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7657399				0	br	explore the statistical association of quantitative variables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7957396				0	br	Mark \<emph\>Smooth Lines\</emph\> to draw curves instead of straight line segments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id8919339				0	br	You can choose an XY chart variant on the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\>, or by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Chart Type \</item\>for a chart in edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id8925138				0	br	Your XY chart may have more than one data series.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id9280373				0	br	\<emph\>B-Spline\</emph\> uses the data points as control points to form a B-spline curve. Those curves are built piecewise from polynomials. The \<emph\>Data points order\</emph\> sets the degree k of these polynomials. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id9611499				0	br	This variant shows points and lines at the same time.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Chart Type XY				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	hd_id6942045				0	br	Additional elements				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id1058992				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays grid lines that are parallel to the y-axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id1069368				0	br	The legend displays the labels from the first row or column, or from the range that you have set in the Data Series dialog. If your chart does not contain labels, the legend displays text like "Row 1, Row 2, ...", or "Column A, Column B, ..." according to the row number or column letter of the chart data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id156865				0	br	It is not possible to link the title text to a cell. You must enter the text directly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id2924283				0	br	The distance of the grid lines corresponds to the interval settings in the Scale tab of the axis properties.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id3614917				0	br	If you enter text for a title, subtitle, or any axis, the necessary space will be reserved to display the text next to the chart. If you do not enter a text, no space will be reserved, leaving more space to display the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id4721823				0	br	For additional elements use the Insert menu of the chart in edit mode. There you can define the following elements:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id4776757				0	br	Grids				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id5781731				0	br	Grid lines are not available for pie charts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id5806756				0	br	Secondary axes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id6034424				0	br	When the chart is finished, you can change the position and other properties by the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id6070436				0	br	Data labels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id6527298				0	br	The visible grid lines can help to estimate the data values in the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id6737876				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays grid lines that are parallel to the x-axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id6998809				0	br	You cannot enter the text directly, it is automatically generated from the Name cell range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id71413				0	br	Select one of the position options. When the chart is finished, you can specify other positions using the Format menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id7366557				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays grid lines that are parallel to the z-axis. This option is only available for three-dimensional charts.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id7564012				0	br	Statistics, for example mean value, error indicator and regression curve				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id8915372				0	br	Minor grids				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id9033783				0	br	Legend				2002-02-02 02:02:02
