helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id2284920				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to go to the named wizard page.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id2414014				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The lines are shown as curves.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id3184301				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a basic chart type.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id3191625				0	br	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\> to see the next wizard page, or click the entries on the left side of the wizard to go to that page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id3267006				0	br	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F1\</item\> and point to a control to see an extended help text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id3453169				0	br	Choose a basic \<link href=\"text/schart/01/choose_chart_type.xhp\"\>chart type\</link\>: click any of the entries labeled Column, Bar, Pie, and so on.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id3860896				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the type of 3D look.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id4041871				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a shape from the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id4485000				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Chart Type dialog.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id5749687				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Stack series display values on top of each other.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id6006958				0	br	On the first page of the Chart Wizard you can \<link href=\"text/schart/01/choose_chart_type.xhp\"\>choose a chart type\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id6649372				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Connects points by ascending X values, even if the order of values is different, in an XY scatter diagram.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id7251503				0	br	Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\> on any wizard page to close the wizard and create the chart using the current settings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id7334208				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Set the number of lines for the Column and Line chart type.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id7617114				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialog to set the curve properties.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id7659535				0	br	Click \<emph\>Back\</emph\> to see the previous wizard page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id79348				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Stack series display values as percent.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id8230231				0	br	Optionally, click any of the options. While you change the settings in the wizard, watch the preview in the document to see how the chart will look.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id8406933				0	br	The contents on the right side will change to offer more options depending on the basic chart type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id8420056				0	br	Click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> to close the wizard without creating a chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id9719229				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enables a 3D look for the data values.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id9930722				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays stacked series for Line charts.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Chart Wizard - Chart Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	bm_id2429578				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>data ranges in charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	hd_id1877193				0	br	To specify a data range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	hd_id8313852				0	br	\<variable id=\"wiz_data_range\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_range.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard - Data Range\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id1363872				0	br	In Calc, click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog, then drag to select the data range. Click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> again to enter the data range. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id1434369				0	br	Click one of the options for data series in rows or in columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id2025818				0	br	Use the Chart Wizard - Data Series page if you need more control over the data ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id2898953				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For data series in columns: The first row in the range is used as names for data series. For data series in rows: The first row in the range is used as categories. The remaining rows comprise the data series. If this check box is not selected, all rows are data series.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id379650				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the data range that you want to include in your chart. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id4357432				0	br	Enter the data range in the text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id4496597				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Data series get their data from consecutive columns in the selected range. For scatter charts, the first data column will contain x-values for all series. All other data columns are used as y-values, one for each series.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5256508				0	br	In the preview you can see how the final chart will look.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5626392				0	br	In Calc, an example data range would be "$Sheet1.$B$3:$B$14". Note that a data range may consist of more than one region in a spreadsheet, e.g. "$Sheet1.A1:A5;$Sheet1.D1:D5" is also a valid data range. In Writer, an example data range would be "Table1.A1:E4".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5924863				0	br	Select the data range. Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id6401867				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Data Ranges dialog where you can edit Data Range and Data Series.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id6823938				0	br	If you want a data range of multiple cell areas that are not next to each other, enter the first range, then manually add a semicolon at the end of the text box, then enter the other ranges. Use a semicolon as delimiter between ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id7524033				0	br	Check whether the data range has labels in the first row or in the first column or both.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id7546311				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For data series in columns: The first column in the range is used as names for data series. For data series in rows: The first column in the range is used as categories. The remaining columns comprise the data columns. If this check box is not selected, all columns are data columns.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id8466139				0	br	This dialog is only available for charts based on a Calc or Writer table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id8829309				0	br	On this page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can select one single source of data range. This range may consist of more than one rectangular range of cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id953703				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Data series get their data from consecutive rows in the selected range. For scatter charts, the first data series will contain x-values for all series. All other data series are used as y-values, one for each series.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Chart Wizard - Data Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	bm_id8641621				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>order of chart data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data series\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id6124149				0	br	\<variable id=\"wiz_data_series\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_series.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard - Data Series\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id7622608				0	br	Editing categories or data labels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id9241615				0	br	Organizing data series				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id9777520				0	br	Editing data series				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id1091647				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Adds a new entry below the current entry in the Data Series list. If an entry is selected, the new data series gets the same chart type.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id1474654				0	br	Click an entry in the list to view and edit the properties for that entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2254402				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows the source range address from the second column of the Data Range list box. You can change the range in the text box or by dragging in the document. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2419507				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows the source range address of the categories (the texts you can see on the x-axis of a category chart). For an XY-chart, the text box contains the source range of the data labels which are displayed for the data points. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2571794				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows all the data ranges used by the data series that is selected in the Data Series list box. Each data range shows the role name and the source range address.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2844019				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves down the selected entry in the Data Series list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2926419				0	br	Click Remove to remove the selected entry from the Data Series list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3931699				0	br	Enter the range or click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog and select the range with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4443800				0	br	Use the Up and Down arrow buttons to move the selected entry in the list up or down. This does not change the order in the data source table, but changes only the arrangement in the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4695272				0	br	The label next to the text box states the currently selected role. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4855189				0	br	In the Data Ranges list box you see the role names and cell ranges of the data series components. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4921720				0	br	To organize the data series, select an entry in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id5201879				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows a list of all data series in the chart. Click an entry to view and edit that data series. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to insert a new series into the list after the selected entry.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id5971556				0	br	The range for a data role, like Y-Values, must not include a label cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id6326487				0	br	If there seem to be too many options on this page, just define the data range on the Chart Wizard - Data Range page and skip this page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id6627094				0	br	Click Add to add another data series below the selected entry. The new data series has the same type as the selected entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id686361				0	br	This dialog is only available for charts based on a Calc or Writer table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id7022309				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves up the selected entry in the Data Series list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id7159337				0	br	In the Data Series list box you see a list of all data series in the current chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id8626667				0	br	If you want a data range of multiple cell areas that are not next to each other, enter the first range, then manually add a semikolon at the end of the text box, then enter the other ranges. Use a semikolon as delimiter between ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id8831446				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Removes the selected entry from the Data Series list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9222693				0	br	Enter or select a cell range that will be used as text for categories or data labels. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9475081				0	br	Click an entry, then edit the contents in the text box below. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9500106				0	br	Depending on the chart type, the texts are shown on the X axis or as data labels. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9651478				0	br	On this page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can change the source range of all data series separately, including their labels. You can also change the range of the categories. You can first select the data range on the Data Range page and then remove unnecessary data series or add data series from other cells here.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
