helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436				0	br	\<variable id=\"eyedropper\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/eyedropper.xhp\" name=\"Replacing Colors\"\>Replacing Colors\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150205				0	br	To replace colors with the Eyedropper tool				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3145362				0	br	This replaces all occurrences of the \<emph\>Source color\</emph\> in the image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3146878				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06030000.xhp\" name=\"Eyedropper\"\>Eyedropper\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3147344				0	br	You can also use the \<emph\>Transparency\</emph\> option to replace the transparent areas of an image with a color.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	br	Similarly, you can use the \<emph\>Eyedropper\</emph\> to make a color on your image transparent.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3148866				0	br	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, select the new color.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3149876				0	br	Click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3150202				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Eyedropper\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3151191				0	br	If you want to replace another color while the dialog is open, select the check box in front of \<emph\>Source color\</emph\> in the next row and repeat steps 3 to 5.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	br	Click the color in the image. The color appears in the first \<emph\>Source color\</emph\> box and the check box next to the color is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	br	Ensure that the image you are using is a bitmap (for example, BMP, GIF, JPG, or PNG) or a metafile (for example, WMF).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704				0	br	Up to four colors can be replaced at once.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3155531				0	br	Click the Eyedropper icon and position the mouse pointer over the color you want to replace in the image. The color appears in the box next to the eyedropper icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	br	You can replace colors in bitmaps with the \<emph\>Eyedropper\</emph\> tool.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	br	If you want to expand or contract the color selection area, increase or decrease the tolerance of the \<emph\>Eyedropper\</emph\> tool and repeat your selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Replacing Colors				2002-02-02 02:02:02
