helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150653				0	br	To adjust the gradient of a drawing object:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792	3			0	br	\<variable id=\"gradient\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/gradient.xhp\" name=\"Creating Gradient Fills\"\>Creating Gradient Fills\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154702				0	br	Creating Custom Gradients				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116				0	br	Type a name for the gradient in the text box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145592				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Gradients\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145791				0	br	You can define your own gradients and modify existing gradients, as well as save and load a list of gradient files.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	br	Select a drawing object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150046				0	br	Select a gradient from the list to use as the basis for your new gradient and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	br	Set the gradient properties and click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> to save the gradient.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150659				0	br	To adjust the transparency of an object, select the object, choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Transparency\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Gradients\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	br	Select a gradient style from the list and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012				0	br	A gradient fill is an incremental blend of two different colors, or shades of the same color, that you can apply to a drawing object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and select \<emph\>Gradient\</emph\> as the \<emph\>Fill\</emph\> type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154844				0	br	Select a drawing object with the gradient that you want to modify.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3156396	16			0	br	Click \<emph\>OK.\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3157905				0	br	You can adjust the properties of a gradient as well as the transparency of a drawing object with your mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id6535843				0	br	The name appears at the end of the gradient list and is selected for editing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	br	Adjust the values for the gradient to suit your needs and click \<emph\>Ok\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
