helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156443				0	br	\<variable id=\"graphic_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/graphic_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Graphics\"\>Inserting Pictures\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150044				0	br	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to insert the picture.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	br	Locate the picture you want to insert. Select the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> check box to insert only a link to the picture. If you want to see the picture before you insert it, select \<emph\>Preview\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764				0	br	After you insert a linked picture, do not change the name of the source picture or move the source picture to another directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Inserting Graphics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150793				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; grouping\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>groups; entering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;group objects\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150205				0	br	Selecting Objects in a Group				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150716				0	br	To group objects:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150793				0	br	\<variable id=\"groups\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/groups.xhp\" name=\"Grouping Objects\"\>Grouping Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	br	Groups can also be grouped in other groups. Actions applied to a group do not affect the relative position of the individual objects to each other in the group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147002				0	br	After you have grouped objects, selecting any part of the group selects the entire group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147346				0	br	Select the objects you want to group and choose \<emph\>Modify - Group\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	br	Temporary - group only lasts as long as all of the combined objects are selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485				0	br	For example, you can group all of the objects in a company logo to move and resize the logo as a single object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3145643\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatgroup.png\" width=\"4.23mm\" height=\"4.23mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145643\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	br	To exit a group, double-click anywhere outside it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3155376\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_entergroup.png\" width=\"4.23mm\" height=\"4.23mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155376\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3151239				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3155264\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_leavegroup.png\" width=\"4.23mm\" height=\"4.23mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155264\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	br	You can combine several objects into a group so that they act as a single object. You can move and transform all objects in a group as a single unit. You can also change the properties (for example, line size, fill color) of all objects in a group as a whole or for individual objects in a group. Groups can be temporary or assigned:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	br	Assigned - group lasts until it is ungrouped through a menu command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3156450				0	br	You can select single objects in a group by entering the group. Double-click a group to enter it and click on the object to select it. You can also add or delete objects to and from a group in this mode. The objects that are not part of the group are grayed out.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Grouping Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145799				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; connecting lines to\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>connecting; lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines; connecting objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>areas; from connected lines\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
