helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	br	You can combine two or more 3D objects into a single object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	br	Select the second 3D object (sphere) and choose \<emph\>Edit - Cut\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3148606				0	br	You cannot intersect or subtract 3D objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3149211				0	br	Double-click the first object (cube) to enter its group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154537				0	br	\<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10090000.xhp\" name=\"Objects in 3D\"\>Objects in 3D\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154652				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>. Both objects are now part of the same group. If you want, you can edit the individual objects or change their position within the group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	br	Insert a 3D object from the \<emph\>3D Objects\</emph\> toolbar (for example, a cube).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	br	Insert a second slightly larger 3D object (for example, a sphere).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
