helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1978514				0	br	Enter the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	br	Double-click the text to edit it or to format text properties, such as font size or font color. Click the border of the text object to edit the object properties, such as border color or arranging in front or behind other objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	46			0	br	There are several types of text you can add to a drawing or presentation: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3146877				0	br	Create a text frame as described in the steps above. The size of the frame determines the size of the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147366	59			0	br	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Callouts\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154508\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_calloutshapes.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154508\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to open the Callouts toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149052				0	br	Drag a text frame to the size you want in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149250	57			0	br	Resizing the frame also resizes the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150272				0	br	Drag to draw the callout.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3151194				0	br	Type or paste your text in the text frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155266	49			0	br	Click the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156450\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_text.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156450\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and move the mouse pointer to where you want to enter the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10824				0	br	Text in a text frame				2002-02-02 02:02:02
