helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148797				0	br	\<variable id=\"main0503\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/main0503.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Draw Features\"\>$[officename] Draw Features\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149207				0	br	Graphic File Formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154320				0	br	Creating 3D Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154491				0	br	Grids and Guides				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154705				0	br	Gallery				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155601				0	br	Connecting Objects to Show Relationships				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155764				0	br	Displaying Dimensions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	br	You can create simple 3D objects such as cubes, spheres, and cylinders in $[officename] Draw and even modify the light source of the objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	br	$[officename] Draw lets you create simple and complex drawings and export them in a number of common image formats. You can also insert tables, charts, formulas and other items created in $[officename] programs into your drawings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3149124				0	br	You can connect objects in $[officename] Draw with special lines called "connectors" to show the relationship between objects. Connectors attach to glue points on drawing objects and remain attached when the connected objects are moved. Connectors are useful for creating organization charts and technical diagrams.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	br	Grids and guides provide a visual cue to help you align objects in your drawing. You can also choose to snap an object to a grid line, guide or to the edge of another object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	br	$[officename] Draw creates vector graphics using lines and curves defined by mathematical vectors. Vectors describe lines, ellipses, and polygons according to their geometry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	br	The Gallery contains images, animations, sounds and other items that you can insert and use in your drawings as well as other $[officename] programs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3155112				0	br	$[officename] Draw can export to many common graphic file formats, such as BMP, GIF, JPG, and PNG.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	br	Technical diagrams often show the dimensions of objects in the drawing. In $[officename] Draw, you can use dimension lines to calculate and display linear dimensions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	$[officename] Draw Features				2002-02-02 02:02:02
