helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148492				0	br	When you are working with database tables, you can only undo the last command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149205	2			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_IMAPDLG_UNDO\"\>Reverses the last command or the last entry you typed. To select the command that you want to reverse, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Undo \</emph\>icon on the Standard bar.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	br	You can cancel the Undo command by choosing Edit - Redo.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155504	4			0	br	If you change the content of a record in a database table that has not been saved, and then use the\<emph\> Undo\</emph\> command, the record is erased.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159147				0	br	The \<emph\>Undo \</emph\>list is cleared when you apply a new layout to a slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
