helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\03170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147009				0	br	To detach the \<emph\>Color Bar\</emph\>, click on a gray area of the toolbar and then drag. To reattach the \<emph\>Color Bar\</emph\>, drag the title bar of the toolbar to the edge of the window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\03170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	br	You can also drag a color from the \<emph\>Color Bar\</emph\> and drop it on a draw object on your slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\03170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153255				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ColorControl\"\>Show or hides the \<emph\>Color Bar\</emph\>. To modify or change the color table that is displayed, choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>, and then click on the \<emph\>Colors\</emph\> tab.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\03170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154186				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_COLOR_CTL_COLORS\"\>Click the color that you want to use. To change the fill color of an object in the current file, select the object and then click a color. To change the line color of the selected object, right-click a color. To change the color of text in a text object, double-click the text-object, select the text, and then click a color.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\03170000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Color Bar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
