helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3144766				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FontColor\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>\<variable id=\"textfarbe\"\>Click to apply the current font color to the selected characters. You can also click here, and then drag a selection to change the text color. Click the arrow next to the icon to open the \<emph\>Font color \</emph\>toolbar. \</variable\>\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145203				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_LB_STRIKEOUT\"\>Select a strikethrough style for the selected text.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145662				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_CB_BLINKING\"\>Makes the selected characters blink. You cannot change the blink frequency.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146924				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_LB_FONTCOLOR\"\>Sets the color for the selected text. If you select\<emph\> Automatic\</emph\>, the text color is set to black for light backgrounds and to white for dark backgrounds.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_LB_RELIEF\"\>Select a relief effect to apply to the selected text. The embossed relief makes the characters appear as if they are raised above the page. The engraved relief makes the characters appear as if they are pressed into the page.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_LB_POSITION\"\>Specify where to display the emphasis marks.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_LB_UNDERLINE\"\>Select the underlining style that you want to apply. To apply the underlining to words only, select the \<emph\>Individual Words \</emph\>box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148944				0	br	The following capitalization effects are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148947				0	br	Lowercase - changes the selected uppercase characters to lower characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149205				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS\"\>Specify the font effects that you want to use.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	br	Title font - changes the first character of each selected word to an uppercase character				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150037				0	br	The text color is ignored if the \<emph\>Print black \</emph\>check box is selected in \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040400.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Writer - Print\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_LB_EFFECTS2\"\>Select the font effects that you want to apply.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150254				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_LB_UNDERLINE_COLOR\"\>Select the color for the underlining.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150496				0	br	If you save your document in MS Word format, all of the strikethrough styles are converted to the single line style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150962				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_TRISTATEBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_CB_SHADOW\"\>Adds a shadow that casts below and to the right of the selected characters.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151053				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010500.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] color tables\"\>$[officename] color tables\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_LB_EMPHASIS\"\>Select a character to display over or below the entire length of the selected text.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152935				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_CB_INDIVIDUALWORDS\"\>Applies the selected effect only to words and ignores spaces.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153147				0	br	If you apply underlining to a superscript text, the underlining is raised to the level of the superscript. If the superscript is contained in a word with normal text, the underlining is not raised.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154280				0	br	Capitals - changes the selected lowercase characters to uppercase characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154937				0	br	Small capitals - changes the selected lowercase characters to uppercase characters, and then reduces their size				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	br	Without - no effect is applied				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159126				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_TRISTATEBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_CB_OUTLINE\"\>Displays the outline of the selected characters. This effect does not work with every font.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id7613757				0	br	The text color is ignored on screen, if the \<emph\>Use automatic font color for screen display\</emph\> check box is selected in \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01013000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME - Accessibility\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B81				0	br	Hidden				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B85				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"svx:TriStateBox:RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS:CB_CHARHIDDEN\"\>Hides the selected characters.\</ahelp\> To display the hidden text, ensure that \<emph\>Non-printing Characters\</emph\> is selected in the \<emph\>View\</emph\> menu. You can also choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\> and select \<emph\>Hidden text\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC2				0	br	To change the color of a text selection, select the text that you want to change, and click the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon. To apply a different color, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon, and then select the color that you want to use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC9				0	br	If you click the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon before you select text, the paint can cursor appears. To change the color of text, select the text with the paint can cursor. To change the color of a single word, double-click in a word. To apply a different color, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon, and then select the color that you want to use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CD6				0	br	To undo the last change, right-click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CDA				0	br	To exit the paint can mode, click once, or press the Escape key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
