helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145416				0	br	The default currency format for a cell is determined by the regional settings of your operating system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3146148				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:CHECKBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT:BTN_THOUSAND\"\>Inserts a separator between thousands. The type of separator that is used depends on your language settings.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147219				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NUMBERFORMAT_TBI_ADD\"\>Adds the number format code that you entered to the user-defined category.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147352	12			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:NUMERICFIELD:RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT:ED_LEADZEROES\"\>Enter the maximum number of zeroes to display in front of the decimal point.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NUMBERFORMAT_LB_FORMAT\"\>Select how you want the contents of the selected cell(s) to be displayed.\</ahelp\> The code for the selected option is displayed in the \<emph\>Format Code\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT:LB_CURRENCY\"\>Select a currency, and then scroll to the top of the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list to view the formatting options for the currency.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148922				0	br	Specify the options for the selected format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774	4			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT:LB_CATEGORY\"\>Select a category from the list, and then select a formatting style in the \<emph\>Format \</emph\>box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150866	99			0	br	The format code for currencies uses the form [$xxx-nnn], where xxx is the currency symbol, and nnn the country code. Special banking symbols, such as EUR (for Euro), do not require the country code. The currency format is not dependent on the language that you select in the\<emph\> Language\</emph\> box. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153095				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020301.xhp\" name=\"Custom format codes\"\>Custom format codes\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT:LB_LANGUAGE\"\>Specifies the language setting for the selected \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>cells \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>fields\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>. With the language set to \<emph\>Automatic\</emph\>, $[officename] automatically applies the number formats associated with the system default language. Select any language to fix the settings for the selected \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>cells \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>fields\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154150				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NUMBERFORMAT_TBI_REMOVE\"\>Deletes the selected number format.\</ahelp\> The changes are effective after you restart $[officename].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:NUMERICFIELD:RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT:ED_DECIMALS\"\>Enter the number of decimal places that you want to display.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT:ED_COMMENT\"\>Enter a comment for the selected number format, and then click outside this box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3157320				0	br	The language setting ensures that date and currency formats are preserved even when the document is opened in an operating system that uses a different default language setting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3159156				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_NUMBERFORMAT:ED_FORMAT\"\>Displays the number format code for the selected format. You can also enter a custom format.\</ahelp\> The following options are only available for user-defined number formats.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
