helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3148440				0	br	If a number contains more digits to the right of the decimal delimiter than there are placeholders in the format, the number is rounded accordingly. If a number contains more digits to the left of the decimal delimiter than there are placeholders in the format, the entire number is displayed. Use the following list as a guide for using placeholders when you create a number format code:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
