helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146147				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER:LB_SHADOWCOLOR\"\>Select a color for the shadow.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	br	You can also apply a shadow effect to borders. For the best results, only apply this effect when all four borders are visible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148643				0	br	If you are in a table or spreadsheet, you can also add or remove predefined borders. Use the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Table Bar\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151097				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BORDER\"\>Sets the border options for the selected objects in Writer or Calc.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151176				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_METRICFIELD_RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER_MF_LEFT\"\>Enter the distance that you want to have between the left border and the contents of the selection.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER:LB_LINESTYLE\"\>Click the border style that you want to apply. The border is applied to the borders selected in the preview.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3152997				0	br	To modify the border of an entire table, place the cursor in a table cell, right-click, choose \<emph\>Table\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> tab. To modify the border of a table cell, select the cell, right-click, choose \<emph\>Table\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153104				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_METRICFIELD_RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER_MF_RIGHT\"\>Enter the distance that you want to have between the right border and the contents of the selection.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153332				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BORDER_CTL_PRESETS\"\>Select a predefined border style to apply.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153364				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BORDER_CTL_SHADOWS\"\>Click a shadow style for the selected borders.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154299				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER_CB_SYNC\"\>Applies the same \<emph\>spacing to contents\</emph\> setting to all four borders when you enter a new distance.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	br	Specify the amount of space that you want to leave between the border and the contents of the selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER:LB_LINECOLOR\"\>Select the line color that you want to use for the selected border(s).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3155351	44			0	br	You can specify the border position, size, and style in Writer or Calc. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>In $[officename] Writer, you can add borders to pages, frames, graphics, tables, paragraphs, and to embedded objects. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:METRICFIELD:RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER:ED_SHADOWSIZE\"\>Enter the width of the shadow.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156212				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_METRICFIELD_RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER_MF_TOP\"\>Enter the distance that you want to have between the top border and the contents of the selection.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3157309				0	br	Graphics or objects that are anchored to a frame in the document cannot exceed the size of the frame. If you apply a shadow to the borders of an object that fills an entire frame, the size of the object is reduced to display the shadows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3158410				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_METRICFIELD_RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER_MF_BOTTOM\"\>Enter the distance that you want to have between the bottom border and the contents of the selection.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109BA				0	br	Merge adjacent line styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109BE				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"700793922\"\>Merges two different border styles of adjacent cells in a Writer table into one border style. This property is valid for a whole table in a Writer document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109C1				0	br	The rules can be condensed to the statement that the stronger attribute wins. If, for example, one cell has a red border of 2 point width, and the adjacent cell has a blue border of 3 point width, then the common border between these two cells will be blue with 3 point width.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A2B				0	br	Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A2F				0	br	Specifies the properties for the current paragraph or the selected paragraphs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A3A				0	br	Merge with next paragraph				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A3E				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"svx:CheckBox:RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER:CB_MERGEWITHNEXT\"\>Merges the border style and the shadow style of the current paragraph with the next paragraph.\</ahelp\> These styles are only merged if the indent, border, and shadow styles of the next paragraph are the same as the current paragraph. This option is also available for Paragraph Styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
