helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3148483				0	br	The Form Navigation bar also displays information about the number of records in the current table. For example, "Record 7 of 9(2)" indicates that two records (2) are selected in a table containing 9 records, and that the cursor is in record number 7.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149064				0	br	Drag and drop only works in \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149150				0	br	You cannot use the data source browser on a database table that is open in Design view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149266				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3156060\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_firstrecord.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156060\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149287				0	br	You can cut, copy, and paste table fields in \<emph\>Data Source\</emph\> view. The Data Source browser also supports the dragging and dropping of table fields, or simple text and numbers from other $[officename] files.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149295				0	br	Hold down Ctrl and click the row header				2002-02-02 02:02:02
