helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145606				0	br	The automatic numbering option is only applied to paragraphs that are formatted with the "Default", "Text body", or "Text body indent" paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145728				0	br	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>Removes empty paragraphs from the current document when you choose \<emph\>Format - AutoFormat - Apply\</emph\>. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	br	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>Creates a table when you press Enter after typing a series of hyphens (-) or tabs separated by plus signs, that is, +------+---+. Plus signs indicate column dividers, while hyphens and tabs indicate the width of a column. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146874				0	br	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>To cancel automatic numbering when you press Enter at the end of a line that starts with a numbering symbol, press Enter again. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146946				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OFAPAGE_AUTOFORMAT_CLB\"\>Select the options for automatically correcting errors as you type, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	br	~~~				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147219				0	br	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>+-----------------+---------------+------+ \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	br	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>Automatically replaces the "Default" paragraph style with the Heading 1 to Heading 8 paragraph styles. To apply the Heading 1 paragraph style, type the text that you want to use as a heading (without a period), and then press Enter twice. To apply a sub-heading, press Tab one or more times, type the text (without a period), and then press Enter. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147580				0	br	===				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	br	---				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148647				0	br	***				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	br	If you type two uppercase letters at the beginning of a "WOrd", the second uppercase letter is automatically replaced with a lowercase letter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149235	16			0	br	Replaces 1/2, 1/4, 3/4 with the corresponding fraction characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149266				0	br	1.0pt single underline				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150420				0	br	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>Converts paragraphs that start with a hyphen (-), a plus sign (+), or an asterisk (*) directly followed by a space or a tab, to bulleted lists. This option only works on paragraphs that are formatted with the "Default", "Text Body", or "Text Body Indent" paragraph styles. To change the bullet style that is used, select this option, and then click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150866				0	br	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>Removes spaces and tabs at the beginning of each line. To use this option, the \<emph\>Apply Styles\</emph\> option must also be selected. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	br	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>Automatically creates a numbered list when you press Enter at the end of a line that starts with a number followed by a period, a space, and text. If a line starts with a hyphen (-), a plus sign (+), or an asterisk (*), followed by a space, and text, a bulleted list is created when you press Enter. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151234				0	br	If you type a letter combination that matches a shortcut in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"replacement table\"\>replacement table\</link\>, the combination is replaced with the text that you specified in the \<emph\>AutoFormat\</emph\> dialog when you press F3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152791				0	br	4.5pt double underline				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152885				0	br	6.0pt double underline				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153124				0	br	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>In text documents, you can choose to apply the AutoCorrect errors while you type [T], or only when you modify existing text [M] with \<emph\>Format - AutoFormat - Apply\</emph\>. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	br	This feature does not work if the formatting characters * or _ are entered with an \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#IME\" name=\"Input Method Editor\"\>Input Method Editor\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	br	9.0pt double underline				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153577				0	br	Automatically applies bold formatting to text enclosed by asterisks (*), and underline to text enclosed by underscores ( _ ), for example, *bold*. The asterisks and underscores are not displayed after the formatting is applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153841				0	br	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:PUSHBUTTON:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOFMT_APPLY:PB_EDIT\"\>Modifies the selected AutoCorrect option.\</ahelp\>\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154162				0	br	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>Combines consecutive single-line paragraphs into a single paragraph. This option only works on paragraphs that use the "Default" paragraph style. If a paragraph is longer than the specified length value, the paragraph is combined with the next paragraph. To enter a different length value, select the option, and then click \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05150104.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Edit\</emph\>\</link\>. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154173	27			0	br	Displays the text characters of ordinals, such as 1st, 2nd, or 3rd, as superscripts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
