helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	hd_id8570513				0	br	Extension Scope				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id1439558				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select an installed extension, then click to open the Options dialog for the extension.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id1856440				0	br	Do any of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id4129459				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click to check for online updates of all installed extensions. To check for updates of the selected extensions only, choose the Update command from the context menu. The check for availability of updates starts immediately.\</ahelp\> You will see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/extensionupdate.xhp\"\>Extension Update\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id4139225				0	br	Open a terminal or command shell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id4163945				0	br	Enter the following command, using the path and file name of your extension:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id4856410				0	br	An extension can show a license dialog. \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Read the license. Click the Scroll Down button to scroll down if necessary. Click Accept to continue the installation of the extension.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id5269020				0	br	On a Web page, click a hyperlink to an \<item type=\"literal\"\>*.oxt\</item\> file (if your Web browser can be configured to start the Extension Manager for this file type).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id671712				0	br	Change to the %PRODUCTNAME\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>\\ \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>/\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>program .				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id7654347				0	br	Double-click the \<item type=\"literal\"\>*.oxt\</item\> file in your system's file browser.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id7857905				0	br	You can find a collection of extension on the Web. Click the "Get more extensions here" link in the Extension Manager to open your Web browser and see the \<link href=\"http://extensions.services.openoffice.org/\"\>http://extensions.services.openoffice.org/\</link\> page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id8714255				0	br	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Extension Manager\</item\>, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>My Extensions\</item\> and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Add\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id9143955				0	br	An extension is available as a file with the file extension *.oxt. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_id9581591				0	br	\<item type=\"literal\"\>unopkg add --shared path_filename.oxt\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_idN10543				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/packagemanager.xhp\"\>Extension Manager\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\packagemanager.xhp	0	help	par_idN10553				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"42772\"\>The Extension Manager adds, removes, disables, enables, and exports %PRODUCTNAME extensions.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
