helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3083281				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToFormatted\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into a formatted field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3144761				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToList\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into a list box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToImageBtn\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into an image button.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145581				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToCheckBox\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into a check box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145646				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToPattern\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into a pattern field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3146927				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToImageControl\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into an image control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147304				0	br	The context menu of a control field has the following commands.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToCombo\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into a combo box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ChangeControlType\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Calls a submenu where you can select a control type to replace the control selected in the document.\</ahelp\> As many properties as possible are adopted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3151381				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToFixed\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into a label.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToDate\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into a date field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3152940				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToTime\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into a time field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153140				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToFileControl\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into a file selection.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153223				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToCurrency\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into a currency field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153369				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToRadio\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into an option button.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154217				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToEdit\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into a text box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToNumeric\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into a numerical field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3161646				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToButton\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into a button.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Context Menu of a Control Field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150774				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>formatted fields; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fields; formatted fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; formatted fields\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150774				0	br	Special properties of a formatted field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	br	If the formatted field is connected to the text field of a database, the entries in this field will be treated as text. If the formatted field is connected to a field of the database that can be displayed as a number, the input is treated as numbers. The date and time are also handled internally as numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150976	129			0	br	\<emph\>Min. value\</emph\> and \<emph\>Max. value\</emph\>: You can enter the minimum and maximum numeric value for a formatted field. The min and max values determine the output of existing data (Example: Min. value is 5, the connected database field contains the integer value 3. The output is 5, but the value in the database is not modified) and the input of new data (Example: Max. value is 10 and you enter 20. The input is corrected and 10 is written in the database). If the fields are not filled in for \<emph\>Min. value \</emph\>and \<emph\>Max. value\</emph\>, no limits will be applied. For formatted fields that are connected to a database text field, these two values and the \<emph\>Default value\</emph\> do not apply.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	br	\<emph\>Default value\</emph\>: This value is set for new records as the default value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410	127			0	br	\<emph\>Formatting\</emph\>: You can set the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>property by clicking the \<emph\>... \</emph\>button in the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> line of the \<emph\>Properties: Formatted Field\</emph\> dialog. The \<emph\>Number Format\</emph\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Special properties of a formatted field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150445				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>date fields; properties\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150445				0	br	Special Tips for Date Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149205				0	br	The pre-set limit value will be saved for each document. If you want to open a document in an older version of StarOffice, in which the limit of 1930 could not be changed, then you must also select the limit value 1930 in your current version of $[officename].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154230				0	br	When you enter a year using two digits, the corresponding four digit value is determined by a setting in \<emph\>Tools - Options - $[officename] - General\</emph\>. For example, if 1935 is set as the lower limiting value and you enter 34 as a date value, then the result is 2034 instead of 1934.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Special Tips for Date Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109850				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>table controls; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; properties of table controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table controls;keyboard-only edit mode\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109850				0	br	Special Tips for Table Controls				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	br	Delete Column				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275				0	br	Column				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148539				0	br	Hide Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149827				0	br	Replace with				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150771				0	br	Show columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	br	Insert Column				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153062				0	br	To enter the special keyboard-only edit mode for Table Controls:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153349				0	br	Keyboard-only control of Table Controls				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153561				0	br	All				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156193				0	br	More				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3144510				0	br	The form document must be in \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170500.xhp\" name=\"design mode\"\>design mode\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	br	Press the Escape key to exit the edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149416				0	br	If you use the keyboard only to travel through controls in your document, you will find one difference to the other types of controls: the Tab key does not move the cursor to the next control, but moves to the next column inside the table control. Press Ctrl+Tab to move to the next control, or press Shift+Ctrl+Tab to move to the previous control.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVX_DLG_SHOWGRIDCOLUMNS:1\"\>In the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog you can select the columns to be shown. Hold down the Shift or Ctrl key to select multiple entries.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504	87			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWALLCOLS\"\>Click \<emph\>All \</emph\>if you want to show all columns.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	br	Press Enter to enter the edit mode. The handles are shown farther out from the control border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152372				0	br	The following fields are possible in a table control: text, date, time and currency field, numeric field, pattern field, check box and combo box. In the case of combined data/time fields, two columns are created automatically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	br	Opens the properties dialog of the selected column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_CHANGECOL\"\>Opens a submenu to select a data field to replace the data field selected in the table control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539				0	br	You can define a table control to display the records as you like. In other words you can define data fields for displaying or editing data like in a database form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_INSERTCOL\"\>Calls a submenu to select a data field to adopt it in the table control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	br	If you want to edit columns, press Shift+Space to enter column edit mode. Now you can rearrange the order of columns with Ctrl+Arrow keys. The Delete key deletes the current column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	br	Press Ctrl+F6 to select the document. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938				0	br	In the edit mode, you can open the edit mode context menu by pressing Shift+F10.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552				0	br	Configure the table control using drag and drop: Open the data source browser and drag the desired fields out of the data source browser and on to the column heads of the table control. A pre-configured column is created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155616				0	br	To insert columns into the table control, click in the column heads and bring up the context menu. The following commands are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_DELETECOL\"\>Deletes the currently selected column.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_HIDECOL\"\>Hides the selected column.\</ahelp\> Its properties are not changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159194				0	br	The number of selected lines, if any are selected, is in parentheses after the total number of records.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159269				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWCOLS_MORE\"\>Calls the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159400				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWCOLS\"\>Calls a submenu where you can select the columns to show again.\</ahelp\> To show only one column, click the column name. You see only the first 16 hidden columns. If there are more hidden columns, choose the \<emph\>More\</emph\> command to call the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3161657				0	br	Press Shift+F4 to select the first control. If the Table Control is not the first control, press Tab until it is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Special Tips for Table Controls				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147102				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>controls; properties of form controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>properties; form controls\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147102				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170100.xhp\" name=\"Control Properties\"\>Control Properties\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	br	\<variable id=\"kontroll\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ControlProperties\"\>Opens a dialog for editing the properties of a selected control.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	br	Completes the input in the field and places the cursor into the next field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
