helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155413				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Data\"\>Data\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159121				0	br	Reference value (on)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3161653				0	br	Filter proposal				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3144504				0	br	For list boxes, an SQL statement may have the following form				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145074				0	br	For combo boxes, an SQL statement may take the following form				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145167				0	br	Fourth case: \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"List Boxes\"\>List Boxes\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145257				0	br	The database field "Field1" is linked to the field specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145295				0	br	For list boxes, you can use value lists. Value lists are lists that define reference values. In this way, the control in the form does not directly display the content of a database field, but rather values assigned in the value list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145357				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_EMPTY_IS_NULL\"\>Defines how an empty string input should be handled.\</ahelp\> If this property is set (Yes), a string with only one or more spaces will be interpreted as a NULL value and stored in the database. If this property is not set (No), the string will be treated as an empty value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145641				0	br	\<emph\>References through linked tables (SQL statements)\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3146767				0	br	The 3rd column of the table is linked to the field specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3146892				0	br	<OPTION VALUE="Value">Item				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3146898				0	br	Second case: The control belongs to a subform that is created by an SQL query.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3147341				0	br	If you want a list box to display data from a database table that is linked by a common data field to the table on which the form is based, the link field of the form table is specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3147494				0	br	For combo boxes, the field of the data source table in which the values entered or selected by the user should be stored is specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>. The values displayed in the list of the combo box are based on an SQL statement, which is entered under \<emph\>List content\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3147611				0	br	Reference values are useful if you design a Web form and the information on the status of the control is to be transmitted to a server. If the control is clicked by the user, the corresponding reference value is sent to the server.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3148427				0	br	The property \<emph\>Bound field\</emph\> is only for forms that are used to access more than one table. If the form is based on only one table, the field to be displayed in the form is specified directly under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>. However, if you want the list box to display data from a table that is linked to the current table over a common data field, the linked data field is defined by the property \<emph\>Bound field\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3148475				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_BOUNDCOLUMN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Use an index to specify the table field or table SQL query to link to the field that is provided under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>. Valid values for this property are 1, 2, 3, and so on.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3148537				0	br	SELECT CustomerName, CustomerNo FROM Customers,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3148773				0	br	For forms with database links, the associated database is defined in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170200.xhp\" name=\"Form Properties\"\>Form Properties\</link\>. You will find the functions for this on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"Data\"\>\<emph\>Data\</emph\>\</link\> tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3149021				0	br	If you want a list box to display data from a table that is linked to the current data source table, under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\> specify the field of the data source table to which the content of the list box refers. Or you can specify the database field that controls the display of the data in the form. This data field provides the link to the other table if both tables can be linked through a common data field. It is usually a data field in which unique identification numbers are stored. The data field whose contents are displayed in the form is specified by an SQL statement under \<emph\>List content\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3149328				0	br	\<emph\>Value lists for HTML documents\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	br	The possible settings of the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab page of a control depend on the respective control. You will only see the options that are available for the current control and context. The following fields are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3149570				0	br	For example, if you have two control fields for the options "feminine" and "masculine", and assign a reference value of 1 to the field "feminine" and the value 2 to the "masculine" field, the value 1 is transmitted to the server if a user clicks the "feminine" field and value 2 is sent if the "masculine" field is clicked.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3149949				0	br	2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150225				0	br	\<emph\>Reference values for Web forms\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150260				0	br	\<emph\>Reference values for database forms\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150365				0	br	If you selected "SQL" under \<emph\>Type of list contents\</emph\>, the SQL command determines the index to be specified. Example: If you specify an SQL command such as "SELECT Field1, Field2 FROM tablename" under \<emph\>List content\</emph\>, refer to the following table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150654				0	br	For database forms, you can also characterize the status of an option or a check box by a reference value, storing it in the database. If you have a set of three options, for example "in progress", "completed", and "resubmission", with the respective reference values, "ToDo", "OK", and "RS", these reference values appear in the database if the respective option is clicked.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150666				0	br	Link				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150887				0	br	1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150991				0	br	SELECT DISTINCT field FROM table,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3151012				0	br	An empty string ("ListBox1=")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3151186				0	br	If you work with reference values of a value list, the contents of the data field that you specified under \<emph\>Data Field\</emph\> in the form are not visible, but rather the assigned values. If you chose "Valuelist" on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab under \<emph\>Type of list contents\</emph\> and assigned a reference value to the visible list entries in the form under \<emph\>List entries\</emph\> (entered in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"General\"\>\<emph\>General\</emph\>\</link\> tab), then the reference values are compared with the data content of the given data field. If a reference value corresponds to the content of a data field, the associated list entries are displayed in the form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3151198				0	br	\<emph\>Transmitted data\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3151213	38			0	br	If a list box in the form is to display contents of a table linked to the form table, then define in the \<emph\>Type of list contents\</emph\> field if the display is determined by an SQL command or the (linked) table is accessed. With the \<emph\>Bound field\</emph\> property, you use an index to specify to which data field of the query or of the table the list field is linked. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3151221	89			0	br	\<variable id=\"filtervorschlag\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_FILTERPROPOSAL\"\>While designing your form, you can set the "Filter proposal" property for each text box in the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab of the corresponding \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog. In subsequent searches in the filter mode, you can select from all information contained in these fields.\</ahelp\> The field content can then be selected using the AutoComplete function. Note, however, that this function requires a greater amount of memory space and time, especially when used in large databases and should therefore be used sparingly. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3152539				0	br	\<emph\>JavaScript\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153067				0	br	If the content of the control is read from a database, you can determine the type of the data source with the other options. For example, you can choose between tables and queries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153109				0	br	""				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153224				0	br	You have several possibilities:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153326				0	br	With the "Valuelist" option, all entries entered in the \<emph\>List entries\</emph\> field of the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"General\"\>\<emph\>General\</emph\>\</link\> tab appear in the control. For database forms, you can use reference values (see the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\" References Using Value Lists\"\>\<emph\>References Using Value Lists\</emph\>\</link\> section).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153689				0	br	"Value"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153764				0	br	The data source table does not contain the data to be displayed, but rather a table linked to the data source table through a common data field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153924				0	br	List boxes work with references. They can either be implemented with linked tables by SQL statements (fourth case) or through value lists:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153949				0	br	Third case: \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"Combo Boxes\"\>Combo Boxes\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154134				0	br	If you selected "Table" under \<emph\>Type of list contents\</emph\>, the table structure defines the index to be specified. Example: If a database table is selected under \<emph\>List content\</emph\>, refer to the following table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154206				0	br	{empty}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154260				0	br	The 1st column of the table is linked to the field specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154269				0	br	Not possible				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154273				0	br	Under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>, specify the field of the SQL statement whose contents you want to be displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154344				0	br	Here "field" is a data field from the list table "table" whose content is displayed in the list of the combo box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154419				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_LISTSOURCETYPE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines the data to fill the lists in list and combo boxes.\</ahelp\>Determines the data to fill the lists in list and combo boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154486				0	br	The 2nd column of the table is linked to the field specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154588				0	br	This property for list boxes defines which data field of a linked table is displayed in the form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154596	27			0	br	the visible list entry ("ListBox1=Item")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154604				0	br	ListBox1.options[0].value="Value"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154668				0	br	<OPTION>Item				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154716				0	br	Bound field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154763				0	br	"$$$empty$$$"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154855				0	br	In the data transfer of a selected entry from a list box or a combo box, both the list of the values displayed in the form, which was entered on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"General\"\>\<emph\>General\</emph\>\</link\> tab under \<emph\>List entries\</emph\>, and the value list entered on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab under \<emph\>List content\</emph\>, are taken into consideration: If a (non-empty) text is at the selected position in the value list (<OPTION VALUE=...>), it will be transmitted. Otherwise, the text displayed in the (<OPTION>) control is sent.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154967				0	br	where "CustomerName" is the data field from the linked table "Customers", and "CustomerNo" is the field of the table "Customers" that is linked to a field of the form table "Orders" specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155147				0	br	ListBox1.options[0].value=""				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155174				0	br	The link is created with an SQL Select, which, if you selected "SQL" or "Native SQL", is specified under \<emph\>Type of list contents\</emph\> in the field \<emph\>List content\</emph\>. As an example, a table "Orders" is linked to the current form control, and in the database a table "Customers" is linked to the "Orders" table. You can use an SQL statement as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155266				0	br	Here "table" is the table whose data is displayed in the list of the control (list table). "field1" is the data field that defines the visible entries in the form; its content is displayed in the list box. "field2" is the field of the list table that is linked to the form table (value table) through the field specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\> if \<emph\>Bound field\</emph\> = 1 was selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155306	2			0	br	The\<emph\> Data \</emph\>tab page allows you to assign a data source to the selected control.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155373				0	br	{empty}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155379				0	br	Bound field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	br	Link				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155852	6			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CONTROLSOURCE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the field of the data source table to which the control refers.\</ahelp\>With database forms, you can link controls with the data fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155870				0	br	Examples of SQL statements:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155944				0	br	<OPTION VALUE="">Item				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3156034				0	br	For HTML forms, you can enter a value list under \<emph\>List content\</emph\>. Select the option "Valuelist" under \<emph\>Type of list contents\</emph\>. The values entered here will not be visible in the form, and are used to assign values to the visible entries. The entries made under \<emph\>List content\</emph\> correspond to the HTML tag <OPTION VALUE=...>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3156064				0	br	The database field "Field2" is linked to the field specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3156188				0	br	SELECT field1, field2 FROM table,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3156309				0	br	The following table shows the connections between HTML, JavaScript, and the $[officename] field \<emph\>List content\</emph\> using an example list box named "ListBox1". In this case, "Item" designates a list entry visible in the form:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3156356				0	br	Under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>, specify the field of the data source table whose contents you want to be displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3156448				0	br	1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3158404				0	br	\<emph\>Entry in value list of the control (List content)\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3159110				0	br	First case: There is only one table in the form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3159171				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_LISTSOURCE\"\>With database forms, specifies the data source for the list content of the form-element. This field can be used to define a value list for documents without a database connection.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3159204				0	br	\<emph\>HTML Tag\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3159226				0	br	The value assigned to the list entry ("ListBox1=Value")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3163377				0	br	If the value list is to contain an empty string, enter the value "$$$empty$$$" under \<emph\>List content\</emph\> at the corresponding position (note uppercase/lowercase). $[officename] interprets this input as an empty string and assigns it to the respective list entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3163808				0	br	\<emph\>References Using Value Lists\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3163812	141			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_REFVALUE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can enter a reference value for the web form, which will be remitted to a server when sending the form. With database forms, the value entered is written in the database field, assigned to the control field.\</ahelp\>You can assign a reference value to option buttons and check boxes. The reference value will be remitted to a server when sending the web form. With database forms the value entered here will be written in the database assigned to the control field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3168456				0	br	In the case of database forms, the data source determines the entries of the list or combo box. Depending on the selected type, you have a choice between different data sources under \<emph\>List content\</emph\>, provided that these objects exist in your database. All available database objects of the type selected under \<emph\>Type of list contents\</emph\> are offered here. If you have selected the "Value List" option as the type, you can use references for database forms. If the display of the control is controlled by an SQL command, the SQL statement is entered here.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108B4				0	br	Reference value (off)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108B8				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Check boxes and radio buttons in Spreadsheets can be bound to cells in the current document. If the control is enabled, the value you enter in Reference value (on) is copied to the cell. If the control is disabled, the value from Reference value (off) is copied to the cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AD2				0	br	If you delete the contents of the \<emph\>Bound field\</emph\> cell in the property browser, the first field of the result set is used to display and to exchange data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN10EE3				0	br	Linked cell				2002-02-02 02:02:02
