helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159197				0	br	Mouse button pressed				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145271	23			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_MOUSEPRESSED\"\>The\<emph\> Mouse button pressed \</emph\>event occurs if the mouse button is pressed while the mouse pointer is on the control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_ACTIONPERFORMED\"\>The\<emph\> When initiating \</emph\>event occurs when an action is started.\</ahelp\> For example, if you have a "Submit" button in your form, the send process represents the action to be initiated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975	33			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_MOUSEMOVED\"\>The\<emph\> Mouse moved \</emph\>event occurs if the mouse moves over the control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618	27			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_MOUSEENTERED\"\>The\<emph\> Mouse inside \</emph\>event takes place if the mouse is inside the control field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148755	42			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_CHANGED\"\>The\<emph\> Changed \</emph\>event takes place when the control loses the focus and the content of the control has changed since it lost the focus.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149582	29			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_MOUSEEXITED\"\>The\<emph\> Mouse outside \</emph\>event takes place when the mouse is outside the control field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149732				0	br	Depending on the control, different events are available. Only the available events for the selected control and context are listed on the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab page. The following events are defined:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150495	11			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_TEXTCHANGED\"\>The\<emph\> Text modified \</emph\>event takes place if you enter or modify a text in an input field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150659	25			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_MOUSERELEASED\"\>The\<emph\> Mouse button released \</emph\>event occurs if the mouse button is released while the mouse pointer is on the control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870	9			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_ITEMSTATECHANGED\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The\<emph\> Item status changed \</emph\>event takes place if the status of the control field has changed.\</ahelp\>The\<emph\> Item status changed\</emph\> event takes place if he status of the control field has changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152350	2			0	br	On the\<emph\> Events \</emph\>tab page you can link macros to events that occur in a form's control fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152940	21			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_KEYTYPED\"\>The \<emph\>Key pressed \</emph\>event occurs when the user presses any key while the control has the focus.\</ahelp\> This event may be linked to a macro for checking entries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153717				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_APPROVEACTIONPERFORMED\"\>This event takes place before an action is triggered by clicking the control.\</ahelp\> For example,clicking a "Submit" button initiates a send action; however, the actual "send" process is started only when the \<emph\>When initiating\</emph\> event occurs. The \<emph\>Before commencing\</emph\> event allows you to kill the process. If the linked method sends back FALSE, \<emph\>When initiating\</emph\> will not be executed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154150	44			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_KEYUP\"\>The\<emph\> Key release \</emph\>event occurs when the user releases any key while the control has the focus.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154218	17			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_FOCUSGAINED\"\>The\<emph\> When receiving focus \</emph\>event takes place if a control field receives the focus.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411	31			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_MOUSEDRAGGED\"\>The\<emph\> Mouse moved while key pressed \</emph\>event takes place when the mouse is dragged while a key is pressed at the same time.\</ahelp\> An example is when, during drag-and-drop, an additional key determines the mode (move or copy).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	br	When the event occurs, the linked macro will be called. To assign a macro to an event, press the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button. An \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05060700.xhp\" name=\"Assign Macro\"\>Assign Macro\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>dialog\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3159252	19			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_FOCUSLOST\"\>The\<emph\> When losing focus \</emph\>event takes place if a control field looses the focus.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_idN108BD				0	br	Note that this event is also used for notifying requests for a popup context menu on the control. If you are using this event by a program macro, you find more information in the "StarOffice 8 Programming Guide for BASIC".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Events				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147285				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>forms; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>properties; forms\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147285				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170200.xhp\" name=\"Form Properties\"\>Form Properties\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088	2			0	br	\<variable id=\"form\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormProperties\" visibility=\"visible\"\>In this dialog you can specify, among others,  the data source and the events for the whole form.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Form Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152551				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>submitting forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>get method for form transmissions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>post method for form transmissions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275				0	br	Submission encoding				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149283				0	br	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151100				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170201.xhp\" name=\"General\"\>General\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152425				0	br	URL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152551				0	br	Type of submission				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154751				0	br	Frame				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155419				0	br	Data transfer of control information				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145065				0	br	Using the "Get" method, the data of every control is transmitted as an environment variable. They are appended to the URL in the form "?Control1=Content1&Control2=Content2&..."; the character string is analyzed by a program on the recipient's server.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	br	The values of pattern fields are sent as text fields, that is, the value visible in the form is sent.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3146794				0	br	The date format is sent in a fixed format (MM-DD-YYYY), regardless of the user's local settings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147226				0	br	Specifies the URL to which the data of the completed form is to be transmitted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563				0	br	Date field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	br	Time field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149734				0	br	A decimal separator is always displayed as a period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	br	Using the "Post" method, a document is created from the content of the form that is sent to the specified URL.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	br	Table control				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150789				0	br	Specifies a name for the form. This name is used to identify the form in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigator\"\>Form Navigator\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984				0	br	How this information is transmitted depends on the selected transfer method (Get or Post) and the coding (URL or Multipart). If the Get method and URL encoding are selected, for example, value pairs in the form <Name>=<Value> are sent.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	br	From the table control, the individual columns are always transmitted. The name of the control, the name of the column, and the value of the column are sent. Using the Get method with URL encoding, the transmission is done in the form <Name of the table control>.<Name of the column>=<Value>, for example, with the value being dependent on the column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252				0	br	Which values are transmitted in each case depends on the respective control. For text fields, the visible entries are transmitted; for list boxes, the selected entries are transmitted; for check boxes and option fields, the associated reference values are transmitted if these fields were activated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361				0	br	Pattern field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539				0	br	A form is a text document or spreadsheet with different form controls. If you create a form for a Web page, the user can enter data into it to send over the Internet. The data from the form controls of a form is transmitted to a server by specifying a URL and can be processed on the server.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153562				0	br	Value Pair				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153698				0	br	Control				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153717				0	br	When sending a form, all controls available in $[officename] are taken into consideration. The name of the control and the corresponding value, if available, are transmitted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153779				0	br	The time format is sent in a fixed format (HH:MM:SS), regardless of the user's local settings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153823				0	br	Numeric field, currency field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	br	Defines the target frame in which the loaded URL is to appear.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SUBMIT_METHOD\"\>Specifies the method to transfer the completed form information.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3157909				0	br	In addition to the controls that are recognized in HTML, $[officename] offers other controls. It should be noted that, for fields with a specific numerical format, the visible values are not transmitted but rather fixed default formats. The following table shows how the data of the $[officename]-specific controls is transmitted:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159147				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SUBMIT_ENCODING\"\>Specifies the type for encoding the data transfer.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
