helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149514				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_IMAGEBUTTON_RID_SVXPAGE_HYPERLINK_MAIL_BTN_ADRESSBOOK\"\>Hides or shows the data source browser.\</ahelp\> Drag the receiver's \<emph\>Email\</emph\> data field from the data source browser into the \<emph\>Receiver\</emph\> text field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149955				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXPAGE_HYPERLINK_MAIL_RB_LINKTYP_NEWS\"\>Assigns a news address to the hyperlink.\</ahelp\> Clicking the hyperlink in the document will open a new message document to the news group you entered in the \<emph\>Receiver\</emph\> field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049				0	br	On the \<emph\>Mail & News\</emph\> page in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink dialog\"\>Hyperlink dialog\</link\> you can edit hyperlinks for e-mail or news addresses.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HYPERDLG_MAIL_PATH\"\>Specifies the full URL of the addressee, in the form mailto:name@provider.com or news:group.server.com.\</ahelp\> You can also use drag-and-drop.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_EDIT_RID_SVXPAGE_HYPERLINK_MAIL_ED_SUBJECT\"\>Specifies the subject that is inserted in the subject line of the new message document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
