helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\10100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152895				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/10100000.xhp\" name=\"Close\"\>Close\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\10100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147143				0	br	If additional views of the current document were opened by \<emph\>Window - New Window\</emph\>, this command will close only the current view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\10100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153910				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01050000.xhp\" name=\"Close the current document\"\>Close the current document\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\10100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155934				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CloseWin\"\>Closes the current window.\</ahelp\> Choose \<emph\>Window - Close\</emph\>, or press Ctrl+F4. In the page preview of $[officename] Writer and Calc, you can close the current window by clicking the \<emph\>Close Preview\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\10100000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Close				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147588				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12000000.xhp\" name=\"Explorer On/Off\"\>Explorer On/Off\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id273445				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the selected database file for editing.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144740				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DSBrowserExplorer\"\>Turns on and off the view of the data source explorer.\</ahelp\> The \<emph\>Explorer On/Off \</emph\>icon is visible on the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0212.xhp\" name=\"Database Bar\"\>Table Data bar\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136				0	br	Explorer On/Off				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	br	In the data source explorer you see the data sources registered in $[officename] with their links, queries and tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151379				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>To rename an entry, call this command and enter the new name.. You can also do this by selecting the entry and pressing F2. The database must support renaming, otherwise this command is not enabled.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153114				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3150710\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dsbrowserexplorer.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150710\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Closes the connection to the data source. See \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Base - Connections\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	br	\<emph\>Establishing a connection\</emph\> - As soon as you select an individual table or query, a connection to the data source is established. Once the connection is opened, the name of the data source, the Queries or Tables entry, and the name of the query or table selected is shown in bold type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id5943479				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialog to add/edit/remove a database file from the list of registered databases. The same dialog opens by choosing \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Explorer On/Off				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152594				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12010000.xhp\" name=\"Sort Ascending\"\>Sort Ascending\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504	5			0	br	\<variable id=\"dialogsortieren\"\>To sort more than one data field, choose \<emph\>Data - Sort\</emph\>, then choose the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100100.xhp\" name=\"Sort Criteria\"\>Sort Criteria\</link\> tab, where you can combine several sort criteria.\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150693	2			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sorts the data of the selected field in ascending order. \</ahelp\> Text fields are sorted alphabetically (A-Z), numerical fields in ascending order (0-9).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154380	4			0	br	\<variable id=\"selektionsortieren\"\>Data of the currently selected field are always sorted. A field is always selected as soon as you place the cursor in the field. To sort within tables, you can also click the corresponding column header.\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3147276\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sortascending.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147276\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159158				0	br	Sort Ascending				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Sort Ascending				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154689				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12020000.xhp\" name=\"Sort Descending\"\>Sort Descending\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144436				0	br	Sort Descending				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149496				0	br	\<image src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sortdescending.png\" id=\"img_id3153255\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153255\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149987	2			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SortDown\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sorts the data of the selected field in descending order.\</ahelp\> Text fields are sorted alphabetically (Z-A), number fields in numerically descending order (9-0).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Sort Descending				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149495				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12030000.xhp\" name=\"AutoFilter\"\>AutoFilter\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	7			0	br	To filter with several field names simultaneously, click the \<emph\>Default Filter \</emph\>icon. The \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12090000.xhp\" name=\"Default Filter dialog\"\>Default Filter\</link\> dialog appears, in which you can combine several filter criteria.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147043				0	br	AutoFilter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148983				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AutoFilter\"\>Filters the records based on the content of the currently selected data field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151234				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3147261\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formfiltered.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147261\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153577				0	br	You can remove the current AutoFilter with the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12040000.xhp\" name=\"Remove Filter/Sorting\"\>Remove Filter/Sorting\</link\> icon or with \<emph\>Data - Filter - Remove Filter\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155355				0	br	Place the cursor in a field name whose content you want to filter and then click the \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> icon. Only those records with content identical to the selected field name are visible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159234				0	br	For example, to view all the customers from New York, click a field name with the entry "New York". AutoFilter then filters all customers from New York from the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	AutoFilter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155069				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12040000.xhp\" name=\"Remove Filter/Sorting\"\>Remove Filter/Sorting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146130				0	br	\<image src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_removefilter.png\" id=\"img_id3151315\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151315\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	br	Remove Filter/Sorting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154094				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RemoveFilterSort\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Cancels the filter settings and displays all of the records in the current table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12040000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Remove Filter/Sorting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154926				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12050000.xhp\" name=\"Refresh\"\>Refresh\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090				0	br	Refresh				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	4			0	br	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Refresh \</emph\>icon to open a submenu with the following commands:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	br	\<emph\>Rebuild\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\"HID_BROWSER_REFRESH_REBUILDVIEW\"\>Rebuilds the view of the database table. Use this command when you have changed the structure of the table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147261				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3153910\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_reload.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153910\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156183				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Refresh\"\>Refreshes the displayed data.\</ahelp\> In a multi-user environment, refreshing the data ensures that it remains current.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	br	\<emph\>Refresh\</emph\> - Displays the refreshed contents of the database table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Refresh				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147000				0	br	Insert Database Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143284				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SbaBrwInsert\"\>\<variable id=\"datenintext\"\>Inserts all fields of the marked record into the current document at the cursor position.\</variable\>\</ahelp\> The icon is only visible if the current document is a text document or a spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	5			0	br	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>In the data source browser, select the records that you want to insert into the document and then click the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> icon, or drag-and-drop data from the data source browser into the document. This opens the \<emph\>Insert Database Columns \</emph\>dialog. Select whether the data should be inserted as a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070100.xhp\" name=\"table\"\>table\</link\>, as \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070200.xhp\" name=\"fields\"\>fields\</link\> or as \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070300.xhp\" name=\"text\"\>text\</link\>.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031	6			0	br	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>The preferences you set in the\<emph\> Insert Database Columns \</emph\>dialog are saved and will be active the next time the dialog is called. This save process is independent of the database and can record the preferences for a maximum of 5 databases.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	br	Data to Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153577	4			0	br	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>In the data source browser, select the record that you want to insert into the document and then click the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> icon. The record is inserted in the document at the cursor position, with the contents of each individual field of the record copied to a table column. You can also select multiple records and transfer them into the document by clicking the \<emph\>Data to Text \</emph\>icon. Each individual record is then written to a new row.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154186				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3147291\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sbabrwinsert.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147291\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156326				0	br	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>If data is inserted into the document as a table, the table properties are not saved along with the data in the document. If you select the \<emph\>AutoFormat\</emph\> function for formatting the table, $[officename] will note the name of the format template. This template will then be used automatically if you insert data as a table again, unless the preferences have been changed.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
