helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153061				0	br	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12040201.xhp\" name=\"More>>\"\>More>>\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155555				0	br	Filter criteria				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147834				0	br	You can define a filter by indicating the type of line, the name of the field, a logical condition and a value or a combination of arguments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_LISTBOX_DLG_FILTERCRIT_LB_WHERECOND3\"\>For the following arguments, you can choose between the logical operators AND / OR.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_LISTBOX_DLG_FILTERCRIT_LB_WHEREFIELD3\"\>Specifies the field names from the current table to set them in the argument.\</ahelp\> You will see the column identifiers if no text is available for the field names.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149716				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DataFilterStandardFilter\"\>Specifies the logical conditions to filter your table data.\</ahelp\> This dialog is called \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> in Spreadsheet documents and \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> in database tables or database forms. The \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> dialog does not contain the \<emph\>More\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149795				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_EDIT_DLG_FILTERCRIT_ET_WHEREVALUE3\"\>Specifies a value to filter the field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150254				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_LISTBOX_DLG_FILTERCRIT_LB_WHERECOMP3\"\>Specifies the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12090101.xhp\" name=\"comparative operators\"\>comparative operators\</link\> through which the entries in the \<emph\>Field name\</emph\> and \<emph\>Value\</emph\> fields can be linked.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150976	14			0	br	The\<emph\> Value \</emph\>list box contains all possible values for the specified \<emph\>Field name\</emph\> . Choose the value to be used in the filter. You can also choose the \<emph\>- empty -\</emph\> or \<emph\>-not empty -\</emph\> entries..				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897	16			0	br	The \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> dialog does not contain the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156118	15			0	br	If you use the filter function in database tables or forms, then type the value in the \<emph\>Value \</emph\>text box to be used for filtering.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_idN105EE				0	br	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/guide/filters.xhp#filters\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Filter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148983				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>comparison operators in default filter dialog\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>operators; default filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>default filters; comparison operators\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filters; comparison operators\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148983				0	br	Comparison Operators				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	br	Less than (<)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145313	3			0	br	\<emph\>Comparative operator\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	br	Shows values equal to the condition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146807				0	br	Greater than (>)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147089	4			0	br	\<emph\>Effect\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	br	Equal (=)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148944				0	br	Shows the values not equal to the condition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149202				0	br	Smallest %				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669				0	br	Largest				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400				0	br	Largest %				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	br	Smallest				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151176				0	br	Shows the smallest N% (numeric value as parameter) of the entire values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153761				0	br	Shows values less than the condition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153823				0	br	Greater than or equal to (> =)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154143				0	br	Shows values that are greater than or equal to the condition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154381				0	br	Shows values that are less than or equal to the condition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154811				0	br	Not equal (< >)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154852				0	br	Shows values greater than the condition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155342				0	br	Less than or equal to (< =)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155364				0	br	The following comparative operators can be set under \<emph\>Condition\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Default Filter\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
