helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_FORMATTER\"\>Specifies that all field formats are considered when searching in the current document.\</ahelp\> Field formats are all visible formats that are created using the following possibilities:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317				0	br	entire field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147588				0	br	\<variable id=\"suchentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RecSearch\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Searches database tables and forms.\</ahelp\>In forms or database tables, you can search through data fields, list boxes, and check boxes for specific values. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148451				0	br	beginning of field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148481				0	br	In this case, standard formatting is formatting that refers to the internally stored data. It is not always visible to the user, especially if it is used for simulating data types (for example, time fields in dBase databases). This depends on the database used and the individual data type. Searching with field formatting is appropriate if you only want to find what is actually shown. This includes fields of type Date, Time, Date/Time and Number/Double.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148539				0	br	Your search terms will be saved as long as the table or the formula document is open. If you are running more than one search and you would like to repeat the search term, you can select a previously used search term from the combo box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148590				0	br	off				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148673				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_POSITION\"\>Specifies the relationship of the search term and the field contents.\</ahelp\> The following options are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148803				0	br	*				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148874				0	br	for exactly one arbitrary character				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	br	The search function is also available for table controls. When calling the search function from a table control, you can search each column of the table control corresponding to the database columns of the linked database table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	br	Specifies the fields for the search.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149209				0	br	Search with regular expressions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_WILDCARD\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Allows a search with a * or ? wildcard.\</ahelp\> You can use the following wildcards:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149355				0	br	When searching a table, the data fields of the current table are searched. When searching in a form, the data fields of the table linked with the form are searched.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149401				0	br	The following examples show possible issues when searching without field formatting. These issues depend on the database used and only occur for certain internal default formatting:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	br	You have a date field, which is saved in "DD.MM.YY" format in the database (for example, 17.02.65). The format of the entry is changed in the data source view to "DD. MMM YYYY" (17 Feb 1965). Following this example, a record containing February 17 is only found when the \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> option is on:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	br	in table design mode for field properties,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150298				0	br	Meaning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150365				0	br	"?loppy" returns "Floppy"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150384				0	br	.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150428				0	br	.*				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150488				0	br	in data source view on column formatting,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150593				0	br	Apply field format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150982				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_REGULAR\"\>Searches with regular expressions.\</ahelp\> The same regular expressions that are supported here are also supported in the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\" name=\"Find & Replace dialog\"\>Find & Replace dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150995	119			0	br	If you use \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> when searching in list boxes, you find the text displayed in list boxes. If you do not use \<emph\>Apply field format,\</emph\> you will find the contents corresponding to the standard field format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151045				0	br	?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	br	Note that the fields of the current logical form do not have to be identical to the fields of the form document. If the form document contains fields that point to multiple data sources (that is, multiple logical forms), the \<emph\>All Fields\</emph\> option will only search for the fields linked to data sources in the form document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151183				0	br	If several tables or forms are open, you can set different search options for each document. When you close the documents only the search options of the document last closed are saved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151249				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_BACKWARD\"\>Specifies that the search process will run in reverse direction, from the last to the first record.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151280				0	br	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151321				0	br	It is recommended that you always search using field formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	br	Form documents may contain multiple logical forms. These are individual form components, which are each linked to a table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152886				0	br	If the \<emph\>Wildcard expression\</emph\> check box is marked, this function is not available.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152941				0	br	in forms on control properties.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152971				0	br	Search Results				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153355				0	br	If you are searching check boxes with \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\>, you will receive a "1" for marked check boxes, a "0" for unmarked check boxes, and an empty string for undefined (tristate) check boxes. If the search has been carried out without \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\>, you will see language-dependent default values "TRUE" or "FALSE".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SINGLEFIELD\"\>Searches through a specified data field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	br	The search described here is carried out by \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>. If you want to use the SQL server to search in a database, then you should use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12110000.xhp\" name=\"Form-based Filters\"\>Form-based Filters\</link\> icon on the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Form Bar\"\>Form Bar\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418				0	br	"2" is returned, but not "Feb".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	br	Specifies the type of search.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153543				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SEARCHFORNULL\"\>Specifies that fields will be found that contain no data.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153705				0	br	Search with wildcard expression				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	br	Returns all fields containing the search pattern at the end of the field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153793				0	br	*				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153836				0	br	"5" returns "14:00:00" as a time				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_ALLFIELDS\"\>Searches through all fields.\</ahelp\> If you are running a search in a table, all fields in the table will be searched. If you are running a search in a form, all fields of the logical form (entered under \<emph\>Form\</emph\>) will be searched. If you are running a search in a table control field, all columns that are linked to a valid database table field will be searched.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	br	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154127				0	br	Returns all fields containing the search pattern as an exact match to the contents of the field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154273				0	br	Cause				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_BTN_SEARCH\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Starts or cancels the search.\</ahelp\> If the search is successfully completed, the corresponding field in the table is highlighted. You can continue the search by clicking the \<emph\>Search\</emph\> button again. You can cancel a search process by clicking the \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154477				0	br	The \<emph\>State\</emph\> line shows the records returned by the search. If the search reaches the end (or the beginning) of a table, the search is automatically continued at the other end.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507	31			0	br	However, searching without \<emph\>Apply field format \</emph\>is appropriate for larger databases with no formatting issues, because it is faster.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154718				0	br	Searching with regular expressions offers more options than searching with wildcard expressions. If you search with regular expressions, the following characters correspond to those used in searches with wildcards:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SEARCHFORTEXT\"\>Enter the search term in the box or select it from the list.\</ahelp\> The text under the cursor is already copied into the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> combo box. Note that while running a search in a form, tabs and line breaks cannot be processed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	br	end of field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429				0	br	Returns all fields containing the search pattern at the beginning of the field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155434	107			0	br	The\<emph\> Form \</emph\>combo box is only visible if the current document is a form document with more than one logical form. It does not appear during a search in tables or queries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155518				0	br	The view shown does not match what is stored internally. For example, if value 45.789 is stored in the database as a field of type Number/Double and the shown formatting is set to display only two decimals, "45.79" is only returned in searches with field formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155582				0	br	"M*er" returns all entries starting with an "M" and ending in "er" (for example, Miller, Moller, Mather)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764				0	br	"45.79" does not return "45.79" although the \<emph\>entire field\</emph\> option is selected under \<emph\>Position\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155850				0	br	"Feb" is returned, but not "2".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156138				0	br	for 0 or more arbitrary characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156166				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_BTN_CLOSE\"\>Closes the dialog. The settings of the last search will be saved until you quit \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	br	anywhere in the field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156316				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_STARTOVER\"\>Restarts the search. A forward search restarts with the first record. A backwards search restarts with the last record.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156332				0	br	Time fields are not defined for dBase databases and must be simulated. To internally display the time "14:00:00", a 5 is necessary.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156736				0	br	If the \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> box is marked, the data source view of the table or form is searched using the formatting set there. If the box is not marked, the database is searched using the formatting saved in the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3157965				0	br	"00:00:00" returns all records of a standard date field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158408				0	br	Defines settings to control the search.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158411				0	br	?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159176				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_LB_FORM\"\>Specifies the logical form in which you want the search to take place.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_CASE\"\>Specifies that upper and lower case are taken into consideration during the search.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3163720				0	br	In very large databases, finding the record in reverse search order can take some time. In this case, the status bar informs you that the records are still being counted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	br	"M?ller" returns, for example, Miller and Moller				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Find Record				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147000				0	br	\<variable id=\"formfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12110000.xhp\" name=\"Form-based Filters\"\>Form-based Filters\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149751				0	br	Form-based Filters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152918				0	br	Unlike the normal search, which is activated by the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100200.xhp\" name=\"Find Record\"\>Find Record\</link\> icon on the \<emph\>Form\</emph\> Bar, you can search more quickly by using the form-based filter. Usually a quick database server is charged with the search. Also, you can enter more complex search conditions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3147226\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formfilter.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147226\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154230				0	br	\<variable id=\"formfiltertext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilter\"\>Prompts the database server to filter the visible data by specified criteria.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12110000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Form-based Filters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149748				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12120000.xhp\" name=\"Apply Filter\"\>Apply Filter\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090				0	br	Apply Filter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147226	4			0	br	The\<emph\> Apply Filter \</emph\>function retains \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12110000.xhp\" name=\"form-based filters\"\>form-based filters\</link\> that have been set. You do not need to redefine them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149495				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFiltered\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Switches between the filtered and unfiltered view of the table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149999				0	br	\<image src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formfiltered.png\" id=\"img_id3146130\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3146130\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12120000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Apply Filter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
