helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id296334				0	br	In the \<emph\>Name of the Adabas D database \</emph\>box, enter the name of the server, a colon, and the name of the database on the server, for example, computername:database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145298	73			0	br	switches the database to COLD.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145761	70			0	br	Close any other open tasks that show the database contents. On multi-user systems, ensure that all users are disconnected from the database, and then restart $[officename].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146135	84			0	br	On the server, start the x_server program in \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>adabas\\bin \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Adabas\\bin\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147004	62			0	br	The following is a list of possible error messages and solutions for working with the Adabas D database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147045				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Database\</emph\> to open the Database Wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147252	76			0	br	xutil -d <DBNAME> -u <CONTROLUSER>,<CONTROLPASSWORD> restart				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147361	72			0	br	strt -d <DBNAME> -NoDBWindow -NoDBService				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	br	Click \<emph\>Connect to an existing database\</emph\>, and then select "Adabas" in the listbox (scroll up in the listbox).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148479	79			0	br	completely shuts down the database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149210	83			0	br	Under Windows, start the xtcpupd.exe support program on both the client and the server, and ensure that "Remote SQL via TCP/IP" is selected in the xtcpupd.exe dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149337	92			0	br	You can only create a new database on the server.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149378				0	br	Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/30100000.xhp\" name=\"Create New Adabas Database\"\>\<emph\>Create New Adabas Database\</emph\>\</link\> dialog to create an Adabas database:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150499	2			0	br	The Adabas D database that you may have installed together with $[officename] is a limited version of the database. For more information on Adabas, visit the Software AG Web site at http://www.softwareag.com/adabas/.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150787	87			0	br	Restart $[officename], and then change the database properties.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151111				0	br	The Adabas database that you may have installed together with $[officename] is restricted to a size of 100 MB, and a maximum of three users on a network. See the "License.txt" file in the Adabas directory for more details. The Adabas database must be installed in a separate directory from $[officename].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153197	66			0	br	This error occurs if you try to access an Adabas D database more than one time.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153254				0	br	Under Windows, the Adabas setup application adds the DBROOT environment variable that contains the path information for the database. If the setup application finds this variable, it does not install the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153268	64			0	br	This error occurs if you try to access an Adabas D database that has not been started. Ensure that you have defined a Control User for the database, and then start the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153927	45			0	br	Determine which directories are referred to by the system variables DBCONFIG and DBWORK. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>Under Windows these variables are defined in the system settings or in the c:\\Autoexec.bat file. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\> Under Unix these variables are defined in a start script. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154200	81			0	br	To run Adabas on a network, you need to install the Adabas server on one machine and the client on the workstations that you want to access the database from.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154663	77			0	br	switches the database to WARM.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	br	The name of an Adabas file cannot exceed 8 characters. The path to the Adabas file, including the file name, cannot exceed 30 characters, and must be compliant with the 7-bit ASCII code. Both the path and the file name cannot contain spaces.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154965	75			0	br	switches the database to COLD.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155141	104			0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Database\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155508	105			0	br	Fill in the remaining pages of the Database Wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	br	Follow the remaining pages of the Database Wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155608	78			0	br	stp -d <DBNAME> -NoDBService				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155961	74			0	br	xutil -d <DBNAME> -u <CONTROLUSER>,<CONTROLPASSWORD> shutdown				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156374	46			0	br	In the $DBCONFIG$\\Config directory, delete the file that has the same name as the database, for example, " C:\\Adabas\\Sql\\Config\\Big".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156712	47			0	br	In the $DBWORKS$\\Wrk directory, delete the directory that has the same name as the database., for example "C:\\Adabas\\Sql\\Wrk\\Big".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3157869				0	br	To delete the reference to an Adabas database, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</emph\>. Select the database, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159264	94			0	br	In the $DBCONFIG$ directory, delete the three files that have the same name as the database, but with different extensions. For example, for a database named "Big", delete the "Big.sys", "Big.trs", and "Big.dat" files in the "C:\\Adabas\\".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428	88			0	br	Click \<emph\>Connect to an existing database\</emph\>, and select "Adabas D" in the listbox. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3479720				0	br	If you are using OpenOffice.org software, the Adabas D software package can be downloaded and installed separately (see www.adabas.com).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id842310				0	br	Adabas D by Software AG is installed when you install the commercial office software by Sun Microsystems, Inc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
