helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159176				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/30100000.xhp\" name=\"Create New Adabas Database\"\>Create New Adabas Database\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145607				0	br	Drives containing parts of the Serverdb are called DEVSPACEs. To improve performance, store each DEVSPACE on separate drives.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_SYSUSR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the name of the database administrator.\</ahelp\> The administrator name and password is assigned when you create an Adabas database. Apart from the administrator, two more users can access the Adabas database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146985				0	br	The file path for a DEVSPACE, including its file name, cannot exceed 40 characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_TRANSACTIONLOG_SIZE\"\>Enter the size of the transaction file in megabytes.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	br	If the DATADEVSPACE reaches full capacity during a database operation, Adabas shuts down, increases the capacity of the DATADEVSPACE (up to 100 MB), and restarts the database. Saved data is not lost.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148674				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_DOMAINPWD\"\>Enter a password.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149064				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_SYSDEVSPACE\"\>Enter the path for the system DEVSPACE.\</ahelp\> The SYSDEVSPACE manages the configuration data for the database. The size of the SYSDEVSPACE depends on the size of the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149294				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_CONUSR\"\>Enter the name of a user that you want to give limited control to modify some parameters of the database. Normally, the default settings for the name and the password of the control user are not changed.\</ahelp\> The control user does not affect the three-user limitation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149378	31			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_CACHE_SIZE\"\>Enter the size of the data cache in megabytes. \</ahelp\> The data buffer can be simultaneously accessed by all users and stores the most recently accessed pages from the DATADEVSPACEs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	br	The maximum size for a DATADEVSPACE in the limited version Adabas database is 100MB.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150115				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_DATADEVSPACE_SIZE\"\>Enter the size of the database in megabytes here. The maximum size is 100 MB.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152597				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_DATADEVSPACE\"\>Enter the path for the data DEVSPACE.\</ahelp\> This file stores user data, such as tables and indexes, as well as the SQL catalog (schema info). The data contained in one user table is evenly distributed across all DATADEVSPACEs. The combined size of all DATADEVSPACEs corresponds to the size of the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153091				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_PBDATADEVSPACE\"\>Locate the directory where you want to save the file, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153362				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_USR\"\>Enter the name of the domain user that is used by Adabas internally. Normally, the default settings for the name and password of the domain user are not changed.\</ahelp\> The domain user does not affect the three-user limit.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154190				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_TRANSACTIONLOG\"\>Enter the path for the transaction log file.\</ahelp\> This file records all modifications that are made to the database during a transaction, and overwrites them when the transaction is completed. The TRANSACTIONLOG is also used for the rollback of a transaction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154515				0	br	Creates a new \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/30000000.xhp\" name=\"Adabas database\"\>Adabas database\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3158432				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_DBNAME\"\>Type the name of the database.\</ahelp\> The name is added to the \<emph\>Data source URL\</emph\> field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Create New Adabas Database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvprop.xhp	0	help	par_id3998840				0	br	In a database window, choose \<emph\>Edit - Database - Properties\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Advanced Properties\</emph\> tab				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvprop.xhp	0	help	par_idN10550				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabaadvprop.xhp\"\>Advanced Properties\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvprop.xhp	0	help	par_idN10560				0	br	Specifies advanced properties for the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvprop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Advanced Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	hd_id1101718				0	br	Form data input checks for required fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	hd_id3534958				0	br	End text lines with CR + LF				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id3783989				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>When you enter a new record or update an existing record in a form, and you leave a field empty which is bound to a database column which requires input, then you will see a message complaining about the empty field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id3837397				0	br	The control box is available for all data source types which support write access to their data. The control box does not exist for spreadsheets, text, csv, and the various read-only address books.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id4572283				0	br	The availability of the following controls depends on the type of database:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id6151921				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select to use the CR + LF code pair to end every text line (preferred for DOS and Windows operating systems).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id6684163				0	br	If this control box is not enabled, then the forms in the current database will not be checked for required fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id7679372				0	br	In a database window, choose \<emph\>Edit - Database - Advanced Settings\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10556				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabaadvpropdat.xhp\"\>Special Settings\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10566				0	br	Specifies the way you can work with data in a database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10590				0	br	Use SQL92 naming constraints				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10594				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Only allows characters that conform to the SQL92 naming convention in a name in a data source. All other characters are rejected. Each name must begin with a lowercase letter, an uppercase letter, or an underscore ( _ ). The remaining characters can be ASCII letters, numbers, and underscores.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN1059E				0	br	Append the table alias name in SELECT statements				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A2				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Appends the alias to the table name in SELECT statements.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A5				0	br	Use Outer Join syntax '{OJ }'				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A9				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Use escape sequences for outer joins. The syntax for this escape sequence is {oj outer-join}\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105BE				0	br	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	br	select Article.* from {oj item LEFT OUTER JOIN orders ON item.no=orders.ANR}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C4				0	br	Ignore the privileges from the database driver				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C8				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Ignores access privileges that are provided by the database driver.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CB				0	br	Replace named parameters with ?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CF				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Replaces named parameters in a data source with a question mark (?).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D2				0	br	Display version columns (when available)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D6				0	br	Some databases assign version numbers to fields to track changes to records. The version number of a field is incremented by one each time the contents of the field are changed. \<ahelp hid=\"HID_DSADMIN_SUPPRESS_VERSIONCL\"\>Displays the internal version number of the record in the database table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FA				0	br	Use the catalog name in SELECT statements				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FE				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Uses the current data source of the catalog. This option is useful when the ODBC data source is a database server. Do not select this option if the ODBC data source is a dBase driver.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10613				0	br	Use the schema name in SELECT statements				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Allows you to use the schema name in SELECT statements.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	br	Create index with ASC or DESC statement				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Creates an index with ASC or DESC statements.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10621				0	br	Comparison of Boolean values				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10625				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select the type of Boolean comparison that you want to use.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
