helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN10563				0	br	Specifies the options for automatically generated values for new data records.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN1058C				0	br	Retrieve generated values				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN10590				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enables $[officename] support for auto-incremented data fields in the current ODBC or JDBC data source. Select this option if the auto-increment feature in the SDBCX layer of the database is not supported. In general, the auto-increment is selected for the primary key field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN10593				0	br	Auto-increment statement				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN10597				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the SQL command specifier that instructs the data source to auto-increment a specified Integer data field.\</ahelp\> For example, the following MySQL statement used the AUTO_INCREMENT statement to increase the "id" field each time the statement creates a data field:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A0				0	br	CREATE TABLE "table1" ("id" INTEGER AUTO_INCREMENT)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN105AA				0	br	Query of generated values				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN105B1				0	br	SELECT LAST_INSERT_D();				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN10634				0	br	For this example, you must enter AUTO_INCREMENT into the \<emph\>Auto-increment statemen\</emph\>t box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter an SQL statement that returns the last auto-incremented value for the primary key data field.\</ahelp\> For example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
