helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id1180455				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the level of detail by which a group is kept together on the same page.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id1371501				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to open a list from which you can select a field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id2091433				0	br	When you specify to keep together some records on the same page, you have three choices:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id2188787				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the sorting order.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id2855616				0	br	For fields of type AutoNumber, Currency, or Number, you specify an interval.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3068636				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>In the Sorting and Grouping dialog of \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Builder\</link\>, you can define the fields that should be sorted in your report, and the fields that should be kept together to form a group.\</ahelp\> If you group your report by a certain field, all records with the same value of that field will be kept together in one group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3405560				0	br	By default a new group is created on every changed value of a record from the selected field. You can change this property depending on the type of field:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3409527				0	br	For fields of type Text, you can select Prefix Characters and enter a number n of characters in the text box below. The records which are identical in the first n characters will be grouped together.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3729361				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select to create a new group on each changed value, or on other properties.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3939634				0	br	The sorting and grouping will be applied in the order of the list from top to bottom.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id4661702				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves the selected field up in the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id5092318				0	br	No - page boundaries are not taken into account.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id5833307				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select to show or hide the Group Header.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id599688				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Lists the fields that will be used for sorting or grouping. The field at the top has the highest priority, the second field has the second priority, and so on.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id7112338				0	br	For fields of type Date/Time, you can group the records by the same year, quarter, month, week, day, hour, or minute. You can additionally specify an interval for weeks and hours: 2 weeks groups data in biweekly groups, 12 hours groups data in half-day groups.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id7700430				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the group interval value that records are grouped by.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id7726676				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select to show or hide the Group Footer.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id7868892				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves the selected field down in the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id876186				0	br	The Groups box shows the fields in an order from top to bottom. You can select any field, then click the Move Up or Move Down button to move this field up or down in the list. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id9089022				0	br	With First Detail - prints the group header on a page only if the first detail record also can be printed on the same page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id9312417				0	br	Whole Group - prints the group header, detail section, and group footer on the same page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
