helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] assistive technology\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>assistive technology in $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen readers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	br	Requirements to use assistive tools in $[officename]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	br	\<variable id=\"assistive\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/assistive.xhp\" name=\"Assistive Tools in $[officename]\"\>Assistive Tools in $[officename]\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149795				0	br	Supported Assistive Tools				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153061				0	br	Supported Input Devices				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	br	$[officename] supports some assistive technology tools like screen magnification software, screen readers, and on-screen keyboards. Most of these tools communicate with $[officename] by means of the Java(TM) Access Bridge software, that uses the Java Accessibility API, a part of the Java runtime environment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	br	Most recent version of the software for your assistive tool				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	br	Java Runtime Environment (JRE) version 1.4.1_01 and higher, or version 1.4.0_02 with the locale set to "en_us".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474				0	br	GNOME On Screen Keyboard (GOK), using GNOME at-spi and Java Accessibility API software				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3148617				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01013000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - $[officename] - Accessibility\"\>Tools - Options - $[officename] - Accessibility\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149045				0	br	Screen magnification software allow users with low vision to work in $[officename] with caret and focus tracking.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	15			0	br	On Windows systems, \<link href=\"http://www.sun.com/access/downloads/\" name=\"Java Access Bridge\"\>Java Access Bridge\</link\> software version 1.0.3 or higher 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	br	On UNIX(R) systems, the GNOME 2 desktop environment with the Java Access Bridge software for GNOME				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149808				0	br	When accessibility support in $[officename] is enabled, the Java Runtime Environment is loaded, and increases the startup time for $[officename].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	br	On-screen keyboards enable users to perform almost all data input and commands with a mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010800.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - $[officename] - View\"\>Tools - Options - $[officename] - View\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	br	Screen readers allow visually impaired users to access $[officename] with text-to-speech and Braille displays.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	br	On Windows systems, $[officename] directly supports most on-screen keyboard software. Additional support for assistive tools is provided by the Java Access Bridge software. The following is a list of some assistive tools that use the Java Access Bridge software to exchange data with $[officename]:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155430				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01012000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - $[officename] - Appearance\"\>Tools - Options - $[officename] - Appearance\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	br	Gnopernicus Screen Reader and Magnifier, using GNOME Assistive Technology Service Provider Interface (at-spi) and Java Accessibility API software				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024				0	br	$[officename] provides the ability to use alternative input devices for access to all functions of $[officename].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156329				0	br	ZoomText Screen Magnifier (version 7.11 or higher)(Windows)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
