helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153394				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; copying between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; draw objects between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;draw objects from other documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145609				0	br	Inserting into a spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147573				0	br	Inserting into a text document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153394				0	br	\<variable id=\"copy_drawfunctions\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/copy_drawfunctions.xhp\" name=\"Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\"\>Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	br	Select the drawing object or objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149234				0	br	Insert the drawing object, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	br	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current paragraph. You can change the anchor by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>OLE-Object\</emph\> toolbar or the \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> toolbar. This opens a popup menu where you can select the anchor type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210	30			0	br	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current cell. You can change the anchor between cell and page by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149456\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleanchortype.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149456\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	br	Switch to the other document and place the cursor where the drawing object is to be inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	28			0	br	In $[officename] it is possible to copy drawing objects between text, spreadsheets and presentation documents. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	br	Copy the drawing object to the clipboard, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154186				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>tables; inserting spreadsheet cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; cell ranges from spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;cell ranges from spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations;inserting spreadsheet cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents;inserting spreadsheet cells\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154186				0	br	\<variable id=\"copytable2application\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/copytable2application.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Data From Spreadsheets\"\>Inserting Data From Spreadsheets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	br	To copy a cell range into a text document, select the cell range in the sheet and then use either the clipboard or drag-and-drop to insert the cells into the text document. You will then find an OLE object in the text document, which you can edit further.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	br	If you drag cells to the normal view of a presentation document, the cells will be inserted there as an OLE object. If you drag cells into the outline view, each cell will form a line of the outline view. If you just drag the cells you will move the cells. The cells will only be copied if you press the Shift key when dragging.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	br	Use the clipboard to copy the contents of a single cell. You can also copy a formula from a cell into the clipboard (for example, from the input line of the formula bar) so that the formula can be inserted into a text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3148538				0	br	When you copy a cell range from $[officename] Calc to the clipboard, the drawing objects, OLE objects and charts within this range are also copied. They are also copied when you start a drag-and-drop action. However, the objects will be inserted only if you drop them within the same document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	br	If you insert a cell range with an enclosed chart, the chart will keep its link to the source cell range only if you copied the chart and the source cell range together.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Inserting Data From Spreadsheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152924				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>sending; AutoAbstract function in presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoAbstract function for sending text to presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>outlines; sending to presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; copying by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; copying and pasting text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;data from text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;data from text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;data from text documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152924				0	br	\<variable id=\"copytext2application\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/copytext2application.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Data From Text Documents\"\>Inserting Data From Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156024				0	br	Copying Text Using Drag-and-Drop				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3145316				0	br	If you want to transfer each heading together with its accompanying paragraphs, select the \<emph\>File - Send - AutoAbstract to Presentation\</emph\> command. You must have formatted the headings with a corresponding Paragraph Style to be able to see this command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303				0	br	If you select text and drag it into a spreadsheet with drag-and-drop, it will be inserted as text into the cell where you release the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	br	If you copy text to the clipboard, you can paste it with or without text attributes. Use the shortcut keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C to copy and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V to paste.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3149655				0	br	If you drag text to the normal view of a presentation, an OLE object is inserted as a $[officename] plug-in.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	br	If you drag the text to the outline view of a presentation, it will be inserted at the cursor location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3143270\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_paste.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3143270\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155				0	br	If a text document contains headings formatted with the Heading Paragraph Style, choose \<emph\>File - Send - Outline to Presentation\</emph\>. A new presentation document is created, which contains the headings as an outline.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	br	You can insert text into other document types, such as spreadsheets and presentations. Note that there is a difference between whether the text is inserted into a text frame, a spreadsheet cell, or into the outline view of a presentation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	br	To select the format in which the clipboard contents will be pasted, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Paste\</emph\> icon on the Standard bar, or choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>, then select the proper format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Inserting Data From Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153662				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>CTL;complex text layout languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>languages;complex text layout\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text;CTL languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text layout;special languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>right-to-left text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entering text from right to left\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bi-directional writing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Hindi;entering text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Hebrew;entering text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Arabic;entering text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Thai;entering text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153662				0	br	\<variable id=\"ctl\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/ctl.xhp\" name=\"Languages Using Complex Text Layout\"\>Languages Using Complex Text Layout\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	br	You can change the text writing direction directly be pressing one of the following keys:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Language Settings - Languages\"\>Tools - Options - Language Settings - Languages\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	br	Currently, $[officename] supports Hindi, Thai, Hebrew, and Arabic as \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#ctl\" name=\"CTL languages\"\>CTL languages\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	br	In $[officename] Writer text formatted in \<emph\>Thai language\</emph\> has the following features:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149047				0	br	Ctrl+Shift+A or Ctrl+Left Shift Key - switch to left-to-right text entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	br	The modifier-only key combinations only work when CTL support is enabled.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149809				0	br	Use the Right or Left Arrow key to jump to the next or previous whole composite character. To position the cursor into a composite character, use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	br	In multicolumn pages, sections or frames that are formatted with text flow from right to left, the first column is the right column and the last column is the left column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3153770				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01150300.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Language Settings - Complex Text Layout\"\>Tools - Options - Language Settings - Complex Text Layout\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	br	Ctrl+Shift+D or Ctrl+Right Shift Key - switch to right-to-left text entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3154909				0	br	Use the Delete key to delete a whole composite character. Use the Backspace key to delete the last part of the previous composite character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3155420				0	br	If you select the text flow from right to left, embedded Western text still runs from left to right. The cursor responds to the arrow keys in that Right Arrow moves it "to the text end" and Left Arrow "to the text start".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	br	In paragraphs with justified alignment, the characters are stretched to flush the lines at the margins. In other languages the spaces between words are stretched.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Languages Using Complex Text Layout				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152823				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>data sources; registering address books\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>address books; registering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>system address book registration\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>registering; address books\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149096				0	br	Address Data Source Wizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	br	Registering An Existing Address Book Manually				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228				0	br	\<variable id=\"data_addressbook\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_addressbook.xhp\" name=\"Registering an Address Book\"\>Registering an Address Book\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	br	To call the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Address Data Source\"\>Address Data Source\</link\> wizard, choose \<emph\>File - Wizards - Address Data Source\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084				0	br	Under \<emph\>Field assignment\</emph\>, match the fields for first name, company, department, and so on to the actual field names used in your address book.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	br	In order for the replacement to take place, you must tell \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> which address book you use. The wizard asking for this information appears automatically the first time you activate, for example, a business letter template. You can also call the wizard by following the steps listed below.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	br	In the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> combo box, select the system address book or the data source you want to use as an address book.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	br	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> templates and wizards use fields for the contents of the address book. When activated, the general fields in the templates are automatically replaced with the fields from the data source of your address book.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669	11			0	br	If you have not yet registered the system address book in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> as the data source, click the \<emph\>Administrate\</emph\> button. This takes you to the \<emph\>Address Book Data Source Wizard\</emph\>, in which you can register your address book as a new data source in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149983				0	br	Now your data source is registered in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> as the address book. If you now open a template from the \<emph\>Business Correspondence\</emph\> category, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> can automatically insert the correct fields for a form letter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Address Book Source\</emph\>. The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110101.xhp\" name=\"Templates: Address Book Assignment\"\>\<emph\>Templates: Address Book Assignment\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	br	In the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> combo box, select the database table you want to use as the address book.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3154927				0	br	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> you can register different data sources. The contents of the data fields are then available to you for use in various fields and controls. Your system address book is such a data source.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id5941648				0	br	The address book data is read-only in %PRODUCTNAME Base. It is not possible to add, edit, or delete address data from within Base.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_idN10784				0	br	When finished, close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Registering an Address Book				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157896				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>databases; text formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats; databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; tables in text format\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; spreadsheets to text format\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145313				0	br	Importing Data into $[officename]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150400				0	br	Exporting in CSV Text Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154824				0	br	\<variable id=\"data_dbase2office\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_dbase2office.xhp\" name=\"Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format\"\>Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id1977904				0	br	Select "Text CSV" from the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> combo box. Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	br	Export the desired data from the source database in a text format. The CSV text format is recommended. This format separates data fields by using delimiters such as commas or semi-colons, and separates records by inserting line breaks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	br	If you want to exchange data with a database that does not have an ODBC link and does not allow dBase import and export, you can use a common text format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	br	To exchange data in a text format use the $[officename] Calc import/export filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	br	Save the current $[officename] Calc spreadsheet in dBase format in the folder of a dBase database. To do this, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>, then select the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> "dBase" and the folder of the dBase database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	br	The \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Text Import\"\>\<emph\>Text Import\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears. Decide which data to include from the text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986				0	br	Once the data is in a $[officename] Calc spreadsheet, you can edit it as needed. Save the data as a $[officename] data source:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>\<emph\>Open\</emph\>\</link\> and click the file to import.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140				0	br	You can export the current $[officename] spreadsheet in a text format which can be read by many other applications.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154216				0	br	In \<emph\>File type\</emph\> select the filter "Text CSV". Enter a file name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	br	This opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"dBase Export\"\>\<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, in which you can select the character set, field delimiter and text delimiter. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. A warning informs you that only the active sheet was saved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152801				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>SQL; executing SQL commands\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>queries;creating in SQL view\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>commands;SQL\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>executing;SQL commands\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	br	\<variable id=\"data_enter_sql\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_enter_sql.xhp\" name=\"Executing SQL Commands\"\>Executing SQL Commands\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	hd_id9577929				0	br	To execute an SQL statement directly				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	br	In the \<emph\>Query\</emph\> window, choose \<emph\>View - Switch Design View On/Off\</emph\>. Edit the SQL command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786	92			0	br	Select an existing query from the list and click the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156212\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dbqueryedit.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156212\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	br	With the help of SQL commands you can control the database directly, and can also create and edit tables and queries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3149298	98			0	br	Click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> or \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3153159\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_save.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153159\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to save the query.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3151176	91			0	br	Click the \<emph\>Create Query in SQL View\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154071\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dbnewquerysql.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154071\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> or				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3152460	96			0	br	Click the \<emph\>Run\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3152886\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sbanativesql.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152886\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The result of the query is displayed in the upper window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3153223				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Design\"\>Query Design\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3153562				0	br	Not all database types support all SQL instructions. If necessary, find out which SQL commands are supported by your database system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id7923825				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> to open a database file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id9448530				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - SQL\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Executing SQL Commands				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	bm_id5762199				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>opening;forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>design view;creating forms\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F9				0	br	\<variable id=\"data_forms\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_forms.xhp\"\>Working with Forms\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	br	Using forms, you can define how to present the data. Open a text document or a spreadsheet and insert the controls such as push buttons and list boxes. In the properties dialogs of the controls, you can define what data the forms should display.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	br	Creating a New Form With the Form Wizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	br	In %PRODUCTNAME, you can create a new form using the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01090000.xhp\"\>Form Wizard\</link\>:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	br	Open the database file where you want to create the new form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10636				0	br	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Forms\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063E				0	br	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Form\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	br	Creating a New Form Manually				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064C				0	br	Open the database file where you want to create the new form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	br	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Forms\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10658				0	br	Click \<emph\>Create Form in Design View\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	br	A new text document opens. Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\"\>Form Controls\</link\> to insert form controls.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10670				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Forms\</emph\> icon to access all forms that were created from within the current database window. In addition, you can use the \<emph\>Form Controls\</emph\> icons to add database form controls to any Writer or Calc document, but these documents will not be listed in the database window. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Working with Forms				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	bm_id6911546				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>databases;importing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing;databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;exporting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting;databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; datasource records in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; datasource records in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;inserting database records\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data sources;copying records to spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting;from data sources to %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;from data sources to %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id3912778				0	br	Exporting data from Base				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id4547257				0	br	\<variable id=\"data_im_export\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_im_export.xhp\"\>Importing and Exporting Data in Base\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id9999694				0	br	Importing data to Base				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id1175572				0	br	In the Base window, choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id121158				0	br	Open the database file that contains the database table to be exported. Click Tables to view the tables, or click Queries to view the queries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id130619				0	br	Now you can save or export the data to many file types.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	br	In the Base window, right-click the name of the table to export. Choose \<emph\>Copy\</emph\> from the context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	br	Open a Base file of the database type that you want. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id2584002				0	br	On Windows systems, you can also use drag-and-drop instead of Copy and Paste. Also, for registered databases, you can open the datasource browser (press F4) instead of opening the Base window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id2761314				0	br	An easy method to import and export database tables uses Calc as a "helper application".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	br	You copy a table from Base to a new Calc sheet, then you can save or export the data to any file format that Calc supports.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id325632				0	br	For example, to ensure the first column has a text format, you must make sure that the first field of the first valid data row contains text. If a field in the first valid data row contains a number, the whole column is set to number format, and only numbers, no text, will be shown in that column. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3619495				0	br	In the Base window, click \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> to view the tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3791924				0	br	Select the data to be copied to Base. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3806878				0	br	Click cell A1 in the new Calc window, then choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id4644306				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Spreadsheet\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id4815820				0	br	You see the Copy Table dialog. Most databases need a primary key, so you may want to check the \<emph\>Create primary key\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id533768				0	br	If you copy a dBase sheet, include the top row that contains the header data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id5669423				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Copy\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id5871761				0	br	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id6173894				0	br	You can enter a range reference like A1:X500 in the Name Box if you don't want to scroll.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id6531266				0	br	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp#database_main\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	br	Either create a new Base file using the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabawiz00.xhp\"\>Database Wizard\</link\>, or open any existing Base file that is not read-only.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id8494521				0	br	You can import text files, spreadsheet files, and your system address book in read-only mode only. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id9579760				0	br	When you import from a text or spreadsheet file, the file must have a first row of header information. The second row of the file is the first valid data row. The format of every field in the second row determines the format for the entire column. Any format information from a spreadsheet file gets lost when importing to Base.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	br	Open the Calc file that contains the data to be imported to Base. You can open a *.dbf dBase file or many other file types. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Importing and Exporting Data in Base 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_new.xhp	0	help	bm_id6911526				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>creating;databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>new databases\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_new.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	br	\<variable id=\"data_new\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_new.xhp\"\>Creating a New Database\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_new.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C4				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Database\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_new.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CB				0	br	This opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabawiz00.xhp\"\>Database Wizard\</link\>, where you create a new database file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_new.xhp	0	help	par_idN105DD				0	br	In the Database Wizard, select the type of database, and select the option to open the Table Wizard as the next wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_new.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E0				0	br	The \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/tablewizard00.xhp\"\>Table Wizard\</link\> helps you to add a table to the new database file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_new.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FC				0	br	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_new.xhp	0	help	par_idN10604				0	br	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp#database_main\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
