helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3153311\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_recsearch.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153311\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3149178	65			0	br	In spreadsheets and documents in which form controls are used, you can click the \<emph\>Find Record\</emph\> icon on the form bar to open a dialog to find any text and values. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	br	You can search in one or in all data fields. You can select whether the text must be at the beginning, end or any location of the data field. You also can use the ? and * wildcards, as in the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialog. You can find additional information about the database search function in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100200.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Help\"\>$[officename] Help\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Searching Tables and Form Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	bm_id8772545				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>searching; form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>removing;form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering; data in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data;filtering in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms; filtering data\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156042				0	br	\<variable id=\"data_search2\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_search2.xhp\" name=\"Searching With a Form Filter\"\>Searching With a Form Filter\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterExit\"\>If you click on the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button on the \<emph\>Form Filter\</emph\> toolbar, the form is displayed without a filter.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3146898	12			0	br	The filter that has been set can be removed by clicking \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12040000.xhp\" name=\"Remove Filter/Sort\"\>\<emph\>Remove Filter/Sort\</emph\>\</link\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3151318\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_removefiltersort.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151318\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672	6			0	br	On the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> toolbar, click the \<emph\>Form-Based Filters\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149807\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formfilter.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149807\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The current document is displayed with its form controls as an empty edit mask. The \<emph\>Form Filter \</emph\>toolbar appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	br	Open a form document that contains database fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481	8			0	br	More information about wildcards and operators can be found in \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Design\"\>Query Design\</link\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	br	Enter the filter conditions into one or several fields. Note that if you enter filter conditions into several fields, all of the entered conditions must match (Boolean AND).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150114	11			0	br	Click the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12120000.xhp\" name=\"Apply Filter\"\>\<emph\>Apply Filter\</emph\>\</link\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3144764\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_datafilterstandardfilter.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3144764\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> toolbar to change to the filtered view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984	19			0	br	On the \<emph\>Form Object\</emph\> toolbar, click the \<emph\>Design Mode On/Off\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3147618\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_switchcontroldesignmode.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147618\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to turn off the design mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3152462				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterExecute\"\>If you click the \<emph\>Apply Form-Based Filter\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Form Filter\</emph\> toolbar, the filter will be applied.\</ahelp\> You see the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> toolbar and can browse through the found records.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	br	As an example, open an empty text document and press F4. Open the bibliography database table \<emph\>biblio\</emph\> in the data source view. While pressing Shift+Ctrl, drag a few column headers into the document so that the form fields are created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
