helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798				0	br	In the Design view, you can now create the fields for your table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	br	Enter properties for each selected data field. Depending on the database type, some input facilities may not be available.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	br	You can enter an optional \<emph\>Description\</emph\> for each field. The text of the description will appear as a tip on the column headings in the table view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	br	In the next cell to the right, define the \<emph\>Field Type\</emph\>. When you click in the cell, you can select a field type in the combo box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	br	In the \<emph\>Entry required\</emph\> box, specify whether or not the field may remain empty.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3153349				0	br	Enter new fields in rows from top to bottom. Click the \<emph\>Field Name\</emph\> cell and enter a field name for each data field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154288				0	br	Open the database file of the database where you want a new table. Click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon. Choose \<emph\>Create Table in Design View\</emph\> to create a new table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	br	Each field can only accept data corresponding to the specified field type. For example, it is not possible to enter text in a number field. Memo fields in dBase III format are references to internally-managed text files which can hold up to 64KB text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	br	For the \<emph\>Length\</emph\> box, a combo box may be shown that provides the available choices.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	br	This section contains information about how to create a new database table in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05010000.xhp\" name=\"design view\"\>design view\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Table Design				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	bm_id1983703				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>database tables;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table views of databases\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F9				0	br	\<variable id=\"data_tables\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tables.xhp\"\>Working with Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	br	Data is stored in tables. As an example, your system address book that you use for your e-mail addresses is a table of the address book database. Each address is a data record, presented as a row in that table. The data records consist of data fields, for example the first and the last name fields and the e-mail field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	br	Creating a New Table With the Table Wizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	br	In %PRODUCTNAME you can create a new table using the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/tablewizard00.xhp\"\>Table Wizard\</link\>:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	br	Open the database file where you want to create the new table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10636				0	br	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063E				0	br	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	br	Creating a New Table With the Design View				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064C				0	br	Open the database file where you want to create the new table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	br	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10658				0	br	Click \<emph\>Create Table in Design View\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	br	You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tabledefine.xhp\"\>Table Design\</link\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067B				0	br	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10683				0	br	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp#database_main\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10778				0	br	Creating a New Table View				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077C				0	br	Some database types support table views. A table view is a query that is stored with the database. For most database operations, a view can be used as you would use a table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10782				0	br	Open the database file where you want to create the new table view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10786				0	br	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078E				0	br	Click \<emph\>Create Table View\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10795				0	br	You see the View Design window, which is almost the same as the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\"\>Query Design window\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Working with Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	bm_id2339854				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>opening;database files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing; databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data sources;viewing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;viewing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A6				0	br	\<variable id=\"data_view\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_view.xhp\"\>Viewing a Database\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C4				0	br	There are two different methods of viewing a database in %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CA				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> to open the database file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D1				0	br	The \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabadoc.xhp\"\>database file\</link\> gives you full access to tables, queries, reports, and forms. You can edit the structure of your tables and change the contents of the data records.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E3				0	br	Choose \<emph\>View - Data source\</emph\> to view the registered databases.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105EA				0	br	The \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp\"\>data source view\</link\> can be used to drag-and-drop table fields from registered databases into your documents and to produce mail merges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
