helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287				0	br	Click the \<emph\>New\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3145172\" src=\"sfx2/res/sn064.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145172\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the Standard bar or choose \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>. This opens a document of the document type specified.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3148616				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"File - Open\"\>File - Open\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	br	Select the file you want to open and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	br	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	br	The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>Open\</link\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985				0	br	To restrict the display of files in the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> dialog to a certain type select the corresponding \<emph\>File type\</emph\> from the list. Select \<emph\>All Files (*.*)\</emph\> to display all files.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092				0	br	If you click the arrow next to the \<emph\>New\</emph\> icon, a submenu opens in which you can select another document type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126	9			0	br	You can also enter a URL in the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> dialog. This must start with the fully extended form with file:/// or ftp:// or http://.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3422650				0	br	Press Shift+F5 to set the cursor to the last saved position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id5509201				0	br	In general, all documents open with the cursor at the start of the document. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id6594744				0	br	One exception appears when the author of a Writer text document saves and reopens a document: the cursor will be at the same position where it has been when the document was saved. This only works when the author has entered his name in \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME - User Data\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A9				0	br	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AF				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> icon				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	br	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+O\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C4				0	br	When you open a file by an URL from the Windows file dialog, Windows will open a local copy of the file, located in the Internet Explorer cache. The %PRODUCTNAME file dialog opens the remote file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
