helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id2439039				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialog where you can add, edit, and remove icons.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\>, and click on the \<emph\>Toolbars\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	br	Click \<emph\>Add Commands\</emph\> , select the new command, then click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3152922	90			0	br	If you want, you can rearrange the \<emph\>Commands \</emph\>list by selecting a command name and clicking \<emph\>Move Up\</emph\> and \<emph\>Move Down\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3154071	88			0	br	In the\<emph\> Toolbars \</emph\>box, select the toolbar you want to change.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	br	Click the arrow icon at the end of a toolbar and choose \<emph\>Visible Buttons\</emph\> and then select the button you want to display.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Adding Buttons to Toolbars 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153345				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>documents; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sending; documents as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>e-mail attachments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text;sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>attachments in e-mails\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	br	\<variable id=\"email\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/email.xhp\" name=\"Sending Documents as E-mail\"\>Sending Documents as E-mail\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Send - Document as E-mail\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986				0	br	In your e-mail program, enter the recipient, subject and any text you want to add, then send the e-mail.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	br	$[officename] opens your default e-mail program.\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\> If you want to send the current document with another e-mail program, you can select the program to use with \<emph\>Tools - Options - Internet - E-mail\</emph\>. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	br	Working in $[officename], you can send the current document as an e-mail attachment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Sending Documents as E-mail				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150616				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>Error Report Tool\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reporting errors\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>crash reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>activating;Error Report Tool\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148538				0	br	Starting the Error Report Tool				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150616				0	br	\<variable id=\"error_report\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/error_report.xhp\" name=\"Error Report Tool\"\>Error Report Tool\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	br	What Data is Sent?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154046				0	br	Completing the Report				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159399				0	br	Sending the Error Report				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	br	The Error Report Tool gathers all necessary information that can help the program developers to improve the code, so that in later versions this error can possibly be avoided. Please help us to improve the software and send the generated error report.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	br	On the main Error Report Tool dialog, you can enter some additional information that may help the developers to localize the error. For example, if the error only appears after a change in your hardware or software environment, or if you clicked on a button, please include that information.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	br	You will not get an answer to your error report. If you need support, please visit the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0108.xhp\"\>support forum\</link\> on the Internet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	br	With most program crashes the Error Report Tool will start automatically. However, if the program seems to be stuck and the tool does not start automatically, you can start the tool manually:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504				0	br	The Error Report Tool uses the HTTP PUT / SOAP protocol to send the report data. You may optionally enter some descriptive text that will help us to identify the context of the program crash. Then click the \<emph\>Send\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177				0	br	In addition, relevant memory contents and stack traces are gathered by some system standard tools ("dbhhelp.dll" on Windows systems, "pstack" on UNIX systems). This information will be sent also.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	br	The Error Report Tool starts automatically when a program crash occurs. If the program enters into an endless loop, so that it does not respond to mouse-clicks or keypresses, you can also start the Error Report Tool manually.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	br	You may choose to respond to questions that the developers may have about the reported error. Mark the check box if you allow to be contacted by e-mail, should additional information be required. By default this box is not marked, so you will not get any e-mail.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681	3			0	br	Sun Microsystems is committed to respecting your online privacy and recognizes your need for appropriate protection and management of any personally identifiable information you share with us. See the statement at http://www.sun.com/privacy/ on your online data privacy at Sun Microsystems.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	br	The error report consists of several files. The main file contains information about the error type, operating system name and version, memory usage, and the description that you entered. You can click the \<emph\>Show Report\</emph\> button on the main dialog of the Error Report Tool to view what will get sent in the main file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460	6			0	br	Go to the {office_install_path}\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>\\ \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>/\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>program folder and start the crashrep\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>.exe \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\> file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Error Report Tool				2002-02-02 02:02:02
