helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	br	\<variable id=\"floating_toolbar\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/floating_toolbar.xhp\" name=\"Using Toolbars\"\>Using Toolbars\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id4224372				0	br	To Close a Toolbar Temporarily				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id733970				0	br	Context of Toolbars				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id1510055				0	br	Depending on your system's window manager settings, you may also double-click an empty place on the toolbar or window, while holding down the Ctrl key. Or double-click the title bar of the floating toolbar or window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id295724				0	br	Click the icon in the toolbar's title bar, or choose \<emph\>Close Toolbar\</emph\> from the context menu. The toolbar will be shown automatically again when the context becomes active again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	br	Some toolbar icons, for example the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon, can open another toolbar. Click the arrow next to the icon to open a toolbar containing further icons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155450	8			0	br	You now have a choice: either click the icon that you want to activate, or seize the toolbar by its title bar and drag it while holding down the mouse button. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id341196				0	br	Some toolbars open automatically depending on the context. For example, when you click inside a table in a text document, the Table toolbar opens. When you click inside a numbered paragraph, the Bullets and Numbering toolbar opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id6154362				0	br	To reattach a floating window, drag-and-drop the window's title bar to an edge of the document window. The mouse pointer should be very close to the document window's edge when you release the mouse button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id7296975				0	br	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Reset\</emph\> to reset the toolbars to their default context sensitive behavior. Now some toolbars will be shown automatically, dependent on the context.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id9776909				0	br	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars\</emph\> and click the name of a toolbar to remove the check mark. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E9				0	br	To Make a Toolbar a Floating Toolbar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EF				0	br	Click the handle at the start of the toolbar, and drag the toolbar into the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F2				0	br	To Reattach a Floating Toolbar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F7				0	br	Drag the title bar of the toolbar to an edge of the document window. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>Alternatively, double-click a gray empty place without icons on the toolbar, while holding down the Ctrl key. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077E				0	br	To Show a Closed Toolbar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN10785				0	br	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars\</emph\> and click the name of the toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AC				0	br	Docking toolbars and windows by drag-and-drop depends on your system's window manager settings. You must enable your system to show the full window contents when you move a window, instead of showing just the outer frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Using Toolbars				2002-02-02 02:02:02
