helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id1983092				0	br	If you leave the hyperlink by entering a space character directly following the last character, the AutoCorrect - if enabled - will change the target URL to be the same as the visible text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id2690511				0	br	If you leave the hyperlink by positioning the cursor somewhere else, only the visible text will be changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	br	Option 2: Open \<link href=\"text/shared/main0209.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink Bar\"\>Hyperlink Bar\</link\> (\<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>). Click on the hyperlink, do not release the mouse button and drag the hyperlink to the Hyperlink Bar. Edit the URL on the Hyperlink Bar and press the Return key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	br	Open the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	br	Option 1: As described above, open \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink Dialog\"\>Hyperlink Dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3152361				0	br	If the hyperlink is a button, click on the border to select it, or press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while clicking. Open the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog through the context menu. You can edit the label text under "Caption," and modify the address in the "URL" field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410	12			0	br	Option 1: Click on the hyperlink. Then click the \<emph\>Hyperlink \</emph\>icon on the Standard bar. This works only in text documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id333262				0	br	In all document types, you can open the Hyperlink dialog to edit a hyperlink. First set the cursor into the hyperlink or directly in front of the hyperlink, then click the Hyperlink icon on the Standard bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id4124881				0	br	When you Ctrl-click a hyperlink in a Writer document, your web browser opens with the requested web address. If you don't use a mouse, position the cursor inside the hyperlink and open the context menu by Shift+F10, then choose Open Hyperlink.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN10826				0	br	Click the Character Styles icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082C				0	br	Right-click the "Internet Link" or "Visited Internet Link" character style, and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	br	In the dialog, select the new attributes, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
