helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150940				0	br	The upper left handle starts blinking. Press Ctrl+Tab several times, until no handle blinks. This signals that now the anchor of the object is activated. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>In text documents you can press Shift+Ctrl+A to activate the anchor directly. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151000				0	br	Ctrl+Left Arrow or Ctrl+Right Arrow: jump to the previous or to the next split				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	br	If a toolbar is longer than can be displayed on screen, it shows an icon at the right or lower edge. Select the toolbar and press PageUp or PageDown to display the remaining icons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	br	Press Alt or F6 or F10 to select the first menu (the \<emph\>File\</emph\> menu). With right arrow, the next menu to the right is selected; with left arrow, the previous menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151180				0	br	Alt+Up arrow or Alt+Down arrow: moves the border between table view and selection area up or down.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
