helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159201				0	br	You can control \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> without using a mouse device, using only the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159203				0	br	Ctrl+Shift+Left Arrow or Ctrl+Shift+Right Arrow: move a split one position to the left or to the right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159624				0	br	Enter: when a table is selected, the Enter key enters the first data field from the list box into the selection area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3163668				0	br	Shift+Arrow keys: moves the current dividing line a small step in the arrow direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3163808				0	br	Select the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3166442				0	br	Up Arrow or Down Arrow: scroll table down or up one row				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3166450				0	br	Use the Alt and arrow keys to move the selected object by one pixel.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Shortcuts (%PRODUCTNAME Accessibility)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150774				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>labels; creating and synchronizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>business cards; creating and synchronizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>synchronizing;labels and business cards\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147654				0	br	Designing Labels and Business Cards				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150774				0	br	\<variable id=\"labels\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/labels.xhp\" name=\"Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards\"\>Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	br	Designing Business Cards Through a Dialog				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	br	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab, under \<emph\>Inscription\</emph\>, you can choose what you want written on the labels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610				0	br	This often involves database fields, so that the labels can be printed with varying content, when sending "Form Letters" for example. It is also possible to have the same text printed on every label.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	br	$[officename] Writer contains many formats of commercially available sheets for labels, badges, and business cards. You can also add other, user-defined formats.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798	70			0	br	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010300.xhp\" name=\"File - New - Business Cards\"\>\<emph\>File - New - Business Cards\</emph\>\</link\> to open the\<emph\> Business Cards \</emph\>dialog, which allows you to choose how your business cards will look.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3147560				0	br	On the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> tab you can define your own label formats, not covered by the predefined formats. To do this, select "User" from the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list box. On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, you can specify whether all labels or only certain ones are to be created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	br	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab, under \<emph\>Format\</emph\>, define the label format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3149767				0	br	Click on \<emph\>New Document\</emph\> to create a new document with the settings you have entered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3150358				0	br	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab page, make sure that the \<emph\>Synchronize contents\</emph\> box is selected. If this is selected, a label only has to be entered (on the top left label) and edited once.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010300.xhp\" name=\"Business Cards\"\>Business Cards\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	85			0	br	Use the \<emph\>Database \</emph\>and \<emph\>Table \</emph\>list boxes to select the database and table from which the data fields are obtained. Click on the arrow button to transfer the selected data field into the inscription area. Press Enter to insert a line break. You can also enter spaces and any other fixed text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	br	You can design both labels and business cards through the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	br	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010200.xhp\" name=\"File - New - Labels\"\>\<emph\>File - New - Labels\</emph\>\</link\> to open the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	br	As soon as you click on \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>, you will see a small window with the \<emph\>Synchronize Labels\</emph\> button. Enter the first label. When you click on the \<emph\>Synchronize Labels\</emph\> button, the current individual label is copied to all the other labels on the sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>creating;address labels from databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>address labels from databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>labels; from databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>stickers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating labels\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	br	\<variable id=\"labels_database\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/labels_database.xhp\" name=\"Printing Address Labels\"\>Printing Address Labels\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443	43			0	br	You can now synchronize the labels. Click on the \<emph\>Synchronize\</emph\>\<emph\>Labels\</emph\> button in the small window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972	45			0	br	On the Table Data bar, click the \<emph\>Data to Fields\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3148484				0	br	You can then save and/or print the label document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	br	When you see the label document, open the data source view by choosing \<emph\>View - Data Sources\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084	37			0	br	Select the format of the label sheets you want to print on. Remember to mark \<emph\>Synchronize contents\</emph\> on the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3150447	41			0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>, and go to the \<emph\>Database\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3151382	40			0	br	Place the cursor at the last text position (after the last field) in the first label.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596	42			0	br	Select the type \<emph\>Next record\</emph\>, click on \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> and then on \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3153524	39			0	br	Drag the data fields needed for the Address individually into the top left label. For example, click on the column header NAME and, keeping the mouse button depressed, drag it into the label. This inserts a field. Put the fields in order to complete the address in the first label at top left.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Labels\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3154791	44			0	br	In the data source view, select the records for which you would like address stickers, by clicking on the row headers to the left. Use the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl\</item\> key in the usual way to select several records at the same time.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413	58			0	br	In the data source view, select your address data source table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_idN10687				0	br	Click \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
