helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id121158				0	br	Select another UI language in the "User interface" listbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id130619				0	br	If the listbox doesn't list the language that you want, see "Adding More UI Languages".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	br	Open your Web browser and enter \<link href=\"http://oootranslation.services.openoffice.org/pub/OpenOffice.org/\"\>http://oootranslation.services.openoffice.org/pub/OpenOffice.org/\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id2761314				0	br	A standard installation of OOo will give you a user interface (UI) of your chosen language. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id2897427				0	br	Click the big button in the middle of the document page. This starts a macro to display more info and download the dictionary files.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\>. Go to \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Languages\"\>\<emph\>Language Settings - Languages\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3145367				0	br	Open the context menu and select \<emph\>Edit Paragraph Style\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3145649				0	br	Open the Styles and Formatting window and click on the \<emph\>Character Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3146792				0	br	Click on the name of the character style to which you want to apply a different language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3148455				0	br	Select the text to which you want to apply a language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	br	Under \<emph\>Default languages for documents\</emph\>, select the document language for all newly created documents. If you mark \<emph\>For the current document only\</emph\>, your choice will only apply to the current document. Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150040				0	br	The language you select for your document determines the dictionary used for spellcheck, thesaurus and hyphenation, the decimal and thousands delimiter used and the default currency format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150043				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Language Settings - Languages\"\>Tools - Options - Language Settings - Languages\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150321				0	br	Select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150753				0	br	Then open the context menu in the Styles and Formatting window and select \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Character Style\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150872				0	br	Place the cursor in the paragraph whose paragraph style you want to edit.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3152483				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Format - Character - Font\"\>Format - Character - Font\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578				0	br	Within the document, you can apply a separate language to any paragraph style. This has priority over the language of the whole document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3152886				0	br	You can assign a language to selected pieces of text in a paragraph, either by direct formatting or with a character style. This assignment has priority over the paragraph style and document language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3153093				0	br	The language you select applies to the whole document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154164				0	br	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc, choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> and proceed accordingly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	br	Select the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154756				0	br	Select the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942				0	br	All paragraphs formatted with the current paragraph style will have the selected language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	br	Select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3155766				0	br	Now you can apply the character style to your selected text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	br	Select the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3159348				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Character\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	br	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Options - Language Settings - Languages\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413				0	br	Select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3791924				0	br	Install the language pack. Either double-click the exe file, or unpack the tar.gz file according to standard practice on your platform.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3806878				0	br	Click OK and restart the OOo software.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3906979				0	br	Select to install the new files for the current user only or for all users (which requires write permission to the shared folder).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3912778				0	br	Most users download the American English version, which gives you English menu commands and English Online Help. If you want another language for the menus (and for Online Help, if available in that language), change the UI language as follows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3998535				0	br	Click Next.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id4401684				0	br	Select the languages for Spelling and click Next.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id5174108				0	br	The document contains pages in many different languages. Click your own language on the first page to see the following instructions in your own language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id6273995				0	br	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Retrieve the list\</item\> button. After some short delay, you see a list of available Spelling dictionaries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id7082430				0	br	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Retrieve the list\</item\> and select languages for Hyphenation and for Thesaurus.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id7718741				0	br	The macro downloads the files to the appropriate folder. After you click Finish, you must close OOo (including the Quickstarter), and restart OOo.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	br	Select and download the correct language pack for your version of OOo.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id7919248				0	br	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Wizards - Install new dictionaries\</item\> to open a Writer document which helps you to install more languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	br	Close OOo (also close the Quickstarter, if you enabled it).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Selecting the Document Language				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143206				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>arrows; drawing in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indicator lines in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines; drawing in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines; removing automatic lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting; lines in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawing lines in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic lines/borders in text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143206				0	br	\<variable id=\"line_intext\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/line_intext.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Lines in Text\"\>Drawing Lines in Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3144436				0	br	You can incorporate lines into your text with custom angles, width, color, and other attributes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145787				0	br	The lines and other drawing objects that you insert in text are not defined in \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#html\" name=\"HTML\"\>HTML\</link\>, and are therefore not exported directly into HTML format. Instead, they are exported as graphics.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149294				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3159413\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_drawselect.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159413\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	br	3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	br	In your document, click where the line should begin. Hold down the mouse button and drag to the point where you want the line to end. If you also hold down the Shift key, you can draw only horizontal, vertical, and diagonal lines.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3154285\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_line.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154285\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049				0	br	Create a horizontal line by applying the preset Paragraph Style \<emph\>Horizontal Line\</emph\>. Click into an empty paragraph, and double-click the \<emph\>Horizontal Line\</emph\> Style in the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window. If the entry for horizontal lines is not visible in the list of Paragraph Styles, select "All Styles" in the lower listbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153254				0	br	1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	br	To define the line attributes and direction, use the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> drawing object as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361	43			0	br	Release the mouse button once the line has the desired direction and length. You can then draw more lines. End this function by pressing the Esc key or by clicking the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> icon from the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	br	You can draw a line above, beside or below a paragraph by choosing \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Borders\"\>\<emph\>Borders\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154188				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Format - Paragraph - Borders\"\>Format - Paragraph - Borders\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3166410\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertdraw.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3166410\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156117				0	br	2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	br	4.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	br	After clicking the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> icon, you can select all of the lines at the same time by clicking each line while holding down the Shift key. This multiple selection enables you to assign all of them a common color, width or other attribute.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3159400	41			0	br	On the Standard bar, click the \<emph\>Show Draw Functions \</emph\>icon to open the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>toolbar, and click the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> icon. The mouse pointer changes to a cross-hair symbol with a line beside it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id641804				0	br	When you enter a line width, you can append a measurement unit. A zero line width results in a hairline with a width of one pixel of the output medium.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id8849452				0	br	To create a single line, type three or more hyphens (-), or underscores ( _ ), and then press Enter. To create a double line, type three or more equal signs (=), asterisks (*), tildes (~), or hash marks (#), and then press Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C6				0	br	Automatic lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CC				0	br	If you start a new line by typing some consecutive hyphen or underline characters and press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key, the characters are removed and the previous paragraph gets a line as a bottom border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D0				0	br	To remove an automatically drawn border, choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Border\</emph\> and select no border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D8				0	br	To undo an automatic border replacement once, choose \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E0				0	br	To disable the automatic borders, choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect - Options\</emph\> and clear \<emph\>Apply border\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Drawing Lines in Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
