helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	br	To convert Pocket PC formats to and from $[officename] formats, you must first change some options within ActiveSync. To do this, open the ActiveSync window and open its Options dialog. Perform the following steps:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	br	Enter a name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146794				0	br	In Setup, choose the \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> option and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	br	Currently the following filters are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	br	Pocket Excel for Pocket PC compatible devices				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147216				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Conversion Settings\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428				0	br	Open the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box and select the appropriate filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147653				0	br	Installing the Pocket PC filters under Windows will also install a DLL file that supports the synchronize software of your Pocket PC.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148389				0	br	After these steps you can copy documents between $[officename] and your Pocket PC, either by the ActiveSync software or by the Windows Explorer. The filters will be applied to the document files automatically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618				0	br	Select the file and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672				0	br	Open the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box and select the appropriate filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	br	Close $[officename] and the Quickstarter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149064				0	br	Select the \<emph\>Rules\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	br	Repeat steps 4 and 5 for \<emph\>Pocket Excel Workbook\</emph\> selecting \<emph\>$[officename] Calc\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	br	Open the \<emph\>Optional Components\</emph\> entry, then open the \<emph\>Mobile Device Filters\</emph\> entry. Select the filters you want to install.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153061				0	br	Start the $[officename] Setup program:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252				0	br	The Java Runtime Environment is required to use the mobile device filters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	br	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>, \<emph\>Next\</emph\>, \<emph\>Install\</emph\>, \<emph\>Finish\</emph\> to install the filters and exit the Setup program.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154145				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Device to Desktop\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
