helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10655				0	br	You can use the Format Paintbrush tool to copy formatting from a text selection or object and apply the formatting to another text selection or object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10660				0	br	The cursor changes to a paint bucket.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	br	If you want to apply the formatting to more than one selection, double-click the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id209967\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatpaintbrush.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id209967\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. After you apply all the formatting, click the icon again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10667				0	br	On the \<emph\>Standard Bar\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066E				0	br	Select or click the text or object that you want to apply the formatting to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	br	The following table describes the formatting attributes that the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> can copy:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10691				0	br	Type of Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10697				0	br	Comment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069E				0	br	Nothing selected, but cursor is inside a text passage				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A4				0	br	Copies the formatting of the current paragraph and the character formatting of the next character in the text flow direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	br	Text is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B1				0	br	Copies the formatting of the last selected character and of the paragraph that contains the character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B8				0	br	Frame is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BE				0	br	Copies the frame attributes that are defined in Format - Frame dialog. The contents, size, position, linking, hyperlinks, and macros in the frame are not copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	br	Object is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CB				0	br	Copies the object formatting that is defined in the Format - Graphics or Format - Object dialogs. The contents, size, position, hyperlinks, and macros in the object are not copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D2				0	br	Form control is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D8				0	br	Not supported				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DD				0	br	Select the text or object whose formatting you want to copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DF				0	br	Drawing object is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E5				0	br	Copies all formatting attributes. In Impress and Draw, the text contents of the object is also copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EC				0	br	Text within drawing object or within Calc cells is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F2				0	br	Not supported				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F9				0	br	Writer table or cells are selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FF				0	br	Copies the formatting that is specified in Table, Text Flow, Borders, and Background tab pages in the Format - Table dialog. The paragraph and character formatting are also copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	br	Calc table or cells are selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070C				0	br	Copies the formatting that is specified in the Format - Cells dialog as well as the formatting of the cell contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10716				0	br	To exclude paragraph formatting, hold down Ctrl when you click. To exclude character formatting, hold down Ctrl+Shift when you click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Copying Attributes With the Format Paintbrush				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	bm_id3620715				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>clipboard;pasting formatted/unformatted text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;clipboard options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;formatted/unformatted text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats;pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;pasting in special formats\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10725				0	br	\<variable id=\"pasting\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/pasting.xhp\"\>Pasting Contents in Special Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10743				0	br	Contents that are stored on the clipboard can be pasted into your document using different formats. In %PRODUCTNAME you can choose how to paste the contents using a dialog or a drop-down icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10746				0	br	The available options depend on the contents of the clipboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	br	Pasting clipboard contents using an icon menu				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10750				0	br	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Paste\</emph\> icon on the Standard Bar to open the menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10758				0	br	Select one of the options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075B				0	br	If you do not like the result, click the \<emph\>Undo\</emph\> icon and then paste again with another option.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10762				0	br	Pasting clipboard contents using a dialog				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10769				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10771				0	br	Select one of the options and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	br	If you are in a spreadsheet and the contents of the clipboard are spreadsheet cells, then a different \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog appears. Use the \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog to copy cells using basic or advanced options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077E				0	br	\<emph\>Transpose\</emph\>: swaps the rows and the columns of the cell range to be pasted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10785				0	br	\<emph\>Link\</emph\>: pastes the cell range as a link. If the source file changes, the pasted cells change also.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078C				0	br	The other options are explained in the help, when you call the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\> dialog from within %PRODUCTNAME Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BA				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Pasting Contents in Special Formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
