helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148815	61			0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size \</emph\>- \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Mark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	br	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Graphics - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, mark \<emph\>Contents\</emph\>, \<emph\>Position\</emph\> and/or \<emph\>Size\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150775				0	br	All documents that are saved in \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\" name=\"XML format\"\>XML format\</link\> can be saved with a password. Documents that are saved with a password cannot be opened without the password. The content is secured so that it cannot be read with an external editor. This applies to content, graphics and OLE objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152920				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter the correct password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153104				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter and confirm a password of at least 5 characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153226				0	br	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	br	The following is an overview of the different ways of protecting contents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> from being modified, deleted or viewed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153657				0	br	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Graphics - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, unmark as appropriate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153703				0	br	You can protect the content, position and size of inserted graphics. The same applies to frames (in Writer) and OLE objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154286				0	br	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	br	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154991	63			0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size \</emph\>- \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Unmark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3156289				0	br	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3161646				0	br	With every change made in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer, the review function records who made the change. This function can be turned on with protection, so that it can only be turned off when the correct password is entered. Until then, all changes will continue to be recorded. Acceptance or rejection of changes is not possible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	br	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166429	59			0	br	The draw objects that you insert into your documents with the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>toolbar can be protected from being accidentally moved or changed in size. You can do the same with form objects inserted with the \<emph\>Form Controls\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B8C				0	br	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp#digital_signatures\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150499				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>marking changes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changes; review function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function; recording changes example\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499				0	br	\<variable id=\"redlining\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining.xhp\" name=\"Recording and Displaying Changes\"\>Recording and Displaying Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	br	Let's say you also e-mailed a copy of the report to a good friend and colleague who has done research on a similar topic in the past. You asked for a few suggestions, and the document is now returned by e-mail with your colleague's suggestions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	br	For example: You are an editor and are delivering your latest report. But before publication the report must be read by the senior editor and the proofreader, and both will add their changes. The senior editor writes "clarify" after one paragraph and crosses out another entirely. The proofreader corrects the spelling of your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	br	As all your colleagues and the managers in your company work with $[officename], you can produce a final version of the document from the results you get back.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	br	The edited document comes back to you, and you can incorporate or ignore the suggestions of the two reviewers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	br	When several authors are working on the same text or spreadsheet, the review function records and displays who made the various changes. On the final edit of the document, it is then possible to look at each individual change and decide whether it should be accepted or rejected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id4013794				0	br	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Recording and Displaying Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150247				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>changes; accepting or rejecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function;accepting or rejecting changes\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150247				0	br	\<variable id=\"redlining_accept\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_accept.xhp\" name=\"Accepting or Rejecting Changes\"\>Accepting or Rejecting Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id1491134				0	br	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	br	Color-coded entries display the result of the filter that is set. Entries in black can be accepted or rejected and match the filter criteria. Entries in blue do not themselves match the filter criteria, but have subentries that are included by the filter. Gray entries cannot be accepted or rejected and do not match the filter criterion. Green entries do match the filter but cannot be accepted or rejected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	br	If you have put multiple copies of the document in circulation, first merge these into one document (see \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_docmerge.xhp#redlining_docmerge\"/\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	br	If one author has modified another author's change, you will see the changes hierarchically arranged with a plus sign for opening up the hierarchy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	br	When you edit a document in which others have made changes, you can accept or reject the changes individually or all together.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474				0	br	If the list of changes is too long, you can switch to the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> tab in the dialog and specify that you only want to see the changes of certain authors, or only the changes of the last day, or that you want the list to be restricted in some other way.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	br	Open the document and choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Accept or Reject\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Accept or Reject Changes\</emph\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	br	Select a change on the \<emph\>List\</emph\> tab. The change is selected and displayed in the document and you can now enter your decision with one of the buttons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Accepting or Rejecting Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154788				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>documents; comparing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comparing documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>versions; comparing documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changes;comparing to original\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function; comparing documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154788				0	br	\<variable id=\"redlining_doccompare\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_doccompare.xhp\" name=\"Comparing Versions of a Document\"\>Comparing Versions of a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	br	A file selection dialog appears. Select the copy of the document and confirm the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	br	You can now accept the "insertions", in which case the relevant texts stay in their original form, or you can accept the "deletions", in which case the marked text contained in the copy is not inserted in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	br	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> combines both documents into your original document. All text passages that occur in your document but not in the copy are identified as having been inserted, and all text passages that are missing in your original document are identified as deletions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087				0	br	Open your original document and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Compare Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	br	If one of the authors has made changes to a document without recording them, you can compare the changed document to your original document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3995178				0	br	Imagine you have some co-authors or reviewers who collaborate with you writing your original document. One day you send out copies of your document to all reviewers. You ask them to edit the copy and send it back.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id4186223				0	br	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id4208807				0	br	You should always start with opening the newer document and compare it with the older document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id9948423				0	br	Normally, the reviewers enable change tracking by \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Record\</emph\> and you can easily see the changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Comparing Versions of a Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154230				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>documents; merging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>versions;merging document versions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154230				0	br	\<variable id=\"redlining_docmerge\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_docmerge.xhp\" name=\"Merging Versions\"\>Merging Versions\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id2136295				0	br	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	br	Select the copy of the document from the dialog. If there have been no subsequent changes to the original document, the copy is merged into the original.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Merge Document\</emph\>. A file selection dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	br	If changes have been made to the original document, an error dialog appears that informs you that the merge is unsuccessful.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3152425				0	br	Open the original document into which you want to merge all copies.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049				0	br	When a document has been edited by more than one person, it is possible to merge the edited copies into the original. The only requirement is that the documents differ only and exclusively in the recorded changes - all other original text must be identical.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	br	After you merge the documents you will see the recorded changes from the copy in the original document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Merging Versions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155364				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>changes; recording\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recording; changes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comments; on changes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>settings;tracking changes\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	br	\<variable id=\"redlining_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_enter.xhp\" name=\"Recording Changes\"\>Recording Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145669				0	br	Not all changes are recorded. For example, the changing of a tab stop from align left to align right is not recorded. However, all usual changes made by a proofreader are recorded, such as additions, deletions, text alterations, and usual formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	br	1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147530				0	br	To change the settings for tracking changes, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040700.xhp\" name=\"Changes\"\>\<emph\>Changes\</emph\>\</link\> or on the \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060600.xhp\" name=\"Changes\"\>\<emph\>Changes\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473				0	br	You can enter a comment on each recorded change by placing the cursor in the area of the change and then choosing \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Comment\</emph\>. In addition to Extended Tips, the comment is also displayed in the list in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230400.xhp\" name=\"Accept or Reject Changes\"\>\<emph\>Accept or Reject Changes\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	br	To start recording changes, open the document to be edited and choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Changes\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Changes\</emph\>\</link\> and then choose \<emph\>Record\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	br	If you move to a marked change with the mouse pointer, you will see a reference to the type of change, the author, date and time of day for the change in the Help Tip. If the Extended Tips are also enabled, you will also see any available comments on this change.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	br	3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153542				0	br	To stop recording changes, choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Record\</emph\> again. The check mark is removed and you can now save the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153627				0	br	In a text document, you can highlight all lines that you have changed with an additional colored marking. This can be in the form of a red line in the margin, for example.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	br	2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156119				0	br	Changes in a spreadsheet document are highlighted by a border around the cells; when you point to the cell you can see more detailed information on this change in the Help Tip.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	br	Now start making your changes. You will note that all new text passages that you enter are underlined in color, while all text that you delete remains visible but is crossed out and shown in color.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7271645				0	br	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Recording Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>changes; protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>protecting; recorded changes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>records; protecting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201	1			0	br	\<variable id=\"redlining_protect\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_protect.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Records\"\>Protecting Records\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id1631824				0	br	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Protect Records\</emph\>. This opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/password_dlg.xhp\" name=\"Password\"\>\<emph\>Password\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	br	Enter a password consisting of at least 5 characters and confirm it. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	br	To protect the changes made in a document during editing, choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. To turn off the function or to accept or reject changes it is necessary to enter the correct password first.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Protecting Records				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154230				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>versions; of a document\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; version management\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>version management\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154230				0	br	\<variable id=\"redlining_versions\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_versions.xhp\" name=\"Version Management\"\>Version Management\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149399				0	br	You can choose to view individual versions of a document, or you can display the differences between versions with color markings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	br	In the dialog to open a document, you can select from a combo box which version of this document you want to open.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	br	The \<emph\>File\</emph\> menu contains a \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01190000.xhp\" name=\"Versions\"\>\<emph\>Versions\</emph\>\</link\> command that enables you to save multiple versions of a document in the same file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Version Management				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150040				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>corner roundings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rectangles with round corners\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>legends;rounding corners\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>round corners\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>customizing;round corners\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150040				0	br	\<variable id=\"round_corner\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/round_corner.xhp\" name=\"Creating Round Corners\"\>Creating Round Corners\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	par_id3148539				0	br	If you place the cursor on the box it changes to a hand symbol. You can now drag the box to change the amount of rounding. An outline shows a preview of the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	par_id3156136				0	br	When you insert a rectangle or a callout box using the drawing functions and activate the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, you see a small frame at the upper left corner of the object. The frame indicates the amount by which the corners are rounded. When the frame is positioned at the top left corner, no rounding occurs. When the frame is positioned on the handle centered at the top of the object, the corners are rounded as much as possible. You adjust the degree of rounding by moving the frame between these two positions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3150774\" src=\"res/helpimg/hand01.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150774\"\>Mouse pointer as hand\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
