helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159233				0	br	To view file properties for the current document:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3145121				0	br	Right-click and choose\<emph\> Properties\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	br	File properties, such as author name, subject, and keywords, help you manage and identify your documents. $[officename] also tracks file statistics, including the number of words and the number of pages in a document, and automatically adds the statistics as part of the file property.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3147834				0	br	You can view file properties for the current document\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\> or for a document in the Windows File Open dialog \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3153311				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
