helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E5				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xforms.xhp\"\>XML Form Documents (XForms)\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F5				0	br	XForms are a new type of web form that was developed by the World Wide Web Consortium. The XForm model is defined in Extensible Markup Language (XML). The model uses separate sections to describe what a form does and what a form looks like. You can view the specification for XForms at: \<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/MarkUp/Forms/\"\>http://www.w3.org/MarkUp/Forms/\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	br	To Create a New XForms Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070D				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - New - XML Form Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10714				0	br	The XForms design window opens in an empty Writer document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10718				0	br	Design your form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071E				0	br	Insert a control, select the default model in the property browser, and enter a binding statement.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10722				0	br	In the data navigator, add an element to the instance.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10726				0	br	Load a new instance from an XML file and add controls to the relevant XML elements or attributes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10729				0	br	To Open an XForms Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10730				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> and select the XForms document. An XForm document has the same extension as a Writer text document (*.odt).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10737				0	br	To Edit an XForms Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073B				0	br	Open the XForms document and use the following toolbars and windows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10741				0	br	Form Design toolbar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10746				0	br	Working with XForms				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074A				0	br	In %PRODUCTNAME, an XForms document is a special type of Writer document. The Design Mode for an XForm document has additional toolbars and panes. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074D				0	br	After you create and save an XForms document, you can open the document, fill out the form, and submit the changes to a server.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10757				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\"\>Form Controls toolbar\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075B				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\"\>Form Navigator\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075F				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/xformsdata.xhp\"\>Data Navigator\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	XML Form Documents (XForms)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id7007583				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>file filters (XML)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;to XML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>loading;XML files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing;from XML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting;to XML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XSLT filters, see also XML filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distributing XML filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;XML filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>testing XML filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XML filters;creating/testing/distributing/deleting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10923				0	br	About XML Filters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10927				0	br	%PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\"\>stores documents in XML format\</link\>. You can create customized filters that convert the native OpenDocument XML file format used by %PRODUCTNAME into another format. These filters can be integrated into %PRODUCTNAME seamlessly so that you can save or load these formats transparently.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093A				0	br	To create an XML filter, you must have a good understanding of XML and XSLT concepts. These concepts are beyond the scope of this help.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093D				0	br	An XML filter contains \<emph\>stylesheets\</emph\> that are written in the XSLT language. The stylesheets define the transformation from the OpenDocument file format to another XML format through export and import filters. There are three types of XML filters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10947				0	br	\<emph\>Import Filters\</emph\> load external XML files and transform the format of the files into the OpenDocument XML file format. After you install an import filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10960				0	br	\<emph\>Export Filters\</emph\> transform OpenDocument XML files and \<emph\>save\</emph\> the files to a different XML format. After you install an export filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070001.xhp\"\>Export dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10979				0	br	\<emph\>Import/Export Filters\</emph\> load and save OpenDocument XML files into a different XML \<emph\>format\</emph\>. After you install these filters, the names of the filters are added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\> and the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\"\>File Save As dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B39				0	br	\<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/Style/XSL/\"\>World Wide Web Consortium Pages on Extensible \<emph\>Stylesheet\</emph\> Language (XSL)\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B4E				0	br	\<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/XML/\"\>World Wide Web Consortium Pages on Extensible Markup Language (XML)\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D97				0	br	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp#xmlformat\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Working With %PRODUCTNAME XML Filters 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10531				0	br	To create an XML filter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN1053D				0	br	Creating an XML Filter for %PRODUCTNAME				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109A9				0	br	When you create an XML filter for %PRODUCTNAME, you need to design an \<emph\>XSLT stylesheet\</emph\> that can convert to and from the OpenDocument XML file format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109B0				0	br	For more information about the OpenDocument XML format, go to \<link href=\"http://xml.openoffice.org/\"\>http://xml.openoffice.org/\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109C5				0	br	If you want, you can include a \<emph\>template\</emph\> with your filter to apply %PRODUCTNAME styles to an XML document that you import.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109CC				0	br	You can also include the \<emph\>Document Type Definition\</emph\> (DTD) for the for the external XML format so you can validate the XML format, for example, when you test the filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E0				0	br	Create an XSLT transformation \<emph\>stylesheet\</emph\> that maps the elements of the external XML format to the elements of the OpenDocument XML file format and back again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E8				0	br	Create a template that assigns %PRODUCTNAME styles to elements in the external XML format when you import a file in this format into %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109EC				0	br	In %PRODUCTNAME Writer, create a text document, and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109F4				0	br	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109FC				0	br	In the \<emph\>XML Filter\</emph\> dialog, click the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab, and define the properties of the filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A03				0	br	In the \<emph\>Filter Name\</emph\> box, enter a name for the XML filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A09				0	br	In the \<emph\>Application\</emph\> box, select the %PRODUCTNAME application that the filter is for.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A0F				0	br	In the \<emph\>Name of File Type\</emph\> box, enter the file type that the filter is for.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A15				0	br	In the \<emph\>File extension\</emph\> box, enter the extension for the exported file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A1B				0	br	To differentiate the file from other XML files, enter an extension other than *.xml.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A1F				0	br	On the \<emph\>Transformation\</emph\> tab page, define the transformation properties for the filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A26				0	br	(Optional) In the \<emph\>DocType\</emph\> box, enter the document type identifier for the external file format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A2C				0	br	(Optional) In the \<emph\>DTD\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name of the DTD for the external file format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A32				0	br	In the \<emph\>XSLT for export\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name of the XSLT stylesheet that defines the transformation from OpenDocument format to the external format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A38				0	br	In the \<emph\>XSLT for import\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name to the XSLT stylesheet that defines the transformation from the external format to OpenDocument format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A3E				0	br	(Optional) In the \<emph\>Template for import\</emph\> box, enter the path and name of the template that defines the %PRODUCTNAME styles that are used in the imported file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A44				0	br	The files that are specified on the \<emph\>Transformation\</emph\> tab page are copied to the local %PRODUCTNAME users directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A4C				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A56				0	br	To test an XML filter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A5A				0	br	You can perform basic tests on a custom XML filter in %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A60				0	br	Create or open a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A67				0	br	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A6F				0	br	In the list of filters, select the filter that you want to test, and click \<emph\>Text XSLTs\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A82				0	br	To test an \<emph\>Export\</emph\> Filter, do one of the following in the \<emph\>Export\</emph\> area of the dialog:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A91				0	br	The document is not altered by these tests. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A99				0	br	To test an \<emph\>Import\</emph\> Filter, click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Import\</emph\> area of the dialog, select a document, and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CA1				0	br	This name is displayed in the \<emph\>XML Filter Settings\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC6				0	br	This name is displayed in the list of file types in the \<emph\>Open\</emph\>, \<emph\>Export\</emph\>, and \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialogs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D0E				0	br	This identifier is used to detect the file type on import.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D1F				0	br	This DTD is used to validate the files on export.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10DEB				0	br	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\>, select the %PRODUCTNAME document that you want to test, and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10DF7				0	br	To test the current document, click \<emph\>Current Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E32				0	br	To validate the transformed file against the specified DTD, click \<emph\>Validate\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10535				0	br	To delete an installed XML filter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AC0				0	br	You can distribute an XML filter to multiple users using a special package format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AC3				0	br	To save an XML filter as a package				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10ACA				0	br	In Writer, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10ACD				0	br	The XML Filter Settings dialog is only available when a text document is open.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AD9				0	br	Select the filter that you want to distribute and click \<emph\>Save As Package\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AE0				0	br	To install an XML filter from a package				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AE7				0	br	In Writer, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AEA				0	br	The XML Filter Settings dialog is only available when a text document is opened.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AF6				0	br	Click \<emph\>Open Package\</emph\> and select the package file with the filter you want to install.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B0A				0	br	In Writer, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_distribute.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B19				0	br	Select the filter you want to delete and click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
