helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762				0	br	The functions provided allow you to edit the points of a curve or an object converted to a curve. The following icons are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3153951\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleobjectbeziermode.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153951\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3146866				0	br	Symmetric Transition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3147070				0	br	Close Bézier				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3147321				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3146920\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierdelete.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3146920\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3147397				0	br	Move Points				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierMove\"\>Activates a mode in which you can move points.\</ahelp\> The mouse pointer displays a small empty square when resting on a point. Drag that point to another location. The curve on both sides of the point follows the movement; the section of the curve between the next points changes shape.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148420				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierConvert\"\>Converts a curve into a straight line or converts a straight line into a curve.\</ahelp\> If you select a single point, the curve before the point will be converted. If two points are selected, the curve between both points will be converted. If you select more than two points, each time you click this icon, a different portion of the curve will be converted. If necessary, round points are converted into corner points and corner points are converted into round points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148460				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierEdge\"\>Converts the selected point or points into corner points.\</ahelp\> Corner points have two movable control points, which are independent from each other. A curved line, therefore, does not go straight through a corner point, but forms a corner.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148813				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3151183\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziersmooth.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151183\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148917				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierDelete\"\>Use the \<emph\>Delete Points\</emph\> icon to delete one or several selected points. If you wish to select several points click the appropriate points while holding down the Shift key.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148970				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3155385\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziereliminatepoints.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155385\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3149441				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierEliminatePoints\"\>Marks the current point or the selected points for deletion.\</ahelp\> This happens in the event that the point is located on a straight line. If you convert a curve or a polygon with the \<emph\>Convert to Curve \</emph\>icon into a straight line or you change a curve with the mouse so that a point lies on the straight line, it is removed. The angle from which the point reduction is to take place \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>can be set by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01070300.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Drawing - Grid\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Draw - Grid\</emph\>\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>can be set by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01070300.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Presentation - Grid\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - Grid\</emph\>\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>is 15° by default.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481				0	br	Point at the curve between two points or within a closed curve and drag the mouse to shift the entire curve without distorting the form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	br	Edit Points				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	br	If a certain section of the curve is straight, the end points of the line have a maximum of one control point each. They cannot be modified to round points unless the straight line is converted back to a curve.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3150402				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BEZIER_TOOLBOX\"\>The \<emph\>Edit Points \</emph\>Bar appears when you select a polygon object and click \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3151248				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierCutLine\"\>The\<emph\> Split Curve \</emph\>icon splits a curve. Select the point or points where you want to split the curve, then click the icon\</ahelp\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3152581				0	br	Split Curve				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	br	Eliminate Points				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153710				0	br	Insert Points				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153766				0	br	First select the points to be deleted, and then click this icon, or press Del.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153788				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3148489\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziercutline.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148489\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3159218\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziersymmetric.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159218\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153838				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3146969\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierinsert.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3146969\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154096				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3149377\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziermove.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149377\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	br	Smooth Transition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154344				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3148607\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierclose.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148607\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154576				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3154201\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezieredge.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154201\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3155510				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierSmooth\"\>Converts a corner point or symmetrical point into a smooth point.\</ahelp\> Both control points of the corner point are aligned in parallel, and can only be moved simultaneously. The control points may differentiate in length, allowing you to vary the degree of curvature.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3155812				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierSymmetric\"\>This icon converts a corner point or a smooth point into a symmetrical point.\</ahelp\> Both control points of the corner point are aligned in parallel and have the same length. They can only be moved simultaneously and the degree of curvature is the same in both directions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3155961				0	br	Delete Points				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierClose\"\>Closes a line or a curve.\</ahelp\> A line is closed by connecting the last point with the first point, indicated by an enlarged square.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3157846				0	br	If you wish to create a corner point you must first insert either a smooth or a symmetrical point which is then converted to a corner point by using \<emph\>Corner Point\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3158212				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3149036\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierconvert.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149036\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3158445				0	br	Convert To Curve				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3159151				0	br	The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05270000.xhp\" name=\"Edit Points\"\>\<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\>\</link\> icon allows you to activate or deactivate the edit mode for Bézier objects. In the edit mode, individual points of the drawing object can be selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3160478				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierInsert\"\>Activates the insert mode. This mode allows you to insert points.\</ahelp\> You can also move points, just as in the move mode. If, however, you click at the curve between two points and move the mouse a little while holding down the mouse button you insert a new point. The point is a smooth point, and the lines to the control points are parallel and remain so when moved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3166429				0	br	Corner Point				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Edit Points Bar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149495				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0400.xhp\" name=\"Shortcut Keys\"\>Shortcut Keys\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150040				0	br	This section contains descriptions of frequently used shortcut keys in $[officename].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Shortcut Keys				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156183				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0500.xhp\" name=\"Glossaries\"\>Glossaries\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0500.xhp	0	help	par_id3157898				0	br	This section provides a general glossary of technical terms used in $[officename], along with a list of Internet terms.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Glossaries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0600.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154232				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>programming;$[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Basic;programming\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154232				0	br	\<variable id=\"programming\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/main0600.xhp\" name=\"Programming $[officename]\"\>Programming $[officename]\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149760	2			0	br	\<variable id=\"basic\"\>$[officename] can be controlled by using the $[officename] API. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149795				0	br	For more information on $[officename] Basic, select "$[officename] Basic" in the list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0600.xhp	0	help	par_id3151111				0	br	$[officename] provides an Application Programming Interface (API) that enables you to control $[officename] components by using various programming languages. A $[officename] Software Development Kit is available for the programming interface.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153825				0	br	Macros created with $[officename] Basic based on the old programming interface will no longer be supported by the current version.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	br	\<link href=\"http://api.openoffice.org/\" name=\"For more information about $[officename] API Reference, please visit (http://api.openoffice.org/)\"\>For more information about $[officename] API Reference, please visit (http://api.openoffice.org/)\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0600.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Programming $[officename]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153089				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0650.xhp\" name=\"Java Platform Support\"\>Java Platform Support\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3152363				0	br	$[officename] supports the Java platform for running applications, applets and components based on the JavaBeans architecture.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3153822				0	br	Your modifications at the \<emph\>Tools - Options - $[officename] - Java\</emph\> tab page will be used even if the Java Virtual Machine (JVM, a virtual machine for the Java platform) already has been started. After modifications to the ClassPath you must restart $[officename]. The same is true for modifications under \<emph\>Tools - Options - Internet - Proxy\</emph\>. Only the two boxes "Http Proxy" and "Ftp Proxy" and their ports don't require a restart, they will be evaluated when you click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	br	For $[officename] to support the Java platform, you must install the Java 2 Runtime Environment software from Sun Microsystems. When you installed $[officename], you automatically received the option to install these files if they were not yet installed. You can also install these files now if required. The executable setup file is located in the $[officename]/program folder and on the $[officename] CD.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	br	The Java platform support needs to be activated under $[officename] to run Java applications.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	br	Activate Java platform support by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/java.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - $[officename] - Java\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - $[officename] - Java\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id9116183				0	br	Before you can use a JDBC driver, you need to add its class path. Choose Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME- Java, and click the Class Path button. After you add the path information, restart %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Java Platform Support				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153089				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0800.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] and the Internet\"\>$[officename] and the Internet\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0800.xhp	0	help	par_id3155150				0	br	This section provides information on the subject of the Internet. An \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp\" name=\"Internet glossary\"\>Internet glossary\</link\> explains the most important terms.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0800.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	$[officename] and the Internet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
