helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01012000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145120				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sets the colors for the $[officename] user interface.\</ahelp\> You can save the current settings as color scheme and load them later.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01012000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145365				0	br	In order to enhance cursor visibility, if the user sets the application background color between 40% and 60% gray, it is automatically changed to 40% gray.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01012000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SVXPAGE_COLORCONFIG_PB_SAVESCHEME\"\>Saves the current settings as a color scheme that you can reload later.\</ahelp\> The name is added to the \<emph\>Scheme\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01012000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149204				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OPTIONS_COLORCONFIG_COLORLIST_WIN\"\>Select the colors for the user interface elements.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01012000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SVXPAGE_COLORCONFIG_PB_DELETESCHEME\"\>Deletes the color scheme shown in the \<emph\>Scheme\</emph\> box. You cannot delete the Default scheme.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01012000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150769				0	br	To apply a color to a user interface element, ensure that the checkbox in front of the name is marked. To hide a user interface element, clear the check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01012000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	br	Save and delete color schemes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01012000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	br	The \<emph\>Automatic\</emph\> color setting changes the user interface element to the preset color from the color scheme.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01012000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153541				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_COLORCONFIG_LB_COLORSCHEME\"\>Selects the color scheme you want to use.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01012000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154921				0	br	The color settings for "Visited links" and "Unvisited links" only apply to documents created after the settings are applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
