helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01014000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153681				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01014000.xhp\" name=\"Network Identity\"\>Network Identity\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01014000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153881				0	br	User name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01014000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155388				0	br	Authentication Method				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01014000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_SSO_LB_MECHANISM\"\>Choose your security mechanism for access to the LDAP server.\</ahelp\> Choices are Simple or Kerberos.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01014000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_EDIT_RID_SVXPAGE_SSO_ED_USERNAME\"\>Using "simple" authentication method, you enter your user name on the LDAP server here.\</ahelp\> Using "Kerberos", you just see your user name, but cannot edit it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01014000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149797				0	br	Using remote configuration, you can start a copy of $[officename] on any computer in the network with your own user data and personal configuration.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01014000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150358				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_SSO_CB_PASSWORD\"\>Using "simple" authentication method, check this box to make your password persistent.\</ahelp\> If the password is persistent and the same user starts $[officename] later on, the user name and password will not be requested again. Using "Kerberos", this box is not active.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01014000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153562				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sets the options for a remote configuration access to your personal $[officename] settings stored on an LDAP server.\</ahelp\> To see this tab page and to use this feature, remote configuration must be active: You need an account on an LDAP server that is running and configured to store $[officename] user settings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01014000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154939	12			0	br	The password will be stored encrypted in a file called .ssop in your \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>home directory \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>"My Documents" folder\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01014000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156343				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_EDIT_RID_SVXPAGE_SSO_ED_PASSWORD\"\>Using "simple" authentication method, enter your password for access to the LDAP server here.\</ahelp\> Using "Kerberos", this box is not active.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01014000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Network Identity				2002-02-02 02:02:02
