helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156283				0	br	New				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3144767				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:PB_ADD\"\>Click this button to add a new configuration to the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147213				0	br	Compare the URLs with the sample URLs in the fields of this dialog and make a note of the prefixes, suffixes and separators used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317				0	br	Again, copy the contents of the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	br	Copy the URL from your browser's \<emph\>URL\</emph\> field and paste it into a blank document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148647				0	br	Change the conditions for the search in the search engine, if it offers you the choice.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148663				0	br	The links \<emph\>And, Or\</emph\> and \<emph\>Exactly\</emph\> are available.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	br	Search engines handle queries differently according to the way they are constructed. For example, some are case sensitive and some are not. Because of this, it is best to select \<emph\>None\</emph\> as the case match option.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149413				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:PB_NEW\"\>Use this button to include a new search engine.\</ahelp\>\<emph\>New\</emph\> deletes all important entries of the entry mask such as "Name" and "Suffix". Enter the new search engine together with all of the necessary details. As soon as you accept your entries with \<emph\>Add\</emph\>, the new search engine will appear in the search engine list under \<emph\>Search in\</emph\>. Close the dialog with the \<emph\>OK\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149560				0	br	To determine which prefixes, separators and suffixes to use when defining a new search engine:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_SEPARATOR\"\>If you type more than one word while running a search, these words will be separated by the character specified here.\</ahelp\> Most search engines require the "+" character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151320				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:PB_CHANGE\"\>Click this button to apply the modifications made to an existing configuration.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153662				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OPTIONS_SEARCH\"\>Use this tab page to define the settings for searching in the Internet.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:LB_SEARCH\"\>Displays the available search engines.\</ahelp\> Select a search engine to display its configuration in the adjacent text and option boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153970				0	br	The search terms are passed between the prefix and the suffix.\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_POSTFIX\"\>The suffix provides the command sequence, sent at the end of a search.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_URL\"\>This text box displays the URL and the first part of the query command for a search machine. A URL can also be typed directly.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154270				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:PB_DELETE\"\>Click this button to delete the selected search engine from the list. There will be no security response.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:RB_EXACT\"\>Sets the advanced search preferences (and, or, exact) as well as the way the results are defined and displayed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154918				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_CASE\"\>Determines the case match for running a search.\</ahelp\> The list contains the following entries: \<emph\>None\</emph\>, \<emph\>Upper\</emph\> and \<emph\>Lower\</emph\>. The search terms entered are converted according to your selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155449	12			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_SEARCH_NAME\"\>Displays the name of the selected search engine.\</ahelp\> This is the name that will be shown in the sub-menu of the \<emph\>Search\</emph\> icon on the Hyperlink bar. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3157909				0	br	Specifies the search engine and its corresponding configuration.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159255				0	br	Activate the search engine and perform a search with at least two words.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Search				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_idN1054D				0	br	\<variable id=\"email\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01020300.xhp\"\>E-mail\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056B				0	br	On UNIX systems, specifies the e-mail program to use when you send the current document as e-mail.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_idN10576				0	br	E-mail program				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057A				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"703252484\"\>Enter the e-mail program path and name.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_idN10591				0	br	...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_idN10595				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"703255045\"\>Opens a file dialog to select the e-mail program.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	E-mail				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	par_idN105B7				0	br	\<variable id=\"mozilla\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01020400.xhp\"\>Mozilla/Netscape Plug-in\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D5				0	br	Specifies to use the Mozilla plug-in to show %PRODUCTNAME documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D8				0	br	When you click a hyperlink to a %PRODUCTNAME document in your Mozilla or Netscape browser, one of the following can happen:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	par_idN105DE				0	br	The browser asks you whether you want to save the document on your disk, or whether you want to use an application to open the document. This request dialog appears by default when you click a hyperlink to a %PRODUCTNAME document the first time and you did not enable the Mozilla plug-in.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E2				0	br	The browser downloads the document to a temporary folder, then tells your system to run %PRODUCTNAME and open the document in %PRODUCTNAME. This is the default when you did not enable the Mozilla plug-in and chose to open the document with %PRODUCTNAME when you were first asked.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E6				0	br	The browser opens a new browser window that shows some of the %PRODUCTNAME icons, and displays the document in the browser window. This is the default when you enable the Mozilla plug-in. When you click the \<emph\>Edit File\</emph\> icon, a copy of the document is downloaded to a temporary folder on your disk, then %PRODUCTNAME starts and loads the copy for editing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F5				0	br	Viewing of %PRODUCTNAME and MS Office documents in Mozilla/Netscape enabled				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F9				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"736117762\"\>Enables the Mozilla plug-in to show %PRODUCTNAME documents in a browser window. Select, click OK, then restart your browser. Then in the browser window, click a link to a %PRODUCTNAME document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	par_idN10655				0	br	The plug-in needs a version of Mozilla 1.x, Netscape 6.x, or Netscape 7.x installed on your system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Mozilla Plug-in				2002-02-02 02:02:02
