helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_LAYOUT_CB_MARKHDR\"\>Specifies whether to highlight column and row headers in the selected columns or rows.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_LAYOUT_CB_TEXTFMT\"\>Specifies that printer metrics are applied for printing and also for formatting the display on the screen.\</ahelp\> If this box is not checked, a printer independent layout will be used for screen display and printing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_LAYOUT_CB_EDITMODE\"\>Allows you to immediately edit the selected cell after pressing the Enter key.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:METRICFIELD:RID_SCPAGE_LAYOUT:MF_TAB\"\>Defines the tab stops distance.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400	11			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_LAYOUT_CB_FORMAT\"\>Specifies whether to automatically apply the formatting attributes of the selected cell to the empty adjacent cells.\</ahelp\> If, for example, the contents of the selected cell have the bold attribute, this bold attribute will also apply to adjacent cells. Cells that already have a special format will not be modified by this function. You can see the range in question by pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> + * (multiplication sign on the number pad) shortcut. This format also applies to all new values inserted within this range. The normal default settings apply to cells outside this range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150444				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCPAGE_LAYOUT:LB_UNIT\"\>Defines the unit of measure in spreadsheets.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	br	If you insert rows or columns in the middle of a reference area, the reference is always expanded.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150872				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_LAYOUT_CB_REPLWARN\"\>Specifies that, when you paste cells from the clipboard to a cell range that is not empty, a warning appears.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194				0	br	\<emph\>Example:\</emph\> If the range A1:B1 is referenced in a formula and you insert a new column after column B, the reference is expanded to A1:C1. If the range A1:B1 is referenced and a new row is inserted under row 1, the reference is not expanded, since there is only a single cell in the vertical direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_LAYOUT_CB_EXPREF\"\>Specifies whether to expand references when inserting columns or rows adjacent to the reference range. This is only possible if the reference range, where the column or row is inserted, originally spanned at least two cells in the desired direction.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
