helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147530	61			0	br	Now type a selling price (for example, 100) in cell B5. The net price should be shown in cell B6 and the value-added tax should be shown in cell B7. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCPAGE_CALC\"\>Defines the calculation settings for spreadsheets. Defines the behavior of spreadsheets with iterative references, the date settings, the number of decimal places, and if capitalization or lower cases are to be considered when searching within sheets.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148422				0	br	.* in following position:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148686	7			0	br	\<emph\>Example:\</emph\> Calculating the cost of an item without the value-added-tax.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148814	44			0	br	If \<emph\>Search criteria = and <> must apply to whole cells \</emph\>is not enabled, the "win" search pattern acts like ".*win.*". The search pattern can be at any position within the cell when searching with the Calc database functions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149202				0	br	5				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149211				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_MATCH\"\>Specifies that the search criteria you set for the Calc database functions must match the whole cell exactly. When the \<emph\>Search criteria = and <> must apply to whole cells\</emph\> box is marked, $[officename] Calc behaves exactly as MS Excel when searching cells in the database functions.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:NUMERICFIELD:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:ED_PREC\"\>Defines the number of decimals to be displayed for numbers with the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> number format. The numbers are displayed as rounded numbers, but are not saved as rounded numbers.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149795	6			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_ITERATE\"\>Specifies whether formulas with iterative references (formulas that are continuously repeated until the problem is solved) are calculated after a specific number of repetitions.\</ahelp\> If the\<emph\> Iterations \</emph\>box is not marked, an iterative reference in the table will cause an error message.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150644				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_CALC\"\>Specifies whether to make calculations using the rounded values displayed in the sheet. Charts will be shown with the displayed values. If the \<emph\>Precision as shown\</emph\> option is not marked, the displayed numbers are rounded, but they are calculated internally using the non-rounded number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150886				0	br	Finds win and os2win, but not win95 or upwind				2002-02-02 02:02:02
