helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\javaparameters.xhp	0	help	par_idN10545				0	br	Java Start Parameters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\javaparameters.xhp	0	help	par_idN10549				0	br	You can use this dialog to enter optional start parameters for the Java runtime environment (JRE). The settings that you specify in this dialog are valid for any JRE that you start.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\javaparameters.xhp	0	help	par_idN10568				0	br	Java Start parameter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\javaparameters.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056C				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"svx:Edit:RID_SVXDLG_JAVA_PARAMETER:ED_PARAMETER\"\>Enter a start parameter for a JRE as you would on a command line. Click Assign to add the parameter to the list of available start parameters.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\javaparameters.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057B				0	br	To enable debugging in a JRE, enter the following parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
