helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertIntoMetaFile\"\>Converts the selected object to Windows Metafile Format (WMF), containing both bitmap and vector graphic data.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050600.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	To metafile 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050700.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146119				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>converting; to contours\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>contours; converting to\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	br	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13050700.xhp\" name=\"To Contour\"\>To Contour\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050700.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:convert_to_contour\"\>Converts the selected object to a polygon, or a group of polygons.\</ahelp\> If the conversion creates a group of polygons (for example, when you convert a text object), then press F3 to enter the group before you can select an individual polygon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155601	3			0	br	Once you convert a line or a text object to a contour, you can no longer edit it as you normally would. Instead, you can edit the contour as you would any polygon, including using the \<emph\>Edit – Points \</emph\>command to adjust its shape.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050700.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	To Contour 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150012				0	br	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13140000.xhp\" name=\"Combine\"\>Combine\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974	2			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Combine\"\>Combines two or more selected objects into a single shape.\</ahelp\>Unlike \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05290000.xhp\" name=\"grouping\"\>grouping\</link\>, a combined object takes on the properties of the lowermost object in the stacking order. You can \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13150000.xhp\" name=\"split\"\>split\</link\> apart combined objects, but the original object properties are lost.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	br	When you combine objects, the drawing elements are replaced by Bézier curves and holes appear where the objects overlap.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13140000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Combine				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13150000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150439				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>combining; undoing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>splitting; combinations\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13150000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150439				0	br	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13150000.xhp\" name=\"Split\"\>Split\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13150000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Dismantle\"\>Splits a \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13140000.xhp\" name=\"combined\"\>combined\</link\> object into individual objects.\</ahelp\> The resulting objects have the same line and fill properties as the combined object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13150000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Split				2002-02-02 02:02:02
