helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153191	1			0	br	\<variable id=\"footer\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/footer.xhp\" name=\"Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides\"\>Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id4712057				0	br	Adding text objects as header or footer objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id7251808				0	br	Adding predefined header or footer objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1356547				0	br	Every slide is based on a slide master. The text, pictures, tables, fields or other objects that you place on the slide master are visible as a background on all slides that are based on that slide master.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1445966				0	br	Enter or select the contents that should be visible on all slides.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1453901				0	br	By default, the \<emph\>Slide number\</emph\> checkbox is cleared, so no slide numbers are visible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1583300				0	br	To edit a handout master, click the Handout tab above the slide. Click the Normal tab to leave the handout master.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1829889				0	br	Objects that you insert on a slide master are visible on all slides that are based on that slide master.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1876583				0	br	You see a dialog with two tab pages: \<emph\>Slide\</emph\> and \<emph\>Notes and Handouts\</emph\> where you can enter contents to the predefined areas. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1956236				0	br	If you want to change the position and formatting of the master objects, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id204779				0	br	By default, the \<emph\>Footer\</emph\> checkbox is enabled, but the text input box is empty, so no footer is visible on the slides.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id2521439				0	br	Click the Date Area and move the time and date field. Select the <date/time> field and apply some formatting to change the format for the date and time on all slides. The same applies to the Footer Area and the Slide Number Area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295	12			0	br	On the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, select the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154654\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_texttoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154654\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3148866				0	br	Choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149947				0	br	Drag in the master page to draw a text object, and then type or paste your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150476				0	br	You can also add fields, such as the date or page number, to a header or footer by choosing \<emph\>Insert - Fields\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	br	You can add a text object to the master page for your slides to act as a header or a footer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155441				0	br	Choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\> when you are finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155848				0	br	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/04990000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Fields\"\>Insert Fields\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3156320	18			0	br	You can hide the header or footer on the current slide by choosing \<emph\>Format\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"Modify Layout\"\>Slide\<emph\> Layout\</emph\>\</link\>, and clearing the \<emph\>Objects on background\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id4101077				0	br	By default, the \<emph\>Date and Time\</emph\> checkbox is enabled, but the format is set to Fixed and the text input box is empty, so no date and time is visible on the slides.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5015411				0	br	Every type of master has some predefined areas to hold the date, footer, and slide numbers. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5259559				0	br	You see the slide master with areas near the bottom. You can move the areas , and you can select the fields and apply some formatting. You can also enter some text here which will be shown next to the fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5641651				0	br	To edit a notes master, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Notes Master\</emph\>. Click the Close Master View icon on the Master View toolbar, or choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>, to leave the notes master.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id704672				0	br	Masters exist for slides, notes, and handouts. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id7549668				0	br	A predefined Header Area is available only for notes and handouts. If you want a header on all slides, you can move the Footer Area on the slide master to the top.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8217413				0	br	When you switch to the master view, you can move that areas to any position on the master. You can enter additional text and resize the areas. You can select the contents of the areas and apply text formats. For example, you can change the font size or color.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8403576				0	br	To edit a slide master, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>. Click the Close Master View icon on the Master View toolbar, or choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>, to leave the slide master.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8843043				0	br	Choose \<emph\>View - Header and Footer\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides				2002-02-02 02:02:02
