helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155443				0	br	To insert text from a file into a slide:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3143228				0	br	Select all of the text that lies below the visible slide area and press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+X.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313				0	br	In the slide where you want to insert the text, choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3147297				0	br	Repeat steps 1 to 3 until all of the text is on slides.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3148610				0	br	Locate the file containing the text that you want to add, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	br	Double-click in the inserted text to enter edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
