helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id1614734				0	br	The stacking order of objects on your page is determined by the sequence in which you add the objects. You can rearrange the stacking order by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	3			0	br	Layers are available in $[officename] Draw, not in $[officename] Impress. Layers allow you to assemble elements on a page that are related. Think of layers as individual workspaces that you can hide from view, hide from printing, or lock. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146962				0	br	$[officename] Draw provides three default layers:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053				0	br	Controls				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	br	Dimension Lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	br	The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer is the default workspace. The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer determines the location of title, text, and object placeholders on your page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150742				0	br	The \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer can be used for buttons that have been assigned an action, but that should not be printed. Set the layer's properties to not printable. Objects on the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer are always in front of objects on other layers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153073				0	br	Layout				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153085				0	br	The \<emph\>Dimension Lines\</emph\> layer is where you draw, for example, the dimension lines. By switching the layer to show or hide, you can easily switch these lines on and off.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507				0	br	You can lock a layer to protect its contents, or hide a layer and its contents from view or from printing. When you add a new layer to a page, the layer is added to all of the pages in your document. However, when you add an object to a layer, it is only added to the current page. If you want the object to appear on all of the pages, add the object to the master page (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Master\</item\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156397				0	br	You cannot delete or rename the default layers. You can add your own layers by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Layer\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id398876				0	br	The areas on a layer that do not contain objects are transparent.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id7036957				0	br	Layers do not determine the stacking order of objects on your page, except for the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer which is always in front of other layers. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	About Layers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145253				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>line styles;loading\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>line ends;about\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arrows;loading arrow styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles;arrow and line styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>loading;arrow and line styles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145253				0	br	\<variable id=\"line_arrow_styles\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_arrow_styles.xhp\" name=\"Loading Line and Arrow Styles\"\>Loading Line and Arrow Styles\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154485				0	br	To load a line styles file:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154765				0	br	To load an arrow styles file:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145588				0	br	Locate the file containing the line styles that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The file has the format [filename].sod.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145822				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05200000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Line\"\>Format - Line\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149054				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Load Arrow Styles\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	br	Locate the file containing the line styles that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The file has the format [filename].sod.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3151240				0	br	To save a line styles file, click the \<emph\>Save Line Styles\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153070				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Arrow Styles\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017				0	br	You can use styles to organize similar line and arrow types. $[officename] provides a few standard style files that you can load and use in your document. If you want, you can add or delete elements from a style file, or even create a custom style file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154705				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Load Line Styles\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Line Styles\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3166465				0	br	To save a line styles file, click the \<emph\>Save Arrow Styles\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Loading Line and Arrow Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
