helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	hd_id2071596				0	br	How to use the Freeform Line tool				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149377				0	br	\<variable id=\"line_draw\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_draw.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Curves\"\>Drawing Curves\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	hd_id46388				0	br	How to use the Curve tool				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id1122165				0	br	Click where you want the curve to start, and keep holding the mouse button down.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id1556443				0	br	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3148390				0	br	Release the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868	4			0	br	The \<emph\>Curve\</emph\> tool \<image id=\"img_id3150205\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150205\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> lets you draw a curved line that consists of one or more line segments. Each Bézier curve segment is defined by two data points (endpoints) and one or two control points (handles) that you can drag to adjust the arc of the curve. A control point is connected to a data point by a control line. Moving a control point pulls the curve towards it, and changes the shape of a curve.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3149451				0	br	Drag in any direction to define an arc for the curve, and then click to set it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874				0	br	A smooth data point has different line curvatures on either side, and two control lines that move together as a straight line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	br	A Bézier curve has three types of data points:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150435				0	br	A corner data point has one or two control lines and joins different line segments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3151172	9			0	br	Double-click to finish drawing the line. To create a closed shape, double-click the starting point of the line. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	br	Click to draw the curve segment using the current arc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766				0	br	A symmetrical data point has the same line curvature on either side, and two control lines that move together as a straight line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154865	22			0	br	Move the pointer to where you want the curve segment to end and do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155262	5			0	br	Open the \<emph\>Curves\</emph\> toolbar, and select the \<emph\>Curve\</emph\> tool \<image id=\"img_id3145829\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145829\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155928	6			0	br	Click where you want the curve to start, and drag a short distance in the direction you want the curve to go. To create a straight line segment, hold down \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift\</item\> while you drag.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id4907681				0	br	On the Drawing toolbar, open the \<emph\>Curves\</emph\> toolbar \<image id=\"Graphic2\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and select the \<emph\>Freeform Line\</emph\>\<image id=\"Graphic3\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_freeline_unfilled.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> tool.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id5377056				0	br	To create a closed shape, double-click the starting point of the line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id5792107				0	br	Draw the freeform line as you would do with a pencil.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id7734916				0	br	Release the mouse button to finish the line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id8174687				0	br	Hold down \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift\</item\> while you drag to restrict the direction to a 45 degree grid.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id8532364				0	br	Control points are only visible in "Edit Points" mode. Control points are represented by circles, anchor points are represented by squares. The start point is a little bit larger than the other anchor points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
