helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3146963				0	br	Select the text that you want to convert, and do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053				0	br	In $[officename] Draw, choose \<emph\>Modify - Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150336				0	br	Now, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar. Click the object. You can see all the Bézier points of the object. On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> bar, you can find various icons for editing, inserting and deleting points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150395				0	br	In $[officename] Impress, right-click the border of the text object, and then choose \<emph\>Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150746				0	br	If your text contains more than one character, the converted text becomes a grouped object. Double-click the group to edit individual objects. Press Esc when finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	br	You can convert text characters into curves that you can edit and resize as you would any drawing object. Once you convert text into a drawing object, you can no longer edit the content of the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
