helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146904	26			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XGTY\"\>Inserts the \<emph\>greater than \</emph\>relation.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\><?> gt <?>\</emph\> or <?> > <?> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147079				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XDIVIDESY\"\>Inserts the \<emph\>divides\</emph\> character.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\><?> divides <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147098				0	br	orthogonal to				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147258				0	br	The following is a complete list of the relations. The symbol next to the name of the relation indicates that it can be accessed through the Selection window (choose \<emph\>View - Selection\</emph\>) or through the context menu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147279				0	br	double arrow pointing left				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147449	61			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XPARALLELY\"\>Inserts a \<emph\>parallel \</emph\>relation with two placeholders.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\><?>parallel<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147495				0	br	greater than				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147598				0	br	parallel to				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148707				0	br	double arrow pointing left and right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148721				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_DLRARROW\"\>Inserts the logical relation \<emph\>arrow with double bar pointing left and right\</emph\> with two operators.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>dlrarrow\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148877				0	br	less than				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148889				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XLTY\"\>Inserts the \<emph\>less than\</emph\> relation.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\><?>lt<?>\</emph\> or <?> < <?> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148976				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XORTHOY\"\>Inserts a character for an \<emph\>orthogonal\</emph\> (right angled) relation with two placeholders.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\><?> ortho <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	br	does not divide				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XNDIVIDESY\"\>This icon inserts the \<emph\>does not divide\</emph\> character.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\><?>ndivides<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149218				0	br	approximately equal to				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149231	59			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XAPPROXY\"\>Inserts the \<emph\>approximately equal\</emph\> relation with two placeholders.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\><?> approx <?> \</emph\>in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149592				0	br	The \<emph\><?>transr<?>\</emph\> command inserts the \<emph\>original by\</emph\> correspondence character with two placeholders.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149599				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_DLARROW\"\>Inserts the logical relation \<emph\>arrow with double bar pointing left\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>dlarrow\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
