helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090500.xhp	0	help	par_idN113E5				0	br	Examples of single brackets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090500.xhp	0	help	par_idN113E8				0	br	For non-scaled brackets:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090500.xhp	0	help	par_idN113EB				0	br	a = \\{ \\( \\[ b newline				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090500.xhp	0	help	par_idN113EE				0	br	{} + c \\] \\) \\ }				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090500.xhp	0	help	par_idN113F3				0	br	For scaled brackets use \<emph\>none\</emph\> as the bracket name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090500.xhp	0	help	par_idN113FA				0	br	a = left ( a over b right none newline				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090500.xhp	0	help	par_idN113FF				0	br	left none phantom {a over b} + c right )				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090500.xhp	0	help	par_idN11404				0	br	The \<emph\>phantom\</emph\> statement ensures that the last bracket is the correct size.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Brackets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154011				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>attributes; in %PRODUCTNAME Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; attributes in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>accents; in %PRODUCTNAME Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>attributes; accents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>vector arrows as attributes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tilde as attribute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>circumflex attribute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bold attribute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>italic attribute in %PRODUCTNAME Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resizing;fonts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>attributes; changing fonts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing; fonts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>attributes; colored characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>colored characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>attributes; changing defaults\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>circle attribute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>double dot attribute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dot attribute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>line through attribute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>line above attribute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reversed circumflex attribute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>overline attribute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wide vector arrow attribute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wide tilde attribute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wide circumflex attribute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>underline attribute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>triple dot attribute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>transparent character as attribute\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154011				0	br	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090600.xhp\" name=\"Attributes\"\>Attributes\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154650				0	br	Attribute Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3145230	50			0	br	For more information about formatting in \<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME\</emph\>\<emph\>Math\</emph\>, see \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091100.xhp\" name=\"Brackets and Grouping\"\>Brackets and Grouping\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3145618				0	br	Resize				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3145802	2			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_ATTRIBUTES_CAT\"\>You can choose from various attributes for \<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME\</emph\>\<emph\>Math\</emph\> formulas. Some attributes are displayed in the lower part of the Selection window.\</ahelp\> These attributes are also listed in the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#kontextmenue\" name=\"context menu\"\>context menu\</link\> of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window. All attributes not contained in the Selection window or in the context menu must be typed manually in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3146071				0	br	The \<emph\>nbold\</emph\> and \<emph\>nitalic\</emph\> commands remove the bold or italic default fonts of formula components. For example, remove italics from the x in the formula 5 x + 3=28 by typing \<emph\>nitalic\</emph\> before the x as in \<emph\>5 nitalic x + 3=28\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3146322				0	br	Acute accent				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147126				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_WIDEVECX\"\>Inserts a wide vector arrow with a placeholder.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>widevec\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147167				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_CHECKX\"\>Inserts a placeholder with a reverse circumflex ("checkmark") over it.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>check <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147221				0	br	Dot				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147311	57			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_WIDEHATX\"\>Inserts a wide circumflex ("hat") with a placeholder. \</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>widehat\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147344				0	br	Italic font				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147355				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_ITALX\"\>Inserts a placeholder with italic formatting.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>ital <?>\</emph\> or \<emph\>italic <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147492				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_OVERLINEX\"\>Inserts a line over a placeholder.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>overline <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window. The line adjusts itself to correct length.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147621				0	br	Line over				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3148695				0	br	Note that some entries require spaces for the correct structure. This is especially true when you specify attributes with fixed values instead of placeholders.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3148764				0	br	Wide circumflex				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149486				0	br	Line above (bar)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149541				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_DDOTX\"\>Inserts a placeholder with two dots over it.\</ahelp\> You can also directly enter \<emph\>ddot <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149604				0	br	In describing the following attribute functions, the letter "a" in the icon refers to the placeholder that you would like to assign to the respective attribute. You can substitute this character with any other character that you choose.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149626				0	br	 Use the \<emph\>color\</emph\> command to change the color of your formula. Type \<emph\>color\</emph\>, then type the color name (the available colors are white, black, cyan, magenta, red, blue, green and yellow), then the formula, character or character sequence. The input \<emph\>color green size 20 a\</emph\> results in a green letter "a" with a font size of 20.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149774				0	br	Transparent				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149815				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_BARX\"\>Inserts a line ("bar") above a placeholder .\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>bar <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149877				0	br	Grave accent				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149976				0	br	Breve				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150018				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_GRAVEX\"\>Inserts a placeholder with a \<emph\>grave accent\</emph\> (grave).\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>grave <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150089				0	br	Bold font				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150101				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_BOLDX\"\>Inserts a placeholder with bold formatting.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>bold <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150356				0	br	Tilde				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150533				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_ACUTEX\"\>Inserts a placeholder with an acute accent.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>acute <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150612				0	br	The \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091300.xhp\" name=\"attributes\"\>attributes\</link\> "acute", "bar", "breve", "check", "circle", "dot", "ddot", "dddot", "grave", "hat", "tilde" and "vec" have fixed sizes. Their width or length cannot be adjusted when positioned over a long symbol.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153125				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_SIZEXY\"\>Inserts a command for modifying the font size with two placeholders. The first placeholder refers to the font size (for example, 12) and the second one contains the text.\</ahelp\> For proper structure, insert a space between the values. You can also directly enter \<emph\>size <?> <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153258				0	br	Line below				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153269				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_UNDERLINEX\"\>Inserts a line below a placeholder.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>underline <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153292				0	br	Line through (overstrike)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153304				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_OVERSTRIKEX\"\>Inserts a placeholder with a line (or overstrike) through it.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>overstrike <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153516				0	br	Wide vector arrow				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	br	Vector arrow				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_VECX\"\>Inserts a placeholder with a vector arrow.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>vec <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153573				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_CIRCLEX\"\>Inserts a placeholder with a circle over it.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>circle <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153619				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_BREVEX\"\>Inserts a placeholder with an accent breve.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>breve <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154116	55			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_WIDETILDEX\"\>Inserts a wide tilde with a placeholder. \</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>widetilde\</emph\> directly in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154201				0	br	Circumflex				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154221				0	br	Information on \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091300.xhp\" name=\"attributes\"\>attributes\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091200.xhp\" name=\"indexes and exponents\"\>indexes and exponents\</link\>, and \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091400.xhp\" name=\"scaling\"\>scaling\</link\> can help you structure your documents more efficiently.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	br	Circle				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154359				0	br	Change font				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154371				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_FONTXY\"\>Inserts a command for changing the font type, with two placeholders. Replace the first placeholder with the name of one of the \<link href=\"text/smath/01/05010000.xhp\" name=\"custom fonts\"\>custom fonts\</link\>, \<emph\>Serif, Sans\</emph\> or \<emph\>Fixed\</emph\>. Replace the second placeholder with the text.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>font <?> <?>\</emph\> directly in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154570				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_TILDEX\"\>Inserts a placeholder with a tilde.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>tilde <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154707				0	br	Triple dot				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154718				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_DDDOTX\"\>Inserts three dots over a placeholder.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>dddot <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154900				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_DOTX\"\>Inserts a placeholder with a dot over it.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>dot <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155074				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_PHANTOMX\"\>Inserts a placeholder for a transparent character. This character takes up the space of "a" but does not display it.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>phantom <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155621	52			0	br	For size changes you can use \<emph\>size n\</emph\>,\<emph\> +n\</emph\>,\<emph\> -n\</emph\>,\<emph\> *n\</emph\> and\<emph\> /n \</emph\>, where \<emph\>n\</emph\> is a placeholder. This method is useful when the base size of the formula is subject to change. The commands \<emph\>size +n\</emph\> and \<emph\>size -n\</emph\> change point size, and \<emph\>size *n\</emph\> and \<emph\>size /n\</emph\> change the size by a percentage. For example, the command \<emph\>size *1.17\</emph\> increases the size of a character by exactly 17%.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155921				0	br	Double dot				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155962				0	br	The following is a complete list of all attributes available in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Math. The symbol next to the attribute indicates that it can be accessed through the Selection window (choose \<emph\>View - Selection\</emph\>) or through the context menu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156263				0	br	Reverse Circumflex				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156278				0	br	Wide tilde				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3159198				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_HATX\"\>Inserts a placeholder with a circumflex ("hat").\</ahelp\> You can also directly enter \<emph\>hat <?>\</emph\> in the Commands window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
