helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_id3150706				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XINY\"\>Use the icon to insert the \<emph\>is included in\</emph\> set operator with two placeholders.\</ahelp\> You can also enter \<emph\><?> in <?>\</emph\> directly into the Commands window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984				0	br	is not included in				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_id3150997	36			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XNOTINY\"\>Use this icon to insert the \<emph\>is not included in\</emph\> set operator with two placeholders.\</ahelp\> You can also enter \<emph\><?> notin <?> \</emph\>in the Commands window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_id3151088				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XSUPSETY\"\>Use this icon to insert the set operator \<emph\>is a superset of\</emph\> and two placeholders.\</ahelp\> You can also enter \<emph\><?>supset<?>\</emph\> in the Commands window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_id3151119	67			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XSUPSETEQY\"\>Use this icon to insert the set operator \<emph\>is a super set or equal to\</emph\> with two placeholders.\</ahelp\> Alternatively, you can enter \<emph\><?>supseteq<?> \</emph\>in the Commands window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090800.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305				0	br	Superset or equal to				2002-02-02 02:02:02
