helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146932				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:MENUBUTTON:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:1\"\>Click one of the choices from this pop-up menu to access the \<link href=\"text/smath/01/05010100.xhp\" name=\"Fonts\"\>Fonts\</link\> dialog, where you can define the font and attributes for the respective formula and for custom fonts.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147516				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_LISTBOX_RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG_1\"\>You can select the fonts for the variables in your formula.\</ahelp\> For example, in the formula x=SIN(y), x and y are variables, and will reflect the assigned font.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148831				0	br	If you want to mark individual text segments with a font other than that used for the whole text, then enter the \<link href=\"text/smath/01/05010000.xhp\" name=\"FONT\"\>Font\</link\> command in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151108				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:5\"\>You can specify the font to be used for the \<emph\>font serif\</emph\> format.\</ahelp\> Serifs are the small "guides" that can be seen, for example, at the bottom of a capital A when the Times serif font is used. Using serifs is quite helpful since it guides a reader's eye in a straight line and can speed up reading.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151187				0	br	You can define fonts for the variables, functions, numbers and inserted text that form the elements of your formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151315	17			0	br	These custom fonts are used if you set a different font with the FONT command in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152950				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:2\"\>Select the fonts for names and properties of functions.\</ahelp\> For example, the functions in the formula x=SIN(y) are =SIN( ).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153716				0	br	\<variable id=\"schriftartentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FONT\"\>Defines the fonts that can be applied to formula elements.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153780				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:4\"\>Define the fonts for the text in your formula here.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154198				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:7\"\>You can specify the font to be used for \<emph\>fixed\</emph\> font formatting.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154566				0	br	In this section of the \<emph\>Fonts\</emph\> dialog you can define fonts, with which you can format other text components in the formula. The three basic fonts \<emph\>Serif, Sans\</emph\> and \<emph\>Fixed\</emph\> are available. You can add any other font to each standard installed basic font. Every font installed on your system is available for you to use. Select the \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> button to expand the selection offered in the list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154610				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:3\"\>You can select the fonts for the numbers in your formula.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155186				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:PUSHBUTTON:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:2\"\>Click this button to save your changes as the default for all new formulas.\</ahelp\> After confirming the changes, click the \<emph\>Yes\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155900				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:6\"\>You can specify the font to be used for \<emph\>sans\</emph\> font formatting.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156318				0	br	The list boxes in the \<emph\>Fonts\</emph\> dialog display a default font for all elements. To change to a different font, click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>, then select the element type. A new dialog box appears. Select the desired font and check any desired attributes, then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. To set the changes as the default fonts, click the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Fonts				2002-02-02 02:02:02
