helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150671				0	br	Select a registered database that you want to insert the selected field from. You can also change the table or query that the selected field refers to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150700				0	br	Lists the field options, for example, "fixed". If you want, you can click another option for the selected field type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151168				0	br	You can also double-click a field in your document to open the field for editing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151184				0	br	\<variable id=\"feldbefehltext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FieldDialog\"\>Opens a dialog where you can edit the properties of a field. Click in front of a field, and then choose this command.\</ahelp\> In the dialog, you can use the arrow buttons to move to the previous or the next field. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151371				0	br	The following dialog elements are only visible when the corresponding field type is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126				0	br	Displays the text that is linked to a condition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153668				0	br	To change the view between field names and field contents in your document, choose \<emph\>View - Fields\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154039	39			0	br	Displays the database record number that is inserted when the condition specified for the "Any record" field type is met. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154339				0	br	Insert or modify the reference text for the selected field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154624				0	br	Displays the formula of a formula field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155073				0	br	Change the field contents that are displayed depending on whether the field condition is met or not.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155142				0	br	Lists the type of field that you are editing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155341				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3155348\" src=\"res/sc10618.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155348\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156124				0	br	Displays the condition that must be met for the field to be activated. If you want, you can enter a new \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"condition\"\>condition\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id5081637				0	br	If you want to change the actual page number and not the displayed number, do not use the \<emph\>Offset\</emph\> value. To change page numbers, read the \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagenumbers.xhp\" name=\"Page Numbers\"\>\<emph\>Page Numbers\</emph\>\</link\> guide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
