helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id306711				0	br	Bookmarks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3145105				0	br	Inserts the caption label of the reference target. This option is only available when you the reference target is an object with a caption.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3146344				0	br	In master documents, you can also reference from one sub-document to another. Note that the reference name will not appear in the selection field and has to be entered "by hand".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3146883				0	br	Inserts the caption number of the reference target. This option is only available when you the reference target is an object with a caption.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3147422				0	br	Set target for a referenced field. Under \<emph\>Name\</emph\>, enter a name for the reference. When inserting the reference, the name will then appear as an identification in the list box \<emph\>Selection\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3147746				0	br	Inserting a reference to another position in the document. The corresponding text position has to be defined with "Set Reference" first. Otherwise, inserting a reference by choosing a field name under \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> is not possible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148705				0	br	As Page Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728				0	br	Inserts the number of the page containing the reference target using the format specified in the page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148786				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_REF:LB_REFFORMAT\"\>Select the format that you want to use for the selected reference field.\</ahelp\> The following formats are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149556				0	br	In an HTML document, reference fields entered this way will be ignored. For the target in HTML documents, you have to \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04040000.xhp\" name=\"insert a bookmark\"\>insert a bookmark\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
