helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156369				0	br	Value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3143281				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_DB:ED_DBCONDITION\"\>For fields linked to a \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"condition\"\>condition\</link\>, enter the criteria here.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3145771				0	br	Enter the characters that you want to combine. You can combine a maximum of 6 characters. This option is only available for the \<emph\>Combine characters\</emph\> field type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3146865	22			0	br	You can also insert database fields in the \<emph\>Then \</emph\>and \<emph\>Else \</emph\>boxes using the format "databasename.tablename.fieldname".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084				0	br	Select the macro that you want to run when the field is clicked.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147455	65			0	br	This dialog is shown when you click an \<emph\>Input list\</emph\> field in the document. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147473				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_TP_FLD_FUNC_PB_LISTADD\"\>Adds the \<emph\>Item\</emph\> to the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147515	10			0	br	Inserts a text field that runs a macro when you click the field in the document. To assign a macro to the field, click the \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> button. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147524				0	br	Inserts a text field that is hidden when the condition that you specify is met. To use this function, choose \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040600.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Text Document - Formatting Aids\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\>\</link\> and clear the \<emph\>Fields: Hidden text\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147564				0	br	Inserts a text field that displays one item from a list. You can add, edit, and remove items, and change their order in the list. Click an \<emph\>Input list\</emph\> field in your document or press Ctrl+Shift+F9 to display the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090003.xhp\" name=\"Choose Item\"\>\<emph\>Choose Item\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147583				0	br	If the table or the field name does not exist in a database, nothing is inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_FLD_FUNC_LB_LISTITEMS\"\>Lists the items. The topmost item is shown in the document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147733				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_EDIT_TP_FLD_FUNC_ED_LISTNAME\"\>Enter a unique name for the \<emph\>Input list\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3148434				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_DLG_FLD_DROPDOWN_PB_NEXT\"\>Closes the current \<emph\>Input list\</emph\> and displays the next, if available.\</ahelp\> You see this button when you open the \<emph\>Choose Item\</emph\> dialog by Ctrl+Shift+F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3148855				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_DLG_FLD_DROPDOWN_PB_EDIT\"\>Displays the \<emph\>Edit Fields: Functions\</emph\> dialog, where you can edit the \<emph\>Input list\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149173				0	br	Type the text that you want to hide if a condition is met.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149287				0	br	Inserts a text field that you can open by \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090100.xhp\" name=\"clicking\"\>clicking\</link\> it in the document. You can then change the text that is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149558				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_TP_FLD_FUNC_PB_LISTREMOVE\"\>Removes the selected item from the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149837				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_DLG_FLD_DROPDOWN_LB_LISTITEMS\"\>Choose the item that you want to display in the document, then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149881	6			0	br	Inserts text if a certain \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"condition\"\>condition\</link\> is met. For example, enter "sun eq 1" in the \<emph\>Condition\</emph\> box, and then the text that you want to insert when the variable "sun" equals "1" in the \<emph\>Then \</emph\>box. If you want, you can also enter the text that you want to display when this condition is not met in the \<emph\>Else\</emph\> box. To define the variable "sun", click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090005.xhp\" name=\"Variables\"\>\<emph\>Variables\</emph\>\</link\> tab, select "Set variable", type "sun" in the\<emph\> Name\</emph\> box, and its value in the\<emph\> Value\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150111				0	br	The following controls are displayed for \<emph\>Input list\</emph\> fields:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150343				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_EDIT_TP_FLD_FUNC_ED_FUNCVALUE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets additional function parameters for fields. The type of parameter depends on the field type that you select.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537				0	br	Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150688				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_EDIT_TP_FLD_FUNC_ED_LISTITEM\"\>Enter a new item.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150973				0	br	Hidden text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242				0	br	Depending on the field type that you select, you can assign conditions to certain functions. For example, you can define a field that executes a macro when you click the field in the document, or a condition that, when met, hides a field. You can also define placeholder fields that insert graphics, tables, frames and other objects into your document when needed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3151329				0	br	For function fields, the format field is only used for fields of the type placeholder. Here, the format determines the object for which the placeholder stands.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370				0	br	Enter a value for the selected field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3152585				0	br	If you include the quotes in "databasename.tablename.fieldname", the expression is inserted as text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3152946				0	br	Placeholder				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3152999				0	br	Conditional text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153146				0	br	Input field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153351				0	br	Displays the name of the selected macro.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	br	Inserts a placeholder field in the document, for example, for graphics. When you click a placeholder field in the document, you are prompted to insert the item that is missing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153677				0	br	Hides a paragraph when the condition that you specify is met. To use this function, choose \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040600.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Text Document - Formatting Aids\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\>\</link\> and clear the \<emph\>Fields: Hidden paragraph\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153719				0	br	Input list				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154192	39			0	br	Combine characters 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480				0	br	Hidden Paragraph				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154691				0	br	Execute macro				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154830	21			0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_EDIT_TP_FLD_FUNC_ED_FUNCCOND2\"\>Enter the text to display when the condition is met in the \<emph\>Then \</emph\>box, and the text to display when the condition is not met in the \<emph\>Else \</emph\>box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3155149	27			0	br	Type the text that you want to display in the field. If you are inserting a placeholder field, type the text that you want to display as a help tip when you rest the mouse pointer over the field. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3155623				0	br	Meaning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3155912				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_TP_FLD_FUNC_BT_FUNCMACRO\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Macro Selector\</emph\>, where you can choose the macro that will run when you click the selected field in the document.\</ahelp\> This button is only available for the "Execute macro" function field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3155970				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_TP_FLD_FUNC_PB_LISTUP\"\>Moves the selected item up in the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3156221				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_TP_FLD_FUNC_PB_LISTDOWN\"\>Moves the selected item down in the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3156282				0	br	Type the text that you want to appear in the placeholder field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3159199				0	br	Combines up to 6 characters, so that they behave as a single character. This feature is only available when Asian fonts are supported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149608				0	br	Fixed content				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154479				0	br	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090004.xhp\" name=\"DocInformation\"\>DocInformation\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3145262				0	br	Document number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3145774				0	br	Modified				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3146326				0	br	Created				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3146942				0	br	Inserts the subject as entered in the \<emph\>Description \</emph\>tab of the \<emph\>File Properties \</emph\>dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3147490				0	br	Inserts the comment as entered in the \<emph\>Description \</emph\>tab of the \<emph\>File Properties \</emph\>dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3148856				0	br	Info 0 - 3				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3148982				0	br	When you export and import an HTML document containing DocInformation fields, \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090007.xhp#dokumentinfo\" name=\"special $[officename] formats\"\>special $[officename] formats\</link\> are used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149176				0	br	Meaning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149692				0	br	DocInformation fields contain information about the properties of a document, such as the date a document was created. To view the properties of a document, choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149833				0	br	Inserts the name of the author, and the date, or the time when the document was created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149956				0	br	For the "Created", "Modified", and "Last printed" field types, you can include the author, date, and time of the corresponding operation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3150033				0	br	Inserts the title as entered in the \<emph\>Description \</emph\>tab of the \<emph\>File Properties \</emph\>dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3150092				0	br	Title				2002-02-02 02:02:02
