helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3146334				0	br	$[officename] Tag				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147102				0	br	Date is fixed				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147487				0	br	For DocInformation fields, the TYPE parameter equals DOCINFO. The SUBTYPE parameter displays the specific field type, for example, for the "Created" DocInformation field, SUBTYPE=CREATE. For date and time DocInformation fields, the FORMAT parameter equals DATE or TIME, and the SDNUM parameter indicates the number format that is used. The SDFIXED parameter indicates if the content of the DocInformation field is fixed or not.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147501				0	br	The contents of a fixed date or time field are equal to the SDVAL parameter, otherwise the contents are equal to the text found between the SDFIELD HTML tags.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147738				0	br	Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3148863				0	br	<SDFIELD TYPE=DOCINFO SUBTYPE=COMMENT SDFIXED>Description</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3148970				0	br	$[officename] Tag				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149485				0	br	Examples of date and time special HTML tags that are recognized by $[officename] as fields are shown in the following table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149562				0	br	Examples of DocInformation special HTML tags that are recognized by $[officename] as fields are shown in the following table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149696				0	br	For "Date" and "Time" fields, the TYPE parameter equals DATETIME. The format of the date or the time is specified by the SDNUM parameter, for example, DD:MM:YY for dates, or HH:MM:SS for time.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846				0	br	Description (fixed content)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3150110				0	br	Time is variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3150175				0	br	Creation time (fixed content)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3151083				0	br	Creation date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3151257				0	br	Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3152960				0	br	$[officename] Writer fields are identified by the <SDFIELD> tag in an HTML document. The field type, the format, and the name of the special field are included in the opening HTML tag. The format of a field tag that is recognized by an HTML filter depends on the field type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3153298				0	br	<SDFIELD TYPE=DOCINFO SUBTYPE=CREATE FORMAT=DATE SDNUM="1031;1031;QQ YY">1. Quarter 98</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3153634				0	br	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDVAL="35843,4239988426" SDNUM="1031;1031;DD/MM/YY">17/02/98</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3153669				0	br	When you save a document that contains fields as an HTML document, $[officename] automatically converts date, time, and DocInformation fields to special HTML tags. The field contents are inserted between the opening and closing HTML tags of the converted fields. These special HTML tags do not correspond to standard HTML tags.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3154330				0	br	<SDFIELD TYPE=DOCINFO SUBTYPE=CHANGE FORMAT=DATE SDNUM="1031;1031;NN DD MMM, YY">Mo 23 Feb, 98</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155077				0	br	Modification date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155137				0	br	Date is variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155183				0	br	For fixed date and time fields, the date or the time is specified by the SDVAL parameter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155862				0	br	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDNUM="1031;1031;HH:MM:SS">10:10:36</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155915				0	br	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDVAL="35843,4240335648" SDNUM="1031;1031;HH:MM:SS">10:10:36</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3156134				0	br	<SDFIELD TYPE=DOCINFO SUBTYPE=CREATE FORMAT=TIME SDVAL="0" SDNUM="1031;1031;HH:MM:SS AM/PM" SDFIXED>03:58:35 PM</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3156275				0	br	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDNUM="1031;1031;DD/MM/YY">17/02/98</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Special Tags				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147515				0	br	Input Field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153669				0	br	Edit				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155897				0	br	Next				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146041				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FLD_INPUT\"\>Inserts a text field that you can open and edit by clicking it in the document.\</ahelp\> You can use input fields for text, or to assign a new value to a variable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149691				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:DLG_FLD_INPUT:PB_NEXT\"\>Jumps to the next input field in the document.\</ahelp\> This button is only available when you position the cursor directly before an input field, and then press Shift+Ctrl+F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154470				0	br	To change the content of an Input Field in a document, click the field, and then edit the text in the lower box of the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154571				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:MULTILINEEDIT:DLG_FLD_INPUT:ED_EDIT\"\>The upper box displays the name that you entered in the \<emph\>Reference\</emph\> box of the Input Field on the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab of the \<emph\>Fields\</emph\> dialog. The lower box displays the contents of the field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Input Field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145828				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>logical expressions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulating conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditions; in fields and sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fields;defining conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sections;defining conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variables; in conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>user data;in conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;in conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding; database fields\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145218				0	br	Examples of Conditions in Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145828				0	br	\<variable id=\"defining_conditions\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\"\>Defining Conditions\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148791				0	br	User Data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150311				0	br	To display conditional text based on the number of pages:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151375				0	br	Conditions and Variables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154115				0	br	Conditions and Database Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155573				0	br	To display conditional text based on the contents of a database field:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155814				0	br	To display conditional text based on a user-defined Variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145108				0	br	user_country				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145178				0	br	Position				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145231				0	br	The following examples use the Conditional text field, although they can be applied to any fields that can be linked to a condition. The syntax used for conditions is also used for the Hidden text, Hidden paragraph, Any record or Next record fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145242				0	br	Conditions are logical expressions that you can use to control the display of \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\"\>fields\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020000.xhp\"\>sections\</link\> in your document. Although the following examples apply to fields, they also apply to sections.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145259				0	br	x != 1 or x NEQ 1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145412				0	br	Hidden paragraph: hides the paragraph if the condition is true.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145603				0	br	user_state				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145781				0	br	Variables based on the contents of database fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146345				0	br	The condition is true if "x" is a multiple of pi.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146885				0	br	Country				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146911				0	br	Database.Table.Company ==""				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	139			0	br	In the\<emph\> Name\</emph\> box, type "Profit".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147032	140			0	br	In the\<emph\> Value\</emph\> box, type "5000".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147090	23			0	br	If you leave the \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box empty, the condition is interpreted as not being met.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147110				0	br	or type the following				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147123				0	br	NOT Addressbook.Addresses.Company				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147136				0	br	If the COMPANY database field is empty, the condition is true and the paragraph is hidden.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147171				0	br	You can define conditions for the following field types:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147272				0	br	user_lastname				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147417				0	br	x == 1 or x EQ 1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147471				0	br	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, click "Conditional text".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147500				0	br	The condition is true if "x" is equal to 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147515				0	br	Any record and next record: controls the access to database records.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147549	78			0	br	In the document, place the cursor between the two fields, press Space, and then return to the \<emph\>Fields \</emph\>dialog:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147749				0	br	sinx == 0				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148673				0	br	Database.Table.Company NEQ ""				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148687				0	br	Database.Table.Company != ""				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148705				0	br	user_company				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728				0	br	Company				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148733				0	br	Returns TRUE if the COMPANY field is empty. (Exclamation sign represents a logical NOT.)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148762				0	br	Database.Table.Company !="Sun Microsystems"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148811	75			0	br	In the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list, click "Mail merge fields".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148841	76			0	br	In the\<emph\> Database selection\</emph\> box, double-click an address book, click "First Name", and then click\<emph\> Insert\</emph\>. Repeat for "Last Name".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148922				0	br	user_city				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148945				0	br	City				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148980				0	br	When you define a condition, use the same \<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\"\>elements\</link\> for defining a formula, namely comparative operators, mathematical and statistical functions, number formats, variables and constants.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149138				0	br	In the \<emph\>Or \</emph\>box, type "Hello".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149163				0	br	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149174				0	br	Variables based on user data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149289				0	br	Hidden text: hides the contents of the field if the condition is true.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149580				0	br	user_zipcode				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149601				0	br	Last name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149632				0	br	Variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149802	18			0	br	The simplest way to define a condition is to type the logical expression directly in a \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box using the following values:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846				0	br	To use comparative operators with strings, the operands must be bounded by double quotation marks:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149953				0	br	First name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149977				0	br	!Database.Table.Company				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149991				0	br	NOT Database.Table.Company				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150004				0	br	Database.Table.Company EQ ""				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150028				0	br	You can include user data when you define conditions. To change your user data, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - $[officename] - User data\</emph\>. User data must be entered in the form of strings. You can query the user data with "==" (EQ), "!=" (NEQ), or "!"(NOT).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051				0	br	You may want to create a condition that hides an empty field, for example, if the COMPANY field is empty for some of the data records.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150067				0	br	Select the \<emph\>Hidden Paragraph\</emph\> box, and type the following condition: Addressbook.Addresses.Company EQ ""				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150097				0	br	The "equal" comparative operator must be represented by two equal signs (==) in a condition. For example, if you define a variable "x" with the value of 1, you can enter the condition as x==1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150122				0	br	The following examples use a variable called "x":				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150129				0	br	State (not in all $[officename] versions)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150147				0	br	For example, to hide a paragraph, text, or a section from a user with a specific initial, such as "LM", enter the condition: user_initials=="LM".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150162				0	br	Checks if variable "x" contains (true) the "ABC" string, or not (false).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150232				0	br	To display hidden paragraphs on the screen, you can choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\>, and clear the \<emph\>Hidden paragraphs\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150333				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150416				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> tab, and then click "Conditional text" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150523				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Database\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150551				0	br	The condition is true if "x" does not equal 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150574	147			0	br	In the \<emph\>Fields \</emph\>dialog, click the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150605	85			0	br	In the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>box, click "Conditional text".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150640	65			0	br	In the \<emph\>Or \</emph\>box, type "There are several pages".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150662				0	br	Meaning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150770				0	br	user_initials				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150797				0	br	user_tel_work				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150820				0	br	Business telephone number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
