helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05190000.xhp	0	help	par_id3083450				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SplitTable\"\>Splits the current table into two separate tables at the cursor position.\</ahelp\> You can also access this command by right-clicking in a table cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05190000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145411				0	br	When you split a table that contains formulas, the formulas may be affected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05190000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148389				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_SPLIT_TABLE:RB_BOX_PARA\"\>Inserts a blank header row in the second table that is formatted with the style of the first row in the original table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05190000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149027				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_SPLIT_TABLE:RB_BOX_NOPARA\"\>Inserts an additional blank row in the second table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05190000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154503				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_SPLIT_TABLE:RB_CNTNT\"\>Includes the first row of the original table as the first row of the second table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05190000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156318				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_SPLIT_TABLE:RB_BORDER\"\>Splits the table without copying the header row.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
