helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145246				0	br	\<variable id=\"kapnum\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ChapterNumberingDialog\"\>Specifies the number format and the hierarchy for chapter numbering in the current document.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147512				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OUTLINE_FORM\"\>Saves or loads an outline number format. A saved outline number format is available to all text documents.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147567	55			0	br	To highlight the screen display of outline numbers, choose \<emph\>View -\</emph\>\<emph\>Field Shadings\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150350				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NUM_OUTL_NAMED_NUMS\"\>Select the predefined numbering style that you want to assign to the selected outline level.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150934				0	br	Outline numbering is linked to paragraph styles. By default, the "Heading" paragraph styles (1-10) are assigned to the corresponding outline number levels (1-10). If you want, you can assign different paragraph styles to the outline number level.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150979				0	br	The \<emph\>Format\</emph\> button is only available for outline numbering. For numbered or bulleted list styles, modify the Numbering Styles of the paragraphs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154200				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_NUM_NAMES:LB_FORM\"\>Click a numbering style in the list, and then enter a name for the style. The numbers correspond to the outline level that the styles are assigned to.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NUM_OUTL_NUM_SAVEAS\"\>Opens a dialog where you can save the current settings for the selected outline level. You can then load these settings from another document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id8237250				0	br	If you want numbered headings, use the \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\> menu command to assign numbering to a paragraph style. Do not use the Numbering icon on the Formatting toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Outline Numbering				2002-02-02 02:02:02
