helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147224				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_OUTLINE_NUM:LB_CHARFMT\"\>Select the format of the numbering character.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147513				0	br	A, B, C, ...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147575				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:TP_OUTLINE_NUM:NF_ALL_LEVEL\"\>Select the number of outline levels to include in the chapter numbering. For example, select "3" to display three levels of chapter numbering: 1.1.1\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148968				0	br	No numbering symbol. Only the character or symbol defined in the \<emph\>Separator\</emph\> fields appears at the beginning of the numbered line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149298				0	br	A,... AA,... AAA,...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149760				0	br	\<emph\>Description\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149820				0	br	Alphabetical numbering with identical lower case letters, where the number of letters indicates the chapter level. For example, the third number in level two is "cc".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150018				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_OUTLINE_NUM:LB_LEVEL\"\>Click the outline level that you want to modify, and then specify the numbering options for the level.\</ahelp\> To apply the numbering options, except for the paragraph style, to all of the levels, click "1-10".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150258				0	br	\<emph\>Selection\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150360				0	br	i, ii, iii, ...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
