helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147170				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:DLG_SORTING:CB_KEY3\"\>Specifies additional sorting criteria. You can also combine sort keys.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149752				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_SORTING:DLB_KEY3\"\>Select the sorting option that you want to use.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150015				0	br	\<variable id=\"sort\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SortDialog\"\>Sorts the selected paragraphs or table rows alphabetically or numerically.\</ahelp\> You can define up to three sort keys as well as combine alphanumeric and numeric sort keys. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150350				0	br	Paragraphs are separated by nonprinting paragraph marks. You can also specify that tabs or a character act as separators when you sort paragraphs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150973				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_SORTING:RB_COL\"\>Sorts the columns in the table according to the current sort options.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151252				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_DLG_SORTING_LB_LANG\"\>Select the language that defines the sorting rules.\</ahelp\> Some languages sort special characters differently than other languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151268	8			0	br	To sort paragraphs, select the \<emph\>Paragraph \</emph\>option in the \<emph\>Separator\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152946				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_SORTING:RB_DN3\"\>Sorts in descending order (for example, 9, 8, 7 or z, y, x).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153677				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_SORTING:RB_ROW\"\>Sorts the rows in the table or the paragraphs in the selection according to the current sort options.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154270				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_SORTING:RB_UP3\"\>Sorts in ascending order, (for example, 1, 2, 3 or a, b, c).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154644				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:DLG_SORTING:ED_KEY3\"\>Enter the number of the table column that you want to use as a basis for sorting.\</ahelp\> The valid number range is 1 to 99.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154838				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_DLG_SORTING_CB_CASE\"\>Distinguishes between uppercase and lowercase letters when you sort a table. For asian languages special handling applies.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_DLG_SORTING_PB_DELIM\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Special Characters\</emph\> dialog, where you can select the character that you want to use as a separator.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155902				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_SORTING:RB_TAB\"\>If the selected paragraphs correspond to a list separated by tabs, select this option.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159196				0	br	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:DLG_SORTING:ED_TABCH\"\>Enter the character that you want to use as a separator in the selected area.\</ahelp\> By using the separator, $[officename] can determine the position of the sorting key in the selected paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10895				0	br	For asian languages, select \<emph\>Match case \</emph\>to apply multi-level collation. In the multi-level collation, the primitive forms of the entries are first compared with the cases of the forms and diacritics ignored. If the forms are the same, the diacritics of the forms are compared. If the forms are still the same, the cases, character widths, and Japanese Kana differences of the forms are compared.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Sort    				2002-02-02 02:02:02
