helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	br	In Writer, you can define borders around OLE objects, plug-ins, diagrams/charts, graphics and frames. The name of the menu to be used depends on the object selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	br	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	4			0	br	Click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>OLE-Object\</emph\> toolbar or \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> toolbar to open the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3150447				0	br	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to Contents\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	br	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	br	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3154071	10			0	br	Replace (object name) with the actual name of the object type you selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	br	Select the object for which you want to define a border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3156344	9			0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - (object name) - Borders\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3159176				0	br	Click one of the predefined border styles. This replaces the current border style of the object with the selected style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
