helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1053498				0	br	Line arrangement area				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1069368				0	br	You can apply a variety of different cell borders to selected cells in a Writer table and to the whole table. Other objects in text documents can have user defined borders, too. For example, you can assign borders to page styles, to frames, and to inserted pictures or charts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1076998				0	br	One cell selected in a table of more that one cell size, or cursor inside a table with no cell selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1108432				0	br	Depending on the selection of cells, the area looks different.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
