helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1820734				0	br	In the \<emph\>User defined\</emph\> area, you can click to set or remove individual lines. The preview shows lines in three different states. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2055421				0	br	Meaning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2210760				0	br	All cells in a Writer table have at least a left and a lower line by default. Most cells on the table perimeter have more lines applied by default. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2316660				0	br	A white line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will be removed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
