helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7741325				0	br	To set a lower border, click the lower edge repeatedly until you see a thick line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8141117				0	br	In the dialog, click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id82399				0	br	The thick gray lines inside an icon show the lines that will not be changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9441206				0	br	Click the second icon from the left to set an outer border and to remove all other lines.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9474166				0	br	A gray line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will not be changed. No line will be set or removed at this position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
