helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149909				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; calculating in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formula bar in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references;in Writer tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149909				0	br	\<variable id=\"calculate\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate.xhp\" name=\"Calculating in Text Documents\"\>Calculating in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149949				0	br	You can insert a calculation directly into a text document or into a text table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149972				0	br	Click in the document where you want to insert the calculation, and then press F2. If you are in a table cell, type an equals sign =.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155547				0	br	Type the calculation that you want to insert, for example, "=10000/12", and then press Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155565				0	br	You can also click the \<emph\>Formula \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Formula Bar\</emph\>, and then choose a function for your formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id8316904				0	br	To reference cells in a Writer text table, enclose the cell address or the cell range in angle brackets. For example, to reference cell A1 from another cell, enter =<A1> into the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Calculating in Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147692				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>pasting;results of formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>clipboard;calculating in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas;pasting results in text documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147692				0	br	\<variable id=\"calculate_clipboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_clipboard.xhp\" name=\" Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document\"\> Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150512	40			0	br	Place the cursor where you want to insert the result of the formula, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154250				0	br	Select the formula in the text. The formula can only contain numbers and operators and cannot contain spaces.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155496	38			0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Calculate\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Plus Sign (+).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155547	41			0	br	If the formula is selected, it is replaced by the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156366				0	br	If your text already contains a formula, for example "12+24*2", $[officename] can calculate, and then paste the result of the formula in your document, without using the \<emph\>Formula Bar\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
