helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153899				0	br	\<variable id=\"calculate_intext2\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intext2.xhp\" name=\"Displaying the Result of a Table Calculation in a Different Table\"\>Displaying the Result of a Table Calculation in a Different Table\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3147776				0	br	If you want, you can format the table to behave as normal text. Insert the table into a frame, and then anchor the frame as a character. The frame remains anchored to the adjacent text when you insert or delete text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150508				0	br	Open a text document, insert a table with multiple columns and rows, and then insert another table consisting of one cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150528				0	br	Enter numbers into some of the cells of the large table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3154250				0	br	You can perform a calculation on cells in one table and display the result in a different table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155532				0	br	Place the cursor in the table with the single cell, and then press F2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155551				0	br	In the \<emph\>Formula Bar\</emph\>, enter the function that you want to perform, for example, "=SUM".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155577				0	br	Click in a cell in the larger table that contains a number, press the plus sign (+), and then click in a different cell containing a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155598				0	br	Press \<emph\>Enter\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Displaying the Result of a Table Calculation in a Different Table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154248				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; across multiple text tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text tables;calculating across\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154248				0	br	\<variable id=\"calculate_multitable\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_multitable.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Across Tables\"\>Calculating Across Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	br	In the \<emph\>Formula Bar\</emph\>, enter the function that you want to perform, for example, "=SUM".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	br	Click in a cell containing a number, press the plus sign (+), and then click in a different cell containing a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147274				0	br	Press \<emph\>Enter\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147773				0	br	You can perform calculations that span across more than one table in a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147795				0	br	Open a text document, insert two tables, and type numbers in a few cells in both tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147815				0	br	Place your cursor in an empty cell in one of the tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
