helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153407				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>page styles; left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>blank pages;left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>empty pages;left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pages; left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; even/odd pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title pages; page styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>First Page page style\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Left Page page style\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>right pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>even/odd pages;formatting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153407				0	br	\<variable id=\"even_odd_sdw\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/even_odd_sdw.xhp\" name=\"Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages\"\>Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id888698				0	br	Suppressing printout of empty pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145267				0	br	Select "Right Page" in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145299				0	br	In the list of page styles, right-click "Right Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145596				0	br	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04010000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Break dialog\"\>Insert Break dialog\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147126				0	br	$[officename] can automatically apply alternating page styles on even (left) and odd pages (right) in your document. For example, you can use page styles to display different headers and footers on even and odd pages. The current page style is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\> at the bottom of the workplace.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	br	If you do not want to have a header or a footer on the title page of your document, apply the "First Page" style to the title page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147772				0	br	To add a footer to one of the page styles, choose\<emph\> Insert - Footer\</emph\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the footer to. In the footer frame, type the text that you want to use as a footer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150526				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Page Styles \</emph\>icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153153				0	br	In the list of page styles, right-click "Left Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153179				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154265				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3155876\" src=\"res/sc05539.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155876\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	br	Select "Left Page" in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155561				0	br	Go to the first page in your document, and double-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles in the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155588				0	br	To add a header to one of the page styles, choose\<emph\> Insert - Header\</emph\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the header to. In the header frame, type the text that you want to use as the header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3394573				0	br	If two even or two odd pages directly follow each other in your document, Writer will insert an empty page by default. You can suppress those automatically generated empty pages from printing and from exporting to PDF.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id7594225				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id8147221				0	br	Remove the check mark from \<emph\>Print automatically inserted blank pages\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
