helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145776				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other \</emph\>and click the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150708				0	br	To quickly open all input fields in a document for editing, press Ctrl+Shift+F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153409				0	br	An input field is a variable that you can click in a document to open a dialog where you can edit the variable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154257				0	br	Click \<emph\>Insert \</emph\>and type the text for the variable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155620				0	br	Click \<emph\>Input field \</emph\>in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155888				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
