helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8568681				0	br	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Writer\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id9908444				0	br	Finding styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1371807				0	br	If you closed the dialog, you can press a key combination (Ctrl+Shift+F) to find the next text without opening the dialog. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1780755				0	br	Unlike searching text, replacing text cannot be restricted to the current selection only.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2164677				0	br	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id24109				0	br	Either click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> or \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2448805				0	br	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2467421				0	br	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2696920				0	br	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3406170				0	br	Finding formats only finds direct character attributes, it does not find attributes applied as part of a style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4159062				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4286935				0	br	Enter the text to search in the \<emph\>Search for \</emph\>text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4377269				0	br	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Writer will show you the next text that is equal to your entry. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found text. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4542985				0	br	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4639728				0	br	Use the small Navigation window to quickly jump to the next object or search text in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4646748				0	br	When you have enabled asian language support under \<emph\>Tools - Options - Language Settings - Languages\</emph\>, the Find & Replace dialog offers options to search asian text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4679403				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5597094				0	br	More options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5684072				0	br	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5781426				0	br	The \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box now is a list box, where you can select any of the Paragraph Styles that are applied in the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id611285				0	br	In text documents you can find words, formatting, styles, and more. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all results at once, then apply another format or replace the words by other text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6417432				0	br	Click the icon with the blue circle at the bottom right part of your document to open the small \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6702780				0	br	To find text within the whole document, open the Find & Replace dialog without any active text selection. If you want to search only a part of your document, first select that part of text, then open the Find & Replace dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id679342				0	br	Select the style to search for, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6957304				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id703451				0	br	When you click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>, Writer will search the whole document for the text in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, starting at the current cursor position. When text is found, Writer highlights the text and waits for your response. Click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> to replace the highlighted text in the document with the text in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box. Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> to advance to the next found text without replacing the current selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7421796				0	br	Use the Navigator for inserting objects, links and references within the same document or from other open documents. See the \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/navigator.xhp\"\>Navigator\</link\> guide for more information.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7540818				0	br	When you click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>, Writer replaces all text that matches your entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7783745				0	br	Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8087405				0	br	You want to find all text in your document to which a certain direct character formatting is assigned. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8413953				0	br	You want to find all text in your document to which a certain Paragraph Style is assigned, for example the "Heading 2" style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8533280				0	br	Check the \<emph\>Similarity search\</emph\> option and optionally click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to change the settings. (Setting all three numbers to 1 works fine for english text.)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id896938				0	br	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9147007				0	br	Check \<emph\>Search for Styles\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id924100				0	br	Alternatively, you can use the icons at the lower right of the document to navigate to the next text or to any other object in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9359416				0	br	When you click \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>, Writer selects all text that is equal to your entry. Now you can for example set all found text to bold, or apply a Character Style to all at once.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9919431				0	br	The similarity search can find text that is almost the same as your search text. You can set the number of characters that are allowed to differ.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9934385				0	br	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects. You can also use the Navigator to move and arrange chapters, providing an outline view to your document. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9959410				0	br	Enter the text to replace the found text in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Finding and Replacing in Writer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145819				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>pages; continuation pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>next page number in footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>continuation pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page numbers; continuation pages\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145819				0	br	\<variable id=\"footer_nextpage\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footer_nextpage.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Page Numbers of Continuation Pages\"\>Inserting Page Numbers of Continuation Pages\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147109				0	br	Place the cursor in the footer and choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147134				0	br	In the \<emph\>Fields\</emph\> dialog, click the \<emph\>Document\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150517				0	br	Click a numbering style in the \<emph\>Format \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537				0	br	If you select 'Text' in the \<emph\>Format\</emph\>, only the text that you enter in the \<emph\>Value\</emph\> box is displayed in the field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150727				0	br	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> to insert the field with the page number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150955				0	br	Click 'Page' in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list and 'Next page' in the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154242				0	br	You can easily insert the page number of the next page in a footer by using a field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	br	The page number is only displayed if the following page exists.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\> and select the page style that you want to add the footer to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Inserting Page Numbers of Continuation Pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155624				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>footers; with page numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pages; numbers and count of\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page numbers; footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbering;pages\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155624				0	br	\<variable id=\"footer_pagenumber\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footer_pagenumber.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Page Numbers in Footers\"\>Inserting Page Numbers in Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3150508				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\> and select the page style that you want to add the footer to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Number\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3153155				0	br	If you want, you can align the Page Number field as you would text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3153169	5			0	br	You can also add a page count to the footer, for example, in the form "Page 9 of 12":				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3155532				0	br	Click in front of the Page Number field and type "Page ", click after the field, enter a space and then type "of ".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3155554				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Count\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Inserting Page Numbers in Footers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145819				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>endnotes;inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;footnotes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>removing;footnotes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>organizing;footnotes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footnotes; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145819				0	br	\<variable id=\"footnote_usage\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footnote_usage.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Footnotes or Endnotes\"\>Inserting and Editing Footnotes or Endnotes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155543				0	br	Editing Footnotes or Endnotes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155881				0	br	To insert a footnote or endnote:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145029				0	br	To change the format of a footnote, click in the footnote, press F11 to open the Styles and Formatting window, right-click "Footnote" in the list, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145062				0	br	To jump from the footnote or endnote text to the note anchor in the text, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>PageUp\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145081				0	br	To edit the numbering properties of a footnote or endnote anchor, click in front of the anchor, and choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02150000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Footnote\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Footnote\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147120				0	br	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04030000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Footnote\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Footnote\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147232				0	br	To remove a footnote, delete the footnote anchor in the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147776				0	br	To change the formatting that $[officename] applies to footnotes and endnotes, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Footnotes\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Footnotes\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147813				0	br	To edit the properties of the text area for footnotes or endnotes, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05040600.xhp\" name=\"Footnote\"\>\<emph\>Footnote\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3148843				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3148857\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertfootnote.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148857\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150119				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3150126\" src=\"res/helpimg/refhand.png\" width=\"8.47mm\" height=\"8.47mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150126\"\>Mouse hand cursor\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150167				0	br	The mouse pointer changes to a hand when you rest it over a footnote or endnote anchor in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150508				0	br	In the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Footnote \</emph\>or \<emph\>Endnote\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150704				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150729				0	br	Type the note.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150937				0	br	In the \<emph\>Numbering \</emph\>area, select the format that you want to use. If you select \<emph\>Character\</emph\>, click the browse button (\<emph\>...\</emph\>) and select the character that you want to use for the footnote.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3153176				0	br	You can also insert footnotes by clicking the \<emph\>Insert Footnote Directly\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	br	Footnotes reference more information about a topic at the bottom of a page and endnotes reference information at the end of the document. $[officename] automatically numbers the footnotes and endnotes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3155563				0	br	To edit the text of a footnote or endnote, click in the note, or click the anchor for the note in the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3155903				0	br	Click in your document where you want to place the anchor of the note.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Inserting and Editing Footnotes or Endnotes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147683				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>spacing; endnotes/footnotes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>endnotes; spacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footnotes; spacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders;for footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines;footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147683				0	br	\<variable id=\"footnote_with_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footnote_with_line.xhp\" name=\"Spacing Between Footnotes\"\>Spacing Between Footnotes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3145808				0	br	If you want to increase the spacing between footnote or endnote texts, you can add a top and bottom border to the corresponding paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147110				0	br	In the \<emph\>Default \</emph\>area, click the \<emph\>Set Top and Bottom Borders Only\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3148846				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Format - Paragraph - Borders\"\>Format - Paragraph - Borders\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150519				0	br	In the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area, clear the \<emph\>Synchronize\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150709				0	br	Enter a value in the \<emph\>Top \</emph\>and \<emph\>Bottom \</emph\>boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150740				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150931				0	br	In the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area, click a line in the \<emph\>Style \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150961				0	br	Select "White" in the \<emph\>Color \</emph\>box. If the background of the page is not white, select the color that best matches the background color.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3154251				0	br	Right-click the Paragraph Style that you want to modify, for example, "Footnote", and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	br	Click in a footnote or endnote.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155620				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155884				0	br	Click the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Borders\"\>\<emph\>Borders\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Spacing Between Footnotes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159257				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>form letters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>mail merge\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>letters; creating form letters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wizards;form letters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159257				0	br	\<variable id=\"form_letters\"\>\<variable id=\"form_letters_main\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/form_letters_main.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Form Letter\"\>Creating a Form Letter\</link\>\</variable\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_id3150502				0	br	To create a form letter, you need a text document that contains fields for address data, and an address database. Then you combine or merge the address data and the text document to either print the letters or send them by e-mail.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10653				0	br	The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/mailmerge00.xhp\"\>Mail Merge Wizard\</link\> helps you to create form letters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10664				0	br	To create a form letter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Mail Merge Wizard\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10672				0	br	You see the Mail Merge Wizard dialog. The following is an example of one of many possible ways to navigate the wizard's pages:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10676				0	br	Select \<emph\>Start from a template\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10681				0	br	You see the Templates dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10685				0	br	Select \<item type=\"literal\"\>Business Correspondence\</item\> in the left list, and then \<item type=\"literal\"\>Modern letter\</item\> in the right list. Click OK to close the Templates dialog, and click Next in the wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BD				0	br	On the next step of the wizard, click the \<emph\>Select Address List\</emph\> button to check that you are using the correct address list. Select an address block type and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	br	Next follows the \<emph\>Create a salutation\</emph\> step. Deselect the \<emph\>Insert personalized salutation\</emph\> box. Under \<emph\>General salutation\</emph\>, select the salutation that you want on top of all letters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D5				0	br	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\> on the following pages of the wizard. The pages are created, and you have the option to edit the created documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Creating a Form Letter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145246				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>master documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subdocuments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>central documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subsidiary documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; master documents and subdocuments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Navigator;master documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; master documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bookmarks; master documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indexes; master documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145246				0	br	\<variable id=\"globaldoc\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/globaldoc.xhp\"\>Using Master Documents and Subdocuments\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	hd_id7904904				0	br	Example of using styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id1590014				0	br	In the master document you now see the new style Style1 from the first subdocument. All Style1 paragraphs in the master document will be shown using the Style1 attributes from the first subdocument. However, the second subdocument by itself will not be changed. You see the Style1 paragraphs from the second subdocument with different attributes, depending whether you open the sub2.odt document by itself or as part of the master document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3149806				0	br	A master document lets you manage large documents, such as a book with many chapters. The master document can be seen as a container for individual \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer files. The individual files are called subdocuments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150096				0	br	When you print a master document, the contents of all subdocuments, indexes, and any text that you entered are printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153400				0	br	You can create a table of contents and index in the master document for all of the subdocuments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154382				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator in master mode\"\>Navigator in master mode\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155180				0	br	When you add a document to a master document or create a new subdocument, a link is created in the master document. You cannot edit the content of a subdocument directly in the master document, but you can use the Navigator to open any subdocument for edit.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	br	Styles that are used in subdocuments, such as new paragraph styles, are automatically imported into the master document after you save the master document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3419598				0	br	Subdocuments never get changed by changes made to the master document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id5817743				0	br	A master document master.odm consists of some text and links to the subdocuments sub1.odt and sub2.odt. In each subdocument a new paragraph style with the same name Style1 is defined and used, and the subdocuments are saved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id5878780				0	br	To avoid confusion, use the same document template for the master document and its subdocuments. This happens automatically when you create the master document and its subdocuments from an existing document with headings, using the command \<emph\>File - Send - Create Master Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id9033783				0	br	When viewing the master document, styles that are already present in the master document take precedence over styles with the same name that are imported from subdocuments. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id9169591				0	br	When you save the master document, the styles from the subdocuments are imported into the master document. First, the new style Style1 from the sub1.odt is imported. Next, the new styles from sub2.odt will be imported, but as Style1 now already is present in the master document, this style from sub2.odt will not be imported. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Using Master Documents and Subdocuments				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145228				0	br	To export a master document as a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> text document:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153127				0	br	To create a master document: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153656				0	br	To start each subdocument on a new page:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145114				0	br	In the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> for master documents (should open automatically, else press F5 to open), click and hold the \<emph\>Insert \</emph\>icon, and do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145205				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145405				0	br	To create a new subdocument, choose \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>, type a name for the file, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Text Flow \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148580				0	br	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> list, select a text document file format and click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148677				0	br	To add text to a master document, right-click an item in the Navigator list, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Text\</emph\>. A text section is inserted before the selected item in the master document where you can type the text that you want. You cannot insert a text section next to another text section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148949				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id3148959\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20246.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148959\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	br	Open an existing document and choose \<emph\>File - Send - Create Master Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149634				0	br	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149770				0	br	In the \<emph\>Breaks \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then select \<emph\>Page \</emph\>in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873				0	br	If you are creating a new master document, the first entry in the Navigator should be a \<emph\>Text \</emph\>entry. Type an introduction or enter some text. This ensures that after you edit an existing style in the master document, you see the changed style when viewing the subdocuments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149956				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Master Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149982				0	br	To reorder the subdocuments in a master document, drag a subdocument to a new location in the Navigator list. You can also select a subdocument in the list, and click the \<emph\>Move down\</emph\> or \<emph\>Move up \</emph\>icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	br	If you want each subdocument to start on an odd page, select \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>, and select "Right page" in the box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3150315				0	br	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Export\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3152760				0	br	Ensure that each subdocument starts with a heading that uses the same paragraph style, for example "Heading 1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153022				0	br	To add an index, such as a table of contents, right-click in the Navigator list, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Index\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153382				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153632				0	br	To update an index in a master document, select the index in the Navigator, and then click the \<emph\>Update\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	br	In the master document, choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153907				0	br	Right-click "Heading 1" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	br	Use the Navigator for rearranging and editing the subdocuments in a master document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3154382				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator in master mode\"\>Navigator in master mode\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3155879				0	br	To open a subdocument for editing, double-click the name of the subdocument in the Navigator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3155931				0	br	To remove a subdocument from the master document, right-click the subdocument in the Navigator list and choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. The subdocument file is not deleted, only the entry in the Navigator is removed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3156240				0	br	To insert an existing file as a subdocument, choose \<emph\>File\</emph\>, locate the file that you want to include, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id8550981				0	br	To insert some text between subdocuments, choose \<emph\>Text\</emph\>. Then type the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C40				0	br	When you insert an object like a frame or a picture into a master document, do not anchor the object "to page". Instead, set the anchor "to paragraph" on the \<emph\>Format - (Object type) - Type\</emph\> tab page, and then set the object's position relative to "Entire Page" in the \<emph\>Horizontal\</emph\> and \<emph\>Vertical\</emph\> list boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155863				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>headers;about\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers;about\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; headers and footers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150704				0	br	Headers and Footers in HTML Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863				0	br	\<variable id=\"header_footer\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_footer.xhp\" name=\"About Headers and Footers\"\>About Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3146876				0	br	To use different headers or footers in your document, you must add them to different \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>, and then apply the styles to the pages where you want the headers or footer to appear.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147119				0	br	To add a footer to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150511				0	br	The page style for the current page is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717	34			0	br	Some of the header and footer options are also available for HTML documents. Headers and footers are not supported by HTML and instead are exported with special tags, so that they can be viewed in a browser. Headers and footers are only exported in HTML documents if they are enabled in Web Layout mode. When you reopen the document in $[officename], the headers and footers are displayed correctly, including any fields that you inserted. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153174				0	br	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	br	You can also choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Header\</emph\> or \<emph\>Footer \</emph\>tab, and then select \<emph\>Header on \</emph\>or \<emph\>Footer on\</emph\>. Clear the \<emph\>Same content left/right\</emph\> check box if you want to define different headers and footers for even and odd pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	br	Headers and footers are areas in the top and the bottom page margins, where you can add text or graphics. Headers and footers are added to the current page style. Any page that uses the same style automatically receives the header or footer that you add. You can insert \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\>, such as page numbers and chapter headings, in headers and footers in a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	br	To add a header to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	About Headers and Footers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155920				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>headers;defining for left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers;defining for left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page styles; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining; headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>mirrored page layout\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155920				0	br	\<variable id=\"header_pagestyles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Defining Different Headers and Footers\"\>Defining Different Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145263				0	br	Double-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles to apply the style to the current page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145284	43			0	br	Enter text or graphics in the header for the Left Page style. After the next page is added to your document, enter text or graphics in the header for the Right Page style. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3146865				0	br	In the \<emph\>Next Style \</emph\>box, select "Left Page".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3146889				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147061				0	br	In the \<emph\>Next Style \</emph\>box, select "Right Page".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147086				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147105				0	br	You can also use the mirrored page layout if you want to add a header to a page style that has different inner and outer page margins. To apply this option to a page style, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, click the\<emph\> Page\</emph\> tab, and in the\<emph\> Layout settings\</emph\> area, choose\<emph\> Mirrored\</emph\> in the\<emph\> Page layout\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	br	For example, you can use page styles to define different headers for even and odd pages in a document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150510				0	br	Right-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150536				0	br	In the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> dialog, click the \<emph\>Header \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150714				0	br	In the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, right-click "Left Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150748				0	br	In the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> dialog, click the \<emph\>Header \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150929				0	br	Open a new text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150946				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon in the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153172				0	br	Select\<emph\> Header on\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	br	Select\<emph\> Header on\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	br	You can use different headers and footers on different pages in your document, so long as the pages use different page styles. $[officename] provides several predefined page styles, such as \<emph\>First page\</emph\>, \<emph\>Left page\</emph\> and \<emph\>Right page\</emph\>, or you can create a custom page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Defining Different Headers and Footers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155919				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>running titles in headers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>floating titles in headers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; chapter information\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chapter names in headers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>names; chapter names in headers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150505				0	br	To insert the chapter name and number in a header or a footer:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154244				0	br	To create a paragraph style for chapter titles:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155919				0	br	\<variable id=\"header_with_chapter\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_with_chapter.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer\"\>Inserting a Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3146863				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the\<emph\> Document\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147065				0	br	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147095				0	br	The header on every page that uses the current page style automatically displays the chapter name and number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124				0	br	Select the numbering style for the chapter titles in the \<emph\>Number \</emph\>box, for example, "1,2,3...".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150219				0	br	Type "Chapter" followed by a space in the \<emph\>Before \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150245				0	br	Enter a space in the \<emph\>After \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150527				0	br	Apply the paragraph style that you defined for chapter titles to the chapter headings in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150949				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153175				0	br	Click "Chapter" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list and "Chapter number and name" in the \<emph\>Format \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	br	Before you can insert chapter information into a header or footer, you must first set the outline numbering options for the paragraph style that you want to use for chapter titles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153729				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Header \</emph\>or \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153762				0	br	Click in the header or footer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155874				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155898				0	br	In the \<emph\>Style \</emph\>box, select the paragraph style that you want to use for chapter titles, for example, "Heading 1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Inserting a Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154866				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>inserting; lines under headers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines; under headers/above footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers;formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers;formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>shadows;headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders;for headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
