helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145108				0	br	To hide the variable in your document, select \<emph\>Invisible\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145391				0	br	Click in the document where you want to add the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145409	5			0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147011				0	br	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Section\"\>Insert - Section\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147029				0	br	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\" name=\"List of Operators\"\>List of Operators\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3148603				0	br	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Fields - Other\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3148697				0	br	Select the text that you want to hide in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3148950				0	br	In the\<emph\> Hide\</emph\> area, select\<emph\> Hide\</emph\>, and then enter an expression in the\<emph\> Condition\</emph\> box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter "Hide==1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149585				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149620				0	br	Type a name for the variable in the \<emph\>Name \</emph\>box, for example, "Hide".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149640	21			0	br	Click the \<emph\>Variables \</emph\>tab and click "Set Variable" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149869				0	br	Enter a value for the variable in the \<emph\>Value \</emph\>box, for example, "1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149970	22			0	br	Click "General" in the \<emph\>Format \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149991				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	br	You can use fields and sections to hide or display text in your document if a condition is met.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153019				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153131				0	br	Click in your document and choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153371	31			0	br	Type the text that you want to hide in the \<emph\>Hidden text \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153409				0	br	Before you can hide text, you must first create a variable to use in the condition for hiding the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153636				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154404				0	br	Enter a statement in the \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter "Hide==1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154853				0	br	Click in the paragraph where you want to add the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154872	35			0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155325	29			0	br	Click "Hidden Text" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155902	6			0	br	Click "Hidden Paragraph" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155947				0	br	Enter a statement in the \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter "Hide==1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3793450				0	br	You must enable this feature by removing the check mark from menu \<emph\>View - Hidden Paragraphs\</emph\>. When the check mark is set, you cannot hide any paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
