helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3148846				0	br	On the Standard bar, click the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635				0	br	The name of the item is inserted in the document as an underlined hyperlink.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149833				0	br	Open the document(s) containing the items you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153133				0	br	Drag the item to where you want to insert the hyperlink in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	br	In the list at the bottom of the Navigator, select the document containing the item that you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	br	In the Navigator list, click the plus sign next to the item that you want to insert as a hyperlink.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	br	You can insert a cross-reference as a hyperlink in your document using the Navigator. You can even cross-reference items from other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> documents. If you click the hyperlink when the document is opened in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>, you are taken to the cross-referenced item.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156108				0	br	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Drag Mode\</emph\> icon, and ensure that \<emph\>Insert as Hyperlink \</emph\>is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3147036	29			0	br	To quickly exclude a word from hyphenation, select the word, choose \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Font \</emph\>tab, and select "None" in the \<emph\>Language \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3147125				0	br	If the list is empty, click \<emph\>New\</emph\> to create a dictionary.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3150218	42			0	br	In the\<emph\> Word\</emph\> box, type the word you want to exclude from hyphenation, followed by an equal sign (=), for example, "pretentious=".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3150247				0	br	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3153634	40			0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - Language Settings - Writing Aids\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3153658	41			0	br	Select a dictionary in the \<emph\>User-defined dictionary \</emph\>list, and then click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
