helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149689				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; defining entries in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; defining entries in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entries; defining in indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147119				0	br	Defining Table of Contents Entries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149689				0	br	\<variable id=\"indices_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_enter.xhp\" name=\"Defining Index or Table of Contents Entries\"\>Defining Index or Table of Contents Entries\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150230				0	br	To use a custom paragraph style as a table of contents entry:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155862				0	br	Defining Index Entries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147132				0	br	The best way to generate a table of contents is to apply the predefined heading paragraph styles, such as "Heading 1", to the paragraphs that you want to include in your table of contents. You can also use custom paragraph styles, so long as you assign them one of the predefined outline levels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147409				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Entry\</emph\>, and do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150523				0	br	In the \<emph\>Level\</emph\> list, click the hierarchical level that you want to apply the paragraph style to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150933				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Numbering\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150964				0	br	Select the paragraph style that you want to include in your table of contents in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153417				0	br	To change the text that appears in the index, type the text that you want in the \<emph\>Entry\</emph\> box. The text that you type here does not replace the selected text in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153730	17			0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You can now apply the style to headings in your document and include them in your table of contents. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	br	To add an index mark to similar words in your document, select \<emph\>Apply to all similar texts\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155889				0	br	To add the entries to a custom index, click the \<emph\>New User-defined Index\</emph\> icon, enter the name of the index, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156380				0	br	Click in a word, or select the words in your document that you want to use as an index entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Defining Index or Table of Contents Entries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155855				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; index format\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entries; in tables of contents, as hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; hyperlinks as entries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; in tables of contents and indexes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;indexes and tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146878				0	br	To assign hyperlinks to entries in a table of contents:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155855				0	br	\<variable id=\"indices_form\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_form.xhp\" name=\"Formatting an Index or a Table of Contents\"\>Formatting an Index or a Table of Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155888				0	br	To apply a different paragraph style to an index level:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3146890				0	br	You can assign a cross-reference as a hyperlink to entries in a table of contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147060				0	br	Repeat for each heading level that you want to create hyperlinks for, or click the \<emph\>All levels\</emph\> button to apply the formatting to all levels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147110				0	br	Right-click in the index or table of contents, and then choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147135	46			0	br	Click the \<emph\>Styles \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3148399				0	br	Click the heading level that you want to assign hyperlinks to in the \<emph\>Level \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3148424	53			0	br	In the \<emph\>Structure \</emph\>area, click in the box in front of \<emph\>E#\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150229	47			0	br	Click an index level in the \<emph\>Levels \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150516				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150712				0	br	Right-click in the table of contents, and then choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150738				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Entries\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150934	48			0	br	Click the style that you want to apply in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150960				0	br	Click the assign button \<emph\><\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3153171				0	br	Click in the box behind the \<emph\>E\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3154259				0	br	You can apply different paragraph styles, assign hyperlinks to entries, change the layout of indexes, and change the background color of indexes in the \<emph\>Insert Index\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Formatting an Index or a Table of Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155911				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>concordance files;indexes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indexes; alphabetical indexes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>alphabetical indexes\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155911				0	br	\<variable id=\"indices_index\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_index.xhp\" name=\"Creating Alphabetical Indexes\"\>Creating Alphabetical Indexes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3147114				0	br	If you want to use a concordance file, select \<emph\>Concordance file\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Options \</emph\>area, click the \<emph\>File\</emph\>, and then locate an existing file or create a new concordance file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223	28			0	br	Set the formatting options for the index, either on the current tab, or on any of the other tabs of this dialog. For example, if you want to use single letter headings in your index, click the \<emph\>Entries\</emph\> tab, and then select \<emph\>Alphabetical delimiter\</emph\>. To change the formatting of levels in the index, click the \<emph\>Styles\</emph\> tab. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3150502				0	br	To update the index, right-click in the index, and then choose \<emph\>Update Index/Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3150946				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3152760				0	br	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120250.xhp\" name=\"Creating a concordance file\"\>Creating a concordance file\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	br	Click in your document where you want to insert the index.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3154252				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3155884				0	br	On the \<emph\>Index/Table\</emph\> tab, select "Alphabetical Index" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Creating Alphabetical Indexes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
