helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156383				0	br	\<variable id=\"number_date_conv\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/number_date_conv.xhp\" name=\"Turning Number Recognition On or Off in Tables\"\>Turning Number Recognition On or Off in Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3149966				0	br	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040500.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Text Document - Table\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3155179				0	br	$[officename] can automatically format dates that you have entered into a table, according to the regional settings specified in your operating system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3155527				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</emph\>, and select or clear the \<emph\>Number recognition \</emph\>check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3155919				0	br	Right-click in a table cell and choose \<emph\>Number recognition\</emph\>. When this feature is on, a check mark is displayed in front of the \<emph\>Number recognition \</emph\>command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Turning Number Recognition On or Off in Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>number ranges; defining for similar items\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbering;quotations\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	br	\<variable id=\"number_sequence\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/number_sequence.xhp\" name=\"Defining Number Ranges\"\>Defining Number Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	par_id3149829				0	br	Type the text that you want to assign numbering to, for example, "Quotation Number ".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	br	Type "Quotation" in the \<emph\>Name \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	par_id3153387				0	br	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	par_id3154250				0	br	Type a number in the \<emph\>Value \</emph\>box, or leave the box empty to use automatic numbering.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	par_id3154851	58			0	br	Select the outline level where you want the numbering to restart in the \<emph\>Level \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	par_id3155048				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Variables \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	br	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	par_id3155918				0	br	You can automatically number similar items, such as quotations, in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	par_id3156240				0	br	Click "Number range" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Defining Number Ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150101				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>line numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; line numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines in text; numbering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbering; lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; line numbering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>marginal numbers on text pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;line numbers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146880				0	br	To specify the starting line number:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150101				0	br	\<variable id=\"numbering_lines\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/numbering_lines.xhp\" name=\"Adding Line Numbers\"\>Adding Line Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153410				0	br	To add line numbers to an entire document:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156241				0	br	To add line numbers to specific paragraphs:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3145101				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3146864				0	br	You can also create a paragraph style that includes line numbering, and apply it to the paragraphs that you want to add line numbers to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3148389				0	br	Select the \<emph\>Include this paragraph in line numbering \</emph\>check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3148414				0	br	Select \<emph\>Restart at the paragraph \</emph\>check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	br	Select \<emph\>Show numbering\</emph\>, and then select the options that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3149640				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Line Numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3149842				0	br	$[officename] can automatically count and add line numbers to the lines in an entire document or to selected paragraphs in your document. Line numbers are included when you print your document, but not when you save the document as HTML. You can specify the line numbering interval, the starting line number, and whether to count blank lines or lines in frames. You can also add a separator between line numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150222				0	br	All paragraph styles are based on the "Default" style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150520				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150703				0	br	Click in a paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150721				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Numbering \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150931				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Numbering\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150956				0	br	In the \<emph\>Line Numbering \</emph\>area, clear the \<emph\>Include this paragraph in line numbering \</emph\>check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3151077				0	br	Select the paragraph(s) where you want to add the line numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3151096				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Numbering \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153385				0	br	Select \<emph\>Show numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153733				0	br	Select \<emph\>Include this paragraph in line numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153758				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153779				0	br	Enter a line number in the \<emph\>Start with \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153804				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153934				0	br	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06180000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Line Numbering\"\>Tools - Line Numbering\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153960				0	br	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030800.xhp\" name=\"Format - Paragraph - Numbering\"\>Format - Paragraph - Numbering\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	br	Press F11 to open the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, and then click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3154853				0	br	Right-click the "Default" paragraph style and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3156264				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Line Numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id7184972				0	br	Line numbers are not available in HTML format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Adding Line Numbers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149637				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>numbering; removing/interrupting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bullet lists; interrupting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists;removing/interrupting numbering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>removing;numbers in lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>interrupting numbered lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;starting numbers in lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>modifying;numbering in lists\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145107				0	br	To remove the number from a paragraph in a numbered list:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149637				0	br	\<variable id=\"numbering_paras\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/numbering_paras.xhp\" name=\"Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List\"\>Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154856				0	br	To change the number that a numbered list starts with:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id2172612				0	br	If you want numbered headings, use the \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\> menu command to assign a numbering to a paragraph style. Do not use the Numbering icon on the Formatting toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3145092				0	br	You can remove the numbering from a paragraph in a numbered list or change the number that a numbered list starts with.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3147116				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3148691	22			0	br	Enter the number you want the list to start with in the \<emph\>Start at\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3153366				0	br	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3153390				0	br	To remove the number while preserving the indent of the paragraph, press the Backspace key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	br	To remove the number and the indent of the paragraph, click the \<emph\>Numbering on/off\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> Bar. If you save the document in HTML format, a separate numbered list is created for the numbered paragraphs that follow the current paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3155877				0	br	Click anywhere in the numbered list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3156248				0	br	Click in front of the first character of the paragraph that you want to remove the numbering from.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155183				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>page breaks; inserting and deleting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; page breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;page breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pages; inserting/deleting page breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>manual page breaks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149624				0	br	To delete a manual page break that occurs before a table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149833				0	br	To insert a manual page break:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153135				0	br	To delete a manual page break:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155183				0	br	\<variable id=\"page_break\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/page_break.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Deleting Page Breaks\"\>Inserting and Deleting Page Breaks\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3145111				0	br	Right-click in the table, and choose \<emph\>Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3149608				0	br	Press Backspace.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641				0	br	Click in front of the first character on the page that follows the manual page break.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3153119				0	br	Press Ctrl+Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3153380				0	br	Clear the \<emph\>Break\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3153402				0	br	Click in your document where you want the new page to begin.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3154249				0	br	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04010000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Break dialog\"\>Insert Break dialog\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3156254				0	br	Click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05090300.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>\<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Inserting and Deleting Page Breaks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	bm_id8431653				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>page backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page styles;backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds; different pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;page backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pages;backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	br	\<variable id=\"pagebackground\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagebackground.xhp\"\>Changing Page Background\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10812				0	br	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the background of the pages in a document. For example, to change the page background of one or more pages in a document to a watermark, you need to create a page style that uses the watermark background, and then apply the page style to the pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10820				0	br	To Change the Page Background				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10827				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	br	In the list of page styles, right-click an item, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1083F				0	br	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab page, type a name for the page style in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084B				0	br	In the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, select the page style that you want to apply to the next page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10855				0	br	To only apply the new page style to a single page, select "Default".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10859				0	br	To apply the new page style to all subsequent pages, select the name of the new page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1085F				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10867				0	br	In the list box at the top, select whether you want a solid color or a graphic. Then select your options from the tab page. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1086B				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1087A				0	br	To Change the Page Background of All Pages in a Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1087E				0	br	Before you begin, ensure that you have created a page style that uses a page background. See \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagebackground.xhp#define\"\>To Change the Page Background\</link\> for details.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10892				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1089A				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A2				0	br	Double-click the page style that uses the page background that you want to apply.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A5				0	br	To Use Different Page Backgrounds in the Same Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A9				0	br	Before you begin, ensure that you have created a page style that uses a page background. See \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagebackground.xhp#define\"\>To Change the Page Background\</link\> for details.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108BD				0	br	Click in front of the first character of the paragraph where you want to change the page background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C1				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C9				0	br	Select \<emph\>Page break\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D1				0	br	In the \<emph\>Style \</emph\>box, select a page style that uses the page background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108DB				0	br	To change the background of the current page only, select a page style where the Next Style option is set to "Default".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108DF				0	br	To change the background of the current and subsequent pages, select a page style where the Next Style option is set to the name of the page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E2				0	br	If you want to change the page background later on in the document, repeat steps 1 to 3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E8				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Changing Page Backgrounds				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id5918759				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>page numbers;inserting/defining/formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page styles;page numbering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>starting page numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;page numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;starting page numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;page numbers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id2551652				0	br	Starting with a defined page number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id413830				0	br	\<variable id=\"pagenumbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagenumbers.xhp\" name=\"Page Numbers\"\>Page Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id5051728				0	br	Using different page number styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id5298318				0	br	To apply a manually inserted Page Style change				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id6091494				0	br	Inserting page numbers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id7519150				0	br	Formatting the page number style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id9364909				0	br	To apply a different page style to the first page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1541184				0	br	In Writer, you will need different Page Styles. The first Page Style has a footer with a page number field formatted for roman numbers. The following Page Style has a footer with a page number field formatted in another look.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1558885				0	br	You need some pages with the roman numbering style, followed by the remaining pages in another style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1617175				0	br	In Writer, a page number is a field that you can insert into your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1654408				0	br	The new page number is an attribute of the first paragraph of the page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id18616				0	br	Both Page Styles must be separated by a page break. In Writer, you can have automatic page breaks and manually inserted page breaks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1911679				0	br	It depends on your document what is best: to use a manually inserted page break between Page Styles, or to use an automatic change. If you just need one title page with a different style than the other pages, you can use the automatic method:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2318796				0	br	Now your title page has the style "First Page", and the next pages automatically have the "Default" style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2632831				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Text flow\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2678914				0	br	However, these fields will change position when you add or remove text. So it is best to insert the page number field into a header or footer that has the same position and that is repeated on every page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id291451				0	br	A \<emph\>manually inserted page break\</emph\> can be applied without or with a change of page styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3032319				0	br	Double-click directly before the page number field. You see the \<emph\>Edit Fields\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3341776				0	br	If you just press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\>, you apply a page break without a change of styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3496200				0	br	In the Style list box, select a Page Style. You may set a new page number, too. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id399182				0	br	You can now for example insert a footer for the "Default" Page Style only, or insert footers to both Page Styles, but with differently formatted page number fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4191717				0	br	Double-click the "First Page" style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4313791				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4331797				0	br	In the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4395275				0	br	In the Breaks area, enable \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. Enable \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\> just to be able to set the new \<emph\>Page number\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4473403				0	br	Click into the first page of your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4569231				0	br	For example, the "First Page" Page Style has "Default" as the next style. To see this, you may press F11 to open the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon, right-click the First Page entry. Choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> from the context menu. On the Organizer tab, you can see the "next style".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5757621				0	br	Click into the first paragraph of your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5947141				0	br	If you choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual break\</emph\>, you can insert a page break without or with a change of style or with a change of page number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6111941				0	br	Now you want some more control on page numbers. You are writing a text document that should start with page number 12.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6138492				0	br	An \<emph\>automatic page break\</emph\> appears at the end of a page when the Page Style has a different "next style".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id614642				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Header - (name of page style)\</emph\> or \<emph\>Insert - Footer - (name of page style)\</emph\> to add a header or footer to all pages with the current Page Style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6604510				0	br	If you see the text "Page number" instead of the number, choose \<emph\>View - Field names\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id7588732				0	br	Click at the start of the first paragraph on the page where a different Page Style will be applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id7599108				0	br	The selected page style will be used from the current paragraph to the next page break with style. You may need to create the new Page Style first, see .				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id8611102				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Number\</emph\> to insert a page number at the current cursor position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id9029206				0	br	You want roman page numbers running i, ii, iii, iv, and so on.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id9139378				0	br	Select a number format and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
