helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2962126				0	br	To change the page orientation only for the current page, you first need a page style, then apply that style:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id5256508				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7069002				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7524033				0	br	To change the page orientation for all pages that use the current page style:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7994323				0	br	Under \<emph\>Paper format\</emph\>, select \<emph\>Portrait\</emph\> or \<emph\>Landscape\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id9681997				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FF				0	br	\<variable id=\"pageorientation\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pageorientation.xhp\"\>Changing Page Orientation\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071D				0	br	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the orientation of the pages in a document. For example, to change the page orientation of one or more pages in a document from portrait to landscape in a document, you need to create a page style that uses the landscape orientation, and then apply the page style to the pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10727				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10741				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	br	Right-click, and choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	br	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab page, type a name for the page style in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box, for example "My Landscape".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075D				0	br	In the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, select the page style that you want to apply to the next page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10775				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077D				0	br	Under \<emph\>Paper format\</emph\>, select \<emph\>Portrait\</emph\> or \<emph\>Landscape\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AE				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
