helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156109				0	br	To define a new page style:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145110				0	br	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147122				0	br	Click in the document where you want a new page to start.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	br	Double-click a name in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149614				0	br	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab, type a name in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641				0	br	In the list of page styles, right-click an item, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846				0	br	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the layout of a page, including the page orientation, background, margins, headers, footers, and text columns. To change the layout of an individual page in a document, you must create and apply a custom page style to the page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150235				0	br	Select \<emph\>Page break\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150939				0	br	In the \<emph\>Style \</emph\>box, select the page style that you want to apply to the page that follows the manual break.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150965				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153133				0	br	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153376				0	br	To apply the custom page style to more than one page, select its name in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box. To stop using the style, insert a manual page break and assign it a different page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153411	3			0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting.\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154252				0	br	Use the tabs in the dialog to set the layout options for the page style, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154873				0	br	Click in the page that you want to apply the page style to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3155888				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the\<emph\> Page Style\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3156252				0	br	To apply the custom page style to a single page, select the default page style that is used in your document in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
