helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	br	Select the text. Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section - Section\</emph\>, then under \<emph\>Write protection\</emph\> mark the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> and \<emph\>With password\</emph\> check boxes. (If the section already exists: \<emph\>Format - Sections\</emph\>.) Enter and confirm a password of at least 5 characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145643				0	br	Place the cursor in a cell or select cells. Right-click to open the context menu, then choose \<emph\>Cell - Protect\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145767				0	br	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147173				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Sections - Section\</emph\> and under \<emph\>Write protection\</emph\> clear the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> check box. Enter the correct password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147322				0	br	Use Shift+Ctrl+T to remove protection for the entire current table or all selected tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147497				0	br	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148463	49			0	br	Place the cursor in the index. First of all, if necessary, under \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids \</emph\>, mark \<emph\>Cursor in protected areas - Enable\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042				0	br	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150592				0	br	Any section of a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text document can be protected against changes with a password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3151189				0	br	Select the table in the Navigator, open the context menu and select \<emph\>Table - Unprotect\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152774				0	br	In the Navigator, select the index, then open the context menu in the Navigator and select \<emph\>Index - Read-only\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152968				0	br	From the context menu choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>. On the Index/Table tab page, unmark \<emph\>Protected against manual changes\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153786				0	br	Place the cursor in the index/table of contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153966				0	br	Tables of contents and indexes created automatically in a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text are automatically protected against accidental changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154118				0	br	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360				0	br	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480				0	br	You can protect the contents of individual cells of a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text table from changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178				0	br	Place the cursor in the cell or select the cells. First, if necessary, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\> and mark \<emph\>Cursor in protected areas - Enable\</emph\>. Then right-click the cell to open the context menu, choose \<emph\>Cell - Unprotect\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3159088				0	br	From the context menu choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>. On the Index/Table tab page, mark \<emph\>Protected against manual changes\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413				0	br	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id363170				0	br	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the cells against accidential changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id4545426				0	br	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the section against accidential changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id814539				0	br	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the contents against accidential changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145087				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>references; inserting cross-references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-references; inserting and updating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>OLE objects;cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145087				0	br	\<variable id=\"references\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/references.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Cross-References\"\>Inserting Cross-References\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149833				0	br	Cross-Referencing Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149980				0	br	Cross-Referencing an Object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151115				0	br	Updating Cross-References				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153370				0	br	To create a cross-reference to a target:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156105				0	br	To insert a target:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3145110				0	br	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. The name of the target is added to the \<emph\>Selection \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3147123				0	br	Click in the document where you want to insert the cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	br	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\> when finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149614				0	br	Type a name for the target in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box. The selected text is displayed in the \<emph\>Value\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149634				0	br	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select \<emph\>Set Reference\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846				0	br	Before you can insert a cross-reference, you must first specify the targets in your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149992				0	br	You can cross-reference most objects in your document, such as graphics, drawing objects, OLE objects, and tables, so long as they have a caption. To add a caption to an object, select the object, and then choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Caption\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150212				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150236				0	br	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select the caption category of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150535				0	br	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150942				0	br	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list, select the caption number of the object that you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150968				0	br	In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list, select the format of the cross-reference. The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"format\"\>format\</link\> specifies the type of information that is displayed as the cross-reference. For example, "Reference" inserts the caption category and caption text of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3151092				0	br	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\> when finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153125				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153392				0	br	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select "Insert Reference".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153408				0	br	Select the text that you want to use as a target for the cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153594				0	br	To manually update the cross-references in a document, press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	br	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list, select the target that you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3154856				0	br	In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list, select the format for the cross-reference. The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"format\"\>format\</link\> specifies the type of information that is displayed as the cross-reference. For example, "Reference" inserts the target text, and "Page" inserts the page number where the target is located.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3155860				0	br	Objects with captions and bookmarks can be used as targets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	br	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	br	Leave the dialog open and proceed to the next section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3159263				0	br	Cross-references allow you to jump to specific text passages and objects in a single document. A cross-reference consists of a target and a reference that are inserted as \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields.xhp\" name=\"fields\"\>fields\</link\> in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Inserting Cross-References				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149291				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>references; modifying cross-references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-references; modifying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>searching;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149291				0	br	\<variable id=\"references_modify\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/references_modify.xhp\" name=\"Modifying Cross-References\"\>Modifying Cross-References\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	par_id3145101				0	br	Set the options that you want, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	par_id3149632				0	br	If you cannot see the field shading of the cross-reference, choose \<emph\>View - Field Shadings\</emph\> or press \<emph\>Ctrl+F8\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	par_id3153132				0	br	Click in front of the cross-reference that you want to modify.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	br	Use the arrow buttons in the \<emph\>Edit Fields \</emph\>dialog to browse through the cross-references in the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Modifying Cross-References				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	bm_id4825891				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>rows; register-true text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines of text; register-true\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pages;register-true\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs;register-true\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>register-true;pages and paragraphs\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spacing;register-true text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;register-true text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10652				0	br	\<variable id=\"registertrue\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/registertrue.xhp\"\>Printing Register-true\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065E				0	br	Setting a document to register-true printing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10665				0	br	Select the whole document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10669				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page - Page\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	br	Select the \<emph\>Register-true\</emph\> checkbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10678				0	br	All the paragraphs in the document will be printed register-true, unless otherwise specified.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067B				0	br	Exempting paragraphs from register-true printing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	br	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10685				0	br	Select all the paragraphs you want to exempt, then choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068C				0	br	Open the Styles and Formatting window, click the Paragraph Style you want to exempt, right-click that style, choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. In the dialog, click the \<emph\>Indents & Spacing\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10698				0	br	Clear the \<emph\>Register-true\</emph\> checkbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AA				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030100.xhp\"\>Register-true\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Printing Register-true				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149687				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>hard returns in pasted text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraph marks;finding & replacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>line breaks;removing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>removing; line breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copies;removing line breaks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155916				0	br	\<variable id=\"removing_line_breaks\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/removing_line_breaks.xhp\"\>Removing Line Breaks\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145093				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	br	Select the text containing the line breaks that you want to remove.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149645				0	br	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, ensure that \<emph\>Combine single line paragraphs if length greater than 50%\</emph\> is selected. To change the minimum percentage for the line length, double-click the option in the list, and then enter a new percentage.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153138	5			0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect.\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153388				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - AutoFormat - Apply\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153413	3			0	br	This AutoFormat feature only works on text that is formatted with the "Default" paragraph style. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	br	Use the AutoFormat feature to remove line breaks that occur within sentences. Unwanted line breaks can occur when you copy text from another source and paste it into a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156253				0	br	In the \<emph\>Apply Style \</emph\>box on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> bar, choose \<emph\>Default\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Removing Line Breaks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149963				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>formats; resetting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>font attributes; resetting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fonts; resetting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resetting; fonts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>direct formatting;exiting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;exiting direct formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exiting direct formatting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149963				0	br	\<variable id=\"reset_format\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/reset_format.xhp\" name=\"Resetting Font Attributes\"\>Resetting Font Attributes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3154091				0	br	You can quickly exit manual formatting by pressing the right-arrow key. For example, if you are pressed Ctrl+B to apply the bold typeface to the text that you type, press the right arrow to return to the default character format of the paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	br	To reset all direct formatting of existing text, select that text, then choose the menu command \<emph\>Format - Default Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Resetting Font Attributes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\resize_navigator.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145088				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>Navigator;docking and resizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Styles and Formatting window;docking and resizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Gallery;docking and resizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>docking; Navigator window\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resizing;windows\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\resize_navigator.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145088				0	br	\<variable id=\"resize_navigator\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/resize_navigator.xhp\" name=\"Docking and Resizing Windows\"\>Docking and Resizing Windows\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\resize_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	br	To dock or undock the Navigator or the Styles and Formatting window, hold down the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl\</item\> key and double-click on a gray area in the window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\resize_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3155916				0	br	You can dock, undock and resize most $[officename] program windows such as the Navigator or the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\resize_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3156096				0	br	To resize the window, drag a corner or an edge of the window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\resize_navigator.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Docking and Resizing Windows				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	bm_id8186284				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>rulers;using rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>horizontal rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>vertical rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indent settings on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;indents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page margins on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table cells;adjusting the width on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adjusting page margins and cell widths\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149038				0	br	Changing Indents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149686				0	br	Adjusting Page Margins				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3145769				0	br	To change the first line indent of a selected paragraph, drag the top left triangle on the horizontal ruler to a new location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	br	You can also double-click anywhere on the horizontal ruler, and adjust the indents in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030000.xhp\" name=\"Paragraph\"\>\<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3152776	26			0	br	To change the left or the right paragraph indent, select the paragraph(s) that you want change the indent for, drag the bottom left or the bottom right triangle on the horizontal ruler to a new location. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3153631				0	br	Indents are adjusted with the three small triangles on the horizontal ruler.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3155175				0	br	The margins of a page are indicated by the filled areas at the ends of the rulers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	br	\<variable id=\"ruler\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/ruler.xhp\"\>Using Rulers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067D				0	br	To show or hide rulers, choose \<emph\>View - Ruler\</emph\>. To show the vertical ruler, choose \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040200.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Writer - View\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - View\</emph\>\</link\>, and then select \<emph\>Vertical ruler\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Ruler\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Using Rulers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150099				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>searching; with wildcards\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>regular expressions;searching\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wildcards; searching in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples for regular expressions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150099				0	br	\<variable id=\"search_regexp\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/search_regexp.xhp\"\>Using Wildcards in Text Searches\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153401				0	br	Regular Expression Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id2142399				0	br	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149609				0	br	The wildcard combination to search for zero or more occurrences of any character is a period and asterisk (.*).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641				0	br	The wildcard for a single character is a period (.).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149843				0	br	In the \<emph\>Search for \</emph\>box, type the search term and the wildcard(s) that you want to use in your search.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149854				0	br	The wildcard for the end of a paragraph is a dollar sign ($). The wildcard character combination for the start of a paragraph is a caret and a period (^.).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149875				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100001.xhp\" name=\"List of Wildcards\"\>List of Wildcards\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3153136				0	br	The wildcard for zero or more occurrences of the previous character is an asterisk. For example: "123*" finds "12" "123", and "1233".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	br	You can only search for regular expressions within the same paragraph. That is, you cannot search for one term in a paragraph and a different term in the next paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182				0	br	You can use wildcards when you find and replace text in a document. For example, "s.n" finds "sun" and "son".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	br	Select the \<emph\>Regular expressions\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	br	Click \<emph\>Find \</emph\>or\<emph\> Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Using Wildcards in Text Searches				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149816				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>sections; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>read-only sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>protecting;sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;sections, into normal text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;sections\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149816				0	br	\<variable id=\"section_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/section_edit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Sections\"\>Editing Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149609				0	br	To hide a section, select the \<emph\>Hide \</emph\>check box in the \<emph\>Hide \</emph\>area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149631				0	br	To make a section read-only, select the \<emph\>Protected \</emph\>check box in the \<emph\>Write Protection \</emph\>area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149848				0	br	In the \<emph\>Section \</emph\>list, click the section you want to modify.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874	21			0	br	Set the other options that you want, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153120				0	br	To convert a section into normal text, click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153397				0	br	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154224				0	br	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02170000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Sections\"\>\<emph\>Format - Sections\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	br	You can protect, hide, and convert sections to normal text in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3156255				0	br	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02170000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Sections\"\>Format - Sections\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Editing Sections				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>sections; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents;inserting linked sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;linked sections, manually\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links;inserting sections\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149635				0	br	To insert a section as a link:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	br	\<variable id=\"section_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/section_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Sections\"\>Inserting Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863				0	br	To insert a new section:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145104				0	br	Click in your document where you want to insert the linked section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	br	When you open a document that contains linked sections, $[officename] prompts you to update the contents of the sections. To manually update a link, choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - Links\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149648				0	br	Before you can insert a section as link, you must first create sections in the source document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149843				0	br	Click in your document where you want to insert a new section, or select the text that you want to convert to a section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149860				0	br	You can also insert linked sections in HTML documents. When you view the page in a web browsers, the content of the sections corresponds to the content of the sections at the time the HTML document was last saved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149978				0	br	In the \<emph\>Section \</emph\>box, select the section that you want to insert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150003				0	br	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	br	Set the options for the section, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	br	In the \<emph\>New Section \</emph\>box, type a name for the section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153387				0	br	In the \<emph\>Link \</emph\>area, select the \<emph\>Link \</emph\>check box. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>Under Windows, you can also select the \<emph\>DDE\</emph\> check box to automatically update the contents of the section when the section in the source document is changed. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153404				0	br	In the \<emph\>New Section \</emph\>box, type a name for the section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154852				0	br	Click the browse button (\<emph\>...\</emph\>) next to the \<emph\>File name \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155882				0	br	Locate the document containing the section that you want to link to, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155917				0	br	You can insert new sections, or links to sections in other documents into the current document. If you insert a section as a link, the content of the link changes when you modify the source document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156103				0	br	If you select a text that occurs within a paragraph, the text is automatically converted into a new paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156241				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Inserting Sections				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149832				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>multicolumn text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; multicolumn\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; on text pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sections; remarks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text sections;using\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sections; columns in\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149832				0	br	\<variable id=\"sections\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/sections.xhp\" name=\"Using Sections\"\>Using Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154242				0	br	Sections and Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149284				0	br	To prevent text from being edited.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	br	To insert sections of text that uses a different column layout than the current page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149630				0	br	To show or hide text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149647				0	br	To reuse text and graphics from other $[officename] documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149855				0	br	A section contains at least one paragraph. When you select a text and create a section, a paragraph break is automatically inserted at the end of the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	br	You can insert sections from a text document, or an entire text document as a section into another text document. You can also insert sections from a text document as links in another text document, or in the same document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3153128				0	br	Sections are named blocks of text, including graphics or objects, that you can use in a number of ways:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3153367	39			0	br	To insert a new paragraph immediately before or after a section, click in front or behind the section, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	br	You can insert sections into an existing section. For example, you can insert a section containing two columns into a section that contains one column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3154845				0	br	A section layout, for example on the number of columns, has priority over the page layout defined in a page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3155883				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#dde\" name=\"DDE\"\>DDE\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Using Sections				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\select_language.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152443				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>languages; recognition of\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recognition of languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spellcheck;activating for all languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>checking spelling;all languages\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\select_language.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152443	33			0	br	\<variable id=\"select_language\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/select_language.xhp\" name=\"Checking Spelling in Other Languages\"\>Checking Spelling in Other Languages\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\select_language.xhp	0	help	par_id3149643	39			0	br	Activate the AutoSpellcheck icon in the Standard bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\select_language.xhp	0	help	par_id3153122	35			0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - Language Settings - Writing Aids\</emph\>, and ensure that the \<emph\>Check in all languages\</emph\> check box in the \<emph\>Options \</emph\>list is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\select_language.xhp	0	help	par_id3155914	34			0	br	$[officename] can check the spelling of words in more than one language, provided that you have installed dictionaries for the other languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\select_language.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257	37			0	br	If you do not enable the \<emph\>Check in all languages \</emph\>feature, words that do not occur in the default language of the document are underlined by a wavy red line. To assign the underlined word to another language, right-click the word, and then choose\<emph\> Word is \</emph\>or \<emph\>Paragraph is\</emph\>, where the suggested language and country is shown in the command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\select_language.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Checking Spelling in Other Languages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145087				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>text documents; publishing in HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; creating from text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>homepage creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;in HTML format\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145087				0	br	\<variable id=\"send2html\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/send2html.xhp\" name=\"Saving Text Documents in HTML Format\"\>Saving Text Documents in HTML Format\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	br	In the \<emph\>Styles \</emph\>box, select the paragraph style that you want to use to generate a new HTML page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3149825				0	br	You can save a $[officename] Writer document in HTML format, so that you can view it in a web browser. If you want, you can associate a page break with a specific heading paragraph style to generate a separate HTML page each time the style appears in the document. $[officename] Writer automatically creates a page containing hyperlinks to each of these pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3153407				0	br	Enter a path and a name for the HTML document, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3155868				0	br	Apply one of the default $[officename] heading paragraph styles, for example, "Heading 1", to the paragraphs where you want to generate a new HTML page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	br	When you save a text document in HTML format, any graphics in the document are saved in JPEG format. The name of the HTML document is added as a prefix to the name of the graphic file. The JPEG images are saved in the same folder as the HTML document and are referenced with <IMG> tags in the HTML code.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3156100				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Send - Create HTML Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Saving Text Documents in HTML Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
