helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149689				0	br	\<variable id=\"shortcut_writing\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/shortcut_writing.xhp\" name=\"Applying Text Formatting While You Type\"\>Applying Text Formatting While You Type\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155909				0	br	To apply bold formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0400.xhp\" name=\"Keyboard shortcut in $[officename]\"\>Keyboard shortcut in $[officename]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	par_id3149648				0	br	\<link href=\"text/swriter/04/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Keyboard shortcut for text documents\"\>Keyboard shortcut for text documents\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	par_id3149836	5			0	br	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+B.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	br	Select the text that you want to format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	par_id3156112	6			0	br	You can also press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+B, type the text that you want to format in bold, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+B when you are finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Applying Text Formatting While You Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155622				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>smart tags; using\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id2376476				0	br	To enable and disable Smart Tags				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3563951				0	br	\<variable id=\"smarttags\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/smarttags.xhp\"\>Using Smart Tags\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id8142338				0	br	Smart Tags menu				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id9298379				0	br	Installing Smart Tags				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1216467				0	br	Text that is recognized as a Smart Tag is not checked by the automatic spellcheck.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1827448				0	br	Smart Tags can be supplied as \<link href=\"text/shared/01/packagemanager.xhp\"\>extensions\</link\> to %PRODUCTNAME Writer. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1917477				0	br	Any text in a Writer document can be marked with a Smart Tag, by default a magenta colored underline. You can change the color in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME - Appearance\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id192266				0	br	When you point to a Smart Tag, a tip help informs you to Ctrl-click to open the Smart Tags menu. If you don't use a mouse, position the cursor inside the marked text and open the context menu by Shift+F10.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1998962				0	br	In the Smart Tags menu you see the available actions that are defined for this Smart Tag. Choose an option from the menu. The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Smart Tags Options\</item\> command opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040700.xhp\"\>Smart Tags\</link\> page of Tools - Autocorrect.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id2508621				0	br	To install a Smart Tag, do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id349131				0	br	When you have installed at least one Smart Tags extension, you see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040700.xhp\"\>Smart Tags\</link\> page in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Autocorrect\</item\>. Use this dialog to enable or disable Smart Tags and to manage the installed tags.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id368358				0	br	Smart Tags provide additional information and functionality to specified words in a Writer document. The available features can be different for different Smart Tags extensions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id3856013				0	br	Save the *.oxt extension file to your harddrive, then double-click the *.oxt file in your file manager. Alternatively, in %PRODUCTNAME choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Extension Manager\</item\> to open the Extension Manager, click Add and browse to the file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id7814264				0	br	Click a Smart Tag *.oxt file link on a web page and open the link with the default application. This requires a properly configured Web browser.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Using Smart Tags				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149684				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>spellcheck; checking text documents manually\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>checking spelling;manually\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149684				0	br	\<variable id=\"spellcheck_dialog\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/spellcheck_dialog.xhp\" name=\"Checking Spelling Manually\"\>Checking Spelling Manually\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3145099				0	br	To accept a correction, click the suggestion, and then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3147107				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06010000.xhp\" name=\"Spellcheck dialog\"\>Spellcheck dialog\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149814				0	br	You can manually check the spelling of a text selection or the entire document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149828				0	br	The spellcheck starts at the current cursor position, or at the beginning of the text selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149836				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Spellcheck\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149861				0	br	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155859				0	br	Click in the document, or select the text that you want to check.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	br	To add the unknown word to a user-defined dictionary, click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3156104				0	br	When a possible spelling error is encountered, the \<emph\>Spellcheck \</emph\>dialog opens and $[officename] offers some suggested corrections.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3156241				0	br	Edit the sentence in the upper text box, and then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Checking Spelling Manually				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145084				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>fill format mode\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>brush for copying styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles; transferring\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145084				0	br	\<variable id=\"stylist_fillformat\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/stylist_fillformat.xhp\" name=\"Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode\"\>Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090	17			0	br	Click the style, and then click the \<emph\>Fill Format Mode\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149644\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fillstyle.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149644\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153128				0	br	Click the icon of the style category that you want to apply.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153371				0	br	Move the mouse pointer to where you want to apply the style in the document, and click. To apply the style to more than one item, drag to select the items, and then release.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	br	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Esc\</item\> when finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	br	You can quickly apply styles, such as paragraph and character styles, in your document by using the Fill Format Mode in the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3156114				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3159259				0	br	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155911				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>styles; creating from selections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>creating;new styles from selections\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153373				0	br	To create a new style by drag-and-drop:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155911				0	br	\<variable id=\"stylist_fromselect\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/stylist_fromselect.xhp\" name=\"Creating New Styles From Selections\"\>Creating New Styles From Selections\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149829				0	br	You can quickly create a new style from an existing style that you have applied manual formatting to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149988				0	br	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153119				0	br	Click in the document where you want to copy the style from, for example, in a paragraph that you applied manual formatting to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153138				0	br	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon and choose \<emph\>New Style from Selection \</emph\>from the submenu				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153402				0	br	Click the icon of the style category that you want to create.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	br	Click the icon of the style category that you want to create.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154411				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154851				0	br	Select at least one character, or object, in the style that you want to copy. For page and frame styles, select at least one character or object in the page or frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154871				0	br	Drag the character or object to the Styles and Formatting window and release.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3156097				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3156260				0	br	Type a name in the \<emph\>Style Name \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	br	For Paragraph and Character Styles, you can drag-and-drop onto the respective icon in the Styles and Formatting window. You do not need to open that style category in advance.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B5				0	br	You can also drag-and-drop a frame into the Styles and Formatting window to create a new frame style: Click the frame, wait a moment with the mouse button pressed down, but without moving the mouse, then drag to the Styles and Formatting window and drop the frame onto the Frame Styles icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Creating New Styles From Selections				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155915				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>Stylist, see Styles and Formatting window\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles; updating from selections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates; updating from selections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Styles and Formatting window; updating from selections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating; styles, from selections\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155915				0	br	\<variable id=\"stylist_update\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/stylist_update.xhp\" name=\"Updating Styles From Selections\"\>Updating Styles From Selections\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3149283				0	br	In the document, click where you want to copy the updated style from. For example, click a paragraph that you applied manual formatting to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3149838				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3153119				0	br	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon and choose \<emph\>Update Style\</emph\> from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3153402				0	br	In the Styles and Formatting window, click the style that you want to update.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3155498				0	br	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3156107				0	br	Click the icon of the style category that you want to update.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
