helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id6618243				0	br	\<variable id=\"table_cellmerge\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_cellmerge.xhp\" name=\"Merging and Splitting Cells\"\>Merging and Splitting Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id9156468				0	br	Splitting Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id1211890				0	br	You can select adjacent cells, then merge them into a single cell. Conversely, you can take a large cell and divide it into individual cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3415936				0	br	Place the cursor in the cell to be split.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id4044312				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Table - Split Cells\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id5708792				0	br	Select the adjacent cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id6301461				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Table - Merge Cells\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id634174				0	br	A dialog allows you to split the cell into two or more cells, horizontally or vertically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Merging and Splitting Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
