helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3358867				0	br	To change the width and height of a table, do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id4190496				0	br	Tables within HTML pages do not offer the full range of properties and commands as tables in OpenDocument format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id5009308				0	br	To wrap text to the sides of a table, and to arrange two tables next to another, you must insert the tables into a frame. Click inside the table, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+A\</item\> twice to select the whole table, then choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id5366679				0	br	Click inside the table. In the rulers, drag the border between the white and the gray area to resize the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
