helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155856				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>table mode selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>proportional distribution of tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative distribution of table cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; adapting the width by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; adapting the width by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keyboard;modifying the behavior of rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>behavior of rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155856				0	br	\<variable id=\"tablemode\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/tablemode.xhp\" name=\"Modifying the Behavior of Rows and Columns for Table\"\>Modifying Rows and Columns by Keyboard\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149613				0	br	\<emph\>Fixed, proportional\</emph\> - changes affect the entire table, and wide cells shrink more than narrow cells. For example, when you widen a cell, the adjacent cells become proportionally narrower, but the width of the table remains constant.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149638				0	br	\<emph\>Fixed\</emph\> - changes only affect the adjacent cell, and not the entire table. For example, when you widen a cell, the adjacent cell becomes narrower, but the width of the table remains constant.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149835				0	br	When you insert or delete cells, rows or columns in a table, the \<emph\>Behavior of rows/columns\</emph\> options determine how the neighboring elements are affected. For example, you can only insert new rows and columns into a table with \<emph\>Fixed\</emph\> row and column dimensions if space permits.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149864				0	br	\<emph\>Variable\</emph\> - changes affect the table size. For example, when you widen a cell, the width of the table increases.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3156110				0	br	To set the \<emph\>Behavior of rows/columns \</emph\>options for tables in text documents, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</emph\>, or use the \<emph\>Fixed\</emph\>, \<emph\>Fixed/Proportional\</emph\>, and \<emph\>Variable\</emph\> icons on the \<emph\>Table Bar\</emph\>. There are three display modes for tables:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id7344279				0	br	Note that these properties are valid only for changes to the column width that are made using the keyboard. Using the mouse, you are free to make any column width changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Modifying Rows and Columns by Keyboard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149688				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>document templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates; creating document templates\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149688				0	br	\<variable id=\"template_create\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/template_create.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Document Template\"\>Creating a Document Template\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147422				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149492				0	br	You can create a template to use as the basis for creating new text documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149636				0	br	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110300.xhp\" name=\"File - Templates - Save\"\>File - Templates - Save\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149829				0	br	In the \<emph\>New Template \</emph\>box, type a name for the new template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3153404				0	br	To create a document based on the template, choose\<emph\> File - New - Templates and Documents\</emph\>, select the template, and then click\<emph\> Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3155915				0	br	Create a document and add the content and formatting styles that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3156098				0	br	Select a template category in the \<emph\>Categories \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Creating a Document Template				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155913				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>default templates; defining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults; templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates; default templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text;default templates\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149867				0	br	To reset the default template:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155913				0	br	\<variable id=\"template_default\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/template_default.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Default Template\"\>Changing the Default Template\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3145102				0	br	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"File - Templates - Organize\"\>\<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3145569				0	br	The default template contains the default formatting information for new text documents. If you want, you can create a new template and use it as the default template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149283				0	br	In the \<emph\>New Template\</emph\> box, type a name for the new template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149582				0	br	Right-click a folder in the category list, choose\<emph\> Reset Default Template - Text Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149620				0	br	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149838				0	br	Create a document and the content and formatting styles that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149952				0	br	In the category list, double-click the "My Templates" folder.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149970				0	br	Right-click the template that you created, and choose \<emph\>Set as Default Template\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3153140				0	br	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"File - Templates - Organize\"\>\<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3153409				0	br	In the \<emph\>Categories \</emph\>list, select "My Templates", and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3156101				0	br	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3156245				0	br	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Changing the Default Template				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153396				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>formatting styles; styles and templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles; styles and templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>organizing; templates (guide)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates; organizing (guide)\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149613				0	br	Viewing and Organizing Styles in Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153396				0	br	\<variable id=\"templates_styles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/templates_styles.xhp\" name=\"Templates and Styles\"\>Templates and Styles\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635				0	br	A template is a document that contains specific formatting styles, graphics, tables, object, and other information. A template is used as the basis for creating other documents. For example, you can define paragraph and character styles in a document, save the document as a template, and then use the template to create a new document with the same styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149957				0	br	Unless you specify otherwise, every new $[officename] text document is based on the default template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149974				0	br	$[officename] has a number of \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"predefined templates\"\>predefined templates\</link\> that you can use to create different types or text documents, such as business letters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153377				0	br	To copy a style, drag it to another template or document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B0				0	br	Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"Template Management\"\>Template Management\</link\> dialog to copy styles from one document to another.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Templates and Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151182				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>text animation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>effects; text animation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>animating text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151182				0	br	\<variable id=\"text_animation\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_animation.xhp\" name=\"Animating Text\"\>Animating Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3145080				0	br	You can only animate text that is contained in a drawing object, such as rectangles, lines, or text objects. For example, draw a rectangle, then double-click the rectangle and enter your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	br	Set the properties of the effect, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	br	Select the drawing object containing the text that you want to animate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149819				0	br	In the \<emph\>Effect \</emph\>box, select the animation that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Text Attributes\</emph\>, and then click the\<emph\> Text Animation\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Animating Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155182				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>characters; uppercase or lowercase\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; uppercase or lowercase\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lowercase letters; text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>uppercase; formatting text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>capital letters;changing to small letters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;cases of text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>initial capitals in titles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149644				0	br	To change text to lowercase:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155182				0	br	\<variable id=\"text_capital\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_capital.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Case of Text\"\>Changing the Case of Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155861				0	br	To capitalize text:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3145093	5			0	br	Choose\<emph\> Format - Character\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Font Effects\</emph\> tab, and then select "Lowercase" in the\<emph\> Effects\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3147420				0	br	Select the text that you want to capitalize.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149606				0	br	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149841				0	br	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149855	7			0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Change Case - Lowercase\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149964				0	br	Select the text that you want to change to lowercase.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414	4			0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Font Effects\</emph\> tab, and then select the type of capitalization in the \<emph\>Effects\</emph\> box. "Capitals" capitalizes all of the letters in the selection. "Title" capitalizes the first letter of each word in the selection. "Small capitals" capitalizes every letter in the selection, but in a reduced font size.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3155916				0	br	You can change the case of text, format text with small capitals, or capitalize the first letter of each word in a selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3156109	6			0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Change Case - Uppercase\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	br	When you apply a formatting to your text by \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>, the text stays the same, it is only displayed in another way. On the other hand, when you choose \<emph\>Format - Change Case\</emph\>, the text is permanently changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Changing the Case of Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155177				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>text frames; centering on pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>centering;text frames on pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title pages; centering text on\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155177				0	br	\<variable id=\"text_centervert\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_centervert.xhp\" name=\"Using a Frame to Center Text on a Page\"\>Using a Frame to Center Text on a Page\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145098				0	br	To resize the frame, drag the edges of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149615				0	br	To hide the borders of the frame, select the frame, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Frame\</emph\>. Click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> tab, and then click in the\<emph\> Set No Border\</emph\> box in the\<emph\> Line Arrangement\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149844				0	br	In the \<emph\>Size \</emph\>area, set the dimensions of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152765				0	br	In the \<emph\>Anchor \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>To page\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153410				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155868				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155920				0	br	Select the text that you want to center on the page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156114				0	br	In the \<emph\>Position \</emph\>area, select "Center" in the \<emph\>Horizontal \</emph\>and \<emph\>Vertical \</emph\>boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Using a Frame to Center Text on a Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155178				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>text; cursor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entering text with direct cursor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>direct cursor; settings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>writing with direct cursor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cursor;direct cursor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>settings;direct cursor\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155178				0	br	\<variable id=\"text_direct_cursor\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_direct_cursor.xhp\" name=\"Using the Direct Cursor\"\>Using the Direct Cursor\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_id3155908				0	br	The direct cursor allows you to enter text anywhere on a page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_id3155921				0	br	To set the behavior of the direct cursor, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A3				0	br	On the \<emph\>Tools\</emph\> bar, click the \<emph\>Direct Cursor\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149846\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_shadowcursor.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149846\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	br	Click in a free space in the text document. The mouse pointer changes to reflect the alignment that will be applied to the text that you type:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C8				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id5471987\" src=\"res/helpimg/dircursleft.png\" width=\"3.7mm\" height=\"8.2mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5471987\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> Align left				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E4				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id5730253\" src=\"res/helpimg/dircurscent.png\" width=\"6.09mm\" height=\"8.2mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5730253\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> Centered				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN10700				0	br	\<image id=\"img_id6953622\" src=\"res/helpimg/dircursright.png\" width=\"3.97mm\" height=\"8.2mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6953622\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> Align right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071D				0	br	Type your text. %PRODUCTNAME automatically inserts the required number of blank lines, and, if the options are enabled, tabs and spaces.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Using the Direct Cursor				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149820				0	br	\<bookmark_value\>text; emphasizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>emphasizing text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149820				0	br	\<variable id=\"text_emphasize\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_emphasize.xhp\" name=\"Emphasizing Text\"\>Emphasizing Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	br	Select the text and apply a different font style or effect, such as \<emph\>bold\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3149840	68			0	br	Right-click in a paragraph, choose \<emph\>Paragraph, \</emph\>set the options that you want, for example, the background color, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	br	Select the text, and then choose \<emph\>Insert Frame\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	br	Here are a few examples of how to emphasize text in a document:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id6924649				0	br	Use the Text tool on the Drawing toolbar. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
