helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3147414				0	br	Automatic hyphenation inserts hyphens where they are needed in a paragraph. This option is only available for paragraph styles and individual paragraphs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3148850				0	br	Right-click in a paragraph, and choose \<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3148949	63			0	br	To insert the hyphen in another part of the word, click the arrow buttons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149582				0	br	In the \<emph\>Hyphenation\</emph\> area, select the \<emph\>Automatically\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149644				0	br	If you want to automatically hyphenate more than one paragraph, use a paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149867				0	br	Right-click the paragraph style that you want to hyphenate, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149956				0	br	For example, enable the automatic hyphenation option for the "Default" paragraph style, and then apply the style to the paragraphs that you want to hyphenate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3150101				0	br	In the \<emph\>Hyphenation \</emph\>area, select the \<emph\>Automatically\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153017	27			0	br	To accept the hyphenation suggestion, click \<emph\>Hyphenate\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153121				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	br	To quickly insert a hyphen, click in the word where you want to add the hyphen, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Hyphen(-).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154244				0	br	If you insert a manual hyphen in a word, the word is only hyphenated at the manual hyphen. No additional automatic hyphenation is applied for this word. A word with a manual hyphen will be hyphenated without regard to the settings on the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154361				0	br	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>Text Flow\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154400				0	br	You can insert a hyphen where you want on a line, or let $[officename] search for the words to hyphenate, and then offer a suggested hyphenation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154869				0	br	Select the text that you want to hyphenate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	br	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Language - Hyphenation\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3155918	31			0	br	By default, $[officename] moves words that do not fit on a line to the next line. If you want, you can use automatic or manual hyphenation to avoid this behavior: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3155943	62			0	br	When $[officename] encounters a word to hyphenate, do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3156104				0	br	Click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>\<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3156250				0	br	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	tit				0	br	Hyphenation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
