helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346	91			0	br	If there is more than one word in the AutoCorrect memory that matches the three letters that you type, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Tab\</item\> to cycle through the available words. To cycle in the opposite direction, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Shift+Tab\</item\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	br	\<variable id=\"word_completion\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion.xhp\"\>Word Completion for Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076F				0	br	$[officename] collects words that you frequently use in the current session. When you later type the first three letters of a collected word, $[officename] automatically completes the word. If you want, you can also save the current list of collected words so that it can be used in the next session. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078D				0	br	 Using word completion 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN10794				0	br	By default, you accept the word completion by pressing the Enter key. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079B				0	br	 To reject the word completion, continue typing with any other key. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079E				0	br	 Switching off the word completion 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A5				0	br	 Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect - Word Completion\</emph\> . 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AD				0	br	 Clear \<emph\>Enable word completion\</emph\> . 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
